l", "target_name": "Aqueo", "similarity": 0.889}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "agua", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Aqueo", "similarity": 0.881}], "id": 0, "stable_key": "clu_e346559b4a2d1303", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "water", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A transparent liquid essential for life, used medicinally and as a medium.", "note": "Includes Portuguese ('agua'), French ('eau'), and generic terms ('fluid').", "wikipedia_extract": "Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans and the fluids of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}, "member_count": 13, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "fluids", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 393, "target_cluster_name": "fluids", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Water is a quintessential example of a fluid and was often used synonymously or as the primary referent when discussing fluids in general.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Water is a quintessential example of a fluid and was often used synonymously or as the primary referent when discussing fluids in general.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "iolitej", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id"