rocess of separating liquids", "process to obtain water"]}, {"entity_id": "distillation", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Distillation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 5, "variants": ["Distillation", "distillation", "distillatona"], "contexts": ["practice mentioned in context of purification", "process of extracting liquids"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "distillation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "distillation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Distillation", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Distillation", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2, "stable_key": "clu_ab25fdc8334e86d4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "distillation", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "A process of heating and cooling to separate or purify substances.", "wikipedia_extract": "Distillation, also classical distillation, is the process of separating the component substances of a liquid mixture of two or more chemically discrete substances; the separation process is realized by way of the selective boiling of the mixture and the condensation of the vapors in a still. Distillation can operate over a wide range of pressures from 0.14 bar (e.g., ethylbenzene/styrene) to nearly 21 bar (e.g., propylene/propane) and is capable of separating feeds with high volumetric flowrates and various components that cover a range of relative volatilities from only 1.17 (o-xylene/m-xylene) to 81.2 (water/ethylene glycol). Distillation provides a convenient and time-tested solution to separate a diversity of chemicals in a continuous manner with high purity. However, distillation has an enormous environmental footprint, resulting in the consumption of approximately 25% of all industrial energy use. The key issue is that distillation operates based on phase changes, and this separation mechanism requires vast energy inputs. Dry distillation (thermolysis and pyrolysis) is the heating of solid materials to produce gases that condense either into fluid products or into solid products."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Condensation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1255, "target_cluster_name": "condensations", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Condensation is the complementary process to boiling, which is the first step in distillation. Vapors are condensed to form the purified liquid.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Condensation is the complementary process to boiling, which is the first step in distillation. Vapors are condensed to form the purified liquid."}, {"found_name": "Antimonio Diaphoretico", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "Ao Antimonio Diaphoretico chamou Fa. bro , 26 Unicornio mineral. Ao Mercurio Diaphoretico fixo 27. chamão muytos , Diafeltetafon. ACaparroſa depois de deſtillada , que ja nao tenha olto ,nem coula que", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "Unicorno mineral", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "Ao Antimonio Diaphoretico chamou Fa. bro , 26 Unicornio mineral. Ao Mercurio Diaphoretico fixo 27. chamão muytos , Diafeltetafon. ACaparroſa depois de deſtillada , que ja nao tenha olto ,nem coula que", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "Mercurio Diaphoretico fixo", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "Ao Antimonio Diaphoretico chamou Fa. bro , 26 Unicornio mineral. Ao Mercurio Diaphoretico fixo 27. chamão muytos , Diafeltetafon. ACaparroſa depois de deſtillada , que ja nao tenha olto ,nem coula que", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "Diafeltetafon", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name"