rimarily composed of carbon and mineral compounds resulting from combustion. Carbon is a fundamental component of spodium.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ashes are primarily composed of carbon and mineral compounds resulting from combustion. Carbon is a fundamental component of spodium.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "carvaó", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2480, "target_cluster_name": "carvaó", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Charcoal is a form of carbon.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Charcoal is a form of carbon.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "carbureted hydrogen gas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2601, "target_cluster_name": "carbureted hydrogen gas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ethane is a hydrocarbon, meaning it is composed of hydrogen and carbon. Historical discussions of ethane would likely be situated within broader conversations about carbon and its properties.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ethane is a hydrocarbon, meaning it is composed of hydrogen and carbon. Historical discussions of ethane would likely be situated within broader conversations about carbon and its properties.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "count": 9, "variants": ["creation", "Creation"], "contexts": ["special act of creation", "theory of divine origin"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["creation", "Creation"], "contexts": ["the universe and all within it", "act of bringing into existence"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 2, "variants": ["creation"], "contexts": ["the act of bringing something into existence", "act of bringing something into existence"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Creation"], "contexts": ["the act of bringing the universe into existence"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Creation"], "contexts": ["harmony and wisdom of God"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Creation", "creation"], "contexts": ["act of bringing into existence", "religious concept of origin"]}, {"entity_id": "creation", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Creation", "creation"], "contexts": ["the universe and its existence", "the act of making the world"]}, {"entity_id": "theory_of_creation", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "theory of creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "count": 6, "variants": ["theory of creation"], "contexts": ["explanation for species distribution", "explanation of life's origin by a creator"]}, {"entity_id": "theory_of_creation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "theory of creation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "count": 2, "variants": ["theory of creation"], "contexts": ["explanation of the origin of the universe", "explanation for the origin of the universe"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "creation", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "creation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "creation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Creation", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Creation", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 12, "stable_key": "clu_82b49559776b1e70", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Creationism", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Contexts suggest a theory of how species originated, contrasting with Darwinian evolution.", "wikidata_id": "Q1430216", "wikidata_description": "doctrine that God creates a soul for each body that is generated, as opposed to pre-existing before birth or being generated during conception", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Creationism%20%28soul%29", "wikipedia_extract": "Creationism is the religious belief that nature, and aspects such as the universe, Earth, life, and humans, originated with supernatural acts of divine creation, and is often pseudoscientific. In its broadest sense, creationism includes various religious views, which differ in their acceptance or rejection of modern scientific concepts, such as evolution, that describe the origin and development of natural phenomena. The term creationism most often refers to belief in special creation: the claim that the universe and lifeforms were created as they exist today by divine action, and that the only true explanations are those which are compatible with a Christian fundamentalist literal interpretation of the creation myth found in the Bible's Genesis creation narrative. Since the 1970s, the most common form of this has been Young Earth creationism which posits special creation of the universe and lifeforms within the last 10,000 years on the basis of flood geology, and promotes pseudoscientific creation science. From the 18th century onward, Old Earth creationism accepted geological time harmonized with Genesis through gap or day-age theory, while supporting anti-evolution. Modern old-Earth creationists support progressive creationism and continue to reject evolutionary explanations."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Divinity", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2345, "target_cluster_name": "Divinity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Creationism posits Divinity as the ultimate creator of the universe.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Creationism posits Divinity as the ultimate creator of the universe.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Divine wisdom", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3269, "target_cluster_name": "Divine Wisdom", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Creationism is a religious belief centered on divine acts of creation, and divine wisdom is a concept closely associated with the nature and intent of a creator.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Creationism is a religious belief centered on divine acts of creation, and divine wisdom is a concept closely associated with the nature and intent of a creator."}, {"found_name": "Cosmos", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 941, "target_cluster_name": "heavens", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Creationism posits that the cosmos originated from supernatural acts of divine creation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Creationism posits that the cosmos originated from supernatural acts of divine creation."}, {"found_name": "Belief", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2125, "target_cluster_name": "belief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Creationism is fundamentally a religious belief system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Creationism is fundamentally a religious belief system."}, {"found_name": "dissolve", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1327, "target_cluster_name": "dissolve", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pralaya is a concept of cosmic dissolution in Hindu eschatology, which is a counterpart to the concept of creation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Pralaya is a concept of cosmic dissolution in Hindu eschatology, which is a counterpart to the concept of creation.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Christ", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 