ome of the Earth's highest peaks, including the highest, Mount Everest. More than 100 peaks exceeding elevations of 7,200 m (23,600 ft) above sea level lie in the Himalayas. The Himalayas abut on or cross territories of five countries: Nepal, India, China, Bhutan and Pakistan. The sovereignty of the range in the Kashmir region is disputed among India, Pakistan, and China. The Himalayan range is bordered on the northwest by the Karakoram and Hindu Kush ranges, on the north by the Tibetan Plateau, and on the south by the Indo-Gangetic Plain."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alps", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 285, "target_cluster_name": "Alpes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are major mountain ranges in Asia and Europe, respectively, and are often discussed in geographical contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are major mountain ranges in Asia and Europe, respectively, and are often discussed in geographical contexts."}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Himalayas are a prominent geographical feature within the continent of Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Himalayas are a prominent geographical feature within the continent of Asia."}, {"found_name": "Madhjadeca", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "literature, habits, and conditions of society) an individual form in the Magodha of Madhya Desa,* a district that is bounded by the great chain p 36 of Himalaya and the smaller range of the Vindhya. [", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}]}