Animals form a clade, meaning that they arose from a single common ancestor. Over 1.5 million living animal species have been described, of which around 1.05 million are insects, over 85,000 are molluscs, and around 65,000 are vertebrates. It has been estimated there are as many as 7.77 million animal species on Earth. Animal body lengths range from 8.5 μm (0.00033 in) to 33.6 m (110 ft)."}, "member_count": 16, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Insects", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4, "target_cluster_name": "insects", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Insects are a major class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Insects are a major class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals."}, {"found_name": "Mammals", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 266, "target_cluster_name": "mammals", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Mammals are a class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Mammals are a class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals."}, {"found_name": "Reptiles", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 122, "target_cluster_name": "reptiles", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Reptiles are a class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Reptiles are a class within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals."}, {"found_name": "Fish", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 