_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "soil", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "terra", "similarity": 0.923}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "soil", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Soil", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "terra", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Soil", "similarity": 0.923}], "id": 21, "stable_key": "clu_1de856d369fb63c7", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Earth", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "The term 'terra' (Spanish/Portuguese) and 'earth' (English) refers to soil, land, or the element earth in classical and early modern contexts.", "wikidata_id": "Q36133", "wikidata_description": "natural body consisting of layers that are primarily composed of minerals", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soil", "country": "Global", "wikipedia_extract": "Soil, also commonly referred to as earth, is a mixture of organic matter, minerals, gases, water, and organisms that together support the life of plants and soil organisms. Some scientific definitions distinguish dirt from soil by restricting the former term specifically to displaced soil. Soil consists of a solid collection of minerals and organic matter (the soil matrix), as well as a porous phase that holds gases (the soil atmosphere) and a liquid phase that holds water and dissolved substances both organic and inorganic, in ionic or in molecular form (the soil solution). Accordingly, soil is a complex three-state system of solids, liquids, and gases. Soil is a product of several factors: the influence of climate, relief (elevation, orientation, and slope of terrain), organisms, and the soil's parent materials (original minerals) interacting over time. It continually undergoes development by way of numerous physical, chemical and biological processes, which include weathering with associated erosion."}, "member_count": 8, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "lignites", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1760, "target_cluster_name": "lignites", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lignite is a substance found within the Earth's crust, often associated with sedimentary deposits.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lignite is a substance found within the Earth's crust, often associated with sedimentary deposits.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Terra Lemnia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 482, "target_cluster_name": "Terra Lemnia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lemnian Earth is a specific type of earth, and 'Earth' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lemnian Earth is a specific type of earth, and 'Earth' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "substancia terrea", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1485, "target_cluster_name": "substancia terrea", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The entity 'earthy matter' is a direct component or characteristic of the planet 'Earth'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The entity 'earthy matter' is a direct component or characteristic of the planet 'Earth'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "north pole", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2136, "target_cluster_name": "north pole", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The North Pole is a specific location on the planet Earth. Discussions of the North Pole are inherently tied to discussions of the Earth itself.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The North Pole is a spe