 the rest, many are gymnosperms or softwoods. Trees tend to be long-lived, some trees reaching several thousand years old."}, "member_count": 12, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "arvore", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1632, "target_cluster_name": "arvore", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for Tree", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Portuguese for Tree", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "coquo", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 836, "target_cluster_name": "coco", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "chama jcai\\ialindi, que quer dizer no^ da índia; e Serapio* e Rasis chamam ao arvore j ar alnare, que quer àizcr ^arvore que dá coquos; e os Malabares chamam ao arvore tengamaram, e o firuito, quando ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Portuguese name for the fruit of the tree"}, {"found_name": "sanguis draconis", "link_type": "contested_identity", "link_strength": 0.7, "target_cluster_id": 1168, "target_cluster_name": "Sangue di drago", "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "deluded, who conceive _sperma Coeti_ which is found about the head, to be the spawn of the Whale: Or take _sanguis draconis_ (which is the gumme of a tree,) to be the blood of a Dragon. By the same Lo", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "contested_identity", "found_relationship": "gum of a tree, mistaken for blood of Dragon"}, {"found_name": "Bark", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1836, "target_cluster_name": "Bark", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Bark is a component of a tree.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Bark is a component of a tree."}, {"found_name": "Branches", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_