at encompasses it. Historical texts often discuss the nature and properties of light, with sunlight being a primary example.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sunlight is a specific form of light, and 'Light' is a broader category that encompasses it. Historical texts often discuss the nature and properties of light, with sunlight being a primary example.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "light polarized", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4531, "target_cluster_name": "light polarized", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Polarized light is a specific phenomenon of light, and 'Light' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Polarized light is a specific phenomenon of light, and 'Light' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "red light", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2588, "target_cluster_name": "red light", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Red light is a specific type of light, and 'Light' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Red light is a specific type of light, and 'Light' is a broader category that encompasses it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "aërolites", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 678, "target_cluster_name": "aerolites", "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "considerably lowered the lines which had, perhaps with some degree of temerity, been usually termed the boundaries of the atmosphere; but processes of light may be evolved independently of the presenc", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "contested_identity", "found_relationship": "objects that may be ignited by light phenomena"}, {"found_name": "Nebulous stars", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "contracts), nor with the so-called planetary nebulae, whose circular or slightly oval disks manifest in all their parts a perfectly uniform degree of faint light. 'Nebulous stars' are not merely accid", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for celestial objects"}]}, {"canonical_name": "memory", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 182, "members": [{"entity_id": "memory", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Memory", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["Memory"], "contexts": ["mental faculty improved by treatment", "faculty of retaining and recalling information"]}, {"entity_id": "memory", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "memory", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 143, "variants": ["memory", "MEMORY", "Memory"], "contexts": ["ability to recall past experiences", "Soul's faculty"]}, {"entity_id": "memoria", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "memoria", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["memoria"], "contexts": ["faculty Ambar can improve"]}, {"entity_id": "memoria", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "memoria", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 22, "variants": ["Memoria", "memoria"], "contexts": ["memory", "faculty of the soul for retention"]}, {"entity_id": "memory", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "memory", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["memory"], "contexts": ["faculty of recalling past experiences"]}, {"entity_id": "memories", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Memories", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Memories"], "contexts": ["faculty of retaining information", "faculty of retaining past experiences"]}, {"entity_id": "memories", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "memories", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 7, "variants": ["memories"], "contexts": ["recollection of past experiences", "stored information from past experiences"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Memory", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "memory", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Memory", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "memoria", "similarity": 0.92}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Memory", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "memoria", "similarity": 0.92}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Memory", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "memory", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "memory", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "memoria", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "memory", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "memoria", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "memory", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "memory", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "memoria", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "memoria", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "memoria", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "memory", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "memoria", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "memory", "similarity": 0.949}], "id": 35, "stable_key": "clu_be4d8906790b0e36", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Memory", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q492", "wikidata_description": "mental faculties and processes involved in storing and retrieving information", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory", "wikipedia_extract": "Memory is the faculty of the mind by which data or information is encoded, stored, and retrieved when needed. It is the retention of information over time for the purpose of influencing future action. If past events could not be remembered, it would be impossible for language, relationships, or personal identity to develop. Memory loss is usually described as forgetfulness or amnesia. Memory is often understood as an informational processing system with explicit and implicit functioning that is made up of a sensory processor, short-term (or working) memory, and long-term memory. This can be related to the neuron."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Association of Ideas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1992, "target_cluster_name": "association of ideas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The 'Association of Ideas' is a specific theory about how memories are linked and retrieved, making it a directly related concept to memory itself.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The 'Association of Ideas' is a specific theory about how memories are linked and retrieved, making it a directly related concept to memory itself."}, {"found_name": "Cognition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 656, "target_cluster_name": "cognition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition encompasses memory as one of its core functions, involving the mental processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cognition encompasses memory as one of its core functions, involving the mental processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding."}, {"found_name": "Experience", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 105, "target_cluster_name": "experience", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Experience is the direct observation of or participation in events, which forms the basis for many memories.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Experience is the direct observation of or participation in events, which forms the basis for many memories."}, {"found_name": "past", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2571, "target_cluster_name": "past", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Memory is the faculty by which the mind stores and remembers information from the past.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Memory is the faculty by which the mind stores and remembers information from the past.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Paris", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 170, "members": [{"entity_id": "paris", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Paris", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 95, "variants": ["Paris", "PARIS", "de Paris"], "contexts": ["city where Jardin des Plantes is located", "capital of France"]}, {"entity_id": "paris", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Paris", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 13, "variants": ["Paris"], "contexts": ["city revisited after ten years' absence", "city where L'Automatisme Psychologique was published"]}, {"entity_id": "paris", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "n