mboldt"], "contexts": ["author of 'Cosmos'", "cited for astronomical observations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Humboldt", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Humboldt", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 42, "stable_key": "clu_c1cfa071b54fde44", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1769, "death_year": 1859, "description": "Prussian explorer and naturalist, key figure in biogeography", "wikidata_id": "Q6694", "wikidata_description": "Prussian geographer, naturalist and explorer (1769–1859)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander%20von%20Humboldt", "wikipedia_extract": "Friedrich Wilhelm Heinrich Alexander von Humboldt (14 September 1769 – 6 May 1859) was a German polymath, geographer, naturalist, explorer, and proponent of Romantic philosophy and science. He was the younger brother of the Prussian minister, philosopher, and linguist Wilhelm von Humboldt (1767–1835). Humboldt's quantitative work on botanical geography laid the foundation for the field of biogeography, while his advocacy of long-term systematic geophysical measurement pioneered modern geomagnetic and meteorological monitoring. Humboldt and Carl Ritter are both regarded as the founders of modern geography as they established it as an independent scientific discipline. Between 1799 and 1804, Humboldt travelled extensively in the Americas, exploring and describing them for the first time from a non-Spanish European scientific point of view. On these travels, along with French explorer Aimé Bonpland, he traversed thousands of miles through some of the most difficult and little-known places on Earth, to include identifying the source of the Orinoco River and in 1802 climbing the highest mountain in Ecuador to a height of 19,286 feet, at the time a world record altitude for a Westerner."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Darwin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 118, "target_cluster_name": "Darwin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Influential naturalist and explorer whose work inspired Darwin.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Influential naturalist and explorer whose work inspired Darwin.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Pallas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 446, "target_cluster_name": "Pallas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent naturalists and explorers active in the late 18th and early 19th centuries, undertaking extensive scientific expeditions and contributing significantly to the understanding of geography, zoology, and botany.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent naturalists and explorers active in the late 18th and early 19th centuries, undertaking extensive scientific expeditions and contributing significantly to the understanding of geography, zoology, and botany.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Drake", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 461, "target_cluster_name": "Drake", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were renowned explorers and naturalists who significantly contributed to the understanding of geography and natural sciences through their extensive voyages and detailed observations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were renowned explorers and naturalists who significantly contributed to the understanding of geography and natural sciences through their extensive voyages and detailed observations.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Sir John Herschel", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 554, "target_cluster_name": "Sir John Herschel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent scientists and explorers who made significant contributions to natural history and geography. Humboldt's extensive work in exploration and scientific observation likely influenced or was known to Herschel.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent scientists and explorers who made significant contributions to natural history and geography. Humboldt's extensive work in exploration and scientific observation likely influenced or was known to Herschel.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Boussingault", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 572, "target_cluster_name": "Boussingault", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent scientists who traveled extensively and conducted significant research in various fields, particularly in natural sciences and exploration. Humboldt's work on geography, geology, and botany, and Boussingault's on agricultural chemistry and South American exploration, show overlapping interests and a shared era of scientific discovery.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent scientists who traveled extensively and conducted significant research in various fields, particularly in natural sciences and exploration. Humboldt's work on geography, geology, and botany, and Boussingault's on agricultural chemistry and South American exploration, show overlapping interests and a shared era of scientific discovery.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Helmholtz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 624, "target_cluster_name": "Helmholtz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent scientists of the 19th century, known for their contributions to physics and physiology, and likely interacted within the scientific community.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent scientists of the 19th century, known for their contributions to physics and physiology, and likely interacted within the scientific community.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Encke", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 659, "target_cluster_name": "Encke", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alexander von Humboldt was a renowned naturalist and explorer whose work in physical geography and astronomy overlapped with Encke's astronomical research and interest in celestial mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Alexander von Humboldt was a renowned naturalist and explorer whose work in physical geography and astronomy overlapped with Encke's astronomical research and interest in celestial mechanics.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Saussure", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 707, "target_cluster_name": "Saussure", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence