sbourg is a prefecture and largest city of the Grand Est region of eastern France.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "opus cirinaico", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "cheira a benjuy, e que os doctos são d'este parecer, scilicet, que he benjuy; e que este he o opus cirinaico ou çumo cirinaico, que pario Judéa e deitou em França; e assi diz que se havia de chamar be", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for benzoin"}, {"found_name": "çumo cirinaico", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "cheira a benjuy, e que os doctos são d'este parecer, scilicet, que he benjuy; e que este he o opus cirinaico ou çumo cirinaico, que pario Judéa e deitou em França; e assi diz que se havia de chamar be", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for benzoin"}, {"found_name": "calambac", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "que os traductores o representa- ram algumas vezes por h. Do Itnaloes 55 RUANO Sinforiano diz que nunqua vio verdadeiro Itnaloes^ senão em Liam de França. ORTA Venha qua, e pagueo bem, e leváloa; mas,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a very good type of substance"}]}, {"canonical_name": "madre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 110, "members": [{"entity_id": "mother", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Mother", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 33, "variants": ["Mother"], "contexts": ["strangled with the mother", "affected by pains"]}, {"entity_id": "mother", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "mother", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["mother"], "contexts": ["female parent in reproduction"]}, {"entity_id": "madre", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "madre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 13, "variants": ["madre"], "contexts": ["mother (referring to the womb)", "uterus"]}, {"entity_id": "madre", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "madre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["madre"], "contexts": ["womb, affected by calamus", "womb, benefited by fruit preserve"]}, {"entity_id": "madre", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "madre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 60, "variants": ["madre", "Madre", "madredeytade"], "contexts": ["mother, referring to dura mater", "membrane connected to the head"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Mother", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "mother", "similarity": 0.992}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Mother", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.981}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Mother", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.981}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Mother", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.981}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "mother", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.986}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "mother", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.986}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "mother", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 0.986}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "madre", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "madre", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "madre", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "madre", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 47, "stable_key": "clu_b6ed7355ecfef4a7", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Womb", "confidence": "high", "type": "anatomy", "description": "The organ in female mammals where offspring develop.", "note": "Also refers to 'dura mater' in some contexts.", "wikipedia_extract": "The uterus (from Latin uterus, pl.: uteri or uteruses) or womb () is the organ in the reproductive system of most female mammals, including humans, that accommodates the embryonic and fetal development of one or more fertilized eggs until birth. The uterus is a hormone-responsive sex organ that contains glands in its lining that secrete uterine milk for embryonic nourishment. (The term uterus is also applied to analogous structures in some non-mammalian animals.) In humans, the lower end of the uterus is a narrow part known as the isthmus that connects to the cervix, the anterior gateway leading to the vagina. The upper end, the body of the uterus, is connected to the fallopian tubes at the uterine horns; the rounded part, the fundus, is above the openings to the fallopian tubes. The connection of the uterine cavity with a fallopian tube is called the uterotubal junction. The fertilized egg is carried to the uterus along the fallopian tube. It will have divided on its journey to form a blastocyst that will implant itself into the lining of the uterus – the endometrium, where it will receive nutrients and develop into the embryo proper, and later fetus, for the duration of the pregnancy."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Embryo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3006, "target_cluster_name": "embryo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The womb is the organ that accommodates embryonic development.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The womb is the organ that accommodates embryonic development."}, {"found_name": "Female reproductive system", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3327, "target_cluster_name": "Feminine parts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The womb is a primary organ within the female reproductive system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The womb is a primary organ within the female reproductive system."}, {"found_name": "Biological structure", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2276, "target_cluster_name": "structure", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The womb is a biological structure.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The womb is a biological structure."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Wine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 110, "members": [{"entity_id": "wine", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Wine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 101, "variants": ["Wine", "wine"], "contexts": ["used in decoction for serpent bites", "liquid used with seeds"]}, {"entity_id": "vino", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "vino", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["vino"], "contexts": ["drink to take root with in winter"]}, {"entity_id": "wine", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "wine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 2, "variants": ["wine"], "contexts": ["generous, mixed with pepper"]}, {"entity_id": "wine", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Wine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 5, "variants": ["wine", "Wine"], "contexts": ["alcoholic beverage", "mixed with ashes for pain relief"]}, {"entity_id": "wine", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Wine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Wine"], "contexts": ["liquid drawn up in glass"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Wine", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "vino", "similarity": 0.98}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Wine", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "wine", "similarity": 0.993}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "vino", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "wine", "similarity": 0.986}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Wine", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Wine", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 48, "stable_key": "clu_5503b86649ed71b2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Wine", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "An alcoholic beverage made from fermented grapes.", "note": "Includes different types of wine and by-products like wine lees.", "wikipedia_extract": "Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques. Wine has been produced for thousands of years, the earliest evidence dating from c. 6000 BCE in present-day Georgia. Its popularity spread around the Mediterranean during Classical antiquity, and was sustained in Western Europe by winemaking monks and a secular trade for general drinking. New World wine was established by settler colonies from the 16th century onwards, and the wine trade increased dramatically up to the latter half of the 19th century, when European vineyards were largely destroyed by the invasive pest phylloxera. After the Second World War, the wine market improved dramatically as winemakers focused on quality and marketing to cater for a more discerning audience, and wine remains a popular drink in much of the world."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "vino", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1554, "target_cluster_name": "vino", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Spanish for wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Spanish for wine.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "vinho tinto", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1637, "target_cluster_name": "vinho tinto", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Red wine is a specific type of wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Red wine is a specific type of wine.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Beer", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2169, "target_cluster_name": "Beer", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both beer and wine are common fermented alcoholic beverages.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both beer and wine are common fermented alcoholic beverages.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 203, "members": [{"entity_id": "brain", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["brain"], "contexts": ["affected by drink spirits", "organ infected by poison"]}, {"entity_id": "brain", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["brain"], "contexts": ["central organ of the nervous system"]}, {"entity_id": "brain", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 101, "variants": ["BRAIN", "brain", "Brain"], "contexts": ["physical basis for thoughts and feelings", "central organ of the nervous system"]}, {"entity_id": "brain", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["brain"], "contexts": ["organ of thought and control"]}, {"entity_id": "brain", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "brain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["brain"], "contexts": ["organ of the nervous system", "organ of the body"]}, {"entity_id": "cérebro", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "cérebro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 6, "variants": ["cérebro"], "contexts": ["body part that amber benefits", "organ of the nervous system"]}, {"entity_id": "cerebro", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "cerebro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 89, "variants": ["cerebro", "Cerebri", "Cerebro", "Cerebropelos", "cerebeldes", "cerebri", "cerebrum"], "contexts": ["brain", "organ of the body"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "brain", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "brain", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 49, "stable_key": "clu_22617cb70b0d7524", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Brain", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brain", "note": "While 'cerebro' directly translates to brain, in early modern texts it often referred to the concept of the seat of intellect and memory, as well as the physical organ.", "wikipedia_extract": "The brain is an organ that serves as the center of the nervous system in all vertebrate and most invertebrate animals. It consists of nervous tissue and is typically located in the head (cephalization), usually near organs for special senses such as vision, hearing, and olfaction. Being the most specialized organ, it is responsible for receiving information from the sensory nervous system, processing that information (thought, cognition, and intelligence) and the coordination of motor control (muscle activity and endocrine system). While invertebrate brains arise from paired segmental ganglia (each of which is only responsible for the respective body segment) of the ventral nerve cord, vertebrate brains develop axially from the midline dorsal nerve cord as a vesicular enlargement at the rostral end of the neural tube, with centralized control over all body segments. All vertebrate brains can be embryonically divided into three parts: the forebrain (prosencephalon, subdivided into telencephalon and diencephalon), midbrain (mesencephalon) and hindbrain (rhombencephalon, subdivided into metencephalon and myelencephalon). The spinal cord, which directly interacts with somatic functions below the head, can be considered a caudal extension of the myelencephalon enclosed inside the vertebral column."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Cerebrum and Cerebellum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1850, "target_cluster_name": "cerebellum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The cerebrum and cerebellum are specific parts of the brain, making them directly related anatomical structures.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The cerebrum and cerebellum are specific parts of the brain, making them directly related anatomical structures."}, {"found_name": "nerves", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 137, "target_cluster_name": "nerves", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, which is composed of nerves and nerve tissue.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, which is composed of nerves and nerve tissue.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "human mind", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 424, "target_cluster_name": "human mind", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is historically considered the physical seat of the human mind.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is historically considered the physical seat of the human mind.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "nerve", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 468, "target_cluster_name": "nerve", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is the central processing unit of the nervous system, and nerves are the pathways that connect the brain to the rest of the body. They are inseparable in function and structure.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is the central processing unit of the nervous system, and nerves are the pathways that connect the brain to the rest of the body. They are inseparable in function and structure.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cord", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2799, "target_cluster_name": "cord", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The spinal cord is a direct extension of the brain and forms the central nervous system along with it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The spinal cord is a direct extension of the brain and forms the central nervous system along with it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cabeça", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1508, "target_cluster_name": "cabeça", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is a primary organ located within the head.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is a primary organ located within the head.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "nervous system", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1588, "target_cluster_name": "nervous system", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is a central and critical organ within the nervous system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is a central and critical organ within the nervous system.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "amygdaloid", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1797, "target_cluster_name": "amygdaloid", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The amygdaloid is a nuclear complex within the cerebral hemispheres of the vertebrate brain, specifically located in the temporal lobes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The amygdaloid is a nuclear complex within the cerebral hemispheres of the vertebrate brain, specifically located in the temporal lobes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cerebellum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1850, "target_cluster_name": "cerebellum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The cerebrum and cerebellum are major parts of the brain.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The cerebrum and cerebellum are major parts of the brain.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cranium", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1876, "target_cluster_name": "cranium", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The cranium encloses and protects the brain.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The cranium encloses and protects the brain.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cerebral circulation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2583, "target_cluster_name": "cerebral circulation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cerebral circulation is the circulation of blood specifically within the brain.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cerebral circulation is the circulation of blood specifically within the brain.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "nervous actions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2584, "target_cluster_name": "nervous actions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, responsible for generating and processing nervous actions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, responsible for generating and processing nervous actions.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 106, "members": [{"entity_id": "stomach", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Stomach", "stomach"], "contexts": ["organ where sponge swells", "digestive organ"]}, {"entity_id": "stomach", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 100, "variants": ["Stomach", "Stomachs", "Stomack", "Stomi••s", "Sto∣mach", "Sto∣machs", "stomach"], "contexts": ["body part treated by the herb", "organ warmed by herb"]}, {"entity_id": "stomach", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["stomach"], "contexts": ["organ for digesting food", "organ for digestion"]}, {"entity_id": "stomach", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["stomach"], "contexts": ["digestive organ"]}, {"entity_id": "stomach", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "stomach", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["stomach"], "contexts": ["organ for digesting food"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Stomach", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Stomach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "stomach", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "stomach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "stomach", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "stomach", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 50, "stable_key": "clu_f97eb5dc22aad2e8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Stomach", "confidence": "high", "type": "anatomical_part", "description": "The organ responsible for digestion and processing food.", "note": "Includes variations in spelling and the mention of its 'tunicas' (linings).", "wikipedia_extract": "The stomach is a muscular, hollow organ in the upper gastrointestinal tract of humans and many other animals, including several invertebrates. The Ancient Greek name for the stomach is gaster which is used as gastric in medical terms related to the stomach. The stomach has a dilated structure and functions as a vital organ in the digestive system. The stomach is involved in the gastric phase of digestion, following the cephalic phase in which the sight and smell of food and the act of chewing are stimuli. In the stomach a chemical breakdown of food takes place by means of secreted  digestive enzymes and gastric acid. It also plays a role in regulating gut microbiota, influencing digestion and overall health."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 100, "members": [{"entity_id": "liver", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 5, "variants": ["liver", "Liver"], "contexts": ["organ where gall is seated", "abdominal organ"]}, {"entity_id": "liver", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 87, "variants": ["Liver"], "contexts": ["organ involved in digestion and detoxification", "organ that is cleansed and helped"]}, {"entity_id": "liver", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["liver"], "contexts": ["organ that secretes bile", "organ involved in activity"]}, {"entity_id": "liver", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Liver", "liver"], "contexts": ["organ of the body", "an organ of the body"]}, {"entity_id": "liver", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "liver", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["liver"], "contexts": ["commences as multiplication of cells", "organ developing from intestine wall"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Liver", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Liver", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Liver", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "liver", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Liver", "similarity": 0.934}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "liver", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Liver", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "liver", "similarity": 0.934}], "id": 51, "stable_key": "clu_8c3aeff51a8005ae", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Liver", "confidence": "high", "type": "anatomy", "description": "Large organ in the abdomen involved in detoxification and metabolism.", "wikipedia_extract": "The liver is a major metabolic organ exclusively found in vertebrates, which performs many essential biological functions such as detoxification of the organism, and the synthesis of various proteins and various other biochemicals necessary for digestion and growth. In humans, it is located in the right upper quadrant of the abdomen, below the diaphragm and mostly shielded by the lower right rib cage. Its other metabolic roles include carbohydrate metabolism, the production of a number of hormones, conversion and storage of nutrients such as glucose and glycogen, and the decomposition of red blood cells. Anatomical and medical terminology often use the prefix hepat- from ἡπατο-, from the Greek word for liver, such as hepatology, and hepatitis. The liver is also an accessory digestive organ that produces bile, an alkaline fluid containing cholesterol and bile acids,  which emulsifies and aids the breakdown of dietary fat. The gallbladder, a small hollow pouch that sits just under the right lobe of liver, stores and concentrates the bile produced by the liver, which is later excreted to the duodenum to help with digestion."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "glandulas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1832, "target_cluster_name": "glandulas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The liver is a gland.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The liver is a gland.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "English Rubarb", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "Urine, and helpeth the dimness of the Sight. The Roots of this Ba∣stard Rubarb are used in opening and purging Diet Drinks with other things, to open the Liver, and to clens and cool the Blood. The po", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a variety of rhubarb"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Océan", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 101, "members": [{"entity_id": "ocean", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["ocean"], "contexts": ["vast body of saltwater", "vast body of water for bird transportation"]}, {"entity_id": "océan", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Océan", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 67, "variants": ["OCÉAN", "ocÉAN", "Océan"], "contexts": ["ocean causing erosions", "ocean name"]}, {"entity_id": "ocean", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 11, "variants": ["Ocean", "ocean"], "contexts": ["depths of the ocean", "vast expanse of ocean"]}, {"entity_id": "ocean", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 17, "variants": ["Ocean", "ocean"], "contexts": ["large body of saltwater", "body of water on Earth's surface"]}, {"entity_id": "ocean", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["ocean"], "contexts": ["large body of saltwater", "large bodies of saltwater on Earth"]}, {"entity_id": "océans", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Océans", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": 