"Solanaceae", "description": "Plant species of the genus Nicotiana, widely cultivated for its leaves.", "note": "Includes the term 'tabaxir', which refers to a siliceous deposit from bamboo, but contextually relates to the broader discussion of medicinal plant substances.", "wikipedia_extract": "Nicotiana tabacum, or cultivated tobacco, is an annually grown herbaceous plant of the genus Nicotiana. N. tabacum is the most commonly grown species in the genus Nicotiana, as the plant's leaves are commercially harvested to be processed into tobacco for human use. The plant is tropical in origin, is commonly grown throughout the world, and is often found in cultivation. It grows to heights between 1 and 2 metres (3.3 and 6.6 ft). Research is ongoing into its ancestry among wild Nicotiana species, but it is believed to be a hybrid of Nicotiana sylvestris, N. tomentosiformis, and possibly N. otophora. It is an annual plant that grows 1 to 3 metres (3 to 10 feet) high and is sticky haired on all parts."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Coca", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2856, "target_cluster_name": "Coca", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are plants historically used for their psychoactive properties and consumed by chewing.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are plants historically used for their psychoactive properties and consumed by chewing."}, {"found_name": "laureola", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "duas vezes na ſomana quatro grãos de pò de folhas de laureola, a que os noſſos Herbolarios chamão Oriola , forvidospelasventas do nariz à maneyra de tabaco ; porquenãoſe pode encarecer aefficacia que ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Oriola"}, {"found_name": "tabaxir", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "porque estas equivocaçôes dam causa a muytos erros, e porque os da fisica sam mais periguosos, sam estes maiores erros. RUANO Pêra isso dizei o que he o tabaxir, segundo os doutores e a gente desta te", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for tabaxir"}, {"found_name": "açucare de mambum", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "quer dizer, açucare de mambum, porque áquellas canas daquella arvore chamam os índios onde nasce, mambú. E porém já lhe chama aguora a gente da terra tabaxir; porque debaixo deste nome lho pedem os Mo", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym of tabaxir"}, {"found_name": "Oriola", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "duas vezes na ſomana quatro grãos de pò de folhas de laureola, a que os noſſos Herbolarios chamão Oriola , forvidospelasventas do nariz à maneyra de tabaco ; porquenãoſe pode encarecer aefficacia que ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vernacular name for laureola"}]}, {"canonical_name": "equator", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 83, "members": [{"entity_id": "equator", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Equator", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 7, "variants": ["Equator"], "contexts": ["Earth's equatorial line", "imaginary line dividing Earth into hemispheres"]}, {"entity_id": "equator", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "equator", "category": "PLACE",