digenous to Bioko, are the second largest group at approximately 6.5% of the population. Its capital is Ciudad de la Paz, replacing former capital Malabo in 2026, while its largest city is Bata."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The country is named for its location near the Equator and in Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The country is named for its location near the Equator and in Africa."}, {"found_name": "tropiques", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 261, "target_cluster_name": "tropiques", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The tropics are defined by their proximity to the Equator.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The tropics are defined by their proximity to the Equator.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "temperate zones", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 471, "target_cluster_name": "temperate zones", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Equator is the central line of latitude that divides the Earth into the Northern and Southern Hemispheres. Temperate zones are located between the equatorial regions and the polar regions, making the Equator a fundamental reference point for defining climate zones.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Equator is the central line of latitude that divides the Earth into the Northern and Southern Hemispheres. Temperate zones are located between the equatorial regions and the polar regions, making the Equator a fundamental reference point for defining climate zones.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Universe", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_str