on", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 71, "stable_key": "clu_ba8e996dbde32884", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Isaac Newton", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1643, "death_year": 1727, "description": "English mathematician, physicist, astronomer, and alchemist, laws of motion.", "wikidata_id": "Q935", "wikidata_description": "English mathematician and physicist (1642–1727)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac%20Newton", "wikipedia_extract": "Sir Isaac Newton ( ; 4 January [O.S. 25 December] 1643 – 31 March [O.S. 20 March] 1727) was an English polymath who was a mathematician, physicist, astronomer, alchemist, theologian, author and inventor. He was a key figure in the Scientific Revolution and the Enlightenment that followed. His book Philosophiæ Naturalis Principia Mathematica (Mathematical Principles of Natural Philosophy), first published in 1687, achieved the first great unification in physics and established classical mechanics. Newton also made seminal contributions to optics, and shares credit with the German mathematician Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz for formulating infinitesimal calculus, although he developed calculus years before Leibniz."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Gauss", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1176, "target_cluster_name": "Gauss", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Gauss is often referred to as the 'Prince of Mathematicians', a title that echoes the profound impact and foundational work of Isaac Newton in mathematics and physics. Gauss's work built upon and extended Newtonian principles in many areas, particularly in celestial mechanics and optics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Gauss is often referred to as the 'Prince of Mathematicians', a title that echoes the profound impact and foundational work of Isaac Newton in mathematics and physics. Gauss's work built upon and extended Newtonian principles in many areas, particularly in celestial mechanics and optics.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Galen", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 29, "target_cluster_name": "Galen", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Newton engaged with and built upon the scientific and medical traditions of figures like Galen, particularly in his studies of optics and anatomy, though he also critiqued and superseded some of Galen's theories.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Newton engaged with and built upon the scientific and medical traditions of figures like Galen, particularly in his studies of optics and anatomy, though he also critiqued and superseded some of Galen's theories."}, {"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Newton, like many scientists of his era, engaged with and often departed from the Aristotelian framework of natural philosophy, particularly in physics and cosmology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Newton, like many scientists of his era, engaged with and often departed from the Aristotelian framework of natural philosophy, particularly in physics and cosmology."}, {"found_name": "Archimedes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 480, "target_cluster_name": "Archimedes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Newton's work on calculus and mechanics owes a significant intellectual debt to the foundational mathematical and physical principles established by Archimedes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Newton's work on calculus and mechanics owes a significant intellectual debt to the foundational mathematical and physical principles establish