political philosophy, often seen as intellectual successors in the broader context of English intellectual history.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Sir John Herschel", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 554, "target_cluster_name": "Sir John Herschel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Newton was a foundational figure in physics and mathematics, and Herschel, as an astronomer and mathematician, worked within the scientific tradition established by Newton. Herschel's astronomical work, in particular, built upon Newtonian principles.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Newton was a foundational figure in physics and mathematics, and Herschel, as an astronomer and mathematician, worked within the scientific tradition established by Newton. Herschel's astronomical work, in particular, built upon Newtonian principles.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Helmholtz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 624, "target_cluster_name": "Helmholtz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Helmholtz's work in physics, particularly on the conservation of energy, built upon the foundations laid by Newton's laws of motion and universal gravitation. Newton represents a foundational figure in the scientific tradition that Helmholtz belonged to.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Helmholtz's work in physics, particularly on the conservation of energy, built upon the foundations laid by Newton's laws of motion and universal gravitation. Newton represents a foundational figure in the scientific tradition that Helmholtz belonged to.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Kepler", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 695, "target_cluster_name": "Kepler", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Kepler's laws of planetary 