: "Distinguished from the Javary river in Brazil.", "wikipedia_extract": "Java is one of the Greater Sunda Islands in the South East Asian country of Indonesia. It is bordered by the Indian Ocean to the south and the Java Sea (a part of Pacific Ocean) to the north. With a population of 156.9 million people (including Madura) in mid 2024, projected to have risen to 158 million by mid-2025, Java is the world's most populous island, home to approximately 56% of the Indonesian population while constituting only 7% of its land area. Indonesia's capital city, Jakarta, is on Java's northwestern coast. Many of the best known events in Indonesian history took place on Java. It was the centre of powerful Hindu-Buddhist empires, the Islamic sultanates, and the core of the colonial Dutch East Indies."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Great Indian Archipelago", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1471, "target_cluster_name": "Great Indian Archipelago", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Java is a major island within the Indonesian Archipelago.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Java is a major island within the Indonesian Archipelago.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "East Indies", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 497, "target_cluster_name": "East Indies", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Java is a major island within the historical and geographical region known as the East Indies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Java is a major island within the historical and geographical region known as the East Indies."}, {"found_name": "Malay Archipelago", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2275, "target_cluster_name": "Malay Archipelago", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Java is a major island within the Malay 