 give a few well-known cases, taken from physiological optics, as examples. Every eye probably contains _muscæ volitantes_, so called; t", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "blind spot", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "evidence_snippet": "experiments, that when one of his eyes is closed there is a great gap, the so-called 'blind spot,' not far from the middle of the field of the open eye, in which he sees nothing at all, but which he f", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "equivalent"}, {"found_name": "Galls", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "Heron be commonly termed Galls, yet is not this Animal deficient in that part, but containeth it in the Liver. And thus when it is conceived that the eyes of _Tobias_ were cured by the gall of the fis", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}]}, {"canonical_name": "attraction", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 37, "members": [{"entity_id": "attraction", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "attraction", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Attraction", "attraction"], "contexts": ["force of pulling together", "force drawing objects together"]}, {"entity_id": "attraction", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "ATTRACTION", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["ATTRACTION", "attraction"], "contexts": ["force drawing objects together", "mental force analogous to physical attraction"]}, {"entity_id": "attraction", "book_id": "kosmos_hum