 of the beginning of summer varies according to definition, climate, tradition, and culture. When it is summer in the Northern Hemisphere, it is winter in the Southern Hemisphere, and vice versa. The modern English summer derives from the Middle English somer, via the Old English sumor."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Autumn", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 911, "target_cluster_name": "Autumn", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Summer is one of the four temperate seasons, occurring immediately before Autumn.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Summer is one of the four temperate seasons, occurring immediately before Autumn."}, {"found_name": "July", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1523, "target_cluster_name": "July", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "July is a month that falls within the season of Summer in the Northern Hemisphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: July is a month that falls within the season of Summer in the Northern Hemisphere.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Março", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2332, "target_cluster_name": "Março", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "March is the end of Summer in the Southern Hemisphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: March is the end of Summer in the Southern Hemisphere.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Brakes", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "them. Place. They both grow on Heaths, and in shady places neer the Hedg sides in all Countries of this Land. Time. They flourish and give their Seed at Mid∣summer. The Femal Fern is that plant which ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Female Fern"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "book_count": 9, "total_mentions": 71, "members": [{"entity_id": "fish", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 15, "variants": ["fish", "Fish"], "contexts": ["aquatic prey of Mustela vison", "aquatic vertebrate with gills"]}, {"entity_id": "fish", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 2, "variants": ["fish"], "contexts": ["aquatic vertebrate animal", "food source containing phosphorus"]}, {"entity_id": "fish", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 3, "variants": ["fish"], "contexts": ["fossil impression found in rocks", "coprolites of fish found"]}, {"entity_id": "fish", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 7, "variants": ["fish", "Fish"], "contexts": ["peculiar tribe inhabiting ocean depths", "decaying substances emitting light"]}, {"entity_id": "fish", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "fish", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 4, "variants": ["fish"], "contexts": ["aquatic vertebrates", "food source from the sea"]}, {"entity_id": "fishes", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Fishes", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 3, "variants": ["Fishes"], "contexts": ["aquatic animals with fins", "category of aquatic animals"]}, {"entity_id": "fishes", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "fishes", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "FISH", "count": 9, "variants": ["fishes", "Fishes"], "contexts": ["aquatic vertebrates with swimbladders", "electric organs of fishes"]}, {"entity_id": "