 the more common jawed fish, the latter including all living cartilaginous and bony fish, as well as the extinct placoderms and acanthodians. In a break from the long tradition of grouping all fish into a single class (Pisces), modern phylogenetics views fish as a paraphyletic group that includes all vertebrates except tetrapods. In English, the plural of \"fish\" is fish when referring to individuals and fishes when referring to species. Most fish are cold-blooded, their body temperature varying with the surrounding water, though some large, active swimmers like the white shark and tuna can maintain a higher core temperature. Many fish can communicate acoustically with each other, such as during courtship displays."}, "member_count": 15, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "tiburones", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 4129, "target_cluster_name": "tiburones", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tiburones is Spanish for sharks, which are a type of fish.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tiburones is Spanish for sharks, which are a type of fish."}, {"found_name": "animals", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 19, "target_cluster_name": "animals", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fish are a diverse group of aquatic animals within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Fish are a diverse group of aquatic animals within the kingdom Animalia, sharing fundamental characteristics with other animals.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Lepidosiren", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2722, "target_cluster_name": "Lepidosiren", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lepidosiren is a genus of lungfish, which are a type of fish.", "confide