", "target_name": "crocodile", "similarity": 0.952}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "crocodile", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "crocodiles", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "crocodile", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "crocodiles", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "crocodile", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "crocodile", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "crocodiles", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "crocodiles", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "crocodiles", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "crocodile", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "crocodiles", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "crocodile", "similarity": 0.965}], "id": 108, "stable_key": "clu_1637c67d669d341b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Crocodile", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "description": "Large semi-aquatic reptiles, sometimes referred to as Cayman in specific contexts.", "wikipedia_extract": "A crocodile (family Crocodylidae) or true crocodile is a large, semiaquatic reptile that lives throughout the tropics in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Australia. The term \"crocodile\" is sometimes used more loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes the alligators and caimans (both members of the family Alligatoridae), the gharial and false gharial (both members of the family Gavialidae) as well as other extinct taxa. This article will use \"crocodile\" or \"true crocodile\" to refer only to the species taxonomically included in the Crocodylidae family, extant or extinct. Crocodile size, morphology, behaviour and ecology differ among species. However, they have many similarities in these areas as well. All crocodiles are semiaquatic and tend to congregate in freshwater habitats such as rivers, lakes, wetlands and sometimes in brackish water and saltwater."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "alligators", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2988, "target_cluster_name": "Alligators", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The description explicitly states that 'crocodile' is sometimes used loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes alligators.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The description explicitly states that 'crocodile' is sometimes used loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes alligators."}, {"found_name": "cayman", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "evidence_snippet": "\"Ventura liarcaiztegui et à Don Francisco Lemaur. * Tom. III, p. 30C. 402 LIVRE X. nom de cayman , l'autre par le nom de crocodile , ou , comme on dit com- munément en es[)agnol , de cocodrilo. Ils no", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for crocodile"}, {"found_name": "caymans", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "evidence_snippet": "Sauriens. « Dans la baie de Campêche , dit-il , je n'ai vu que des caymans ou alligators ,• à l'ile du Grand-Cayman , il y a des crocodiles et pas à' alligators ^ à l'ile des Pinos et dans les innombr", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for crocodile"}, {"found_name": "cocodrilo", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "evidence_snippet": "\"Ventura liarcaiztegui et à Don Francisco Lemaur. * Tom. III, p. 30C. 402 LIVRE X. nom de cayman , l'autre par le nom de crocodile , ou , comme on dit com- munément en es[)agnol , de cocodrilo. Ils no", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "common Spanish name for crocodile"}]}, {"canonical_name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["air"], "contexts": ["gaseous mixture surrounding Earth"]}, {"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 5, "variants": ["air"], "contexts": ["substance to be purged from instruments", "gaseous atmosphere"]}, {"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["air"], "contexts": ["gaseous mixture", "passes through throat and nose"]}, {"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 7, "variants": ["air"], "contexts": ["contact with free air", "absent on the Moon"]}, {"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 11, "variants": ["air"], "contexts": ["gaseous element involved in decomposition", "medium for shining in example phrase"]}, {"entity_id": "air", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Air", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory"