_1890", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Plato", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Plato", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 113, "stable_key": "clu_93d668d18e3fbd8a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Plato", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": -428, "death_year": -348, "description": "Ancient Greek philosopher, founder of the Academy.", "wikidata_id": "Q859", "wikidata_description": "4th-century BCE Greek philosopher", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plato", "wikipedia_extract": "Plato ( PLAY-toe; Greek: Πλάτων, Plátōn; born c. 428–423 BC, died 348/347 BC) was an ancient Greek philosopher of Classical Athens who is most commonly considered the foundational thinker of the Western philosophical tradition. An innovator of the literary dialogue and dialectic forms, Plato influenced all the major areas of theoretical philosophy and practical philosophy, and was the founder of the Platonic Academy, a philosophical school in Athens where Plato taught the collection of philosophical theories that would later become known as Platonism. Plato's most famous contribution is his Theory of Forms (or Ideas), which aims to solve what is now known as the problem of universals. He was influenced by the pre-Socratic thinkers Pythagoras, Heraclitus, and Parmenides, although much of what is known about them is derived from Plato himself. Along with his teacher Socrates, and his student Aristotle, Plato is a central figure in the history of Western philosophy."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Aristotle was Plato's student and successor at the Academy, and his philosophy is deeply intertwined with Plato's ideas, often in direct response or critique.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Aristotle was Plato's student and successor at the Academy, and his philosophy is deeply intertwined with Plato's ideas, often in direct response or critique.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Socrates", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 460, "target_cluster_name": "Socrates", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Plato was Socrates' student and wrote dialogues featuring him.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Plato was Socrates' student and wrote dialogues featuring him."}, {"found_name": "Anaxagoras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1057, "target_cluster_name": "Anaxagoras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anaxagoras was an early influence on Plato's thought.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Anaxagoras was an early influence on Plato's thought."}, {"found_name": "Pythagoras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 354, "target_cluster_name": "Pythagoras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pythagorean philosophy influenced