ime borders with the United Kingdom, Germany, and Belgium. The official language is Dutch, with West Frisian as a secondary official language in the province of Friesland. Dutch, English, and Papiamento are official in the Caribbean territories."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Amsterdam", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 980, "target_cluster_name": "Amsterdam", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amsterdam is a major city and the capital of the Netherlands.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Amsterdam is a major city and the capital of the Netherlands."}, {"found_name": "Flanders", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2622, "target_cluster_name": "Flandres", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Flanders was historically a region closely associated with and often politically linked to the Netherlands.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Flanders was historically a region closely associated with and often politically linked to the Netherlands."}, {"found_name": "Belgium", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 963, "target_cluster_name": "Belgique", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Belgium shares a long border and historical ties with the Netherlands, having been part of the same political entities for significant periods.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Belgium shares a long border and historical ties with the Netherlands, having been part of the same political entities for significant periods."}, {"found_name": "Europe", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 30, "target_cluster_name": "Europe", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Netherlands is a country located in Europe.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label"