ant city located on the Nile River.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Aswan is a significant city located on the Nile River."}, {"found_name": "Mediterranean Sea", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 256, "target_cluster_name": "Méditerranée", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Nile River flows into the Mediterranean Sea.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Nile River flows into the Mediterranean Sea."}, {"found_name": "Amazone", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1520, "target_cluster_name": "Amazone", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Amazon River's length is disputed with the Nile.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Amazon River's length is disputed with the Nile.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Syene", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2784, "target_cluster_name": "Syene", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Aswan (Syene) is historically situated on the Nile River.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Aswan (Syene) is historically situated on the Nile River.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "April", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 19, "members": [{"entity_id": "april", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "April", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["April"], "contexts": ["month when Alder-Tree flowers", "month when Bilberries flower"]}, {"entity_id": "abril", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Abril", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Abril"], "contexts": ["month when amber fruit is ripe"]}, {"entity_id": "abril", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "abril", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["abril"], "contexts": ["month for pearl diving"]}, {"entity_id": "aprile", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Aprile", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Aprile"], "contexts": ["month of April"]}, {"entity_id": "abril", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Abril", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Abril"], "contexts": ["emetic preparation", "month of the year"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "April", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "abril", "similarity": 0.953}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "April", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Aprile", "similarity": 0.979}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Abril", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "abril", "similarity": 0.917}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Abril", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Abril", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "abril", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Aprile", "similarity": 0.947}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "abril", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Abril", "similarity": 0.917}], "id": 129, "stable_key": "clu_a2da1305d0d4b84a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "April", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April", "wikipedia_extract": "April is the fourth month of the year in the Gregorian and Julian calendars. Its length is 30 days. April is commonly associated with the season of spring in the Northern Hemisphere, and autumn in the Southern Hemisphere, where it is the seasonal equivalent to October in the Northern Hemisphere and vice versa. The Romans gave this month the Latin name Aprilis but the derivation of this name is uncertain. The traditional etymology is from the verb aperire, \"to open\", in allusion to its being the season when trees and flowers begin to \"open\", which is supported by comparison with the modern Greek use of άνοιξη (ánixi) (opening) for spring. Since some of the Roman months were named in honor of divinities, and as April was sacred to the goddess Venus, her Veneralia being held on the first day, it has been suggested that Aprilis was originally her month Aphrilis, from her equivalent Greek goddess name Aphrodite (Aphros), or the Etruscan name Apru."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Autumn", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 911, "target_cluster_name": "Autumn", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "April is described as the seasonal equivalent to October in the Northern Hemisphere, and Autumn in the Southern Hemisphere, indicating a direct seasonal relationship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "April is described as the seasonal equivalent to October in the Northern Hemisphere, and Autumn in the Southern Hemisphere, indicating a direct seasonal relationship."}, {"found_name": "Spring", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1628, "target_cluster_name": "fontes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "April is commonly associated with the season of spring in the Northern Hemisphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "April is commonly associated with the season of spring in the Northern Hemisphere."}, {"found_name": "October", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 386, "target_cluster_name": "Outubro", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "April is described as the seasonal equivalent to October in the Northern Hemisphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "April is described as the seasonal equivalent to October in the Northern Hemisphere."}, {"found_name": "June", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 69, "target_cluster_name": "June", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "April and June are consecutive months in the Gregorian calendar, and their temporal proximity often leads to discussions of seasonal changes and agricultural cycles.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: April and June are consecutive months in the Gregorian calendar, and their temporal proximity often leads to discussions of seasonal changes and agricultural cycles.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "September", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 121, "target_cluster_name": "September", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "September is the month immediately preceding April in the Julian and Gregorian calendars, and is the ninth month of the year.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: September is the month immediately preceding April in the Julian and Gregorian calendars, and is the ninth month of the year.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Seasons", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 401, "target_cluster_name": "Seasons", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "April is a month within a season.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: April is a month within a season.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Aries", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 787, "target_cluster_name": "Aries", "so