"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "nerves", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "nerves", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 137, "stable_key": "clu_4630e36e6abf5885", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "nerves", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "The text mentions 'neruos' and 'nerari' in the context of nerves affected by cramps, pointing to the anatomical concept of nerves.", "wikidata_id": "Q3234179", "wikidata_description": "short story by Anton Chekhov", "wikipedia_extract": "A nerve is an enclosed, cable-like bundle of nerve fibers (called axons). Nerves have historically been considered the basic units of the peripheral nervous system. A nerve provides a common pathway for the electrochemical nerve impulses called action potentials that are transmitted along each of the axons to peripheral organs or, in the case of sensory nerves, from the periphery back to the central nervous system. Each axon is an extension of an individual neuron, along with other supportive cells such as some Schwann cells that coat the axons in myelin. Each axon is surrounded by a layer of connective tissue called the endoneurium. The axons are bundled together into groups called fascicles, and each fascicle is wrapped in a layer of connective tissue called the perineurium.", "wikipedia_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Les_Nerfs"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Auditory nerve", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3092, "target_cluster_name": "auditory nerve", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The auditory nerve is a specific type of nerve, directly related to the general category of nerves.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The auditory nerve is a specific type of nerve, directly related to the general category of nerves."}, {"found_name": "Ganglion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1080, "target_cluster_name": "ganglia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ganglia are clusters of nerve cell bodies, closely associated with the function and structure of nerves.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ganglia are clusters of nerve cell bodies, closely associated with the function and structure of nerves."}, {"found_name": "Brain", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 49, "target_cluster_name": "brain", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, which is composed of nerves and nerve tissue.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The brain is the central organ of the nervous system, which is composed of nerves and nerve tissue."}, {"found_name": "Artery", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1775, "target_cluster_name": "arterias", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arteries are blood vessels that carry blood away from the heart, and are often discussed alongside nerves in anatomical contexts, though they are distinct structures.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arteries are blood vessels that carry blood away from the heart, and are often discussed alongside nerves in anatomical contexts, though they are distinct structures."}, {"found_name": "parts", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 467, "target_cluster_name": "parts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Nerves are a type of body part responsible for transmitting signals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Nerves are a type of body part responsible for transmitting signals.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "minerals", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "minerals", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Minerals", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Minerals"], "contexts": ["inorganic solid substances", "non-living materials"]}, {"entity_id": "minerals", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "minerals", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["Minerals", "minerals"], "contexts": ["artificial imitation of substances", "materials composing the earth's crust"]}, {"entity_id": "minerales", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "minerales", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Minerales", "minerales"], "contexts": ["minerals mentioned by Dioscorides", "one of four things where poison is found"]}, {"entity_id": "minerali", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "minerali", "category": "SUBST