tly by different people", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quality%20%28business%29", "wikipedia_extract": "In business, engineering, and manufacturing, quality – or high quality – has a pragmatic interpretation as the non-inferiority or superiority of something (goods or services); it is also defined as being suitable for the intended purpose (fitness for purpose) while satisfying customer expectations. Quality is a perceptual, conditional, and somewhat subjective attribute and may be understood differently by different people. Consumers may focus on the specification quality of a product/service, or how it compares to competitors in the marketplace. Producers might measure the conformance quality, or degree to which the product/service was produced correctly. Support personnel may measure quality in the degree that a product is reliable, maintainable, or sustainable. In such ways, the subjectivity of quality is rendered objective via operational definitions and measured with metrics such as proxy measures."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Abstraction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 894, "target_cluster_name": "abstraction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Quality is a concept that can be abstracted from specific instances or objects.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Quality is a concept that can be abstracted from specific instances or objects."}, {"found_name": "Character", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 962, "target_cluster_name": "character", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Quality is a fundamental aspect of character, describing its nature and attributes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Quality is a fundamental aspect of character, describing its nature and attributes."}, {"found_name": "Chemical properties", "link_type": 