{"modern_name": "Solomon", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Biblical king associated with wisdom and knowledge.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomon", "wikipedia_extract": "Solomon (), also called Jedidiah, was a king of the Kingdom of Israel and Judah, according to the Hebrew Bible. The successor of his father David, he is described as the penultimate ruler of all Twelve Tribes of Israel under a united Israel and Judah. His reign is hypothesized to have lasted from c. 970–931 BCE. According to the biblical narrative, his reign brought commercial prosperity through alliances and trade, but his accumulation of wealth, horses, and foreign wives, many of whom introduced idolatry, led to divine punishment. After Solomon's death, his son Rehoboam’s harsh policies led the northern Israelites to reject the Davidic line and follow Jeroboam, splitting the kingdom into Israel in the north and Judah in the south, according to the Hebrew Bible."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "David", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1392, "target_cluster_name": "David", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "David was Solomon's father and predecessor as King of Israel and Judah.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "David was Solomon's father and predecessor as King of Israel and Judah."}]}, {"canonical_name": "world", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "world", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "World", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["World"], "contexts": ["the Earth and its inhabitants"]}, {"entity_id": "world", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "World", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": 