vilizations, most of Iran was first united as a nation by the Medes under Cyaxares in the 7th century BC and reached its territorial height in the 6th century BC, when Cyrus the Great founded the Achaemenid Empire."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Tartaria", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 390, "target_cluster_name": "Tartaria", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "provincia dita XJzbeque, que he parte da Tartaria, que nós chamamos, ou <los Moguoras, como elles chamão qua; bem que Andreas £elunensis chame áquella parte Pérsia, mas isto he largo xnodo tomando Pér", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "larger region containing XJzbeque, and possibly synonymous with a broader Persia"}, {"found_name": "Abolahi", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1492, "target_cluster_name": "Avicena", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "tem culpa senão o traductor, ou os tempos, que gastão tudo*, mas no arábio está cebar. RUANO Acerca dos indios he usado? ORTA Acerca dos fisicos da Pérsia, Arábia e Turquia se usa desta mezinha, porqu", "confidence": 0.8, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Persian/Arabic name for Avicenna"}, {"found_name": "Cananor", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1915, "target_cluster_name": "Cananor", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "açajram da ten^a. • ORTA Essa mezinha he pêra falar nella, porque a usam India- nos médicos; e he mezinha e mercadoria que se leva muyta pêra Arábia e Pérsia; e nesta cidade ha pouco delia, e no Malav", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "city in Malabar"}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidenc