ain, Kuwait, Oman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and Yemen, as well as southern Iraq and Jordan. The largest of these is Saudi Arabia. In ancient antiquity, particularly from the 9th century BC to the 7th century AD, the Sinai Peninsula was also considered a part of Arabia. The Arabian Peninsula formed as a result of the rifting of the Red Sea between 56 and 23 million years ago, and is bordered by the Red Sea to the west and south-west, the Persian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman to the north-east, the Levant and Mesopotamia to the north and the Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean to the south-east."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Persia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 168, "target_cluster_name": "Persia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arabia is geographically adjacent to and historically intertwined with Persia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arabia is geographically adjacent to and historically intertwined with Persia.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arabia is a peninsula in West Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arabia is a peninsula in West Asia."}, {"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arabia is situated north-east of Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arabia is situated north-east of Africa."}, {"found_name": "Barbary Coast", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3179, "target_cluster_name": "Berbéria", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The