o_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Foglie", "similarity": 0.922}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "hojas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "folhas", "similarity": 0.928}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "folhas", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Foglie", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "folhas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "folhas", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Foglie", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "folhas", "similarity": 0.924}], "id": 195, "stable_key": "clu_14f3b928e73ed1c0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Leaf", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "description": "The part of a plant attached to a stem or branch.", "wikipedia_extract": "A leaf (pl.: leaves) is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata (pores that intake and output gases), the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Veronica", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 3224, "target_cluster_name": "veronica", "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "deaguabebão oximel muyto brando, em quedeytemde infuſaohuma mãocheadeAbro- tanumfemina,aqueosHerbolarios chamão Veronica ,que tem (alem dehú cheyromuyto agradavel )as folhas dofeytiodas do Acyprefte ,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "a plant also called Abrotanum semen"}, {"found_name": "Folio", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 358, "target_cluster_name": "Folio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for 'leaves', a direct translation of the entity 'Leaf'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Portuguese for 'leaves', a direct translation of the entity 'Leaf'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Branches", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 806, "target_cluster_name": "Branches", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Leaves grow on branches.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Leaves grow on branches.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Abrotanum semina", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "deaguabebão oximel muyto brando, em quedeytemde infuſaohuma mãocheadeAbro- tanumfemina,aqueosHerbolarios chamão Veronica ,que tem (alem dehú cheyromuyto agradavel )as folhas dofeytiodas do Acyprefte ,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "a plant also called Veronica"}, {"found_name": "tembul", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "outros cheiros ; e postoque Autuario diga que os Mouros lhe chamam tembul, também se enganou como outros. ... RUANO Plinio diz* que o ha em Siria em folhas retortas, donde sae o olio pêra o unguento; ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for the substance derived from the plant"}]}, {"canonical_name": "sun", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 197, "members": [{"entity_id": "sun", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Sun", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 6, "variants": ["Sun"], "contexts": ["Sun, the fixed Stars lesser than the Moon", "celestial body, one of the great lights"]}, {"entity_id": "suns", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Suns", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Suns"], "contexts": ["celestial bodies"]}, {"entity_id": "sun", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "sun", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["sun"], "contexts": ["celestial body providing light and heat", "celestial body"]}, {"entity_id": "sun", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "sun", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 184, "variants": ["sun", "Sun"], "contexts": ["star at the center of our solar system", "celestial body with parallax"]}, {"entity_id": "suns", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "suns", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["suns"], "contexts": ["celestial bodies, incandescent matter"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Sun", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "sun", "similarity": 0.992}, {"source_book"