It is the main source of energy for life on Earth. The Sun has been an object of veneration in many cultures and a central subject for astronomical research since antiquity. The Sun orbits the Galactic Center at a distance of 24,000 to 28,000 light-years. Its mean distance from Earth is about 1.496×108 kilometres or about 8 light-minutes."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Cancer", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1709, "target_cluster_name": "Cancer", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Sun is a celestial body with significant astrological associations, particularly in relation to zodiac signs.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Sun is a celestial body with significant astrological associations, particularly in relation to zodiac signs.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Venery", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2268, "target_cluster_name": "Venery", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Venus is a planet in the solar system, which includes the Sun.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Venus is a planet in the solar system, which includes the Sun.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Stars", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2672, "target_cluster_name": "Stars", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Sun is a star, and its study is fundamental to understanding stars in general.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Sun is a star, and its study is fundamental to understanding stars in general.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Liverwort", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2888, "target_cluster_name": "epatica", "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "notwithstanding obtaineth that name from the figure of its leaves, and is one kind of Liverwort, or _Hepatica_. In _Milium Solis_, the Epithete of the Sun hath enlarged its opinion; which hath indeed ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a type of"}, {"found_name": "Hepatica", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "notwithstanding obtaineth that name from the figure of its leaves, and is one kind of Liverwort, or _Hepatica_. In _Milium Solis_, the Epithete of the Sun hath enlarged its opinion; which hath indeed ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Liverwort"}, {"found_name": "Lithospermon", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "notwithstanding obtaineth that name from the figure of its leaves, and is one kind of Liverwort, or _Hepatica_. In _Milium Solis_, the Epithete of the Sun hath enlarged its opinion; which hath indeed ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Milium Solis"}, {"found_name": "Grummel", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "notwithstanding obtaineth that name from the figure of its leaves, and is one kind of Liverwort, or _Hepatica_. In _Milium Solis_, the Epithete of the Sun hath enlarged its opinion; which hath indeed ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Milium Solis"}, {"found_name": "Milium Soler", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epid