"principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "attention", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "effort of attention", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "effort of attention", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "effort of attention", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "attention", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "attention", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "attention", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "attention", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 198, "stable_key": "clu_dcb552a2355cd384", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Attention", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q6501338", "wikidata_description": "behavioral and cognitive process of selectively concentrating on a discrete aspect of information, whether deemed subjective or objective, while ignoring other perceivable information", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attention", "wikipedia_extract": "Attention is the concentration of awareness directed at some phenomenon while mostly excluding others. Across disciplines, the nature of this directedness is conceptualized in different ways. In cognitive psychology, attention is often described as the allocation of limited cognitive processing resources to a subset of information, thoughts, or tasks. In neuropsychology, attention is understood as a set of mechanisms by which sensory cues and internal goals modulate neuronal tuning and orient behavioral and cognitive processes. Attention is not a unitary phenomenon but an umbrella term for multiple related processes, including selective attention (prioritizing some stimuli over others), sustained attention (maintaining focus), divided attention (sharing resources across tasks), and orienting (shifting focus in space or time). These processes are supported by distributed neural networks in frontal, parietal, and subcortical regions and are closely linked to working memory, executive functions, and consciousness."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Concentration", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 4042, "target_cluster_name": "concentration", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The definition of attention explicitly states it is the 'concentration of awareness'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The definition of attention explicitly states it is the 'concentration of awareness'."}, {"found_name": "Association of Ideas", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1992, "target_cluster_name": "association of ideas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historical texts often link attention to the ability to associate ideas, as focused attention is necessary for forming these associations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historical texts often link attention to the ability to associate ideas, as focused attention is necessary for forming these associations."}, {"found_name": "observation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 117, "target_cluster_name": "observation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Effective observation requires focused attention to perceive and record phenomena accurately.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Effective observation requires focused attention to perceive and record phenomena accurately.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "sights", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4260, "target_cluster_name": "sights", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sight is a primary mode of attention and perception.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sight is a primary mode of attention and perception.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "vision", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 353, "target_cluster_name": "vision", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Vision is often directed by attention, and attention can be focused on visual stimuli.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Vision is often directed by attention, and attention can be focused on visual stimuli.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "cognition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 656, "target_cluster_name": "cognition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a key cognitive function that enables the selection and processing of information, and is therefore intrinsically related to cognition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is a key cognitive function that enables the selection and processing of information, and is therefore intrinsically related to cognition.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "calmas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 854, "target_cluster_name": "calmas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calm technology is defined by its relationship to user attention, specifically by operating in the periphery rather than the center of attention.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Calm technology is defined by its relationship to user attention, specifically by operating in the periphery rather than the center of attention.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "faculties", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 943, "target_cluster_name": "faculties", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a fundamental mental faculty that enables focus and processing of information.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is a fundamental mental faculty that enables focus and processing of information.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mental activity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1179, "target_cluster_name": "mental activity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a specific type of mental activity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is a specific type of mental activity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "optical impressions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1200, "target_cluster_name": "optical impressions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is crucial for effective visual perception, as it directs and focuses the processing of visual information.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is crucial for effective visual perception, as it directs and focuses the processing of visual information.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "interest", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1991, "target_cluster_name": "interest", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Interest is a primary driver of attention; one pays attention to things that interest them.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Interest is a primary driver of attention; one pays attention to things that interest them.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mental states", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2058, "target_cluster_name": "mental states", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a cognitive process and a mental state involving focused awareness on a particular object or thought.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is a cognitive process and a mental state involving focused awareness on a particular object or thought.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "visual perception", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2419, "target_cluster_name": "visual perception", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Visual perception requires and is influenced by attention.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Visual perception requires and is influenced by attention.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "conscious states", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2424, "target_cluster_name": "conscious states", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a key component of consciousness, as it involves the selective focus of awareness on particular stimuli or thoughts, and is often discussed in conjunction with different states of consciousness.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Attention is a key component of consciousness, as it involves the selective focus of awareness on particular stimuli or thoughts, and is often discussed in conjunction wit