ncluding Pliny the Elder's 'Natural History', particularly in the sections on natural sciences and cosmology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Isidore of Seville's 'Etymologiae' incorporated and synthesized a vast amount of information from classical authors, including Pliny the Elder's 'Natural History', particularly in the sections on natural sciences and cosmology.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Columella", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1295, "target_cluster_name": "Columella", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Columella was a Roman writer on agriculture and rural economy, and Pliny the Elder was a Roman author and naturalist whose encyclopedic work 'Naturalis Historia' covered a vast range of topics including agriculture. Both were key figures in Roman natural history and agricultural writing.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Columella was a Roman writer on agriculture and rural economy, and Pliny the Elder was a Roman author and naturalist whose encyclopedic work 'Naturalis Historia' covered a vast range of topics including agriculture. Both were key figures in Roman natural history and agricultural writing.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Dodon", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2273, "target_cluster_name": "Dodon", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pliny's 'Natural History' was a significant source of botanical knowledge for Renaissance scholars like Dodoens.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Pliny's 'Natural History' was a significant source of botanical knowledge for Renaissance scholars like Dodoens.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "J. Pereira", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2795, "target_cluster_name": "J. Pereira", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were encyclopedic writers whose works covered natural history and materia medica, influencing later scientific thought. Pereira's comprehensive approach to pharmacology echoes Pliny's broad scope.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were encyclopedic writers whose works covered natural history and materia medica, influencing later scientific thought. Pereira's comprehensive approach to pharmacology echoes Pliny's broad scope.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "jasper", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 379, "target_cluster_name": "jaspe", "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "appears to have been given to fragments of 'jaspachat', and to a substance which the ancients termed 'jasponyx', which we now know as 'opal-jasper'. Pliny considers a piece of jasper eleven inches in ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a type of stone mentioned by Pliny"}, {"found_name": "jasponyx", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "appears to have been given to fragments of 'jaspachat', and to a substance which the ancients termed 'jasponyx', which we now know as 'opal-jasper'. Pliny considers a piece of jasper eleven inches in ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "an ancient term for a substance now known as opal-jasper"}]}, {"canonical_name": "olio", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 126, "members": [{"entity_id": "oil", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "oil", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["oil"], "contexts": ["viscous liquid substance"]}, {"entity_id": "olio", "bo