"], "contexts": ["awareness of mental states and sensations"]}, {"entity_id": "conscious_experience", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "conscious experience", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["conscious experience"], "contexts": ["subjective awareness of events", "awareness of internal and external stimuli"]}, {"entity_id": "phenomenon_of_consciousness", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "phenomenon of consciousness", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["phenomenon of consciousness"], "contexts": ["observable mental event"]}, {"entity_id": "phenomena_of_consciousness", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "phenomena of consciousness", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["phenomena of consciousness"], "contexts": ["observable aspects of awareness"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "consciousnesses", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 0.931}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "consciousnesses", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 0.931}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "consciousnesses", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 0.931}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "consciousness", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "consciousness", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "consciousness", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "consciousness", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 204, "stable_key": "clu_26b8130574c42bcb", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "consciousness", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "The overwhelming number of occurrences of 'consciousness' and related terms in William James's work firmly identifies this cluster.", "wikidata_id": "Q4313500", "wikidata_description": "medical condition that inhibits consciousness, sprituality", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disorder%20of%20consciousness", "wikipedia_extract": "Consciousness is being aware of something internal to one's self or being conscious of states or objects in one's external environment. It has been the topic of extensive explanations, analyses, and debate among philosophers, scientists, and theologians for millennia. There is no consensus on what exactly needs to be studied, or even if consciousness can be considered a scientific concept. In some explanations, it is synonymous with mind, while in others it is considered an aspect of it. In the past, consciousness meant one's \"inner life\": the world of introspection, private thought, imagination, and volition. Today, it often includes any kind of cognition, experience, feeling, or perception."}, "member_count": 14, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "conception", "link_type": "contested_identity", "link_strength": 0.7, "target_cluster_id": 282, "target_cluster_name": "conception", "source_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "evidence_snippet": "the same way that we think of minor objects. What conception, then, do we form of it? the reader may ask. That its name calls up in us some state of consciousness is unquestionable; and if this state ", "confidence": 0.8, "auto_label": "contested_identity", "found_relationship": "a state that may be confused with consciousness"}, {"found_name": "Association of Ideas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1992, "target_cluster_name": "association of ideas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historical philosophical traditions often linked consciousness to the way ideas are associated and processed in the mind.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historical philosophical traditions often linked consciousness to the way ideas are associated and processed in the mind."}, {"found_name": "Experience", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 105, "target_cluster_name": "experience", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Consciousness is fundamentally tied to subjective experience, the awareness of sensations, thoughts, and feelings.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Consciousness is fundamentally tied to subjective experience, the awareness of sensations, thoughts, and feelings."}, {"found_name": "Feeling", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 245, "target_cluster_name": "feeling", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Feelings are a direct manifestation of conscious experience, representing subjective emotional states.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Feelings are a direct manifestation of conscious experience, representing subjective emotional states."}, {"found_name": "Self-awareness", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3530, "target_cluster_name": "consciousness of Self", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Self-awareness is a key aspect of consciousness, involving the recognition of oneself as an individual.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Self-awareness is a key aspect of consciousness, involving the recognition of oneself as an individual."}, {"found_name": "reflection", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 760, "target_cluster_name": "reflection", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Reflection is a key aspect of consciousness, involving self-awareness and the ability to introspect.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Reflection is a key aspect of consciousness, involving self-awareness and the ability to introspect.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "habits", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2105, "target_cluster_name": "habits", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Habits often operate below the level of conscious awareness.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Habits often operate below the level of conscious awareness.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 122, "members": [{"entity_id": "goa", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Goa"], "contexts": ["independent settlement"]}, {"entity_id": "goa", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 117, "variants": ["Goa", "GOA"], "contexts": ["city where Ruano arrived", "City where aloe is used"]}, {"entity_id": "cidade_de_goa", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "cidade de Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["cidade de Goa"], "contexts": ["city where hospital was located"]}, {"entity_id": "goa", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Goa"], "contexts": ["city from which Spodio arrived", "city in India"]}, {"entity_id": "goa", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Goa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "var