he east and south, with the Arabian Sea forming its western coastline. It is India's smallest state by area and fourth-smallest by population. Panaji (Panjim) is the state's capital, while Vasco da Gama is its largest city by population. The state's official language is Konkani, spoken by the majority of its inhabitants."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "India", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 17, "target_cluster_name": "India", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Goa is a state within India, historically a significant Portuguese colony.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Goa is a state within India, historically a significant Portuguese colony.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Malabar", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 216, "target_cluster_name": "Malabar", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Goa is a region located on the Malabar Coast and was a significant historical entity within it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Goa is a region located on the Malabar Coast and was a significant historical entity within it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Deccan", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1808, "target_cluster_name": "Deckan", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Goa is geographically separated from the Deccan highlands by the Western Ghats, indicating a close geographical relationship and distinction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Goa is geographically separated from the Deccan highlands by the Western Ghats, indicating a close geographical relationship and distinction."}, {"found_name": "Cananor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1915, "target_cluster_name": "Cananor", "source_book