r geographical and administrative connections within the colonial period.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ambato and Quito are both cities in Ecuador, located relatively close to each other in the Andean highlands. Historical texts often discuss them in proximity due to their geographical and administrative connections within the colonial period."}, {"found_name": "Antisana", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1867, "target_cluster_name": "Antisana", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Antisana is a volcano located east of Quito, Ecuador. It is a prominent geographical feature in the region and often mentioned in relation to Quito's landscape and environment.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Antisana is a volcano located east of Quito, Ecuador. It is a prominent geographical feature in the region and often mentioned in relation to Quito's landscape and environment."}, {"found_name": "Chimborazo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 708, "target_cluster_name": "Chimborazo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chimborazo is a volcano and the highest mountain in Ecuador, located southwest of Quito. It is a significant geographical landmark in the vicinity of Quito and frequently referenced in descriptions of the region.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chimborazo is a volcano and the highest mountain in Ecuador, located southwest of Quito. It is a significant geographical landmark in the vicinity of Quito and frequently referenced in descriptions of the region."}, {"found_name": "Cotopaxi", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1777, "target_cluster_name": "Cotopaxi", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cotopaxi is an active volcano in the Andes Mountains of Ecuador, located south of Quito. It is a prominent natural feature in the region and often discussed in conjunction with Quito due to its proximity and volcanic activity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cotopaxi is an active volcano in the Andes Mountains of Ecuador, located south of Quito. It is a prominent natural feature in the region and often discussed in conjunction with Quito due to its proximity and volcanic activity."}, {"found_name": "prenadilla", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "opened, and water, fishes, and tufaceous mud are all ejected together. It is through this singular phenomenon* that the inhabitants of the highlands of Quito became acquainted with the existence of th", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "term used by inhabitants of Quito for a type of fish"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 146, "members": [{"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 98, "variants": ["Seed", "Seeds", "seed"], "contexts": ["part of the Arsmart plant", "small, black seed of Ladies-Bedstraw"]}, {"entity_id": "seedling", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seedling", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["seedling"], "contexts": ["young plant"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 3, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["part of a plant", "reproductive unit of plants"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 15, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["reproductive unit of plants", "unit of reproduction for plants"]}, {"entity_id": "seed", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "seed", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 2, "variants": ["seed"], "contexts": ["development into a tree", "reproductive unit of a plant"]}, {"entity_id": "seeds", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "seeds", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 3, "variants": ["seeds"], "contexts": ["determined by seminalities, that is, created and defined seeds", "seeds as big as glasses"]}, {"entity_id": "seeds", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seeds", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 21, "variants": ["seeds"], "contexts": ["food for singing birds", "reproductive units of plants"]}, {"entity_id": "seeds", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "seeds", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 1, "variants": ["seeds"], "contexts": ["reproductive units of plants"]}, {"entity_id": "semilla", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "semilla", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 1, "variants": ["semilla"], "contexts": ["seed used to make oil"]}, {"entity_id": "seeds", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "seeds", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "SEED", "count": 1, "variants": ["seeds"], "contexts": ["part of plant structure"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Seed", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "seedling", "similarity": 0.967}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "seed", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "seed", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 211, "stable_key": "clu_5ed7f4d301b6462a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Seed", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "note": "This cluster refers to the botanical seed, a fundamental part of plant reproduction and dispersal, as well as the early stage of a plant's life.", "wikidata_id": "Q40763", "wikidata_description": "embryonic plant enclosed in a protective outer covering (seed coat)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seed", "wikipedia_extract": "In botany, a seed is a plant structure containing an embryo and stored nutrients in a protective coat called a testa. More generally, the term seed means anything that can be sown, which may include seed and husk or tuber. Seeds are the product of the ripened ovule, after the embryo sac is fertilized by sperm from pollen, forming a zygote. The embryo within a seed develops from the zygote and grows within the mother plant to a certain size before growth is halted. The formation of the seed is the defining part of the process of reproduction in seed plants (spermatophytes). Other plants such as ferns, mosses and liverworts, do not have seeds and use water-dependent means to propagate themselves."}, "member_count": 10, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Folio", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 358, "target_cluster_name": "Folio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Seeds are reproductive units of plants, often developing from flowers which are associated with leaves.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Seeds are reproductive units of plants, often developing from flowers which are associated with leaves.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Poppy Seed", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2957, "target_cluster_name": "Poppy Seed", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Poppy Seed is a specific type of seed, derived from the poppy plant.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Poppy Seed is a specific type of seed, derived from the poppy plant."}, {"found_name": "Root", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 536, "target_cluster_name": "Root", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Seeds are the reproductive units of flowering plants, and the root is the primary organ responsible for anchoring the seedling and absorbing nutrients for its growth.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Seeds are the reproductive units of flowering plants, and the root is the primary organ responsible for anchoring the seedling and absorbing nutrients for its growth.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "especiarias", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2144, "target_cluster_name": "especiarias", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Seeds are listed as one of the plant parts that can be used as spices.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Seeds are listed as one of the plant parts that can be used as spices.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "seedlings", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2525, "target_cluster_name": "seedlings", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A seedling is a young plant grown from a seed.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A seedling is a young plant grown from a seed.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Acorns", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2922, "target_cluster_name": "Acorns", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Acorns contain a seedling and are a form of seed dispersal.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Acorns contain a seedling and are a form of seed dispersal.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "pimenta canarim", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "longa alguma delias, porque mais convém, entre si, a branca e a preta, que com a longa. E porque vos não fique alguma pimenta por saber, vedes aqui estas sementes vans, a que nesta terra chamam piment", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "a local name for certain seeds used as medicine"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 118, "members": [{"entity_id": "serapion", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Serapion", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 5, "variants": ["Serapion"], "contexts": ["ancient medical writer", "Serapion the Moor, an Author"]}, {"entity_id": "serapis", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Serapis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Serapis"], "contexts": ["temple where chariot was suspended"]}, {"entity_id": "serapio", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Serapio", "Seapio"], "contexts": ["medieval medical authority", "attributed mental and heart benefits to Balm"]}, {"entity_id": "serapio", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Serapio", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 105, "variants": ["Serapio", "Sarapio", "Serapiam", "Serapião"], "contexts": ["medical authority", "ancient medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "serapione", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Serapione", "category": "PERSON", "subcatego