was a physician who lived in the 3rd century BC. He belonged to the Empiric school, and so much extended and improved the system of Philinus of Cos, that the creation of the school is attributed to him by some ancient writers. Serapion wrote against Hippocrates with much vehemence, but neither this, nor any of his other works, have survived. He is several times mentioned by Celsus, Galen, Caelius Aurelianus, Aëtius, Paulus Aegineta, and Nicolaus Myrepsus. This article incorporates text from a publication now in the public domain: Smith, William, ed. (1870). Dictionary of Greek and Roman Biography and Mythology."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Ben\\acarta", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1631, "target_cluster_name": "Rasis", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "Serapio e Aviçena*, acho muitos nomes que de- vem ser corrompidos, scilicet, os nomes dos autores ; folga- ria muyto me dixestes disto o que sabeis. • Serapio, 3 19; Avicena, Lib. 2, cap. 3 18 (nota d", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for Rasis"}, {"found_name": "Cumcam", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "Cumcam, que he a fralda do mar, paicam; e em Axabio cassab aldirira. RUANO Pois Serapiam, que he arábio e de auctoridade, o chama assabel diriri*. • SerapiO) cap. 2o5 (nota do auctor). 142 Colóquio un", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for the known entity"}, {"found_name": "paicam", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "Cumcam, que he a fralda do mar, paicam; e em Axabio cassab aldirira. RUANO Pois Serapiam, que he arábio e de auctoridade, o chama assabel diriri*. • S