: "people from or residents of Portugal", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese%20people", "wikipedia_extract": "The Portuguese people (Portuguese: Portugueses – masculine – or Portuguesas) are a Romance-speaking ethnic group and nation indigenous to Portugal, a country that occupies the west side of the Iberian Peninsula in south-west Europe, who share culture, ancestry and language. The Portuguese state began with the founding of the County of Portugal in 868. Following the Battle of São Mamede (1128), Portugal gained international recognition as a kingdom through the Treaty of Zamora and the papal bull Manifestis Probatum. This Portuguese state paved the way for the Portuguese people to unite as a nation. The Portuguese explored distant lands previously unknown to Europeans—in the Americas, Africa, Asia and Oceania (southwest Pacific Ocean). In 1415, with the conquest of Ceuta, the Portuguese took a significant role in the Age of Discovery, which culminated in a colonial empire."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Afonso V of Portugal", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3733, "target_cluster_name": "Dom Affonio V", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Afonso V was a significant historical figure and monarch of Portugal, directly associated with the Portuguese people.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Afonso V was a significant historical figure and monarch of Portugal, directly associated with the Portuguese people."}, {"found_name": "Amato Lusitano", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2328, "target_cluster_name": "Amato Lusitano", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amato Lusitano was a prominent Portuguese physician and humanist of the Renaissance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Amato Lusitano was a prominent Portuguese physician and hum