 country spanning the northeast corner of Africa and southwest corner of Asia via the Sinai Peninsula. It is bordered by the Mediterranean Sea to the north, Palestine and Israel to the northeast, the Red Sea to the east, Sudan to the south, and Libya to the west. The Gulf of Aqaba in the northeast separates Egypt from Jordan and Saudi Arabia. Cairo is the capital, largest city, and leading cultural centre, while Alexandria is the second-largest city and an important hub of industry and tourism. With over 107 million inhabitants, Egypt is the third-most populous country in Africa and 15th-most populated in the world. Egypt has one of the longest histories of any country, tracing its heritage along the Nile Delta back to the 6th–4th millennia BCE.", "country": "Egypt"}, "member_count": 16, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Nile River", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 128, "target_cluster_name": "Nil", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Nile River is intrinsically linked to the history and civilization of Egypt, often referred to as the 'lifeblood' of the country.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Nile River is intrinsically linked to the history and civilization of Egypt, often referred to as the 'lifeblood' of the country."}, {"found_name": "Alexandria", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 92, "target_cluster_name": "Alexandria", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alexandria is a major city located in Egypt.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Alexandria is a major city located in Egypt.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Nil", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 128, "target_cluster_name": "Nil", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Nile River is historically and geographically central to