e of equilibrium. A system is unstable if it deviates from an equilibrium state and its deviations grow over time.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "vibration", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2586, "target_cluster_name": "vibration", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Vibrations often occur as a displacement from a state of equilibrium.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Vibrations often occur as a displacement from a state of equilibrium.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Faraday", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 49, "members": [{"entity_id": "faraday", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Faraday", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Faraday"], "contexts": ["example of departed spirit"]}, {"entity_id": "faraday", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Faraday", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 9, "variants": ["Faraday"], "contexts": ["scientist known for electromagnetic induction", "scientist mentioned with Melloni"]}, {"entity_id": "faraday", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Faraday", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 37, "variants": ["Faraday"], "contexts": ["discovered affinity properties", "reduced gases to liquid state by compression"]}, {"entity_id": "faraday", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Faraday", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Faraday"], "contexts": ["discovered magnetism's effect on polarized light", "scientist studying electricity and magnetism"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Faraday", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Faraday", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 248, "stable_key": "clu_5f273b6e2aefc44b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Michael Faraday", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1791, "death_year": 1867, "description": "English scientist known for electromagnetism and electrochemistry", "wikidata_id": "Q8750", "wikidata_description": "British scientist (1791–1867)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael%20Faraday", "wikipedia_extract": "Michael Faraday ( FAR-uh-day; 22 September 1791 – 25 August 1867) was an English chemist and physicist who contributed to the study of electrochemistry and electromagnetism. His main discoveries include the principles underlying electromagnetic induction, diamagnetism, and electrolysis. Although Faraday received little formal education, as a self-made man, he was one of the most influential scientists in history. It was by his research on the magnetic field around a conductor carrying a direct current that Faraday established the concept of the electromagnetic field in physics. Faraday also established that magnetism could affect rays of light and that there was an underlying relationship between the two phenomena. He similarly discovered the principles of electromagnetic induction, diamagnetism, and the laws of electrolysis."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alessandro Volta", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 966, "target_cluster_name": "Volta", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volta was a key figure in the development of electricity, a field in which Faraday made foundational contributions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Volta was a key figure in the development of electricity, a field in which Faraday made foundational contributions."}, {"found_name": "André-Marie Ampère", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2134, "target_cluster_name": "Ampère", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ampère's work on the mathematical theory of electromagnetism directly preceded and influenced Faraday's experimental investigations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ampère's work on the mathematical theory of electromagnetism directly preceded and influenced Faraday's experimental investigations."}, {"found_name": "Benjamin Franklin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 343, "target_cluster_name": "Franklin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Franklin's early experiments with electricity laid groundwork for later discoveries in the field, including those of Faraday.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Franklin's early experiments with electricity laid groundwork for later discoveries in the field, including those of Faraday."}, {"found_name": "Carl Wilhelm Scheele", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1258, "target_cluster_name": "Scheele", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Scheele was a chemist whose work on oxygen and other elements was foundational to chemistry, a field Faraday also contributed to.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Scheele was a chemist whose work on oxygen and other elements was foundational to chemistry, a field Faraday also contributed to."}, {"found_name": "Charles Darwin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 118, "target_cluster_name": "Darwin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both Faraday and Darwin were seminal figures in 19th-century science, making groundbreaking discoveries in their respective fields (electromagnetism and evolution).", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both Faraday and Darwin were seminal figures in 19th-century science, making groundbreaking discoveries in their respective fields (electromagnetism and evolution)."}, {"found_name": "Humphry Davy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1877, "target_cluster_name": "Sir Humphry Davy", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Davy was Faraday's mentor and a significant chemist and physicist in his own right. Faraday worked as his assistant at the Royal Institution.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Davy was Faraday's mentor and a significant chemist and physicist in his own right. Faraday worked as his assistant at the Royal Institution."}, {"found_name": "Helmholtz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 624, "target_cluster_name": "Helmholtz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were highly influential scientists in the 19th century, with Helmholtz making significant contributions to electromagnetism, a field Faraday pioneered. They would have been contemporaries and aware of each other's work.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were highly influential scientists in the 19th century, with Helmholtz making significant contributions to electromagnetism, a field Faraday pioneered. They would have been contemporaries and aware of each other's work.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Tyndall", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 976, "target_cluster_name": "Tyndall", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were highly influential physicists of the 19th century. Faraday's foundational work in electromagnetism and Tyndall's subsequent research in related areas, including diamagnetism and the absorption of heat by gases, indicate a strong intellectual lineage and shared field of study.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were highly influential physicists of the 19th century. Faraday's foundational work in electromagnetism and Tyndall's subsequent research in related areas, including diamagnetism and the absorption of heat by gases, indicate a strong intellectual lineage and shared field of study.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Matteucci", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1078, "target_cluster_name": "Matteucci", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were leading experimental physicists of the 19th century who made fundamental discoveries in electricity and magnetism. Faraday's work on electromagnetic induction and the nature of electric fields was highly influential for physicists like Matteucci studying bioelectrical phenomena.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were leading experimental physicists of the 19th century who made fundamental discoveries in electricity and magnetism. Faraday's work on electromagnetic induction and the nature of electric fields was highly influential for physicists like Matteucci studying bioelectrical phenomena.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Grove"