control which becomes automatized (e.g. see Heckhausen and Kuhl; Gollwitzer; Boekaerts and Corno)."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Free will", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 3567, "target_cluster_name": "free-will", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Free will is a philosophical concept that is directly synonymous with or a core component of volition, emphasizing the capacity to make uncoerced choices.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Free will is a philosophical concept that is directly synonymous with or a core component of volition, emphasizing the capacity to make uncoerced choices."}, {"found_name": "Cognition", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 656, "target_cluster_name": "cognition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volition is described as a cognitive process, making cognition a broader category that encompasses volition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Volition is described as a cognitive process, making cognition a broader category that encompasses volition."}, {"found_name": "Cognitive processes", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2579, "target_cluster_name": "intellectual operations", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volition is explicitly defined as a cognitive process, indicating a direct relationship where volition is a type of cognitive process.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Volition is explicitly defined as a cognitive process, indicating a direct relationship where volition is a type of cognitive process."}, {"found_name": "Bodily action", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 3565, "target_cluster_name": "bodily action", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volition is the cognitive process that leads to a decision and commitment to a course of action, which often manifests as bodily action.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Volition is the cognitive process that leads to a decision and commitment to a course of action, which often manifests as bodily action."}, {"found_name": "Ambition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4281, "target_cluster_name": "Ambition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ambition is a strong desire and determination to achieve success, which is closely related to volition as a driving force behind committed action.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ambition is a strong desire and determination to achieve success, which is closely related to volition as a driving force behind committed action."}, {"found_name": "Appetite", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2030, "target_cluster_name": "Appetite", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Appetite, in a broader sense, can refer to a strong desire or craving, which is a precursor or component of volitional striving.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Appetite, in a broader sense, can refer to a strong desire or craving, which is a precursor or component of volitional striving."}, {"found_name": "Desire", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 925, "target_cluster_name": "desire", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Desire is a fundamental aspect of motivation that often precedes and informs volitional decisions and actions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Desire is a fundamental aspect of motivation that often precedes and informs volitional decisions and actions."}, {"found_name": "Emotion and Will", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3531, "target_cluster_name": "Emotion and Will", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This entry directly links emotion and will, suggesting a close relationship between affective states and volitional processes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "This entry directly links emotion and will, suggesting a close relationship between affective states and volitional processes."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Iron", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 55, "members": [{"entity_id": "iron", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Iron", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 23, "variants": ["Iron"], "contexts": ["common metal", "material exhibiting magnetism"]}, {"entity_id": "iron", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Iron", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Iron", "iron"], "contexts": ["metal quenched in water for remedy", "mentioned as a substance"]}, {"entity_id": "iron", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "iron", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 14, "variants": ["iron"], "contexts": ["metal found in meteoric dust", "element found in dust"]}, {"entity_id": "iron", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "iron", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 8, "variants": ["iron"], "contexts": ["metal that rusts in water", "material used by an artizan"]}, {"entity_id": "ferrum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "ferrum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["ferrum"], "contexts": ["Latin for iron"]}, {"entity_id": "fer", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "fer", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 4, "variants": ["fer"], "contexts": ["metal found in chain", "metal found in mounds"]}, {"entity_id": "ferri", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "ferri", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["ferri"], "contexts": ["Latin for iron"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Iron", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Iron", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "iron", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "iron", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 251, "stable_key": "clu_8347f52ef8d63248", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "iron", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "Q677", "wikidata_description": "chemical element with symbol Fe and atomic number 26", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron", "wikipedia_extract": "Iron is a chemical element; it has symbol Fe (from Latin  ferrum 'iron') and atomic number 26. It is a metal that belongs to the first transition series and group 8 of the periodic table. It is, by mass, the most common element on Earth, forming much of Earth's outer and inner core. It is the fourth most abundant element in the Earth's crust. In its metallic state it was mainly deposited by meteorites. Extracting usable metal from iron ores requires kilns or furnaces capable of reaching 1,500 °C (2,730 °F), about 500 °C (900 °F) higher than that required to smelt copper."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Hematite", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2678, "target_cluster_name": "Hematites", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hematite is a primary ore of iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hematite is a primary ore of iron."}, {"found_name": "Iron oxide", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 3119, "target_cluster_name": "oxyd of iron", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron oxide is a compound of iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iron oxide is a compound of iron."}, {"found_name": "Iron oxides", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 4377, "target_cluster_name": "peroxyd of iron", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron oxides are compounds of iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iron oxides are compounds of iron."}, {"found_name": "Iron preparations", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2027, "target_cluster_name": "Crocus Martis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron preparations are derived from iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iron preparations are derived from iron."}, {"found_name": "Iron sand", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2685, "target_cluster_name": "Ironsand", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron sand is a naturally occurring form of iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iron sand is a naturally occurring form of iron."}, {"found_name": "Iron wire", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 3834, "target_cluster_name": "Iron wire", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron wire is a manufactured form of iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iron wire is a manufactured form of iron."}, {"found_name": "Crocus Martis", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2027, "target_cluster_name": "Crocus Martis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Crocus Martis is a historical name for preparations of iron, often referring to iron oxides or other iron compounds used medicinally or in alchemy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_