aps all other Earth sciences, including hydrology. It is integrated with Earth system science and planetary science. Geology describes the structure of the Earth on and beneath its surface and the processes that have shaped that structure. Geologists study the mineralogical composition of rocks in order to get insight into their history of formation."}, "member_count": 10, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "botany", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1098, "target_cluster_name": "botany", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Geology can inform paleobotany through the study of fossil-bearing strata.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Geology can inform paleobotany through the study of fossil-bearing strata.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "physical science", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 834, "target_cluster_name": "physical science", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Geology is a subfield of physical science.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Geology is a subfield of physical science.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "natural science", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 990, "target_cluster_name": "natural science", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Geology is a core component of natural science.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Geology is a core component of natural science.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Géogr.", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3432, "target_cluster_name": "Géogr.", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Geology is the study of the Earth's physical structure and substance, its history, and the processes which act on it. It is closely related to