 is credited with having discovered the chemical composition of purified hydrogen sulfide in 1777. Hydrogen sulfide is toxic to humans and most other animals by inhibiting cellular respiration in a manner similar to hydrogen cyanide. When it is inhaled or its salts are ingested in high amounts, damage to organs occurs rapidly with symptoms ranging from breathing difficulties to convulsions and death."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Sulfur", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1820, "target_cluster_name": "Sulfur", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hydrogen sulfide is a compound containing sulfur, often referred to as 'sulfurated hydrogen' in historical texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Hydrogen sulfide is a compound containing sulfur, often referred to as 'sulfurated hydrogen' in historical texts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Air", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 109, "target_cluster_name": "air", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas found in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas found in the atmosphere."}, {"found_name": "Gaseous substances", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2321, "target_cluster_name": "gaseous", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas."}, {"found_name": "Gas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 171, "target_cluster_name": "gas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hydrogen sulfide is a gas."}, {"found_name": "Chemica