4, comprises nearly half of zinc's total abundance. In some respects, zinc is chemically similar to magnesium: both elements exhibit only one normal oxidation state (+2), and the Zn2+ and Mg2+ ions are of similar size."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Brass", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 440, "target_cluster_name": "Brass", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Brass is an alloy primarily composed of copper and zinc.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Brass is an alloy primarily composed of copper and zinc."}, {"found_name": "Cadmium", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2885, "target_cluster_name": "Cadmia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cadmium is a chemical element in the same group (Group 12) of the periodic table as zinc.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cadmium is a chemical element in the same group (Group 12) of the periodic table as zinc."}, {"found_name": "Copper", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 274, "target_cluster_name": "copper", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Copper is often found in association with zinc ores, and they are commonly alloyed to form brass.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Copper is often found in association with zinc ores, and they are commonly alloyed to form brass."}, {"found_name": "Metal", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 87, "target_cluster_name": "metal", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Zinc is a chemical element classified as a metal.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Zinc is a chemical element classified as a metal."}, {"found_name": "Metal oxides", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4543, "target_cluster_name": "Protoxides of metals", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Zinc forms various oxides, such as zinc oxide, which are compounds of zinc and oxygen.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Zinc forms various oxides, such as zinc oxide, which are compounds of zinc and oxygen."}, {"found_name": "Cadmia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2885, "target_cluster_name": "Cadmia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cadmium is chemically similar to zinc and often found in zinc ores.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cadmium is chemically similar to zinc and often found in zinc ores.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Cirurgiaó", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "chirurgeons", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Chirurgeons", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 1, "variants": ["Chirurgeons"], "contexts": ["surgical practitioners"]}, {"entity_id": "chirurgiens", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "chirurgiens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 2, "variants": ["chirurgiens", "cirujanos"], "contexts": ["surgical practitioners in Havana"]}, {"entity_id": "chirurgo", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Chirurgo", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 2, "variants": ["Chirurgo", "Chirurghi"], "contexts": ["surgeon", "surgeons"]}, {"entity_id": "cirurgiaó", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Cirurgiaó", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 25, "variants": ["Cirurgiaó", "Chirurgis", "Chirurgo", "Chirurgus", "Cirurgia", "Cirurgiao", "Cirurgiaó ManoelNogueyra", "Cirurgiaō", "Cirurgioens", "Cirurgião", "Cirurgiões"], "contexts": ["healed a wound", "surgeon"]}, {"entity_id": "chyrurgions", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Chyrurgions", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 1, "variants": ["Chyrurgions"], "contexts": ["surgeons using knives and lances"]}, {"entity_id": "chyrurgion", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Chyrurgion", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 1, "variants": ["Chyrurgion"], "contexts": ["surgical practitioner"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Chirurgeons", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "chirurgiens", "similarity": 0.963}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Chirurgeons", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Chirurgo", "similarity": 0.91}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "chirurgiens", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Chirurgo", "similarity": 0.904}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "chirurgiens", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Cirurgiaó", "similarity": 0.883}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Chirurgo", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Cirurgiaó", "similarity": 0.93}], "id": 289, "stable_key": "clu_7cf741c45c6e7794", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Surgeon", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Medical practitioner specializing in surgical procedures.", "wikidata_id": "Q774306", "wikidata_description": "physician with surgical specialty", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surgeon", "wikipedia_extract": "In  medicine, a surgeon is a medical doctor who performs surgery. Even though there are different traditions in different times and places, a modern surgeon is a licensed physician and received the same medical training as physicians before specializing in surgery. In some countries and jurisdictions, the title of 'surgeon' is restricted to maintain the integrity of the craft group in the medical profession. A specialist regarded as a legally recognized surgeon includes podiatry, dentistry, and veterinary medicine. It is estimated that surgeons perform over 300 million surgical procedures globally each year. The first person to document a surgery was the 6th century BC Indian physician-surgeon, Sushruta."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Plata", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 30, "members": [{"entity_id": "platine", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "platine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 7, "variants": ["platine", "Platine"], "contexts": ["found in abundance in Choco and Barbacoas", "metal found in Clioco and Barbacoas"]}, {"entity_id": "platinum", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "platinum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["platinum"], "contexts": ["precious metal", "metal with high density"]}, {"entity_id": "plata", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Plata", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 19, "variants": ["Plata", "plata"], "contexts": ["silver, a metal", "silver"]}, {"entity_id": "platina", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Platina", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Platina", "platina"], "contexts": ["incandescent metal for heat source", "incandescent material for heat source"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "platine", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "platinum", "similarity": 0.985}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "platine", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Plata", "similarity": 0.908}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "platine", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Platina", "similarity": 0.932}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "platinum", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Plata", "similarity": 0.895}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "platinum", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Platina", "similarity": 0.921}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Plata", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Platina", "similarity": 0.963}], "id": 290, "stable_key": "clu_29bc88ddbd489182", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": null, "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "While 'Plata' can mean silver, the context of 'platine' and 'Platina' strongly indicates platinum, a distinct precious metal.", "wikidata_id": "Q880", "wikidata_description": "chemical element with symbol Pt and atomic number 78", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum", "wikipedia_extract": "Platinum is a chemical element; it has symbol Pt and atomic number 78. It is a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, precious, silverish-white transition metal. Its name originates from Spanish platina, a diminutive of plata \"silver\". Platinum is a member of the platinum group of elements and group 10 of the periodic table of elements. It has six naturally occurring isotopes. It is one of the rarer elements in Earth's crust, with an average abundance of approximately 5 μg/kg."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "piastres", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1529, "target_cluster_name": "piastres", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The term 'piastre' originates from the Italian word for 'thin metal plate', and was applied to Spanish and Hispanic American pieces of eight, or pesos. 'Plata' is Spanish for silver, and the Spanish peso was a silver coin, making 'Plata' a related concept in the context of currency and coinage.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The term 'piastre' originates from the Italian word for 'thin metal plate', and was applied to Spanish and Hispanic American pieces of eight, or pesos. 'Plata' is Spanish for silver, and the Spanish peso was a silver coin, making 'Plata' a related concept in the context of currency and coinage.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Silver", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 632, "target_cluster_name": "Argento", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The description explicitly states that platinum is a 'precious, silverish-white transition metal' and that its name originates from the Spanish word for silver ('plata'). This indicates a strong association and comparison between the two metals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The description explicitly states that platinum is a 'precious, silverish-white transition metal' and that its name originates from the Spanish word for silver ('plata'). This indicates a strong association and comparison between the two metals."}]}, {"canonical_name": "comet", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "planetary_comets", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "planetary comets", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["planetary comets"], "contexts": ["comets within planetary orbits"]}, {"entity_id": "cometa", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Cometa", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cometa"], "contexts": ["comet"]}, {"entity_id": "comet", "book_