ão", "similarity": 0.881}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Strabo", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Strabão", "similarity": 0.881}], "id": 296, "stable_key": "clu_2ee450a4c7e4e042", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Strabo", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Ancient Greek geographer, historian, and philosopher.", "wikipedia_extract": "Strabo (; Greek: Στράβων, romanized: Strábōn; 64 or 63 BC – c. 24 AD) was an ancient Greek geographer who lived in Asia Minor during the transitional period of the Roman Republic into the Roman Empire. He is best known for his work Geographica, which presented a descriptive history of people and places from different regions of the world known during his lifetime. Additionally, Strabo authored historical works, but only fragments and quotations of these survive in the writings of other authors. Strabo was born to an affluent family from Amaseia in Pontus in around 64 BC. His family had been involved in politics since at least the reign of Mithridates V. Strabo was related to Dorylaeus on his mother's side."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Eratosthenes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1129, "target_cluster_name": "Eratosthenes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent ancient Greek geographers whose works described the known world.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent ancient Greek geographers whose works described the known world."}, {"found_name": "Ptolemy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 824, "target_cluster_name": "Ptolemy", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential ancient geographers whose works were foundational for later geographical understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were influential ancient geographers whose works were foundational for later geographical understanding."}, {"found_name": "Herodotus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 337, "target_cluster_name": "Heródoto", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were ancient Greek writers who described geography and peoples, with Herodotus being a precursor to Strabo's more systematic approach.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were ancient Greek writers who described geography and peoples, with Herodotus being a precursor to Strabo's more systematic approach."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Winter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 39, "members": [{"entity_id": "winter", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Winter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Winter"], "contexts": ["season when maggots lodge in cells"]}, {"entity_id": "winter", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Winter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 23, "variants": ["Winter", "Winter Frosts"], "contexts": ["season affecting the herb's leaves", "season leaving behind phlegm"]}, {"entity_id": "winter", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "winter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["winter"], "contexts": ["coldest season of the year"]}, {"entity_id": "winter", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Winter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["winter", "Winter"], "contexts": ["coldest season affecting moisture", "atmospheric electricity in"]}, {"entity_id": "hiver", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "hiver", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["hiver"], "contexts": ["seas