en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withania%20somnifera", "wikipedia_extract": "Withania somnifera, known commonly as ashwagandha, is an evergreen shrub in the Solanaceae family that is native to the Middle East and North Africa, other African regions, southern Europe, Indian subcontinent, and across Southeast Asia. Several other species in the genus Withania are morphologically similar. Other common names include Indian ginseng and winter cherry. W. somnifera is a short shrub 35–75 cm (14–30 in) tall with tomentose branches, dull green elliptic leaves up to 10–12 cm (3.9–4.7 in) long, small green bell-shaped flowers, and orange-red ripe fruit. It is affected by various pests and diseases in India, which can damage plant health and reduce its secondary metabolite content."}, "member_count": 8, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Autumn", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 911, "target_cluster_name": "Autumn", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Winter immediately follows Autumn.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Winter immediately follows Autumn.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "sight", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 27, "members": [{"entity_id": "sight", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "sight", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["sight"], "contexts": ["faculty of vision"]}, {"entity_id": "sight", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "sight", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 13, "variants": ["Sight", "sight"], "contexts": ["sense affected by eye conditions", "dimness of sight helped by Angelica"]}, {"entity_id": "sight", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "sight", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["sight"], "contexts": ["sense of v