hanics", "wikipedia_extract": "Mechanics (from Ancient Greek  μηχανική (mēkhanikḗ) 'of machines') is the area of physics concerned with the relationships between force, matter, and motion among physical objects. Forces applied to objects may result in displacements, which are changes of an object's position relative to its environment. Theoretical expositions of this branch of physics have their origins in Ancient Greece, for instance, in the writings of Aristotle and Archimedes (see History of classical mechanics and Timeline of classical mechanics). During the early modern period, scientists such as Galileo Galilei, Johannes Kepler, Christiaan Huygens, and Isaac Newton laid the foundation for what is now known as classical mechanics. In the 20th century the concepts of classical mechanics were challenged by new discoveries, leading to fundamentally new approaches including relativistic mechanics and quantum mechanics. The ancient Greek philosophers were among the first to propose that abstract principles govern nature."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Acceleration", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2252, "target_cluster_name": "acceleration", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Acceleration is a fundamental concept within mechanics, describing the rate of change of velocity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Acceleration is a fundamental concept within mechanics, describing the rate of change of velocity."}, {"found_name": "Action and reaction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 961, "target_cluster_name": "Action and reaction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Newton's third law of motion, a cornerstone of mechanics, describes the relationship between action and reaction forces.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Newton's third law of motion, a cornerstone of mechanics, describes the relationship between action and reaction forces."}, {"found_name": "Centrifugal force", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 315, "target_cluster_name": "Centrifugal force", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a concept used in analyzing circular motion within mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Centrifugal force is a concept used in analyzing circular motion within mechanics."}, {"found_name": "Elasticity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 798, "target_cluster_name": "elasticity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Elasticity describes the ability of a material to deform under stress and return to its original shape, a property studied in mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Elasticity describes the ability of a material to deform under stress and return to its original shape, a property studied in mechanics."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Centrifugal force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 22, "members": [{"entity_id": "centrifugal", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "centrifugal", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["centrifugal"], "contexts": ["nerve signals moving away from center"]}, {"entity_id": "centrifugal_force", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "centrifugal force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["centrifugal force"], "contexts": ["force causing compression"]}, {"entity_id": "centrifugal_force", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Centrifugal force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 19, "variants": ["Centrifugal force", "centrifugal force"], "contexts": ["force preventing moon's descent to earth", "outward force from rotation"]}, {"entity_id": "centrifugal_force", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "centrifugal force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["centrifugal force"], "contexts": ["outward force due to rotation"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "centrifugal", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Centrifugal force", "similarity": 0.888}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "centrifugal force", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Centrifugal force", "similarity": 0.983}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "centrifugal force", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "centrifugal force", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Centrifugal force", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "centrifugal force", "similarity": 0.983}], "id": 315, "stable_key": "clu_5127ad9d99844b2c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Centrifugal force", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q178733", "wikidata_description": "type of inertial force", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centrifugal%20force", "wikipedia_extract": "In Newtonian mechanics, a centrifugal force is a kind of fictitious force (or inertial force) that appears to act on all objects when viewed in a rotating frame of reference. It appears to be directed perpendicularly from the axis of rotation of the frame. The magnitude of the centrifugal force F on an object of mass m at the perpendicular distance ρ from the axis of a rotating frame of reference with angular velocity ω is The concept of centrifugal force simplifies the analysis of rotating devices by adopting a co-rotating frame of reference, such as in centrifuges, centrifugal pumps, centrifugal governors, and centrifugal clutches, and in centrifugal railways, planetary orbits and banked curves. The same centrifugal effect observed on rotating devices can be analyzed in an inertial reference frame as a consequence of inertia and the physical forces without invoking a centrifugal force. From 1659, the Neo-Latin term vi centrifuga ('centrifugal force') is attested in Christiaan Huygens' notes and letters. In Latin centrum means 'center' and ‑fugus (from fugiō) means 'fleeing, avoiding'."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "attraction and repulsion", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2658, "target_cluster_name": "attraction and repulsion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Often discussed in conjunction with centripetal forces (a form of attraction) in historical physics, representing opposing forces in rotational motion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Often discussed in conjunction with centripetal forces (a form of attraction) in historical physics, representing opposing forces in rotational motion.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Force", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 59, "target_cluster_name": "Force", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a specific type of force, particularly relevant in rotational motion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Centrifugal force is a specific type of force, particularly relevant in rotational motion.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "attractive", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1309, "target_cluster_name": "attractive", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is often discussed in opposition to or in relation to centripetal force, which is a form of attraction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Centrifugal force is often discussed in opposition to or in relation to centripetal force, which is a form of attraction.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "physics", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 110, "target_cluster_name": "physics", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a concept used to describe the outward effect of inertia in a rotating system, relevant to classical mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Centrifugal force is a concept used to describe the outward effect of inertia in a rotating system, relevant to classical mechanics.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "friction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 155, "target_cluster_name": "friction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both friction and centrifugal force are concepts related to motion and the forces that resist or are generated by it. Understanding one can inform the understanding of the other in mechanical systems.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both friction and centrifugal force are concepts related to motion and the forces that resist or are generated by it. Understanding one can inform the understanding of the other in mechanical systems.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Pressure", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 295, "target_cluster_name": "Pressure", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a concept related to forces that can cause pressure, particularly in rotating systems.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Centrifugal force is a concept related to forces that can cause pressure, particularly in rotating systems.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mechanics", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 314, "target_cluster_name": "mechanics", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a concept used in analyzing circular motion within mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Centrifugal force is a concept used in analyzing circular motion within mechanics.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Acceleration", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2252, "target_cluster_name": "acceleration", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a fictitious force that arises in a rotating frame of reference, which is an accelerating frame. The concept is intrinsically linked to the acceleration experienced by an observer in such a frame.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Centrifugal force is a fictitious force that arises in a rotating frame of reference, which is an accelerating frame. The concept is intrinsically linked to the acceleration experienced by an observer in such a frame."}, {"found_name": "Attraction (physics)", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4186, "target_cluster_name": "attractions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is often discussed in contrast to or in conjunction with real forces like attraction, particularly in the context of circular motion where it opposes centripetal force.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Centrifugal force is often discussed in contrast to or in conjunction with real forces like attraction, particularly in the context of circular motion where it opposes centripetal force."}, {"found_name": "Attractive force", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_i