t_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Jews", "similarity": 0.947}], "id": 356, "stable_key": "clu_401b8ba4c1080063", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Jewish people", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Religious and ethnic group often referenced in historical texts.", "wikidata_id": "Q7325", "wikidata_description": "ethnoreligious group and nation from the Levant", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jews", "wikipedia_extract": "Jews (Hebrew: יְהוּדִים‎, ISO 259-2: Yehudim, Israeli pronunciation: [jehuˈdim]), or the Jewish people, are an ethnoreligious group and nation, originating from the Israelites of ancient Israel and Judah. They traditionally adhere to Judaism. Jewish ethnicity, religion, and community are highly interrelated, as Judaism is an ethnic religion, though many ethnic Jews do not practice it. Religious Jews regard converts to Judaism as members of the Jewish nation, pursuant to the long-standing conversion process. The Israelites emerged from the pre-existing Canaanite peoples to establish Israel and Judah in the Southern Levant during the Iron Age. Originally, Jews referred to the inhabitants of the kingdom of Judah and were distinguished from the gentiles and the Samaritans."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "reino", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 3196, "target_cluster_name": "reino", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamados coaris, e no reino de Cambaiete lhe chamam esparcis, e nós os ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "reverse: synonym used by Portuguese for a group of people", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mercadores", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1256, "target_cluster_name": "mercadores", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "tocar com elles; o seu cuidado he limpar as çugidades das casas e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamado", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Portuguese comparison for esparcis", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Alum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 27, "members": [{"entity_id": "alum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Alum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Alum"], "contexts": ["mineral solution that crystallizes"]}, {"entity_id": "aluminous", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "aluminous", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["aluminous"], "contexts": ["earthy precipitate containing aluminum"]}, {"entity_id": "aluminis", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "aluminis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["aluminis"], "contexts": ["ingredient in a preparation", "related to Amianthus"]}, {"entity_id": "alum", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Alum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 9, "variants": ["Alum", "alum"], "contexts": ["mineral dissolved in water for crystallization", "transmits light, stops heat"]}, {"entity_id": "allum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Allum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["Allum"], "contexts": ["salt attracts weakly", "mineral substance with electrical properties"]}, {"entity_id": "roch-allum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Roch-Allum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Roch-Allum"], "contexts": ["mineral with