ial insemination (AI) and embryo transfer, as well as genome resource banking. The study of reproductive medicine is thought to date back to Aristotle, where he came up with the “Haematogenous Reproduction Theory”. However, evidence-based reproductive medicine is traceable back to the 1970s."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Conception", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 282, "target_cluster_name": "conception", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fertility is the capacity to conceive offspring, making conception a directly related biological process.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Fertility is the capacity to conceive offspring, making conception a directly related biological process."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Indian Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 16, "members": [{"entity_id": "indian_ocean", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Indian Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Indian Ocean"], "contexts": ["ocean where fish range from Pacific", "ocean"]}, {"entity_id": "indian_ocean", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Indian Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 6, "variants": ["Indian Ocean"], "contexts": ["ocean navigated by Chinese vessels", "ocean"]}, {"entity_id": "oceano_indico", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "oceano Indico", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["oceano Indico"], "contexts": ["ocean for trade"]}, {"entity_id": "indian_ocean", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Indian Ocean", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 6, "variants": ["Indian Ocean"], "contexts": ["ocean entered by tidal wave", "ocean with periodic winds called monsoons"]}, {"entity_id": "west_india_seas", "book