ting wastewater into an effluent for return to the water cycle", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wastewater%20treatment", "wikipedia_extract": "Wastewater treatment is a process which removes contaminants from wastewater. The resulting effluent, discharged to a water body, has an acceptable impact on the environment. Domestic wastewater, also called municipal wastewater or sewage, is processed at a sewage treatment plant. Industrial wastewater is often processed at a specially-designed industrial wastewater treatment facility, or at a sewage treatment plant. In the latter case the industry typically performs on-site pretreatment of the waste, before it is sent to the municipal plant. Other types of wastewater treatment plants include agricultural wastewater treatment and leachate treatment plants."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "air", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 109, "target_cluster_name": "air", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historically, air was often classified as a fluid, alongside liquids.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Historically, air was often classified as a fluid, alongside liquids.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Water", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 0, "target_cluster_name": "Water", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Water is a quintessential example of a fluid and was often used synonymously or as the primary referent when discussing fluids in general.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Water is a quintessential example of a fluid and was often used synonymously or as the primary referent when discussing fluids in general."}, {"found_name": "agua azerada", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1289, "target_cluster_name": "agua azerada", "source_book": "llm_generate