is binturong) (; bin-TURE-ong, BIN-ture-ong), also known as the bearcat, is a viverrid native to South and Southeast Asia. It is uncommon in much of its range, and has been assessed as Vulnerable on the IUCN Red List because of a declining population. It is estimated to have declined at least 30% since the mid-1980s. The binturong is the only species in the genus Arctictis. The name \"binturong\" is related to the words benturong and tenturun used in Riau. In the Western Malayo-Polynesian languages spoken in Borneo, the name is related to the root ma-tuRun."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Russia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 146, "target_cluster_name": "Russia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A large part of Russia's territory lies within the Arctic region, including its extensive northern coastline and islands.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A large part of Russia's territory lies within the Arctic region, including its extensive northern coastline and islands.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "rat", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3344, "target_cluster_name": "rat", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Norway has significant Arctic territories and coastlines.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Norway has significant Arctic territories and coastlines.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Polar Circle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 469, "target_cluster_name": "Polar Circle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Arctic Circle is a geographical line of latitude located within the broader Arctic region.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Arctic Circle is a geographical line of latitude l