nd_relationship": "Distribution, in a biological context, is the result of dispersal and subsequent establishment of organisms in new areas."}, {"found_name": "Evaporation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2390, "target_cluster_name": "évaporation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Evaporation is a physical process that can lead to the dispersal of substances, such as water vapor or volatile compounds, into the atmosphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Evaporation is a physical process that can lead to the dispersal of substances, such as water vapor or volatile compounds, into the atmosphere."}, {"found_name": "change", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1334, "target_cluster_name": "change", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dispersal is a type of change involving spreading out or scattering.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Dispersal is a type of change involving spreading out or scattering.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "chemical_composition", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["chemical composition"], "contexts": ["makeup of substances"]}, {"entity_id": "chemical_constitution", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "chemical constitution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["chemical constitution"], "contexts": ["composition of a substance"]}, {"entity_id": "chemical_composition", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["chemical composition"], "contexts": ["molecules of substances"]}, {"entity_id": "chemical_composition", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "chemical composition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["chemical composition"], "contexts": ["influenced by heat", "produces electricity in galvanic battery"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "chemical constitution", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "chemical constitution", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "chemical constitution", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "chemical composition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemical composition", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 449, "stable_key": "clu_cb4cc79db5884490", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Chemical composition", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Both 'chemical composition' and 'chemical constitution' refer to the same fundamental scientific concept.", "wikidata_id": "Q1263816", "wikidata_description": "concept in chemistry that has different, but similar, meanings if referred to a single pure substance or a mixture", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chemical%20composition", "wikipedia_extract": "A chemical composition specifies the identity, arrangement, and ratio of the chemical elements making up a compound by way of chemical and atomic bonds. Chemical formulas can be used to describe the relative amounts of elements present in a compound. For example, the chemical formula for water is H2O: this means that each molecule of water is constituted by 2 atoms of hydrogen (H) and 1 atom of oxygen (O). The chemical composition of water may be interpreted as a 2:1 ratio of hydrogen atoms to oxygen atoms. Different types of chemical formulas are used to convey composition information, such as an empirical or molecular formula. Nomenclature can be used to express not only the elements present in a compound but their arrangement within the molecules of the compound."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Chemistry", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 304, "target_cluster_name": "Chemistry", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chemistry is the scientific discipline that studies chemical composition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Chemistry is the scientific discipline that studies chemical composition.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Chemical analysis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2604, "target_cluster_name": "chemical analysis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chemical analysis is the process of identifying the chemical composition of a substance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chemical analysis is the process of identifying the chemical composition of a substance."}, {"found_name": "Chemical change", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 989, "target_cluster_name": "chemical change", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chemical change alters the chemical composition of a substance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chemical change alters the chemical composition of a substance."}, {"found_name": "Chemical properties", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1251, "target_cluster_name": "chemical properties", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chemical properties are determined by the chemical composition of a substance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chemical properties are determined by the chemical composition of a substance."}, {"found_name": "Chemical reactions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1769, "target_cluster_name": "chemical action", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chemical reactions involve changes in the chemical composition of substances.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chemical reactions involve changes in the chemical composition of substances."}, {"found_name": "Atom", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1411, "target_cluster_name": "Atoms", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Atoms are the fundamental building blocks that determine chemical composition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Atoms are the fundamental building blocks that determine chemical composition."}, {"found_name": "Atomic structure", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3764, "target_cluster_name": "Atomic constitution", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Atomic structure directly influences and defines the chemical composition of elements and compounds.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Atomic structure directly influences and defines the chemical composition of elements and compounds."}, {"found_name": "Atomic theory", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3552, "target_cluster_name": "atomistic philosophy", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Atomic theory provides the framework for understanding how atoms combine to form chemical compositions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Atomic theory provides the framework for understanding how atoms combine to form chemical compositions."}, {"found_name": "propriedades", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 508, "target_cluster_name": "propriedades", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Water's chemical composition (H2O) is central to its properties.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Water's chemical composition (H2O) is central to its properties.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "chimie végétale", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1358, "target_cluster_name": "chimie végétale", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Organic chemistry studies the composition of organic compounds.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Organic chemistry studies the composition of organic compounds.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Clerigo", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "clergé", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "clergé", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 2, "variants": ["clergé"], "contexts": ["religious officials", "religious personnel in Cuba"]}, {"entity_id": "clergyman", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "clergyman", "category": "PERSON", "s