R", "count": 2, "variants": ["Drake"], "contexts": ["explorer", "author"]}, {"entity_id": "drake", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Drake", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Drake"], "contexts": ["author cited in footnote", "reported earth shaking"]}, {"entity_id": "drake", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Drake", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Drake"], "contexts": ["navigator who brought plant"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 0.781}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 0.781}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Drake", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Drake", "similarity": 0.781}], "id": 461, "stable_key": "clu_91748bd920dfd987", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Sir Francis Drake", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1540, "death_year": 1596, "description": "English explorer, sea captain, and privateer who circumnavigated the globe.", "note": "While 'Drake' could refer to other individuals, the context of voyages and exploration strongly points to Sir Francis Drake. The text 'pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646' is known to discuss historical figures.", "wikidata_id": "Q36517", "wikidata_description": "English sailor and privateer (c. 1540 – 1596)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis%20Drake", "wikipedia_extract": "Sir Francis Drake (c. 1540 – 28 January 1596) was an English explorer and privateer best known for making the second circumnavigation of the world in a single expedition between 1577 and 1580 (being the first English expedition to accomplish this). He is also known for participating in the early English slaving voyages of his cousin,  John Hawkins, and John Lovell. Having started as a simple seaman, in 1588 he was part of the fight against the Spanish Armada as a vice admiral. At an early age, Drake was placed into the household of a relative, William Hawkins, a prominent sea captain in Plymouth. In 1572, he set sail on his first independent mission, privateering along the Spanish Main. Drake's circumnavigation began on 15 December 1577."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Christopher Columbus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 327, "target_cluster_name": "Columbus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent English and Spanish explorers, respectively, during the Age of Discovery, undertaking significant voyages that expanded European knowledge of the world.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent English and Spanish explorers, respectively, during the Age of Discovery, undertaking significant voyages that expanded European knowledge of the world."}, {"found_name": "Amerigo Vespucci", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3017, "target_cluster_name": "Amerigo Vespucci", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were key figures in the Age of Discovery, undertaking voyages that expanded European geographical knowledge and contributed to the mapping of the Americas and the circumnavigation of the globe.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were key figures in the Age of Discovery, undertaking voyages that expanded European geographical knowledge and contributed to the mapping of the Americas and the circumnavigation of the globe."}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were renowned explorers and naturalists who significantly contributed to the understanding of geography and natural sciences through their extensive voyages and detailed observations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were renowned explorers and naturalists who significantly contributed to the understanding of geography and natural sciences through their extensive voyages and detailed observations."}, {"found_name": "Francis Bacon", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 185, "target_cluster_name": "Bacon", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential figures in English intellectual history, with Drake being a prominent explorer and Bacon a philosopher and scientist who advocated for empirical methods, reflecting the spirit of the age of exploration and scientific inquiry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were influential figures in English intellectual history, with Drake being a prominent explorer and Bacon a philosopher and scientist who advocated for empirical methods, reflecting the spirit of the age of exploration and scientific inquiry."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Italians", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "italians", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Italians", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OT