smos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Hercules", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Hercules", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 495, "stable_key": "clu_df3fbe4af0f1af7c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Hercules", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Mythological hero known for his strength and labors", "wikidata_id": "Q948140", "wikidata_description": "city in western Contra Costa County, California, United States", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hercules%2C%20California", "wikipedia_extract": "Hercules is a city in western Contra Costa County, California. Situated along the coast of San Pablo Bay, it is located in the eastern region of the San Francisco Bay Area, about 10 miles (16 km) north of Berkeley. As of the 2020 census, its population was 26,016, according to the United States Census Bureau. The site of Hercules was first developed in 1881 as a manufacturing facility of the California Powder Works for the production of its patented dynamite formulation, Hercules powder. In 1882, the Hercules Powder Company was incorporated and assumed responsibility for the Hercules site. It was one of several explosive manufacturers that were active along the Pinole shoreline in the late 19th to the mid-20th century."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Achilles", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3249, "target_cluster_name": "Achilles", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are prominent figures from Greek mythology, known for their strength and heroic deeds.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are prominent figures from Greek mythology, known for their strength and heroic deeds."}, {"found_name": "Apollo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 841, "target_cluster_name": "Apollo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are figures from Greek mythology. Apollo is a god, while Hercules is a demigod/hero, but both are central figures in ancient Greek narratives.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are figures from Greek mythology. Apollo is a god, while Hercules is a demigod/hero, but both are central figures in ancient Greek narratives."}, {"found_name": "Bacchus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3303, "target_cluster_name": "Bacchus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are figures from Roman mythology. Bacchus is a god, while Hercules is a demigod/hero, but both are prominent figures in ancient Roman narratives.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are figures from Roman mythology. Bacchus is a god, while Hercules is a demigod/hero, but both are prominent figures in ancient Roman narratives."}, {"found_name": "Chiron", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3950, "target_cluster_name": "Chyron", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chiron was a centaur and a famous teacher of heroes in Greek mythology, including Achilles. Hercules, as a hero, would have been part of the same mythological tradition and potentially interacted with or been taught by figures like Chiron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chiron was a centaur and a famous teacher of heroes in Greek mythology, including Achilles. Hercules, as a hero, would have been part of the same mythological tradition and potentially interacted with or been taught by figures like Chiron."}, {"found_name": "Cyrus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3886, "target_cluster_name": "Cyrus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are historical/legendary figures known for their military prowess and leadership, often depicted as conquerors or founders of empires in ancient times.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are historical/legendary figures known for their military prowess and leadership, often depicted as conquerors or founders of empires in ancient times."}, {"found_name": "Dioscorides", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 33, "target_cluster_name": "Dioscorides", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dioscorides was a Greek physician and botanist whose work on materia medica was influential. Hercules, as a figure of myth and legend, is often associated with feats of strength and overcoming challenges, which could indirectly relate to the pursuit of health and well-being that physicians like Dioscorides addressed.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dioscorides was a Greek physician and botanist whose work on materia medica was influential. Hercules, as a figure of myth and legend, is often associated with feats of strength and overcoming challenges, which could indirectly relate to the pursuit of health and well-being that physicians like Dioscorides addressed."}, {"found_name": "Empedocles", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2664, "target_cluster_name": "Empedocles", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are figures from ancient Greece. Empedocles was a philosopher and poet, while Hercules is a mythological hero. They represent different facets of ancient Greek thought and culture.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are figures from ancient Greece. Empedocles was a philosopher and poet, while Hercules is a mythological hero. They represent different facets of ancient Greek thought and culture."}, {"found_name": "Eratosthenes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1129, "target_cluster_name": "Eratosthenes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "