"link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2654, "target_cluster_name": "straight line", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A straight line inherently possesses direction, representing the path along which something moves or is oriented.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A straight line inherently possesses direction, representing the path along which something moves or is oriented.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Bruxelles", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "bruxelles", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Bruxelles", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Bruxelles"], "contexts": ["abandoned city", "city near the Gulf of Nicoya"]}, {"entity_id": "brussels", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Brussels", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Brussels"], "contexts": ["location of research publication"]}, {"entity_id": "bruxelles", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Bruxelles", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Bruxelles"], "contexts": ["location of Duprez's publication"]}, {"entity_id": "brussels", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Brussels", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Brussels"], "contexts": ["location of Plateau's experiments"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bruxelles", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Brussels", "similarity": 0.95}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bruxelles", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Bruxelles", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bruxelles", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Brussels", "similarity": 0.95}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Brussels", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Bruxelles", "similarity": 0.95}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Brussels", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Brussels", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Bruxelles", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Brussels", "similarity": 0.95}], "id": 504, "stable_key": "clu_c55abfd8c9e7cb27", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Brussels, officially the Brussels-Capital Region, is a region of Belgium comprising 19 municipalities, including the City of Brussels, which is the capital of Belgium. The Brussels-Capital Region is located in the central portion of the country. It is a part of both the French Community of Belgium and the Flemish Community, and is separate from the Flemish Region (Flanders), within which it forms an enclave, and the Walloon Region (Wallonia), located less than 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) to the south. Brussels grew from a small rural settlement on the river Senne to become an important city-region in Europe. Since the end of the Second World War, it has been a major centre for international politics and home to numerous international organisations, politicians, diplomats and civil servants. Brussels is the de facto capital of the European Union, as it hosts a number of principal EU institutions, including its administrative-legislative, executive-political, and legislative branches (though the judicial branch is located in Luxembourg, and the European Parliament meets for a minority of the year in Strasbourg)."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "discoveries", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["discoveries"], "contexts": ["new findings or inventions", "new findings or insights"]}, {"entity_id": "discoveries", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["discoveries"], "contexts": ["results of past and present inquiry"]}, {"entity_id": "discovery", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "discovery", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["discovery"], "contexts": ["act of finding something new"]}, {"entity_id": "scientific_discoveries", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "scientific discoveries", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["scientific discoveries"], "contexts": ["new findings in science"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "discoveries", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "discovery", "similarity": 0.937}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "scientific discoveries", "similarity": 0.942}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "discovery", "similarity": 0.937}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "discoveries", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "scientific discoveries", "s