", "name": "human nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["human nature"], "contexts": ["abstract idea of man"]}, {"entity_id": "human_nature", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "human nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["human nature"], "contexts": ["essential qualities of humanity"]}, {"entity_id": "human_nature", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Human Nature", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Human Nature"], "contexts": ["fundamental characteristics of humans"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Human Nature", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "human nature", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Human Nature", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "human nature", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Human Nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Human Nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "human nature", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "human nature", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "human nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Human Nature", "similarity": 0.949}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "human nature", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Human Nature", "similarity": 0.949}], "id": 513, "stable_key": "clu_1c01ff3f4eee7101", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Human nature", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q5937288", "wikidata_description": "scientific journal", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_nature", "wikipedia_extract": "Human nature comprises the fundamental dispositions and characteristics—including ways of thinking, feeling, and acting—that humans are said to have naturally. The term is often used to denote the essence of humankind; however, this usage has proven to be controversial in that there is dispute as to whether or not such an essence actually exists. Arguments about human nature have been a central focus of philosophy for centuries and the concept continues to provoke lively philosophical debate. While both concepts are distinct from one another, discussions regarding human nature are typically related to those regarding the comparative importance of genes and environment in human development (i.e., nature versus nurture). Accordingly, the concept also continues to play a role in academic fields, such as both the natural and the social sciences, and philosophy, in which various theorists claim to have yielded insight into human nature. Human nature is traditionally contrasted with human attributes that vary among societies, such as those associated with specific cultures."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "characters", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 995, "target_cluster_name": "characters", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Human nature is often understood as the fundamental qualities and characteristics, or traits, that are inherent to humans.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Human nature is often understood as the fundamental qualities and characteristics, or traits, that are inherent to humans.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Emotion and Will", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3531, "target_cluster_name": "Emotion and Will", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Emotion and Will are fundamental aspects of human disposition and behavior, which are central to the concept of human nature.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Emotion and Will are fundamental aspects of human disposition and behavior, which are central to the concept of human nature."}, {"found_name": "Character", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 962, "target_cluster_name": "character", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Character is a direct manifestation of human nature, representing the distinctive qualities and traits of an individual or group.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Character is a direct manifestation of human nature, representing the distinctive qualities and traits of an individual or group."}, {"found_name": "Belief", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2125, "target_cluster_name": "belief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Belief systems are a significant component of human disposition and understanding, thus closely related to the concept of human nature.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Belief systems are a significant component of human disposition and understanding, thus closely related to the concept of human nature."}, {"found_name": "Ambition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4281, "target_cluster_name": "Ambition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ambition is a specific disposition and drive that is often discussed as a key aspect of human nature.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ambition is a specific disposition and drive that is often discussed as a key aspect of human nature."}, {"found_name": "Affection", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3559, "target_cluster_name": "affection", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_s