ans were highly influential in the development of pharmacy and materia medica, and their knowledge was transmitted to European apothecaries.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arab physicians were highly influential in the development of pharmacy and materia medica, and their knowledge was transmitted to European apothecaries.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Rhafis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 638, "target_cluster_name": "Rhafis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Rhazes was a prominent Persian physician during the Islamic Golden Age, a period characterized by significant contributions from Arab physicians.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Rhazes was a prominent Persian physician during the Islamic Golden Age, a period characterized by significant contributions from Arab physicians.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Mouros", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1557, "target_cluster_name": "Mouros", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Similar to 'Arab', 'Arab physicians' refers to a group strongly associated with the historical Moorish presence and influence in Iberia and the wider Mediterranean world, particularly in the context of scientific and medical knowledge transmission.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Similar to 'Arab', 'Arab physicians' refers to a group strongly associated with the historical Moorish presence and influence in Iberia and the wider Mediterranean world, particularly in the context of scientific and medical knowledge transmission.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Amatus Lusitanus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1620, "target_cluster_name": "Amatus Lusitanus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snipp