"polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Boticarios", "similarity": 0.966}], "id": 587, "stable_key": "clu_6623639ce4f7faa5", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Apothecary", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Prepares and dispenses medicinal drugs.", "wikidata_id": "Q1131236", "wikidata_description": "historical name for a medical professional now called a pharmacist", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apothecary", "wikipedia_extract": "Apothecary () is an archaic English term for a medical professional who formulates and dispenses materia medicacode: lat promoted to code: la  ('medicine') to physicians, surgeons and patients. The modern terms pharmacist and, in British English, chemist have taken over this role. In some languages and regions, terms similar to \"apothecary\" have survived and denote modern pharmacies or pharmacists. Apothecaries' investigation of herbal and chemical ingredients was a precursor to the modern sciences of chemistry and pharmacology. In addition to dispensing herbs and medicine, apothecaries offered general medical advice and a range of services that are now performed by other specialist practitioners, such as surgeons and obstetricians. Apothecary shops sold ingredients and the medicines they prepared wholesale to other medical practitioners, as well as dispensing them to patients."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Litargirio", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 775, "target_cluster_name": "Lithargyro", "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "primeyro lugar ,entre os remedios exteriores , àmanteyga de chumbo , cuja preparação quero enfinar em fer viçodobemcommum. Tomemde fezesdeouro, aqueos Boticarios chamão Litargirio , moidas fubtiliſſim", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "Alchemists", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluste