nd the Pacific Ocean. According to the 2024 census, Chile had an enumerated population of 18.5 million. The country covers a territorial area of 756,102 square kilometers (291,933 sq mi), sharing borders with Peru to the north, Bolivia to the northeast, Argentina to the east, and the Drake Passage to the south. It also administers several Pacific islands, including Juan Fernández, Isla Salas y Gómez, Desventuradas, and Easter Island, and claims about 1,250,000 square kilometers (480,000 sq mi) of Antarctica as the Chilean Antarctic Territory. The capital and largest city is Santiago, and the national language is Spanish."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Andes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 207, "target_cluster_name": "Andes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chile is a country located along the western edge of the Andes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Chile is a country located along the western edge of the Andes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Arica", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2384, "target_cluster_name": "Arica", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arica is a major port city in northern Chile.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arica is a major port city in northern Chile."}, {"found_name": "Chiloé Island", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4048, "target_cluster_name": "Chiloè", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Chiloé Island is located off the coast of southern Chile.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Chiloé Island is located off the coast of southern Chile."}, {"found_name": "Chimborazo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 708, "target_cluster_name": "Chimboraz