unctionally closely related to the kidneys, as it stores urine produced by the kidneys before excretion."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Chymicos", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 43, "members": [{"entity_id": "chemist", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "chemist", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["chemist"], "contexts": ["practitioner of chemistry"]}, {"entity_id": "chymicos", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Chymicos", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 37, "variants": ["Chymicos"], "contexts": ["Relating to alchemy or chemistry", "alchemical"]}, {"entity_id": "chemist", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "chemist", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 5, "variants": ["Chemist", "chemist"], "contexts": ["scientist studying chemistry", "practitioner of chemistry"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "chemist", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Chymicos", "similarity": 0.894}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "chemist", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "chemist", "similarity": 0.918}], "id": 609, "stable_key": "clu_ac7f00fa4f39d63a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Chemist", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "A practitioner of alchemy or chemistry.", "note": "Refers to practitioners of early chemistry or alchemy.", "wikipedia_extract": "A chemist (from Greek chēm(ía) alchemy; replacing chymist from Medieval Latin alchemist) is a graduated scientist trained in the study of chemistry, or an officially enrolled student in the field. Chemists study the composition of matter and its properties. Chemists carefully describe the properties they study in terms of quantities, with detail on the level of molecules and their component atoms. Chemists carefully measure substance proportions, chemical reaction rates, and other chemical properties. In Commonwealth English, pharmacists are often called chemists. Chemists use their knowledge to learn the composition and properties of unfamiliar substances, as well as to reproduce and synthesize large quantities of useful naturally occurring substances and create new artificial substances and useful processes."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Lavoisier", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 475, "target_cluster_name": "Lavoisier", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lavoisier is a central figure in the history of chemistry, often referred to as the 'father of modern chemistry'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lavoisier is a central figure in the history of chemistry, often referred to as the 'father of modern chemistry'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Boticarios", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 587, "target_cluster_name": "Boticarios", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The term 'chemist' is a modern successor to 'apothecary', particularly in British English, and refers to a professional involved in the formulation and dispensing of medicines.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The term 'chemist' is a modern successor to 'apothecary', particularly in British English, and refers to a professional involved in the formulation and dispensing of medicines.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Chemists", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1124, "target_cluster_name": "chemists", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Plural form of the same profession.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Plural form of the same profession."}, {"f