 any two genera of the same family. Thus in Eciton, t", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "contested_identity", "found_relationship": "example of genera with distinct neuters"}]}, {"canonical_name": "banho", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 40, "members": [{"entity_id": "bath", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "bath", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 3, "variants": ["bath", "Bath", "Bathing"], "contexts": ["outward application of St. Johns-wort", "method of treating skin conditions"]}, {"entity_id": "banhos", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "banhos", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["banhos"], "contexts": ["used to treat beribéri"]}, {"entity_id": "banho", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "banho", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 24, "variants": ["banho", "banho de agua", "banho de agua morna", "banho de aguadoce", "banhode agua fervente", "banhos de agua doce", "banhos de agua fria", "banhos de agua morna", "banhos de agua tibia", "banhos de aguadoce", "banhos de aguamuyto quente", "banhos de leite", "banhos deagua doce"], "contexts": ["therapeutic bath with herbs", "therapeutic bath"]}, {"entity_id": "banhos", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "banhos", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["banhos", "banhos de agua"], "contexts": ["baths", "therapeutic practice"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "bath", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "banho", "similarity": 0.912}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "banhos", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "banho", "similarity": 0.941}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "banhos", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "banhos", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 612, "stable_key": "clu_3c945bb1444f2448", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Baths", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Therapeutic practice involving immersion in water or herbal preparations.", "wikipedia_extract": "Balneotherapy (Latin: balneum \"bath\") is a pseudoscientific method of treating diseases by bathing, a traditional medicine technique usually practiced at spas. Since ancient times, humans have used hot springs, public baths and thermal medicine for therapeutic effects. While it is considered distinct from hydrotherapy, there are some overlaps in practice and in underlying principles. Balneotherapy may involve hot or cold water, massage through moving water, relaxation, or stimulation. Many mineral waters at spas are rich in particular minerals such as silica, sulfur, selenium, and radium. Medicinal clays are also widely used, a practice known as 'fangotherapy'. \"Balneotherapy\" is the practice of immersing a subject in mineral water or mineral-laden mud; it is part of the traditional medicine of many cultures and originated in hot springs, cold water springs, or other sources of such water, like the Dead Sea."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "balneis", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2167, "target_cluster_name": "balneis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for 'bath'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Portuguese for 'bath'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "trintabichosde conta", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "trintabichosde conta , a que os: Medicos chamão Afelli, ou Millepedes, dados novinho branco ; mas quando : \" não ourine, meteremos ao doente no ſeguinte banho. Tomem de palhas alhas , dealfavacade cob", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "