ons that affect organisms and environments.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "farinha de cevada", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 40, "members": [{"entity_id": "farine_des_céréales", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "farine des céréales", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["farine des céréales"], "contexts": ["food item"]}, {"entity_id": "farinha_de_trigo", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "farinha de trigo", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["farinha de trigo", "farinha de triguo"], "contexts": ["wheat flour", "ingredient in falcon plaster"]}, {"entity_id": "farinha_de_cevada", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "farinha de cevada", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 36, "variants": ["farinha de cevada", "fari-nha de trigo", "farinha", "farinha Tremès", "farinha de centeyo", "farinha de favas", "farinha de tremoços", "farinha de trigo", "farinha dearroz", "farinha decevada", "farinhade cevada", "farinhade pao", "farinhade tremoços", "farinhade trigo"], "contexts": ["barley flour, a thickening agent", "barley flour"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "farine des céréales", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "farinha de trigo", "similarity": 0.921}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "farine des céréales", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "farinha de cevada", "similarity": 0.919}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "farinha de trigo", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "farinha de cevada", "similarity": 0.939}], "id": 614, "stable_key": "clu_265ad3a887a0a413", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Barley flour", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "description": "Flour made from ground barley grains.", "note": "Includes 'farinha de trigo' (wheat flour) as a related ingredient.", "wikipedia_extract": "Barley flour is a flour prepared from dried and ground barley. Barley flour is used to prepare barley bread and other breads, such as flat bread and yeast breads. There are two general types of barley flour: coarse and fine. Barley groats are milled to make coarse barley flour, and pearl barley is milled to make fine barley flour. Additionally, patent barley flour is a finer barley flour that is ground to a greater degree compared to fine barley flour. Barley flour is used to prepare breads such as barley bread."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Farelos", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 287, "target_cluster_name": "Farelos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Bran is a component of barley, and barley flour is derived from barley.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Bran is a component of barley, and barley flour is derived from barley.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Cevada", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1570, "target_cluster_name": "Cevada", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Barley flour is derived from barley.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Barley flour is derived from barley.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "riz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2191, "target_cluster_name": "riz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both rice and barley are grains, and their flours are used as food staples, often appearing in discussions of food preparation and nutrition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both rice and barley are grains, and their flours are used as food staples, often appearing in discussions of food preparation and nutrition.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "trigo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1828, "target_cluster_name": "trigo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Barley flour is a direct derivative of Barley, a closely related cereal grain to Wheat. Historical texts often discuss these grains and their flours in conjunction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Barley flour is a direct derivative of Barley, a closely related cereal grain to Wheat. Historical texts often discuss these grains and their flours in conjunction.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "alimentos", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 40, "members": [{"entity_id": "alimentos", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "alimentos", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 29, "variants": ["alimentos", "alimento exterior", "alimento interior", "alimentos acres", "alimentos liquidos", "alimentos mordazes", "alimentos muyto aduba", "alimentos muyto adubados", "alimentos muyto humidos", "alimentos máos", "alimentos solidos", "alimentos ſeccos", "alimentum"], "contexts": ["food", "nourishment"]}, {"entity_id": "food", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "food", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["food"], "contexts": ["substance providing nourishment"]}, {"entity_id": "food", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "food", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 10, "variants": ["Food", "food"], "contexts": ["substance providing nourishment", "distinguished by mechanical and chemical actions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "alimentos", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "food", "similarity": 0.976}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "alimentos", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "food", "similarity": 0.976}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "food", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "food", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 615, "stable_key": "clu_267533c63e8dbd62", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "food", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Substances providing nourishment and sustenance.", "wikipedia_extract": "Food is any substance consumed by an organism for nutritional support. Food usually consists of plant, animal, or fungal origin and contains essential nutrients such as carbohydrates, fats, proteins, vitamins, or minerals. The substance is ingested by an organism and assimilated by the organism's cells to provide energy, maintain life, or support growth. Different species of animals have different feeding behaviours that satisfy the needs of their metabolisms and have evolved to fill specific ecological niches within specific geographical contexts. Omnivorous humans are highly adaptable and have adapted to obtaining food in many different ecosystems. Humans generally use cooking to prepare food for consumption."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "bucho", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3698, "target_cluster_name": "bucho", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The stomach's primary function is to receive and digest food.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The stomach's primary function is to receive and digest food.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "boca", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 649, "target_cluster_name": "boca", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Food is taken into the body through the mouth.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Food is taken into the body through the mouth.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Grana", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1036, "target_cluster_name": "Grana", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Grain is a primary type of food for humans and animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Grain is a primary type of food for humans and animals.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "caldo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1505, "target_cluster_name": "caldo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Broth is a type of food.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Broth is a type of food.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "epithimo", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 38, "members": [{"entity_id": "epithimum", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Epithimum", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Epithimum"], "contexts": ["true dodder of time", "herb praised by physicians"]}, {"entity_id": "epithymo", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Epithymo", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 10, "variants": ["Epithymo", "EPITHYMO", "Epahymo", "Epithymio", "Epithynio", "Epitnymo"], "contexts": ["herb mentioned", "plant similar to Cuscuta"]}, {"entity_id": "epitimo", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "epitimo", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 9, "variants": ["epitimo", "Epichymo", "Epirnymo", "Epitbymo", "Epithimo", "Epithymoi", "Epitymo", "epithym-"], "contexts": ["herb used in purgatives", "herb"]}, {"entity_id": "epithimo", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "epithimo", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory":