t or aspect of the broader concept of 'Will'."}, {"found_name": "Free will", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3567, "target_cluster_name": "free-will", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This is a direct synonym or a very closely related concept, often used interchangeably with willpower in philosophical and psychological discussions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "This is a direct synonym or a very closely related concept, often used interchangeably with willpower in philosophical and psychological discussions."}]}, {"canonical_name": "feelings", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 64, "members": [{"entity_id": "feelings", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "feelings", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 27, "variants": ["feelings", "Feelings"], "contexts": ["mental phenomena", "emotional states"]}, {"entity_id": "feelings", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "feelings", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["feelings"], "contexts": ["emotional states", "influenced by sky clarity"]}, {"entity_id": "feelings", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "feelings", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 8, "variants": ["feelings"], "contexts": ["emotional responses", "emotional states"]}, {"entity_id": "emotions", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "emotions", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 7, "variants": ["emotions"], "contexts": ["engendered by association of ideas", "native tendencies to reaction"]}, {"entity_id": "emotions", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "emotions", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["emotions"], "contexts": ["strong feelings"]}, {"entity_id": "emotion", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "emotion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 8, "variants": ["emotion"], "contexts": ["strong feeling", "subjective experience of feeling"]}, {"entity_id": "emotion", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "emotion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["emotion"], "contexts": ["sea of feeling", "feeling or mood"]}, {"entity_id": "emotions", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "emotions", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["emotions"], "contexts": ["feelings and their expression", "feelings and sentiments"]}, {"entity_id": "emotional", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "emotional", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["emotional"], "contexts": ["relating to emotions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "feelings", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "feelings", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "feelings", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "feelings", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "feelings", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "feelings", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 618, "stable_key": "clu_fcb04e713fe5eb99", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "emotions", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q208166", "wikidata_description": "personality disorder characterized by variability of moods and unstable relationships", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Borderline%20personality%20disorder", "wikipedia_extract": "Borderline personality disorder (BPD) is a personality disorder characterized by a pervasive, long-term pattern of significant interpersonal relationship instability, acute fear of abandonment, and intense emotional outbursts. People with BPD frequently exhibit self-harming behaviours and engage in risky activities, primarily caused by difficulties in regulating emotions. Symptoms such as dissociation, a pervasive sense of emptiness, and distorted sense of self are prevalent. Onset of symptoms can be triggered by events others perceive as normal, with the disorder typically manifesting in early adulthood and persisting across diverse contexts. BPD is often comorbid with substance use disorders, depressive disorders, and eating disorders. Studies estimate up to 10 percent of people with BPD die by suicide."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Feeling", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 245, "target_cluster_name": "feeling", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The entity description explicitly states 'historical name: feelings', indicating 'feeling' is an older or alternative term for 'emotions'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "The entity description explicitly states 'historical name: feelings', indicating 'feeling' is an older or alternative term for 'emotions'."}, {"found_name": "Affection", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3559, "target_cluster_name": "affection", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Affection is a specific type of emotion, often characterized by warmth and fondness, and thus closely related to the broader concept of emotions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Affection is a specific type of emotion, often characterized by warmth and fondness, and thus closely related to the broader concept of emotions."}, {"found_name": "Anger", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1206, "target_cluster_name": "anger", "source_book": "llm_generate