"confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Elettaria cardamomum", "family": "Zingiberaceae", "note": "The term 'cardamomo menor' likely refers to a specific variety or preparation of cardamom, but the core referent is cardamom.", "wikidata_id": "Q33466", "wikidata_description": "species of plant", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elettaria%20cardamomum", "wikipedia_extract": "Elettaria cardamomum, commonly known as green cardamom or true cardamom, is a herbaceous, perennial plant in the ginger family, native to southern India. It is the most common of the species whose seeds are used as a spice called cardamom that has a strong aroma used in both savory and sweet cooking. It is cultivated widely in tropical regions and reportedly naturalized in Réunion, Indochina, and Costa Rica. Elettaria cardamomum is a pungent, aromatic, herbaceous, perennial plant, growing to about 2–4 m (6 ft 7 in – 13 ft 1 in) in height. The leaves are alternate in two ranks, linear-lanceolate, 40–60 cm (16–24 in) long, with a long pointed tip. The flowers are white to lilac or pale violet, produced in a loose spike 30–60 cm (12–24 in) long."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "calamo aromático", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 620, "target_cluster_name": "calamo aromático", "source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "evidence_snippet": "Crcfpino , cioè berberi volgare. U^alo armeno. Bolo armeno de irElbabiancOjgùlIo^ ó roffo, ò il roìlb che U porta d'Alcf- fandria . Calaxno odorato* Calamo aromatico delle Spczierie^d ibaccdictti mino", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: vernacular name", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Amomum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2029, "target_cluster_name": "Amomum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amomum is a genus in the same family (Zingiberaceae) 