"target_cluster_id": 399, "target_cluster_name": "Butter", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream, which is derived from milk. Milk is the fundamental source material.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Butter is a dairy product made from the fat and protein components of churned cream, which is derived from milk. Milk is the fundamental source material.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mantimento", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2477, "target_cluster_name": "mantimento", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Milk is a nutrient-rich liquid food produced by mammals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Milk is a nutrient-rich liquid food produced by mammals.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Curdled Milk", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3956, "target_cluster_name": "Curdled Milk", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Curdled Milk is a processed form of Milk.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Curdled Milk is a processed form of Milk."}, {"found_name": "Womens Breasts", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2032, "target_cluster_name": "Womens Breasts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historical texts often describe milk as a substance produced by the breasts, particularly in the context of lactation and nourishment.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Historical texts often describe milk as a substance produced by the breasts, particularly in the context of lactation and nourishment.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Nectar", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2368, "target_cluster_name": "Nectar", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both nectar and milk are nutrient-rich liquids produced by organisms, though from different sources and for different purposes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both nectar and milk are nutrient-rich liquids produced by organisms, though from different sources and for different purposes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Lacteas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2689, "target_cluster_name": "Lacteas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lacteals are vessels that absorb chyle (a milky fluid) from the intestines during digestion. Historically, the milky appearance of this fluid led to the naming of the lacteals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lacteals are vessels that absorb chyle (a milky fluid) from the intestines during digestion. Historically, the milky appearance of this fluid led to the naming of the lacteals.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Rhafis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "rhazis", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Rhazis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Rhazis"], "contexts": ["medieval Persian physician"]}, {"entity_id": "rafis", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Rafis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Rafis"], "contexts": ["ancient authority who classified iron", "medical authority"]}, {"entity_id": "rhafis", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Rhafis", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 29, "variants": ["Rhafis", "Rhaf", "Rhas", "Rhas.", "Rhasis", "Rhazes", "Rhaſis"], "contexts": ["cited ancient/medieval authority", "ancient medical authority"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Rhazis", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Rhafis", "similarity": 0.862}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Rafis", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Rhafis", "similarity": 0.872}], "id": 638, "stable_key": "clu_b14d755e66d358d1", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Rhazes", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 865, "death_year": 925, "description": "Persian polymath, physician, and alchemist, influential in medieval medicine.", "note": "The variations 'Rhazis', 'Rafis', and 'Rhafis' all refer to the famous Persian physician.", "wikidata_id": "Q169234", "wikidata_description": "Persian polymath, physician, chemist and philosopher (854-925)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu%20Bakr%20al-Razi", "wikipedia_extract": "Abū Bakr al-Rāzī, also known as Rhazes (full name: أبو بکر محمد بن زکریاء الرازي, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Zakariyyāʾ al-Rāzī), 864 or 865 – 925 or 935 CE, was a Persian physician, philosopher and alchemist who lived during the Islamic Golden Age. He is widely regarded as one of the most important figures in the history of medicine, and also wrote on logic, astronomy and grammar. He is also known for his criticism of religion, especially with regard to the concepts of prophethood and revelation. However, the religio-philosophical aspects of his thought, which also included a belief in five \"eternal principles\", are fragmentary and only reported by authors who were often hostile to him. A comprehensive thinker, al-Razi made fundamental and enduring contributions to various fields, which he recorded in over 200 manuscripts, and is particularly remembered for numerous advances in medicine through his observations and discoveries. An early proponent of experimental medicine, he became a successful doctor, and served as chief physician of Baghdad and Ray hospitals."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "cap.", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 594, "target_cluster_name": "cap.", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "nomes que de- vem ser corrompidos, scilicet, os nomes dos autores ; folga- ria muyto me dixestes disto o que sabeis. • Serapio, 3 19; Avicena, Lib. 2, cap. 3 18 (nota do auctor). Do Cravo 367 ORTA Não", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "reverse: also called", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Turquia", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 272, "target_cluster_name": "Turquia", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "traductor, ou os tempos, que gastão tudo*, mas no arábio está cebar. RUANO Acerca dos indios he usado? ORTA Acerca dos fisicos da Pérsia, Arábia e Turquia se usa desta mezinha, porque sabem elles de c", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arabic name for Rasis", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Rasis", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1631, "target_cluster_name": "Rasis", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "da Pérsia, Arábia e Turquia se usa desta mezinha, porque sabem elles de cór Avicena, a que chamão elles Abolahi e a seus cinquo livros Canum, e sa- bem Rasis, a quem chamão Benzacaria, e a HaUrodoam e", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arabic name for Rasis", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Arab physicians", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 538, "target_cluster_name": "Arábios", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Rhazes was a prominent Persian physician during the Islamic Golden Age, a period characterized by significant contributions from Arab physicians.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Rhazes was a prominent Persian physician during the Islamic Golden Age, a period characterized by significant contributions from Arab physicians."}, {"found_name": "Avicenna", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1492, "target_cluster_name": "Avicena", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Avicenna was another highly influential Persian physician and philosopher who lived after Rhazes and was part of the same intellectual tradition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Avicenna was another highly influential Persian physician and philosopher who lived after Rhazes and was part of the same intellectual tradition."}, {"found_name": "Galen", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 29, "target_cluster_name": "Galen", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Galen was a foundational figure in Greco-Roman medicine, and Rhazes, like many physicians of his era, built upon and sometimes critiqued Galenic principles.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Galen was a foundational figure in Greco-Roman medicine, and Rhazes, like many physicians of his era, built upon and sometimes critiqued Galenic principles."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Vesuvius", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "vesuvius", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Vesuvius", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 23, "variants": ["Vesuvius"], "contexts": ["volcano height for comparison", "volcano used for distance comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "mount_vesuvius", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Mount Vesuvius", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 4, "variants": ["Mount Vesuvius"], "contexts": ["volcano with changing elevation", "volcano with eruption in 1822"]}, {"entity_id": "mon