ne of the four humors in humoral theory.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: This is the English term for 'bile', one of the four humors in humoral theory.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "baço", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1527, "target_cluster_name": "baço", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The spleen is closely associated with the production and circulation of bile in humoral theory.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The spleen is closely associated with the production and circulation of bile in humoral theory.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "lethargo", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 29, "members": [{"entity_id": "lithargia", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Lithargia", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["Lithargia"], "contexts": ["medical condition related to oblivion"]}, {"entity_id": "lethargy", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Lethargy", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 10, "variants": ["Lethargy", "Lethargie"], "contexts": ["condition treated with Brooklime mixture", "state of abnormal drowsiness"]}, {"entity_id": "lethargo", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "lethargo", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 18, "variants": ["lethargo", "Letargo", "Letargos", "Letharg.", "Lethargo", "Lethargos", "letargo", "lethargicos", "lethargum", "lethargy"], "contexts": ["a condition of excessive sleepiness", "a somnolent condition"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Lithargia", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Lethargy", "similarity": 0.888}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Lithargia", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "lethargo", "similarity": 0.884}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Lethargy", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "lethargo", "similarity": 0.976}], "id": 651, "stable_key": "clu_2d17ea8958d0dc02", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Lethargy", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A medical condition characterized by abnormal drowsiness or sleepiness.", "wikipedia_extract": "Lethargy is a state of tiredness, sleepiness, weariness, fatigue, sluggishness, or lack of energy. It can be accompanied by depression, decreased motivation, or apathy. Lethargy can be a normal response to inadequate sleep, overexertion, overworking, stress, lack of exercise, improper nutrition, drug abuse, boredom, or a symptom of an underlying illness or disorder. It may also be a side effect of medication or caused by an interaction between medications and alcohol. It may also be an altered level of consciousness. When part of a normal response, lethargy often resolves with rest, adequate sleep, decreased stress, physical exercise, and good nutrition."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "sleep", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1316, "target_cluster_name": "sleep", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced activity, which can be an abnormal manifestation or disruption of normal sleep patterns.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced activity, which can be an abnormal manifestation or disruption of normal sleep patterns.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "stupor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2697, "target_cluster_name": "stupor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced responsiveness, which can be a precursor or a milder form of stupor.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced responsiveness, which can be a precursor or a milder form of stupor.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Convulsions", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "convulsions", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Convulsions", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 23, "variants": ["Convulsions", "Convulsion", "convulsions"], "contexts": ["affect sinews", "condition helped by oil"]}, {"entity_id": "movimentos_convulfivos", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "movimentos convulfivos", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 5, "variants": ["movimentos convulfivos", "movimentos convulsivos"], "contexts": ["convulsive movements", "symptom of spasms"]}, {"entity_id": "convulsions", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "convulsions", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["convulsions"], "contexts": ["involuntary muscle contractions"]}, {"entity_id": "fits", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Fits", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Fits"], "contexts": ["episodes of illness", "of agues, altered by remedy"]}, {"entity_id": "fits", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "fits", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["fits"], "contexts": ["sudden episodes of symptoms"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Convulsions", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "movimentos convulfivos", "similarity": 0.904}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Convulsions", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "convulsions", "similarity": 0.935}], "id": 652, "stable_key": "clu_a364860f38e5cb18", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Convulsions", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "Convulsions", "wikidata_id": "Q6279182", "wikidata_description": "disease, disturbance of cortical function due to a sudden, abnormal, exin cells.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seizure", "note": "In early modern medical texts, 'fits' was a common term for sudden episodes of illness, often referring to seizures.", "wikipedia_extract": "A seizure is a sudden disruption of brain activity caused by excessive, synchronized neuronal firing that results in changes in behavior. This neurological condition is common, affecting approximately 50 million individuals around the world. Depending on the regions of the brain involved, seizures can lead to changes in movement, sensation, behavior, awareness, or consciousness. Symptoms vary widely. Some seizures involve subtle changes, such as brief lapses in attention or awareness (as seen in absence seizures), while others cause generalized convulsions with loss of consciousness (tonic–clonic seizures). Most seizures last less than two minutes and are followed by a postictal period of confusion, fatigue, or other symptoms."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Stupor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2697, "target_cluster_name": "stupor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Stupor can be a post-ictal state following a convulsion or seizure, indicating a close temporal and physiological relationship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Stupor can be a post-ictal state following a convulsion or seizure, indicating a close temporal and physiological relationship."}, {"found_name": "Unconsciousness", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1942, "target_cluster_name": "unconsciousness", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Unconsciousness is a common feature or consequence of many types of seizures and convulsions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Unconsciousness is a common feature or consequence of many types of seizures and convulsions."}, {"found_name": "tremor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1480, "target_cluster_name": "tremor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tremors are often associated with or a type of convulsive movement.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Tremors are often associated with or a type of convulsive movement.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Cramps", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1602, "target_cluster_name": "Cramps", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cramps are a type of involuntary muscle contraction, which can be closely related to or a symptom of convulsions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cramps are a type of involuntary muscle contraction, which can be closely related to or a symptom of convulsions.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "palsy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2359, "target_cluster_name": "palsy", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Convulsions can be a symptom or a related neurological event that may co-occur with or be caused by conditions leading to paralysis.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Convulsions can be a symptom or a related neurological event that may co-occur with or be caused by conditions leading to paralysis.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "incenso", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 51, "members": [{"entity_id": 