n Portuguese and Italian texts typically refers to frankincense, derived from Boswellia species.", "wikidata_id": "Q133964", "wikidata_description": "species of plant", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boswellia%20sacra", "wikipedia_extract": "Boswellia sacra, also known as Boswellia carteri and others, and commonly called the frankincense tree or the olibanum tree, is a tree in the genus Boswellia, in the Burseraceae family, from which frankincense, a resinous dried sap, is harvested. The olibanum tree is a plant native to the countries of Oman and Yemen, in the south of the Arabian Peninsula, and to Somalia and Ethiopia, in the Horn of Africa. In 2012, it was replanted in Israel in the Middle East, 1,500 years after dying out there. The Boswellia sacra species is a small deciduous tree that grows to a height of 2 to 8 m (6 ft 7 in to 26 ft 3 in), with one or more trunks. The bark has the texture of paper and can be easily removed. The tree has compound leaves and an odd number of leaflets that grow opposite to one another; the small, yellow-white flowers are gathered in axillary clusters composed of five petals, ten stamens, and a cup with five teeth; new leaves feature a downy covering."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Resin", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1481, "target_cluster_name": "resin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "'Resin' is the English term for the substance harvested from trees like Boswellia sacra, from which frankincense is derived. The provided entity description also mentions 'resinous dried sap'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "'Resin' is the English term for the substance harvested from trees like Boswellia sacra, from which frankincense is derived. The provided entity description also mentions 'resinous dried sap'."}, {"found_name": "Bdellio", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 947, "target_cluster_name": "Bdellio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Bdellium, myrrh, and frankincense are all aromatic resins historically used together in incense and perfumery, and sometimes grouped or confused in ancient texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Bdellium, myrrh, and frankincense are all aromatic resins historically used together in incense and perfumery, and sometimes grouped or confused in ancient texts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Myrrha", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 583, "target_cluster_name": "Myrrha", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Myrrh and Frankincense are both aromatic resins harvested from trees, often used together in ancient religious and medicinal practices.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Myrrh and Frankincense are both aromatic resins harvested from trees, often used together in ancient religious and medicinal practices.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Gomma", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2355, "target_cluster_name": "Gomma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Frankincense is a resin obtained from trees of the genus Boswellia, making it a specific type of plant gum/resin.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Frankincense is a resin obtained from trees of the genus Boswellia, making it a specific type of plant gum/resin.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "estoraque", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2873, "target_cluster_name": "estoraque", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Storax is a natural fragrant resin, and 'Frankincense' is another type of fragrant resin often discussed in similar contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Storax is a natural fragrant resin, and 'Frankincense' is another type of fragrant resin often discussed in similar contexts.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Panno", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 6, "total_mentions": 35, "members": [{"entity_id": "pano", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "pano", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["pano"], "contexts": ["cloth"]}, {"entity_id": "panno", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "panno", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 5, "variants": ["panno", "pannello", "panno fino"], "contexts": ["cloth used for pressing", "cloth for straining"]}, {"entity_id": "panno", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Panno", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 23, "variants": ["Panno", "fios de panno", "panninho", "panno", "panno afpero", "panno de linho", "panno de linho ralo", "panno delinho novo", "pannobem tapado", "pannodelinhonovo", "pannos de láa", "tiras de panno de linhonovo"], "contexts": ["cloth used for application", "cloth for straining"]}, {"entity_id": "cloathes", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Cloathes", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cloathes"], "contexts": ["items wetted with distilled water"]}, {"entity_id": "wardrobe", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Wardrobe", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Wardrobe"], "contexts": ["place with many fine clothes"]}, {"entity_id": "clothes", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "clothes", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 2, "variants": ["clothes"], "contexts": ["items worn on the body", "garments worn for covering and adornment"]}, {"entity_id": "garments", "book_id": "principles_of_ps