en the skin and the environment."}, "member_count": 8, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Handkerchief", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4292, "target_cluster_name": "handkerchief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A handkerchief is a specific type of clothing item.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A handkerchief is a specific type of clothing item."}, {"found_name": "Straw", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2565, "target_cluster_name": "palhas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Straw was historically used as a material for clothing and accessories like hats.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Straw was historically used as a material for clothing and accessories like hats."}, {"found_name": "beads", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4469, "target_cluster_name": "contas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Beads are often used as decorative elements or components of clothing and accessories.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Beads are often used as decorative elements or components of clothing and accessories."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 34, "members": [{"entity_id": "cape_of_good_hope", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Cape of Good Hope", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 12, "variants": ["Cape of Good Hope"], "contexts": ["location of correspondent", "location where John Herschel saw satellites"]}, {"entity_id": "cape_of_good_hope", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Cape of Good Hope", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 9, "variants": ["Cape of Good Hope"], "contexts": ["location for parallax observation", "southern tip of Africa"]}, {"entity_id": "cape_of_good_hope", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Cape of Good Hope", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 7, "variants": ["Cape of Good Hope"], "contexts": ["region with uncivilised man", "region with many plant species"]}, {"entity_id": "good_hope,_the_cape_of", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Good Hope, the Cape of", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Good Hope, the Cape of"], "contexts": ["icebergs drifted to"]}, {"entity_id": "cap_de_bonne-esperance", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "cap de Bonne-Esperance", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["cap de Bonne-Esperance", "Bonne-Espérance"], "contexts": ["cape at southern tip of Africa", "cape for navigation"]}, {"entity_id": "cabo_de_boa_esperança", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Cabo de Boa Esperança", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Cabo de Boa Esperança", "Boa Esperança", "cabo da Boa Esperança"], "contexts": ["cape, geographical reference", "geographical landmark"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Good Hope, the Cape of", "similarity": 0.933}], "id": 655, "stable_key": "clu_2e43fb3040d29e4f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "South Africa", "wikidata_id": "Q370736", "wikidata_description": "Dutch and British colony in Southern Africa", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape%20Colony", "wikipedia_extract": "The Cape Colony (Dutch: Kaapkolonie), also known as the Cape of Good Hope, was a British colony in present-day South Africa named after the Cape of Good Hope. It existed from 1795 to 1802, and again from 1806 to 1910, when it united with three other colonies to form the Union of South Africa, then became the Cape Province, which existed even after 1961, when South Africa had become a republic, albeit temporarily outside the Commonwealth of Nations (1961–94). The British colony was preceded by an earlier corporate colony that became an original Dutch colony of the same name, which was established in 1652 by the Dutch East India Company (VOC). The Cape was under VOC rule from 1652 to 1795 and under rule of the Napoleonic Batavia Republic from 1803 to 1806. The VOC lost the colony to Great Britain following the 1795 Battle of Muizenberg, but it was ceded to the Batavia Republic following the 1802 Treaty of Amiens. It was re-occupied by the British following the Battle of Blaauwberg in 1806, and British possession affirmed with the Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1814."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Cape Colony was located in Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Cape Colony was located in Africa."}, {"found_name": "South Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4004, "target_cluster_name": "South Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Cape Colony was a British colony in present-day South Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Cape Colony was a British colony in present-day South Africa."}, {"found_name": "cabo de Comorim", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1641, "target_cluster_name": "cabo de Comorim", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are significant capes at the southern extremities of major landmasses, historically important for navigation and trade routes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are significant capes at the southern extremities of major landmasses, historically important for navigation and trade routes.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "cognition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 38, "members": [{"entity_id": "cognition", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "cognition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["cognition"], "contexts": ["mental process of knowing"]}, {"entity_id": "cognition", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "cognition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 12, "variants": ["Cognition", "cognition"], "contexts": ["faculty of knowing and understanding", "mental process of acquiring knowledge"]}, {"entity_id": "cognitions", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "cognitions", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["cognitions"], "contexts": ["mental phenomena", "mental acts of knowing"]}, {"entity_id": "cognition", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "cognition", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 11, "variants": ["cognition"], "contexts": ["process of acquiring knowledge", "the process of knowing"]}, {"entity_id": "cognitions", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "cognitions", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["cognitions"], "contexts": ["mental representations of reality", "mental contents or products of thinking"]}, {"entity_id": "cognized", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "cognized", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["cognized"], "contexts": ["known or perceived", "perceived and understood"]}, {"entity_id": "cognize", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "cognize", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["cognize"], "contexts": ["to know or perceive", "process of gaining knowledge"]}, {"entity_id": "cognized", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "cognized", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["cognized"], "contexts": ["perceived or recognized", "process of becoming aware of something"]}, {"entity_id": "intellectual_powers", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Intellectual Powers", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Intellectual Powers"], "contexts": ["work by Reid", "book title"]}, {"entity_id": "intellectual_forces", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "intellectual forces", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["intellectual forces"], "contexts": ["mental and cognitive capabilities"]}, {"entity_id": "intellectual_faculties", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "intellectual faculties", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["intellectual faculties"], "contexts": ["mental powers for thinking"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "cognition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "cognitions", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognitions", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognition", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "cognition", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognitions", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "cognitions", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognition", "similarity": 0.954}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "cognitions", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "cognitions", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 656, "stable_key": "clu_f278e4961d28ecb5", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "cognition", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q3065932", "wikidata_description": "disease of mental health that affects cognitive functions including memory processing, perception and problem solving", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurocognitive%20disorder", "note": "Early modern concepts of 'intellectual powers' encompassed reasoning, memory, perception, and understanding, aligning with modern cognitive science.", "wikipedia_extract": "Neurocognitive disorders (NCDs), also known as cognitive disorders (CDs), are a category of mental health disorders that primarily affect cognitive abilities including learning, memory, perception, and problem-solving. Neurocognitive disorders include delirium, mild neurocognitive disorders, and major neurocognitive disorder (also known as dementia). They are defined by deficits in cognitive ability that are acquired (as opposed to developmental), typically represent decline, and may have an underlying brain pathology. The DSM-5 defines six key domains of cognitive function: executive function, learning and memory, perceptual-motor function, language, complex attention, and social cognition. Although Alzheimer's disease accounts for the majority of cases of neurocognitive disorders, there are various medical conditions that affect mental functions such as memory, thinking, and the ability to reason, including frontotemporal degeneration, Huntington's disease, dementia with Lewy bodies, traumatic brain injury (TBI), Parkinson's disease, prion disease, and dementia/neurocognitive issues due to HIV infection. Neurocognitive disorders are diagnosed as mild and major based on the severity of their symptoms."}, "member_count": 11, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "volition", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 250, "target_cluster_name": "volition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volition is described as a cognitive process, making cognition a broader category that encompasses volition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Volition is described as a cognitive process, making cognition a broader category that encompasses volition.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mental evolution", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2426, "target_cluster_name": "mental evolution", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both 'Mental evolution' and 'Cognition' (aka human thought) deal with the processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding through thought, reasoning, and memory, and the historical development of these processes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both 'Mental evolution' and 'Cognition' (aka human thought) deal with the processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding through thought, reasoning, and memory, and the historical development of these processes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "memory", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 35, "target_cluster_name": "memory", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition encompasses memory as one of its core functions, involving the mental processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition encompasses memory as one of its core functions, involving the mental processes of acquiring knowledge and understanding.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mathematics", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 161, "target_cluster_name": "mathematics", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Mathematics involves abstract thought and reasoning, which are aspects of cognition. Historical discussions of mathematics often touch upon the mental processes involved in understanding and applying mathematical concepts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Mathematics involves abstract thought and reasoning, which are aspects of cognition. Historical discussions of mathematics often touch upon the mental processes involved in understanding and applying mathematical concepts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "conception", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 282, "target_cluster_name": "conception", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Conception is a fundamental aspect of cognition, involving the formation of ideas and understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Conception is a fundamental aspect of cognition, involving the formation of ideas and understanding.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "unity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 409, "target_cluster_name": "unity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition can be understood as a unified mental process.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition can be understood as a unified mental process.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Psychology", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 552, "target_cluster_name": "Psychology", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition, encompassing thought and mental processes, is a core area of study within psychology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition, encompassing thought and mental processes, is a core area of study within psychology.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Association of Ideas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1992, "target_cluster_name": "association of ideas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The 'Association of Ideas' is a historical psychological concept that describes how thoughts and memories are linked, which is a fundamental aspect of how cognition operates and is studied.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The 'Association of Ideas' is a historical psychological concept that describes how thoughts and memories are linked, which is a fundamental aspect of how cognition operates and is studied."}, {"found_name": "Attention", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 198, "target_cluster_name": "attention", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Attention is a key cognitive function that enables the selection and processing of information, and is therefore intrinsically related to cognition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Attention is a key cognitive function that enables the selection and processing of information, and is therefore intrinsically related to cognition."}, {"found_name": "Belief", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2125, "target_cluster_name": "belief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Belief is a cognitive state that involves accepting a proposition as true, and is a core component of cognitive function and understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Belief is a cognitive state that involves accepting a proposition as true, and is a core component of cognitive function and understanding."}, {"found_name": "Calculation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1380, "target_cluster_name": "calculation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calculation is a specific cognitive process involving the manipulation of numbers and symbols, directly falling under the umbrella of cognitive abilities.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Calculation is a specific cognitive process involving the manipulation of numbers and symbols, directly falling under the umbrella of cognitive abilities."}, {"found_name": "Conceit", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2946, "target_cluster_name": "conceit", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Conceit, in the sense of a concept or idea, is a product of cognitive processes and thus related to cognition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Conceit, in the sense of a concept or idea, is a product of cognitive processes and thus related to cognition."}, {"found_name": "reflection", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 760, "target_cluster_name": "reflection", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Reflection is a fundamental cognitive process, involving the active consideration and analysis of information or experiences.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Reflection is a fundamental cognitive process, involving the active consideration and analysis of information or experiences.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "words", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 815, "target_cluster_name": "words", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Words are essential tools for thought and cognition, shaping how we understand and process information.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Words are essential tools for thought and cognition, shaping how we understand and process information.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "ego", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1587, "target_cluster_name": "ego", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Self-assembly, as a process of forming organized structures from disordered components, shares conceptual parallels with cognitive processes, which involve the organization and integration of information to form understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Self-assembly, as a process of forming organized structures from disordered components, shares conceptual parallels with cognitive processes, which involve the organization and integration of information to form understanding.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "reasoning", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1684, "target_cluster_name": "reasoning", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition encompasses the mental processes involved in reasoning, such as perception, attention, memory, and thinking.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition encompasses the mental processes involved in reasoning, such as perception, attention, memory, and thinking.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Principles of Psychology", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2061, "target_cluster_name": "Principles of Psychology", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Psychology is fundamentally the study of cognition, or human thought.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Psychology is fundamentally the study of cognition, or human thought.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "habits", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2105, "target_cluster_name": "habits", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The formation and maintenance of habits involve cognitive processes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The formation and maintenance of habits involve cognitive processes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "common-sense", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2420, "target_cluster_name": "common-sense", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Common sense is a fundamental aspect of human cognition, referring to practical judgment and understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Common sense is a fundamental aspect of human cognition, referring to practical judgment and understanding.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "stimulation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2568, "target_cluster_name": "stimulation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition involves the processing of sensory stimulation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition involves the processing of sensory stimulation.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "nervous action", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2900, "target_cluster_name": "nervous action", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cognition is a higher-level process that is heavily reliant on and mediated by nerve activity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cognition is a higher-level process that is heavily reliant on and mediated by nerve activity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mental", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2124, "target_cluster_name": "mental", "source_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "evidence_snippet": "uniformities of experience, generate absolute uniformities of thought. Does it not follow, then, that this ultimate truth must be a cognition involved in our mental organization? An affirmative answer", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "reverse: a type of", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "living body", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "evidence_snippet": "is still known as a living body; even should it be questioned whether it is organic, it remains beyond question that it is a material object, and it is cognized by being recognized as such. Whence it ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "a state of being that is still known"}, {"found_name": "material object", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "evidence_snippet": "is still known as a living body; even should it be questioned whether it is organic, it remains beyond question that it is a material object, and it is cognized by being recognized as such. Whence it ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "a thing that is recognized as such"}, {"found_name": "cognition of self", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "evidence_snippet": "respect to “the unsophisticated sense of mankind” when it testifies to the objectivity of space. Passing over this, however, it may readily be shown that a cognition of self, properly so called, is ab", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a specific type of cognition being discussed"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Etiópia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 28, "members": [{"entity_id": "æthiopia", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Æthiopia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Æthiopia"], "contexts": ["ancient Ethiopia"]}, {"entity_id": "éthiopiens", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Éthiopiens", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Éthiopiens"], "contexts": ["people from Ethiopia"]}, {"entity_id": "etiópia", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Etiópia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 25, "variants": ["Etiópia", "Ethiopia", "Etíopia"], "contexts": ["region near the strait", "region where amber is found"]}, {"entity_id": "ediiopia", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Ediiopia", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ediiopia"], "contexts": ["region sometimes included in India"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Æthiopia", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Éthiopiens", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Æthiopia", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Etiópia", "similarity": 0.939}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Æthiopia", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Ediiopia", "similarity": 0.929}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Éthiopiens", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Etiópia", "similarity": 0.936}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Éthiopiens", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Ediiopia", "similarity": 0.922}], "id": 657, "stable_key": "clu_e57590655e167cca", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ethiopia", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Ethiopia", "note": "The spelling 'Æthiopia' and 'Etiópia' are historical variants of Ethiopia.", "wikidata_id": "Q115", "wikidata_description": "country in the Horn of Africa", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopia", "wikipedia_extract": "Ethiopia, officially the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia, is a landlocked country located in the Horn of Africa region of East Africa. It shares borders with Eritrea to the north, Djibouti to the northeast, Somalia to the east, Kenya to the south, South Sudan to the west, and Sudan to the northwest. Ethiopia covers a land area of 1,104,300 square kilometres (426,400 sq mi). As of 2025, it has around 135 million inhabitants, making it the 14th-most populous country. The national capital and largest city, Addis Ababa, lies several kilometres west of the East African Rift that splits the country into the African and Somali tectonic plates. Anatomically modern humans emerged from modern-day Ethiopia."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Abyssinia", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2106, "target_cluster_name": "Abyssinia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Abyssinia is a historical name for Ethiopia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "Abyssinia is a historical name for Ethiopia."}, {"found_name": "Egypto", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 232, "target_cluster_name": "Egypto", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ethiopia shares historical and geographical proximity with Egypt, with periods of interaction and influence between the two regions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ethiopia shares historical and geographical proximity with Egypt, with periods of interaction and influence between the two regions.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ethiopia is a country located in Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ethiopia is a country located in Africa."}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historically, the term 'Asia' was sometimes used in a broader sense that could encompass regions like Ethiopia, particularly in older geographical or cosmological frameworks.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historically, the term 'Asia' was sometimes used in a broader sense that could encompass regions like Ethiopia, particularly in older geographical or cosmological frameworks."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Hodgson", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 28, "members": [{"entity_id": "hodgson", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Hodgson", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Hodgson"], "contexts": ["measurer of mountain heights", "measurer of mountain height"]}, {"