ected by remedies"]}, {"entity_id": "urina", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "urina", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 22, "variants": ["urina", "urinam", "urinas", "urine"], "contexts": ["urine, its burning is avoided", "urine, bodily fluid"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Passages of Urine", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "urina", "similarity": 0.914}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Passages of Urine", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "urina", "similarity": 0.914}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "urina", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "urina", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 662, "stable_key": "clu_625b9c30c980a1a0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Urine", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A bodily fluid produced by the kidneys and excreted from the body.", "note": "Refers to the bodily fluid itself and the passages through which it travels.", "wikipedia_extract": "Urine, excreted by the kidneys, is a liquid containing excess water and water-soluble nitrogen-rich by-products of metabolism including urea, uric acid, and creatinine, which must be cleared from the bloodstream. Urinalysis detects these nitrogenous wastes in mammals. In placental mammals, urine travels from the kidneys via the ureters to the bladder and exits the urethra through the penis or vulva during urination. Other vertebrates excrete urine through the cloaca. Urine plays an important role in the earth's nitrogen cycle. In balanced ecosystems, urine fertilizes the soil and thus helps plants to grow."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Kidneys", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 74, "target_cluster_name": "Kidneys", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The kidneys are the primary organs responsible for producing urine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The kidneys are the primary organs responsible for producing urine.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Bladder", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 608, "target_cluster_name": "Bladder", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Urine is the substance stored within the bladder.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Urine is the substance stored within the bladder.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Stones", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2704, "target_cluster_name": "Stones", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calculi (stones) are often associated with urine and urinary tract issues.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Calculi (stones) are often associated with urine and urinary tract issues.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "flores", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 27, "members": [{"entity_id": "fleurs", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "fleurs", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["fleurs"], "contexts": ["delightful scent from the island", "ornaments for religious reposoirs"]}, {"entity_id": "flores", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "flores", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 10, "variants": ["flores", "Flores", "flores brancas"], "contexts": ["part of the tree", "used for strong scent"]}, {"entity_id": "flores", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "flores", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 15, "variants": ["flores", "flor", "flores das violetas", "flores de violas"], "contexts": ["flowers appearing in certain months", "delicate plant part for 