r and gold are frequently discussed together as precious metals, often contrasted or compared in alchemical and economic contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Silver and gold are frequently discussed together as precious metals, often contrasted or compared in alchemical and economic contexts."}, {"found_name": "Copper", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 274, "target_cluster_name": "copper", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Silver and copper are both common metals discussed in relation to metallurgy and coinage.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Silver and copper are both common metals discussed in relation to metallurgy and coinage."}, {"found_name": "Lead", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 368, "target_cluster_name": "Lead", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Silver and lead are often found together in ores and were historically processed together.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Silver and lead are often found together in ores and were historically processed together."}, {"found_name": "Brass", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 440, "target_cluster_name": "Brass", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Brass, an alloy of copper and zinc, is a metal often discussed alongside silver in contexts of metallurgy and material properties.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Brass, an alloy of copper and zinc, is a metal often discussed alongside silver in contexts of metallurgy and material properties."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Senne", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 26, "members": [{"entity_id": "senna", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Senna", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Senna"], "contexts": ["herb for medicinal use", "plant with purging virtues"]}, {"entity_id": "senna", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Senna", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Senna"], "contexts": ["herb used in learned receipts"]}, {"entity_id": "senne", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Senne", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 23, "variants": ["Senne", "Sena", "Sene", "sene", "senn", "senne", "senné"], "contexts": ["used in purgative pills", "herb used as a purgative"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Senna", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Senna", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Senna", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Senne", "similarity": 0.888}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Senna", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Senne", "similarity": 0.888}], "id": 668, "stable_key": "clu_60821cd85c0ca13c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "senna", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Senna alexandrina", "family": "Fabaceae", "description": "A plant whose leaves and pods are used as a laxative.", "wikipedia_extract": "Senna alexandrina (Alexandrian senna, in Arabic عشرج or عشرق or سنامكي and see below) is an ornamental plant in the genus Senna. It is used in herbalism. It grows natively in upper Egypt, especially in the Nubian region, and near Khartoum (Sudan), where it is cultivated commercially. It is also grown elsewhere, notably in India and Somalia. Not native to the USSR, it was farmed in southern Kazakhstan for medicine. Alexandrian Senna is a shrubby plant that reaches 0.5–1 metres (20\" to 40\"), rarely two metres (6') in height with a branched, pale-green erect stem and long spreading branches bearing four or five pairs of leaves."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Canafistula", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 582, "target_cluster_name": "Canafistula", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cassia fistula is closely related to plants in the genus Senna, and historically, the distinction between Cassia and Senna was sometimes blurred or debated in medicinal contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cassia fistula is closely related to plants in the genus Senna, and historically, the distinction between Cassia and Senna was sometimes blurred or debated in medicinal contexts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Cassia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 317, "target_cluster_name": "cássia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Senna is a genus within the family Fabaceae, and Cassia is a related genus, often historically confused or grouped together due to similar properties and appearances. Both are known for their laxative properties.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Senna is a genus within the family Fabaceae, and Cassia is a related genus, often historically confused or grouped together due to similar properties and appearances. Both are known for their laxative properties."}, {"found_name": "Cassia fistula", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 582, "target_cluster_name": "Canafistula", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cassia fistula is a species within the genus Cassia, which is closely related to Senna. Both are known for their medicinal uses, particularly as laxatives.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cassia fistula is a species within the genus Cassia, which is closely related to Senna. Both are known for their medicinal uses, particularly as laxatives."}, {"found_name": "paoGua-plius adultimum uſqueſenium", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "a ſeguinte. Tomem de limadurade paoGua- plius adultimum uſqueſenium,imò ad jaco meyo arratel ,de falſa parrilha feyta em pò tres onças , de folhas de ſene efcolhidoduas onças ,& meya, de agrimonia,&de", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Crocus metallorum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 26, "members": [{"entity_id": "crocus_metallorum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Crocus Metallorum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 2, "variants": ["Crocus Metallorum"], "contexts": ["substance attracts not at all", "preparation that kindles like gunpowder"]}, {"entity_id": "crocus_metallorum", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Crocus Metallorum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 2, "variants": ["Crocus Metallorum"], "contexts": ["preparation used in learned receipts", "preparation used in infusion"]}, {"entity_id": "crocus_metallorum", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Crocus metallorum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 22, "variants": ["Crocus metallorum", "Croci metallorum", "Crocus Metallorum", "Crocus de metallorum", "croci metallorum", "crocus metallorum"], "contexts": ["common name for prepared Antimonio", "emetic medicine for plague"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Crocus Metallorum", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Crocus Metallorum", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Crocus Metallorum", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "