g their people and receiving divine revelations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are central figures in the Old Testament, leading their people and receiving divine revelations.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Thomas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2931, "target_cluster_name": "Thomas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Moses, as the lawgiver in the Old Testament, is a significant figure in the theological framework that Thomas Aquinas developed, particularly concerning divine law and natural law.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Moses, as the lawgiver in the Old Testament, is a significant figure in the theological framework that Thomas Aquinas developed, particularly concerning divine law and natural law.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Madeira", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "madeira", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Madeira", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 15, "variants": ["Madeira"], "contexts": ["islets with many insects", "island for distance comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "madeira", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Madeira", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 8, "variants": ["Madeira"], "contexts": ["river in South America", "river name"]}, {"entity_id": "madeira", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Madeira", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Madeira"], "contexts": ["island with peculiar flora", "vegetation of"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Madeira", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Madeira", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Madeira", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Madeira", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Madeira", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Madeira", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 674, "stable_key": "clu_8ccaa127ff6a42cd", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Madeira", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Portugal", "wikidata_id": "Q26253", "wikidata_description": "Autonomous Region of Portugal in the archipelago of Madeira", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Madeira", "wikipedia_extract": "Madeira, officially the Autonomous Region of Madeira, is an autonomous region of Portugal, in the Atlantic Ocean about 805 km (500 miles) southwest of mainland Portugal. Together with the Azores, it is one of the two autonomous regions of Portugal and a special territory of the European Union. It is the southernmost point and region of Portugal. Madeira is an archipelago situated in the North Atlantic Ocean, in the region of Macaronesia, just under 400 kilometres (250 mi) north of the Canary Islands, Spain, 520 kilometres (320 mi) west of Morocco and 805 kilometres (500 mi) southwest of mainland Portugal. Madeira sits on the African Tectonic Plate, but is culturally, politically and ethnically associated with Europe, with its population predominantly descended from Portuguese settlers. Its population was 251,060 in 2021."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Azores", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 874, "target_cluster_name": "Azores", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Madeira and the Azores are both autonomous regions of Portugal located in the Atlantic Ocean.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Madeira and the Azores are both autonomous regions of Portugal located in the Atlantic Ocean."}]}, {"canonical_name": "pérolas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 31, "members": [{"entity_id": "perlas", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "perlas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Perlas", "perlas"], "contexts": ["gems brought from the Indies", "precious items from the Indies"]}, {"entity_id": "pérolas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "pérolas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 15, "variants": ["pérolas", "PÉROLAS", "Pérolas", "pérolas oríentaes"], "contexts": ["precious gems", "gemstones from the sea"]}, {"entity_id": "perle", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "perle", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 7, "variants": ["perle", "Perla", "Perle"], "contexts": ["pearls for grinding", "ingredient in a preparation"]}, {"entity_id": "perles", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "perles", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["perles"], "contexts": ["production from Panama, Rio Hacha, Marguerite", "formerly famous pearl fisheries"]}, {"entity_id": "perlás", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Perlás", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Perlás"], "contexts": ["prepared pearls, ingredient in a powder"]}, {"entity_id": "perla", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "perla", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["perla"], "contexts": ["Spanish name for pearl", "Latin name for gemstone"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "perlas", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "pérolas", "similarity": 0.927}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "perlas", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "perle", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "pérolas", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "perle", "similarity": 0.909}], "id": 675, "stable_key": "clu_be41a7aa67e793d4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "pearls", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "note": "The term 'perlas' is the Spanish plural for pearl, and 'perla' is singular. 'Perles' in French also means pearls."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Cornelius Celfus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "cornelio_celso", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Cornelio Celso", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cornelio Celso"], "contexts": ["ancient authority on medicine"]}, {"entity_id": "cornelio_celso", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Cornelio Celso", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Cornelio Celso", "Comelio Celso"], "contexts": ["ancient authority who calls calamus alexandrino", "ancient medical writer"]}, {"entity_id": "cornelius_celfus", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Cornelius Celfus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 21, "variants": ["Cornelius Celfus", "Cornel. Celf", "Cornel. Celf.", "Cornel. Cell.", "Cornel. Cels.", "Cornel.Cell.", "Cornelio Cello", "Cornelio Celso", "Cornelio Celſo"], "contexts": ["ancient author of de Re Medica", "author of 'deLienofis morbis'"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Cornelio Celso", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Cornelio Celso", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Cornelio Celso", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Cornelius Celfus", "similarity": 0.875}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Cornelio Celso", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Cornelius Celfus", "similarity": 0.875}], "id": 676, "stable_key": "clu_d46da080623bf5f1", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Aulus Cornelius Celsus", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Roman encyclopedist and medical writer, author of De Medicina.", "wikipedia_extract": "Aulus Cornelius Celsus (c. 25 BC – c. 50 AD) was a Roman encyclopedist, known for his extant medical work, De Medicina, which is believed to be the only surviving section of a much larger encyclopedia. The De Medicina is a primary source on diet, pharmacy, surgery and related fields, and it is one of the best sources concerning medical knowledge in the Roman world. The lost portions of his encyclopedia likely included volumes on agriculture, law, rhetoric, and military arts. He made contributions to the classification of human skin disorders in  dermatology, such as myrmecia, and his name is often found in medical terminology regarding the skin, e.g., kerion celsi and area celsi. He is also the namesake of Paracelsus (lit. Above Celsus), a great Swiss alchemist and physician prevalent in the Medical Renaissance."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Galen", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 29, "target_cluster_name": "Galen", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Celsus, a Roman encyclopedist, wrote on medicine and his work, 'De Medicina,' provides a valuable overview of medical knowledge contemporary with or preceding Galen.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Celsus, a Roman encyclopedist, wrote on medicine and his work, 'De Medicina,' provides a valuable overview of medical knowledge contemporary with or preceding Galen.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Dioscorides", "link_type": "