, "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "This likely refers to scientific laws or theories concerning rotational motion, including planetary rotation and atmospheric circulation.", "wikipedia_extract": "In linear algebra, a rotation matrix is a transformation matrix that is used to perform a rotation in Euclidean space. For example, using the convention below, the matrix {\\displaystyle R={\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos \\theta &-\\sin \\theta \\\\\\sin \\theta &\\cos \\theta \\end{bmatrix}}\\cdot } rotates points in the xy plane counterclockwise through an angle θ about the origin of a two-dimensional Cartesian coordinate system.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rotation_matrix"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Earth's rotation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3632, "target_cluster_name": "Earth's rotation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The 'Law of rotation' is a fundamental concept in describing rotational motion, and 'Earth's rotation' is a specific, prominent example of this phenomenon studied in historical texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The 'Law of rotation' is a fundamental concept in describing rotational motion, and 'Earth's rotation' is a specific, prominent example of this phenomenon studied in historical texts."}, {"found_name": "equatorial", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "to be overthrown in the midst of a dense wood. The general movement of the sea from east to west between p 307 the tropics (termed the equatorial or rotation currnt) is considered to be owing to the p", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for rotation current"}, {"found_name": "rotation currnt", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id