t era."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "epidemics", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 520, "target_cluster_name": "epidemics", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pestilence, as a widespread disease, is a type of epidemic.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Pestilence, as a widespread disease, is a type of epidemic."}, {"found_name": "Infection", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1792, "target_cluster_name": "Infection", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pestilence is a disease that is typically caused by infection.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Pestilence is a disease that is typically caused by infection."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Pestilence", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "pestilence", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Pestilence", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 16, "variants": ["Pestilence", "Pestilences", "Pestilent Feavers"], "contexts": ["highly infectious disease", "infection that the herb defends against"]}, {"entity_id": "pestilenciales", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "pestilenciales", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 1, "variants": ["pestilenciales"], "contexts": ["pestilential fevers"]}, {"entity_id": "pestilencia", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "pestilencia", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 6, "variants": ["pestilencia", "Pestilentis febris"], "contexts": ["pestilence or plague", "plague, a widespread epidemic"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Pestilence", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "pestilenciales", "similarity": 0.943}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Pestilence", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "pestilencia", "similarity": 0.984}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "pestilenciales", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "pestilencia", "similarity": 0.931}], "id": 689, "stable_key": "clu_a50d60775402059c-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Plague", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A highly contagious and often fatal infectious disease.", "note": "Covers terms related to the bubonic plague and similar epidemic diseases.", "wikipedia_extract": "Mark Tonderai (born 1974) is a British-Zimbabwean entrepreneur, film director, writer, actor and former disc jockey. He is co-founder of the London-based production company Shona Productions with his wife Zoe Stewart. He directed the crime drama television series The Five which first aired in April 2016 on the Sky 1 channel. Tonderai began his career in the media working as a writer, producer and presenter for radio. From early 1993 until late 1998 Tonderai was heavily involved in radio, and was the writer and producer of The Mark Tonderai Show, hosted on BBC Radio 1, and the Jam. Tonderai was also involved in numerous BBC Radio 4 projects, such as the Worldly Wise, Rainbow Nation and Week Ending, as well as Kiss 100's Rude Awakening, hosted on Kiss 100 London."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "organ", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "organ", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "organ", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 13, "variants": ["organ"], "contexts": ["functional unit of the body", "part of an organism with a specific function"]}, {"entity_id": "organ", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "organ", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 8, "variants": ["organ"], "contexts": ["general term for body part", "a distinct part of the body with a specific function"]}, {"entity_id": "organ", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "organ", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["organ"], "contexts": ["functional part of a body", "general structure evolution parallels organ evolution"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "organ", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "organ", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "organ", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "organ", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "organ", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "organ", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 690, "stable_key": "clu_5d0978055f91e336", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "organ", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organ_%28biology%29", "wikipedia_extract": "In a multicellular organism, an organ is a collection of tissues joined in a structural unit to serve a common function. In the hierarchy of life, an organ lies between tissue and an organ system. Tissues are formed from same type cells to act together in a function. Tissues of different types combine to form an organ which has a specific function. The intestinal wall for example is formed by epithelial tissue and smooth muscle tissue. Two or more organs working together in the execution of a specific body function form an organ system, also called a biological system or body system."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Sense organs", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1980, "target_cluster_name": "sense-organs", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sense organs are a specific category of organs, directly related to the broader concept of 'organ'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Sense organs are a specific category of organs, directly related to the broader concept of 'organ'."}]}, {"canonical_name": "exercicio", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "exercise", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "exercise", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["exercise"], "contexts": ["physical activity influencing traits"]}, {"entity_id": "exercicio", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "exercicio", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["exercicio"], "contexts": ["physical activity"]}, {"entity_id": "exercicio", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "exercicio", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 21, "variants": ["exercicio", "exerciciodema", "exerciciolaborioſo", "exercise", "exercitar"], "contexts": ["physical activity and regimen", "physical activity for health"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "exercise", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "exercicio", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "exercise", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "exercicio", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "exercicio", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "exercicio", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 691, "stable_key": "clu_a503d1e777cfc50e", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Exercise", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Physical activity undertaken for health or regimen.", "wikipedia_extract": "Exercise or working out is physical activity that enhances or maintains fitness and overall health. It is performed for various reasons, including weight loss or maintenance, to aid growth and improve strength, develop muscles and the cardiovascular system, hone athletic skills, improve health, or simply for enjoyment. Many people choose to exercise outdoors where they can congregate in groups, socialize, and improve well-being as well as mental health. In terms of health benefits, usually, 150 minutes (2 hours and 30 minutes) of moderate-intensity exercise per week is recommended for reducing the risk of health problems. At the same time, even doing a small amount of exercise is healthier than doing none. Only doing an hour and a quarter (11 minutes/day) of exercise could reduce the risk of early death, cardiovascular disease, stroke, and cancer."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Human Body", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4153, "target_cluster_name": "Human Body", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Exercise directly impacts and is performed upon the human body, making it a fundamental related concept.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Exercise directly impacts and is performed upon the human body, making it a fundamental related concept."}, {"found_name": "Locomotion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 463, "target_cluster_name": "locomotion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Many forms of exercise involve locomotion, and the study of movement is central to understanding exercise.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Many forms of exercise involve locomotion, and the study of movement is central to understanding exercise."}, {"found_name": "dieta", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1390, "target_cluster_name": "dieta", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dietary regimen and exercise are often considered together as components of health and physical conditioning.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Dietary regimen and exercise are often considered together as components of health and physical conditioning.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "balneis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2167, "target_cluster_name": "balneis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Baths were often associated with exercise and physical activity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Baths were often associated with exercise and physical activity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "hervapoligano", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "fempre noyva, ou com a hervapoligano, a que vulgarmente chamaó andorinha... 24. Aquarta advertencia he , que os doentes deſta enfermidade façam pouco exercicio , &durmaó muyto ;porqueaffim como naoha ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for a plant used in treatment"}, {"found_name": "andorinha", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "fempre noyva, ou com a hervapoligano, a que vulgarmente chamaó andorinha... 24. Aquarta advertencia he , que os doentes deſta enfermidade façam pouco exercicio , &durmaó muyto ;porqueaffim como naoha ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vulgar name for hervapoligano"}]}, {"canonical_name": "physiciens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "physiciens", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "physiciens", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 9, "variants": ["physiciens", "physicien", "physicien anglois"], "contexts": ["physicists' attempts to observe barometer variations", "scientists making observations"]}, {"entity_id": "physicists", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "physicists", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 3, "variants": ["physicists"], "contexts": ["scientific professionals", "scientists interested in light phenomena"]}, {"entity_id": "physicist", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "physicist", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["physicist"], "contexts": ["scientist studying physics"]}, {"entity_id": "physicists", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "physicists", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 8, "variants": ["physicists"], "contexts": ["scientists studying physical phenomena", "scholars studying physical forces"]}, {"entity_id": "physicist", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "physicist", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PRACTITIONER", "count": 2, "variants": ["physicist", "Physicist"], "contexts": ["scientist studying physics", "practitioner of physics"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "physiciens", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "physicists", "similarity": 0.939}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "physiciens", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "physicist", "similarity": 0.909}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "physicists", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "physicists", "similarity": 0.919}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "physicists", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "physicist", "similarity": 0.842}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "physicist", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "physicists", "similarity": 0.844}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "physicist", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "physicist", "similarity": 0.927}], "id": 692, "stable_key": "clu_568d02ecb976fd7f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "physicist", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "A scientist who studies the fundamental constituents and behavior of matter and energy.", "note": "The term 'physiciens' and 'physicists' in the context of Humboldt's work, especially in 'Kosmos', clearly refers to natural philosophers and early scientists who studied physical phenomena, which aligns with the modern concept of a physicist.", "wikidata_id": "Q169470", "wikidata_description": "scientist who does research in physics", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physicist", "wikipedia_extract": "A physicist is a scientist who specializes in the field of physics, which encompasses the interactions of matter and energy at all length and time scales in the physical universe. Physicists generally are interested in the root or ultimate causes of phenomena, and usually frame their understanding in mathematical terms. They work across a wide range of research fields, spanning all length scales: from sub-atomic and particle physics, through biological physics, to cosmological length scales encompassing the universe as a whole. The field generally includes two types of physicists: experimental physicists who specialize in the observation of natural phenomena and the development and analysis of experiments, and theoretical physicists who specialize in mathematical modeling of physical systems to rationalize, explain and predict natural phenomena. Physicists can apply their knowledge towards solving practical problems or to developing new technologies (also known as applied physics or engineering physics). The study and practice of physics is based on an intellectual ladder of discoveries and insights from ancient times to the present."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Chemist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 609, "target_cluster_name": "Chymicos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historically, the lines between 'physicist' and 'chemist' were often blurred, with many individuals contributing to both fields and the terminology being used interchangeably in some contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historically, the lines between 'physicist' and 'chemist' were often blurred, with many individuals contributing to both fields and the terminology being used interchangeably in some contexts."}, {"found_name": "Geographers", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3771, "target_cluster_name": "physical geographers", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Many early physicists were also involved in geography, particularly in areas like geodesy, cartography, and the study of natural phenomena that informed geographical understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Many early physicists were also involved in geography, particularly in areas like geodesy, cartography, and the study of natural phenomena that informed geographical understanding."}, {"found_name": "Alessandro Volta", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 966, "target_cluster_name": "Volta", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volta was a pioneering physicist known for the invention of the voltaic pile, a precursor to the electric battery, and his work on electricity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Volta was a pioneering physicist known for the invention of the voltaic pile, a precursor to the electric battery, and his work on electricity."}, {"found_name": "André-Marie Ampère", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2134, "target_cluster_name": "Ampère", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ampère was a mathematician and physicist who is considered one of the founders of the science of electromagnetism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ampère was a mathematician and physicist who is considered one of the founders of the science of electromagnetism."}, {"found_name": "Archimedes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 480, "target_cluster_name": "Archimedes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Archimedes was an ancient Greek mathematician, physicist, engineer, inventor, and astronomer, considered one of the leading scientists of classical antiquity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Archimedes was an ancient Greek mathematician, physicist, engineer, inventor, and astronomer, considered one of the leading scientists of classical antiquity."}, {"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Aristotle's work in physics, though largely superseded, laid foundational concepts and methods for scientific inquiry for centuries.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Aristotle's work in physics, though largely superseded, laid foundational concepts and methods for scientific inquiry for centuries."}, {"found_name": "Augustin-Jean Fresnel", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2204, "target_cluster_name": "Fresnel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fresnel was a French physicist who made significant contributions to the theory of light, particularly in optics and wave theory.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Fresnel was a French physicist who made significant contributions to the theory of light, particularly in optics and wave theory."}, {"found_name": "Benjamin Franklin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 343, "target_cluster_name": "Franklin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Franklin was a polymath who made significant contributions to physics, particularly in his studies of electricity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Franklin was a polymath who made significant contributions to physics, particularly in his studies of electricity."}, {"found_name": "Joule", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2155, "target_cluster_name": "Joule", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "James Prescott Joule was a renowned physicist.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: James Prescott Joule was a renowned physicist.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Hamilton", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2299, "target_cluster_name": "Hamilton", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton made significant contributions to physics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sir William Rowan Hamilton made significant contributions to physics.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "rain", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 23, "members": [{"entity_id": "pluie", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "pluie", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["pluie"], "contexts": ["weather condition", "precipitation from the atmosphere"]}, {"entity_id": "rain", "book