Bayan ng Santo Domingo), is a municipality in the province of Nueva Ecija, Philippines. According to the 2024 census, it has a population of 63,750 people. The town is named after Saint Dominic, its patron saint. During the last quarter of the 17th century, Ilocos and Bulacan natives and Tagalogs from Cabanatuan migrated to Santo Domingo. They found in the settlement buri palms. Therefore, these people called the site, Pulong Buli."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "distance", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 21, "members": [{"entity_id": "distance", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "distance", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["distance"], "contexts": ["spatial separation from observer", "spatial separation"]}, {"entity_id": "distance", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "distance", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["distance"], "contexts": ["space between celestial bodies", "spatial separation between bodies"]}, {"entity_id": "distance", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "distance", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 11, "variants": ["distance"], "contexts": ["space between two points", "space between objects"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "distance", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "distance", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "distance", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "distance", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "distance", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "distance", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 711, "stable_key": "clu_eef19e22f90ad76