ce_name": "grecò", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "grego", "similarity": 0.931}], "id": 773, "stable_key": "clu_e15d4e25fcabe27e", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Greece", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Southeastern European country, cradle of Western civilization and ancient knowledge.", "note": "Includes references to the Greek language and people.", "wikipedia_extract": "Greece, officially the Hellenic Republic, is a country in Southeast Europe. Located on the southern tip of the Balkan peninsula, it shares land borders with Albania to the northwest, North Macedonia and Bulgaria to the north, and Turkey to the east. The Aegean Sea lies to the east of the mainland, the Ionian Sea to the west, and the Sea of Crete and the Mediterranean Sea to the south. Greece has the longest coastline on the Mediterranean basin, spanning thousands of islands and nine traditional geographic regions. It has a population of over 10 million. Athens is the nation's capital and largest city, followed by Thessaloniki and Patras."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "perihelion", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 700, "target_cluster_name": "Perihelion", "source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "evidence_snippet": "the ellipse. NOTE 49, p. 9. _Apsides._ The points P and A, fig. 10, at the extremities of the major axis of an orbit. P is commonly called the perihelion, a Greek term signifying _round the sun_; and ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "a point on the major axis of an orbit, defined by a Greek term"}, {"found_name": "aphelion", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 864, "target_cluster_name": "Aphelion", "source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "evidence_snippet": "the ellipse. NOTE 49, p. 9. _Apsides._ The points P and A, fig. 10, at the extremiti