fts. Discussions of monsoons in historical texts are intrinsically linked to the study of atmospheric currents and their behavior.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Monsoons are fundamentally driven by large-scale atmospheric circulation patterns and wind shifts. Discussions of monsoons in historical texts are intrinsically linked to the study of atmospheric currents and their behavior."}]}, {"canonical_name": "quebraduras", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 15, "members": [{"entity_id": "quebradura", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "quebradura", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 2, "variants": ["quebradura"], "contexts": ["hernia"]}, {"entity_id": "quebraduras", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "quebraduras", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["quebraduras"], "contexts": ["Fractures or breaks"]}, {"entity_id": "quebraduras", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "quebraduras", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 12, "variants": ["quebraduras", "Quebraduras", "quebrados", "quebrantos"], "contexts": ["broken bones or injuries", "hernias, a medical condition"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "quebradura", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "quebraduras", "similarity": 0.955}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "quebradura", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "quebraduras", "similarity": 0.955}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "quebraduras", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "quebraduras", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 800, "stable_key": "clu_d1f5c3bb962a6d58", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Fracture", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "Fracture", "note": "The term 'quebradura' in Portuguese and Spanish can refer to both fractures (broken bones) and hernias. Given the contexts mentioning 'broken bones or injuries' and 'fractures or breaks', 'fracture' is the primary referent. However, 'hernia' should be considered a secondary possibility depending on the specific text."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Wounds", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1310, "target_cluster_name": "inward Wounds", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fractures are a type of physical trauma, often occurring alongside or as a result of wounds.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Fractures are a type of physical trauma, often occurring alongside or as a result of wounds."}, {"found_name": "Contusions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3320, "target_cluster_name": "contusões", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Contusions (bruises) are often associated with the trauma that causes fractures.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Contusions (bruises) are often associated with the trauma that causes fractures."}, {"found_name": "Pain", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 70, "target_cluster_name": "pain", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fractures are inherently associated with significant pain.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Fractures are inherently associated with significant pain."}, {"found_name": "Swelling", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 55, "target_cluster_name": "Swellings", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Swelling is a common and direct consequence of a fracture.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Swelling is a common and direct