"high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q7239", "wikidata_description": "any individual living being or physical living system", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organism", "wikipedia_extract": "An organism is any living thing that functions as an individual. Such a definition raises more problems than it solves, not least because the concept of an individual is also difficult. Several criteria, few of which are widely accepted, have been proposed to define what constitutes an organism. Among the most common is that an organism has autonomous reproduction, growth, and metabolism. This would exclude viruses, even though they evolve like organisms. Other problematic cases include colonial organisms; a colony of eusocial insects is organised adaptively, and has germ-soma specialisation, with some insects reproducing, others not, like cells in an animal's body."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Breed", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2181, "target_cluster_name": "breed", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A breed is a specific group of domestic animals having homogeneous appearance, behavior, and other characteristics that distinguish it from other animals within the same species.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A breed is a specific group of domestic animals having homogeneous appearance, behavior, and other characteristics that distinguish it from other animals within the same species."}, {"found_name": "Economy of nature", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1147, "target_cluster_name": "economy of nature", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The economy of nature refers to the interrelationships and balance within the natural world, which is composed of organisms.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The economy of nature refers to the interrelationships and balance within the natural world, which is composed of organisms."}, {"found_name": "Animal Kingdom", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2373, "target_cluster_name": "animal kingdom", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Animal Kingdom is a taxonomic classification that encompasses all organisms belonging to the kingdom Animalia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Animal Kingdom is a taxonomic classification that encompasses all organisms belonging to the kingdom Animalia."}, {"found_name": "Animal life", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2437, "target_cluster_name": "animal life", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Animal life is a direct descriptor of organisms that are animals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Animal life is a direct descriptor of organisms that are animals."}, {"found_name": "Botany", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1098, "target_cluster_name": "botany", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Botany is the scientific study of plants, which are a type of organism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Botany is the scientific study of plants, which are a type of organism."}, {"found_name": "Sexes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2515, "target_cluster_name": "Sexes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Biological 'sex' is a defining characteristic of many 'organisms', influencing their structure, function, and reproductive strategies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Biological 'sex' is a defining characteristic of many 'organisms', influencing their structure, function, and reproductive strategies.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "migration", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "migration", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "migration", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 10, "variants": ["migration"], "contexts": ["movement of species from one region to another", "movement of organisms to new regions"]}, {"entity_id": "migrations", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "migrations", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["migrations"], "contexts": ["movement of organisms from one place to another"]}, {"entity_id": "migration", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "migration", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["migration"], "contexts": ["false hypothesis in botanical language", "seasonal movement of animals"]}, {"entity_id": "migration", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "migration", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["migration"], "contexts": ["movement of people"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "migration", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "migration", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "migration", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "migration", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "migrations", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "migration", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "migrations", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "migration", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "migration", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "migration", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 808, "stable_key": "clu_a38a8727d15da4b4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Migration", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q193145", "wikidata_description": "movement of animals from place to place, usually seasonal", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Animal%20migration", "wikipedia_extract": "Animal migration is the relatively long-distance movement of individual animals, usually on a seasonal basis. It is the most common form of migration in ecology. It is found in all major animal groups, including birds, mammals, fish, reptiles, amphibians, insects, and crustaceans. The cause of migration may be local climate, local availability of food, the season of the year or for mating. To be counted as a true migration, and not just a local dispersal or irruption, the movement of the animals should be an annual or seasonal occurrence, or a major habitat change as part of their life. An annual event could include Northern Hemisphere birds migrating south for the winter, or wildebeest migrating annually for seasonal grazing."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Emigration", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3481, "target_cluster_name": "emigration", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Emigration is a specific type of migration, involving movement away from a place.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Emigration is a specific type of migration, involving movement away from a place."}, {"found_name": "Animal Kingdom", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2373, "target_cluster_name": "animal kingdom", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Migration is a phenomenon observed across various groups within the Animal Kingdom.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Migration is a phenomenon observed across various groups within the Animal Kingdom."}]}, {"canonical_name": "fauna", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "fauna", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "fauna", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["fauna"], "contexts": ["animal life of a particular region or period", "animal life of a region/period"]}, {"entity_id": "faunas", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "faunas", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["faunas"], "contexts": ["assemblages of animals from earlier world", "animal life of a region/period"]}, {"entity_id": "fauna", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "fauna", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["fauna"], "contexts": ["animal life of a region"]}, {"entity_id": "fauna", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "fauna", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 7, "variants": ["Fauna", "fauna"], "contexts": ["animal life of a region", "collective term for animal life"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "fauna", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "faunas", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "fauna", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "fauna", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "fauna", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "fauna", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "faunas", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "fauna", "similarity": 0.973}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "fauna", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "fauna", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 809, "stable_key": "clu_f