ncluded in Scandinavia for their ethnolinguistic relations with Sweden, Norway and Denmark. While Finland differs from other Nordic countries in this respect, some authors call it Scandinavian due to its economic and cultural similarities."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "rat", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3344, "target_cluster_name": "rat", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Norway is a core part of the Scandinavian region.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Norway is a core part of the Scandinavian region.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Denmark", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1030, "target_cluster_name": "Danemark", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Denmark is a core constituent country of Scandinavia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Denmark is a core constituent country of Scandinavia."}, {"found_name": "Norway", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 342, "target_cluster_name": "Norwège", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Norway is a core constituent country of Scandinavia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Norway is a core constituent country of Scandinavia."}, {"found_name": "Sweden", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1869, "target_cluster_name": "Sweden", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sweden is a core constituent country of Scandinavia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Sweden is a core constituent country of Scandinavia."}, {"found_name": "Europe", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 30, "target_cluster_name": "Europe", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Scandinavia is a subregion of northern Europe.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Scandinavia is a subregion of northern Europe."}, {"found_name": "Baltic Sea", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 319, "target_cluster_name": "Baltic", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Baltic Sea borders and is closely associated with Scandinavia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Baltic Sea borders and is closely associated with Scandinavia."}]}, {"canonical_name": "cacao", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "cacao", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "cacao", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 12, "variants": ["CACAO", "Cacao", "cacao"], "contexts": ["product traded on the boat", "product for European trade"]}, {"entity_id": "cacao", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "cacao", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["cacao"], "contexts": ["plant requiring hot climate"]}, {"entity_id": "cacao", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Cacao", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cacao"], "contexts": ["fruit used as currency by Indians"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "cacao", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "cacao", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "cacao", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Cacao", "similarity": 0.901}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "cacao", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "Cacao", "similarity": 0.901}], "id": 811, "stable_key": "clu_7234c73e9a71e513", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cacao", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Theobroma cacao Linnaeus", "family": "Malvaceae", "wikidata_id": "Q42385", "wikidata_description": "tree native to tropical South America producing cocoa beans - the source plant of cacao and chocolate", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theobroma%20cacao", "wikipedia_extract": "Theobroma cacao (cacao tree or cocoa tree) is a small (6–12 m (20–39 ft) tall) evergreen tree in the Malvaceae family. Its seeds—cocoa beans—are used to make chocolate liquor, cocoa solids, cocoa butter and chocolate. Although the tree is native to the tropics of the Americas, the largest producer of cocoa beans in 2022 was Ivory Coast. The plants leaves are alternate, entire, unlobed, 10–50 cm (4–20 in) long and 5–10 cm (2–4 in) broad. The flowers are produced in clusters directly on the trunk and older branches; this is known as cauliflory. The flowers are small, 1–2 cm (3⁄8–13⁄16 in) diameter, with pink calyx."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "café", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 642, "target_cluster_name": "café", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are tropical plants cultivated for their seeds, which are used to produce popular beverages.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are tropical plants cultivated for their seeds, which are used to produce popular beverages.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "tropical plants", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2853, "target_cluster_name": "tropical plants", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cacao is a tropical plant native to the Americas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cacao is a tropical plant native to the Americas.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Coca", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "ta