"medical condition"]}, {"entity_id": "abortion", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "ABortion", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 9, "variants": ["ABortion", "Abortion", "Abortment", "abortion", "abortment"], "contexts": ["condition prevented by plantain root decoction", "risk associated with Briony use"]}, {"entity_id": "abortire", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "abortire", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 3, "variants": ["abortire", "abortive"], "contexts": ["miscarriage", "medical condition of miscarriage"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "abortion", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "ABortion", "similarity": 0.89}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "abortion", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "abortire", "similarity": 0.983}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "ABortion", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "abortire", "similarity": 0.881}], "id": 823, "stable_key": "clu_b57bcb85da5c7ed3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "abortion", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "The premature expulsion of a fetus from the uterus.", "wikipedia_extract": "Abortion is the termination of a pregnancy by removal or expulsion of an embryo or fetus. The unmodified word abortion generally refers to induced abortion, or deliberate actions to end a pregnancy. Abortion occurring without intervention is known as spontaneous abortion or \"miscarriage\", and occurs in roughly 30–40% of all pregnancies. Common reasons for inducing an abortion are birth-timing and limiting family size. Other reasons include maternal health, an inability to afford a child, domestic violence, lack of support, feelings of being too young, wishing to complete an education or advance a career, and not being able, or willing, to raise a child conceived as a result of rape or incest. When done legally in industrialized societies, induced abortion is one of the safest procedures in medicine."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Ptolemy", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "ptolemy", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Ptolemy", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ptolemy"], "contexts": ["ancient astronomer and geographer"]}, {"entity_id": "ptolemy", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ptolemy", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ptolemy"], "contexts": ["ancient geographer and astronomer"]}, {"entity_id": "ptolemies", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ptolemies", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ptolemies"], "contexts": ["dynasty of rulers"]}, {"entity_id": "ptolemy", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Ptolemy", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 10, "variants": ["Ptolemy"], "contexts": ["ancient astronomer", "ancient astronomer and geographer"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ptolemy", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ptolemy", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ptolemy", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ptolemies", "similarity": 0.92}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Ptolemy", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ptolemy", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Ptolemy", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ptolemy", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Ptolemies", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Ptolemy", "similarity": 0.92}], "id": 824, "stable_key": "clu_afc9d36c9ee9b66a", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ptolemy", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 100, "death_year": 170, "description": "Ancient astronomer, geographer, and mathematician", "note": "References may include the ruler dynasty, but astronomical context is primary.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "male given name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy%20%28name%29", "wikipedia_extract": "Ptolemy (Ancient Greek: Πτολεμαῖος, Ptolemaios) is a male given name, derived from Ancient Greek and meaning 'warlike'. It is formed from the Epic Greek πτόλεμος ptolemos meaning 'war'. The name was used throughout the Greek world, but was particularly popular in ancient Macedon and its nobility. The earliest recorded use of the name is in the Iliad of Homer. During the Hellenistic period, Ptolemy I Soter, a general of Alexander the Great, founded the Ptolemaic dynasty which ruled their Kingdom in Ancient Egypt. All male rulers of the dynasty bore the name 'Ptolemy', the last being Ptolemy XII Auletes, father of Cleopatra."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Strabo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 296, "target_cluster_name": "Strabo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential ancient geographers whose works were foundational for later geographical understanding.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were influential ancient geographers whose works were foundational for later geographical understanding.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Alexander the Great", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 697, "target_cluster_name": "Alexandre", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent figures in the Hellenistic world, with Ptolemy being one of Alexander's generals and a founder of a dynasty.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent figures in the Hellenistic world, with Ptolemy being one of Alexander's generals and a founder of a dynasty."}, {"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ptolemy was a major figure in the continuation and development of Aristotelian scientific traditions, particularly in astronomy and geography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ptolemy was a major figure in the continuation and development of Aristotelian scientific traditions, particularly in astronomy and geography."}, {"found_name": "Hipparchus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 909, "target_cluster_name": "Hipparchus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ptolemy built upon and synthesized the astronomical work of Hipparchus, who was a foundational figure in Greek astronomy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ptolemy built upon and synthesized the astronomical work of Hipparchus, who was a foundational figure in Greek astronomy."}, {"found_name": "Eratosthenes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1129, "target_cluster_name": "Eratosthenes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential Greek scholars who made significant contributions to geography and astronomy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were influential Greek scholars who made significant contributions to geography and astronomy."}, {"found_name": "Euclide", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2493, "target_clu