cies of amniotes (land animals with internal bones) have ligaments. It is also known as articular ligament, articular larua, fibrous ligament, or true ligament. Ligaments are similar to tendons and fasciae as they are all made of connective tissue. The differences among them are in the connections that they make: ligaments connect one bone to another bone, tendons connect muscle to bone, and fasciae connect muscles to other muscles.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ligament"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Feet", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 134, "target_cluster_name": "Feet", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Limbs are appendages of the body, and the foot is a part of a limb.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Limbs are appendages of the body, and the foot is a part of a limb.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "spine", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 457, "target_cluster_name": "spine", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ligaments connect the bones of the spine, providing stability and allowing for movement.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ligaments connect the bones of the spine, providing stability and allowing for movement.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "parts", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 467, "target_cluster_name": "parts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ligaments are connective tissues that attach bones to bones, and are considered part of the musculoskeletal system, closely related to body parts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ligaments are connective tissues that attach bones to bones, and are considered part of the musculoskeletal system, closely related to body parts.", "