hich is primarily calcium carbonate."}, {"found_name": "Iceland spar", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1763, "target_cluster_name": "Iceland spar", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iceland spar is a transparent variety of calcite, a mineral form of calcium carbonate.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Iceland spar is a transparent variety of calcite, a mineral form of calcium carbonate."}, {"found_name": "marmo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1062, "target_cluster_name": "marmo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Marble is primarily composed of calcium carbonate.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Marble is primarily composed of calcium carbonate.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "salts", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1114, "target_cluster_name": "salts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calcium carbonate is a common salt, often referred to by its common name 'Lime' in historical texts, and its properties and formation are related to the broader category of salts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Calcium carbonate is a common salt, often referred to by its common name 'Lime' in historical texts, and its properties and formation are related to the broader category of salts.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "alkalies", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 21, "members": [{"entity_id": "alkalies", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "alkalies", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["alkalies"], "contexts": ["in the alkalies, metals discovered", "chemical compounds in Earth's nucleus"]}, {"entity_id": "alkalies", "