cal orbit serves as the baseline from which perturbations are measured."}, {"found_name": "Centrifugal force", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 315, "target_cluster_name": "Centrifugal force", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Centrifugal force is a key concept in understanding orbital mechanics. Perturbations can alter the balance of forces, including centrifugal force, affecting an orbit.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Centrifugal force is a key concept in understanding orbital mechanics. Perturbations can alter the balance of forces, including centrifugal force, affecting an orbit."}, {"found_name": "Attraction (physics)", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4186, "target_cluster_name": "attractions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Orbital perturbations are caused by deviations in the gravitational attraction between celestial bodies. Understanding attraction is fundamental to understanding perturbations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Orbital perturbations are caused by deviations in the gravitational attraction between celestial bodies. Understanding attraction is fundamental to understanding perturbations."}]}, {"canonical_name": "combustion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "combustion", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "combustion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["combustion"], "contexts": ["process of burning"]}, {"entity_id": "combustion", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "combustion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 10, "variants": ["combustion", "Combustion"], "contexts": ["process of burning", "rapid chemical reaction producing heat"]}, {"entity_id": "combustion", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "combustion", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["combustion"], "contexts": ["rapid chemical reaction with heat and light"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "combustion", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "combustion", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "combustion", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "combustion", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "combustion", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "combustion", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 866, "stable_key": "clu_19bdf3faee73007f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Combustion", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q133235", "wikidata_description": "high-temperature exothermic redox chemical reaction between a fuel (the reductant) and an oxidant, usually atmospheric oxygen, that produces oxidized, often gaseous products, in a mixture termed as smoke", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combustion", "wikipedia_extract": "Combustion, or burning, is a high-temperature exothermic redox chemical reaction between a fuel (the reductant) and an oxidant, usually atmospheric oxygen, that produces oxidized, often gaseous products, in a mixture termed as smoke. Combustion does not always result in fire, because a flame is only visible when substances undergoing combustion vaporize, but when it does, a flame is a characteristic indicator of the reaction. While activation energy must be supplied to initiate combustion (e.g., using a lit match to light a fire), the heat from a flame may provide enough energy to make the reaction self-sustaining. The study of combustion is known as combustion science. Combustion is often a complicated sequence of elementary radical reactions. Solid fuels, such as wood and coal, first undergo endothermic pyrolysis to produce gaseous fuels whose combustion then supplies the heat required to produce more of them."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "fogo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 542, "target_cluster_name": "fogo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is a chemical process that involves rapid reaction between a substance with an oxidant, usually oxygen, to produce heat and light. Fire is the visible effect of combustion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Combustion is a chemical process that involves rapid reaction between a substance with an oxidant, usually oxygen, to produce heat and light. Fire is the visible effect of combustion.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Chemistry", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 304, "target_cluster_name": "Chemistry", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is a key process studied within chemistry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Combustion is a key process studied within chemistry.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "chemical combination", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 781, "target_cluster_name": "chemical combination", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is a specific type of chemical reaction that involves rapid reaction between a substance with an oxidant, usually oxygen, to produce heat and light, often resulting in chemical combination.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Combustion is a specific type of chemical reaction that involves rapid reaction between a substance with an oxidant, usually oxygen, to produce heat and light, often resulting in chemical combination.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Explosion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3650, "target_cluster_name": "explosion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion can lead to explosions, especially when rapid and contained.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Combustion can lead to explosions, especially when rapid and contained."}, {"found_name": "Evaporation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2390, "target_cluster_name": "évaporation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both processes involve a change of state, often driven by heat, though combustion is a chemical reaction and evaporation is a physical process.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both processes involve a change of state, often driven by heat, though combustion is a chemical reaction and evaporation is a physical process."}, {"found_name": "Heat", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 197, "target_cluster_name": "calor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is an exothermic reaction that produces heat.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Combustion is an exothermic reaction that produces heat."}, {"found_name": "Fire", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 542, "target_cluster_name": "fogo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is the chemical process that underlies fire.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Combustion is the chemical process that underlies fire."}, {"found_name": "Respiração", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 898, "target_cluster_name": "Respiração", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historical 