professor proving moon's light effect on thermometer"]}, {"entity_id": "e__forbes", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "E. Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 7, "variants": ["E. Forbes"], "contexts": ["speaks confidently about shell coloration", "researches on marine life and depths"]}, {"entity_id": "j__forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "J. Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["J. Forbes"], "contexts": ["invented seismometer", "Professor who invented a self-registering apparatus"]}, {"entity_id": "e__forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "E. Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["E. Forbes"], "contexts": ["professor providing account of Santorino"]}, {"entity_id": "edward_forbes", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Edward Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Edward Forbes"], "contexts": ["admirable palæontologist", "insisted islands connected to continents"]}, {"entity_id": "professor_edward_forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Professor Edward Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Professor Edward Forbes"], "contexts": ["professor and scientific friend"]}, {"entity_id": "edward_forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Edward Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Edward Forbes"], "contexts": ["Professor discussing origin and diffusion of flora"]}, {"entity_id": "edward_forbes", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Edward Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Edward Forbes"], "contexts": ["described naturalists examining animals as skins"]}, {"entity_id": "professor_e__forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Professor E. Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Professor E. Forbes"], "contexts": ["co-author of 'Travels in Lycia'"]}, {"entity_id": "professor_forbes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Professor Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Professor Forbes"], "contexts": ["remarks on distribution of faunas and floras"]}, {"entity_id": "professor_forbes", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Professor Forbes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Professor Forbes"], "contexts": ["scientist who studied solar eclipse", "of Edinburgh, prosecuted subject with success"]}, {"entity_id": "forbes,_professor_e_", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Forbes, Professor E.", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Forbes, Professor E."], "contexts": ["researcher on travels and islands"]}, {"entity_id": "forbes,_professor", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Forbes, Professor", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Forbes, Professor"], "contexts": ["scientist making temperature observations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Forbes", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Forbes", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 912, "stable_key": "clu_7faf6163b71499cd", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Edward Forbes", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "A naturalist and geologist, known for his conclusions on biogeography.", "note": "Distinguished from Forbes Winslow, a different author.", "wikipedia_extract": "Edward Forbes FRS, FGS (12 February 1815 – 18 November 1854) was a Manx naturalist. In 1846, he proposed that the distributions of montane plants and animals had been compressed downslope, and some oceanic islands connected to the mainland, during the recent ice age. This mechanism, which was the first natural explanation to explain the distributions of the same species on now-isolated islands and mountain tops, was discovered independently by Charles Darwin, who credited Forbes with the idea. He also incorrectly deduced the so-called azoic hypothesis, that life under the sea would decline to the point that no life forms could exist below a certain depth. Forbes was born at Douglas in the Isle of Man. His father was a well-to-do banker.", "birth_year": 1815, "death_year": 1854}, "member_count": 15, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alfred Russel Wallace", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2104, "target_cluster_name": "Wallace", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent naturalists who made significant contributions to biogeography and evolutionary theory. Forbes's work on glacial refugia and island biogeography predated and influenced Wallace's later work.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent naturalists who made significant contributions to biogeography and evolutionary theory. Forbes's work on glacial refugia and island biogeography predated and influenced Wallace's later work."}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential naturalists and explorers who conducted extensive fieldwork and made significant contributions to understanding the distribution of life on Earth. Humboldt's work on plant geography and Forbes's work on biogeography are closely related.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were influential naturalists and explorers who conducted extensive fieldwork and made significant contributions to understanding the distribution of life on Earth. Humboldt's work on plant geography and Forbes's work on biogeography are closely related."}, {"found_name": "Charles Lyell", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1710, "target_cluster_name": "Lyell", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lyell was a foundational figure in geology, and Forbes's theories on glacial periods and their impact on species distribution were directly informed by Lyell's work on uniformitarianism and geological time.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Lyell was a foundational figure in geology, and Forbes's theories on glacial periods and their impact on species distribution were directly informed by Lyell's work on uniformitarianism and geological time."}, {"found_name": "Hugh Edwin Strickland", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3966, "target_cluster_name": "Strickland", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent naturalists and ornithologists of the mid-19th century, collaborating and corresponding on various scientific matters, including taxonomy and biogeography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent naturalists and ornithologists of the mid-19th century, collaborating and corresponding on various scientific matters, including taxonomy and biogeography."}]}, {"canonical_name": "fossiliferous strata", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 10, "members": [{"entity_id": "fossiliferous_strata", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "fossiliferous strata", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["fossiliferous strata"], "contexts": ["rock layers containing fossils"]}, {"entity_id": "palæozoic_strata", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Palæozoic strata", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER