e to describe substances that could expand and contract, a characteristic often associated with gases.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Mysore", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "mysore", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Mysore", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 4, "variants": ["Mysore", "Mysoïle"], "contexts": ["location with barometric heights", "location of Kater's observations"]}, {"entity_id": "mysore", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Mysore", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mysore"], "contexts": ["location with granite masses"]}, {"entity_id": "mysore", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Mysore", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 4, "variants": ["Mysore"], "contexts": ["region where cardamom is found", "region in India"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mysore", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Mysore", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mysore", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Mysore", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Mysore", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Mysore", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 965, "stable_key": "clu_1b12950d3b6efcbc", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Mysore", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A historical region and city in Karnataka, India.", "wikipedia_extract": "Mysore (  my-SOR), officially Mysuru (Kannada: [ˈmaɪˈsuːɾu] ), is a city in the southern Indian state of Karnataka. It is the headquarters of Mysore district and Mysore division. As the traditional seat of the Wadiyar dynasty, the city functioned as the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore for almost six centuries (1399 to 1947). Known for its heritage structures, palaces (such as the famous Mysore Palace), and its culture, Mysore has been called the \"City of Palaces\", the \"Heritage City\", and the \"Cultural capital of Karnataka\". It is the second-most populous city in the state and one of the cleanest cities in India according to the Swachh Survekshan. Mysore is situated at the foothills of the Chamundi Hills."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Volta", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "volta", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Volta", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Volta"], "contexts": ["inventor of the electrometer", "inventor of eudiometer"]}, {"entity_id": "volta", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Volta", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Volta"], "contexts": ["inventor of the electrometer", "proposed method for electrometer"]}, {"entity_id": "volta", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Volta", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Volta"], "contexts": ["Professor at Pavia", "called into existence the fiery stream"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Volta", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Volta", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Volta", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Volta", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Volta", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Volta", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 966, "stable_key": "clu_eaad1b0044f20a1b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Alessandro Volta", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1745, "death_year": 1827, "description": "Italian physicist, inventor of the voltaic pile and electric battery.", "wikidata_id": "Q680", "wikidata_description": "Italian physicist, chemist, and pioneer of electricity and power (1745-1827)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alessandro%20Volta", "wikipedia_extract": "Alessandro Giuseppe Antonio Anastasio Volta (UK: , US: ; Italian: [alesˈsandro dʒuˈzɛppe anˈtɔnjo anasˈtaːzjo ˈvɔlta]; 18 February 1745 – 5 March 1827) was an Italian chemist and physicist who was a pioneer of electricity and power, and is credited as the inventor of the electric battery and the discoverer of methane. He invented the voltaic pile in 1799, and reported the results of his experiments in a two-part letter to the president of the Royal Society, which was published in 1800. With this invention, Volta proved that electricity could be generated chemically and debunked the prevalent theory that electricity was generated solely by living beings. Volta's invention sparked a great amount of scientific excitement and led others to conduct similar experiments, which eventually led to the development of the field of electrochemistry. Volta drew admiration from Napoleon Bonaparte for his invention, and was invited to the Institute of France to demonstrate his invention to the members of the institute. Throughout his life, Volta enjoyed a certain amount of closeness with the emperor who conferred upon him numerous honours."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Faraday", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 248, "target_cluster_name": "Faraday", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volta was a key figure in the development of electricity, a field in which Faraday made foundational contributions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Volta was a key figure in the development of electricity, a field in which Faraday made foundational contributions.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Lavoisier", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 475, "target_cluster_name": "Lavoisier", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were pivotal figures in the development of chemistry and physics, with Volta's work on electricity being foundational for many later scientific advancements, including those in chemistry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were pivotal figures in the development of chemistry and physics, with Volta's work on electricity being foundational for many later scientific advancements, including those in chemistry.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "physiciens", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 692, "target_cluster_name": "physiciens", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volta was a pioneering physicist known for the invention of the voltaic pile, a precursor to the electric battery, and his work on electricity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Volta was a pioneering physicist known for the invention of the voltaic pile, a precursor to the electric battery, and his work on electricity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Ritter", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1050, "target_cluster_name": "Ritter", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Volta's invention of the voltaic pile was a foundational development in electricity, a field that Ritter also explored, particularly in relation to chemical effects and light.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Volta's invention of the voltaic pile was a foundational development in electricity, a field that Ritter also explored, particularly in relation to chemical effects and light.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Matteucci", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1078, "target_cluster_name": "Matteucci", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent Italian physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its applications. Volta's work on the voltaic pile directly preceded and influenced later studies in bioelectricity, an area Matteucci pioneered.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent Italian physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its applications. Volta's work on the voltaic pile directly preceded and influenced later studies in bioelectricity, an area Matteucci pioneered.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Fahrenheit", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1629, "target_cluster_name": "Fahrenheit", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent physicists and inventors who made significant contributions to scientific instrumentation and measurement.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent physicists and inventors who made significant contributions to scientific instrumentation and measurement.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Chladni", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2131, "target_cluster_name": "Chladni", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its properties.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its properties.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Ampère", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2134, "target_cluster_name": "Ampère", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were pioneering physicists and mathematicians who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and magnetism. Volta is known for the voltaic pile, a precursor to the battery, while Ampère is renowned for his foundational work on electromagnetism, including Ampère's law.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were pioneering physicists and mathematicians who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and magnetism. Volta is known for the voltaic pile, a precursor to the battery, while Ampère is renowned for his foundational work on electromagnetism, including Ampère's law.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Becquerel", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2216, "target_cluster_name": "Becquerel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its phenomena. Volta is known for the voltaic pile, a precursor to the battery, while Becquerel's work laid groundwork for understanding photoelectric effects.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent physicists who made significant contributions to the understanding of electricity and its phenomena. Volta is known for the voltaic pile, a precursor to the battery, while Becquerel's work laid groundwork for understanding photoelectric effects.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Melloni", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2444, "target_cluster_name": "Melloni", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Melloni was a physicist who studied electricity and magnetism, and Volta was a pioneering physicist in the same fields.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Melloni was a physicist who studied electricity and magnetism, and Volta was a pioneering physicist in the same fields.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Oersted", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2447, "target_cluster_name": "Oersted", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were pioneering physicists in the field of electricity. Volta's invention of the voltaic pile and Oersted's discovery of electromagnetism are key milestones in the early study of electricity and magnetism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were pioneering physicists in the field of electricity. Volta's invention of the voltaic pile and Oersted's discovery of electromagnetism are key milestones in the early study of electricity and magnetism.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Bordeaux", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "bordeaux", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Bordeaux", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Bordeaux"], "contexts": ["city in France", "city between 30° and 45° latitude"]}, {"entity_id": "bordeaux", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Bordeaux", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Bordeaux"], "contexts": ["city where Dr. Azam practiced"]}, {"entity_id": "bordeaux", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Bordeaux", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 6, "variants": ["Bordeaux"], "contexts": ["city in France", "location of Biot's pendulum observations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bordeaux", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "Bordeaux", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bordeaux", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Bordeaux", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Bordeaux", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Bordeaux", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 967, "stable_key": "clu_dda34420e56bd721", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Bordeaux ( bor-DOH; French: [bɔrdo] ; Gascon Occitan: Bordèu [buɾˈðɛw]; Basque: Bordele) is a city on the river Garonne in the Gironde department, southwestern France. A port city, it is the capital of the Nouvelle-Aquitaine region, as well as the prefecture of the Gironde department. Its inhabitants are called \"Bordelais\" (masculine) or \"Bordelaises\" (feminine). The term \"Bordelais\" may also refer to the city and its surrounding region. The city of Bordeaux proper had a population of 259,809 in 2020 within its small municipal territory of 49 km2 (19 sq mi), but together with its suburbs and exurbs the Bordeaux metropolitan area had a population of 1,376,375 that same year (Jan. 2020 census), the sixth-most populated in France after Paris, Lyon, Marseille, Lille, and Toulouse. Bordeaux and 27 suburban municipalities form the Bordeaux Metropolis, an indirectly elected metropolitan authority now in charge of wider metropolitan issues."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Bokhara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "bokhara", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Bokhara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Bokhara"], "contexts": ["city with a man-made mountain", "city in Asia"]}, {"entity_id": "bokhara", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Bokhara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Bokhara"], "contexts": ["city with clear atmosphere for astronomy", "location with pure atmosphere"]}, {"entity_id": "bokhára", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Bokhára", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Bokhára", "Bokhara"], "contexts": ["birthplace of Avicenna", "city in Uzbeque"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bokhara", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Bokhara", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Bokhara", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Bokhára", "similarity": 0.93}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Bokhara", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Bokhára", "similarity": 0.93}], "id": 968, "stable_key": "clu_a062ac2318677bf1", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Bukhara", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Historic city in Uzbekistan, a Silk Road hub.", "wikipedia_extract": "Bukhara ( buu-KHAR-ə) is the seventh-largest city in Uzbekistan by population, with 280,187 residents as of 1 January 2020. It is the capital of Bukhara Region. The Bukhara region has been inhabited for at least five millennia, and the city has existed for half that time. Located on the Silk Road, the city has long served as a center of trade, scholarship, culture, and religion. Bukhara served as the capital of the Uzbek states such as the Khanate of Bukhara, the Emirate of Bukhara and later the Bukhara People’s Soviet Republic. It was the birthplace of the scholar Imam Bukhari."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Bocara", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 4438, "target_cluster_name": "Bocara", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Bokhara is listed as a historical name for Bukhara.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Bokhara is listed as a historical name for Bukhara.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Guadalupe", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": 