disease that affects babies in which the platelet count is decreased because the mother's immune system attacks her fetus' or newborn's platelets. A low platelet count increases the risk of bleeding in the fetus and newborn. If the bleeding occurs in the brain, there may be long-term effects. Platelet antigens are inherited from both mother and father. NAIT is caused by antibodies specific for platelet antigens inherited from the father but which are absent in the mother. Fetomaternal transfusions (or fetomaternal hemorrhage) results in the recognition of these antigens by the mother's immune system as non-self, with the subsequent generation of allo-reactive antibodies which cross the placenta.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neonatal_alloimmune_thrombocytopenia"}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Polipodio", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 666, "target_cluster_name": "Polipodio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Polypody is a genus of ferns.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Polypody is a genus of ferns.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Maidenhair", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2520, "target_cluster_name": "Maidenhair", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Maidenhair Fern is a specific type of Fern.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Maidenhair Fern is a specific type of Fern.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Maidenhair Fern", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 788, "target_cluster_name": "avenca", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Maidenhair Fern is a specific type of fern.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Maidenhair Fern is a specific type of fern."}, {"found_name": "French Mercury", "