 "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3567, "target_cluster_name": "free-will", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historical discussions often explore the tension between 'passion' (as an impulse) and 'free will' (as rational choice).", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historical discussions often explore the tension between 'passion' (as an impulse) and 'free will' (as rational choice)."}, {"found_name": "Love", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 430, "target_cluster_name": "Love", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "While 'love' is not in the candidate list, 'passion' is frequently used to describe an intense form of love or romantic desire.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "While 'love' is not in the candidate list, 'passion' is frequently used to describe an intense form of love or romantic desire."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Eſpinal Medulla", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "medulla", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "medulla", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["medulla"], "contexts": ["part of the brainstem"]}, {"entity_id": "medulla", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "medulla", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["medulla"], "contexts": ["inner part of a plant", "part of the trunk observed"]}, {"entity_id": "eſpinal_medulla", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Eſpinal Medulla", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Eſpinal Medulla", "eſpinal medulla"], "contexts": ["spinal cord", "part of the nervous system connected to uterus"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "medulla", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "medulla", "similarity": 0.787}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "medulla", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Eſpinal Medulla", "similarity": 0.902}], "id": 1043, "stable_key": "clu_1cda65df20bb639c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Spinal Cord", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "The central nerve pathway connecting the brain to the body.", "note": "Refers to the spinal cord and the inner part of a plant stem.", "wikipedia_extract": "The spinal cord is a long, thin, tubular structure made up of nervous tissue that extends from the medulla oblongata in the lower brainstem to the lumbar region of the vertebral column (backbone) of vertebrate animals. The center of the spinal cord is hollow and contains a structure called the central canal, which contains cerebrospinal fluid. The spinal cord is also covered by the meninges and enclosed by the neural arches. Together, the brain and spinal cord make up the central nervous system. In humans, the spinal cord is a continuation of the brainstem and anatomically begins at the occipital bone, passing out of the foramen magnum and then enters the spinal canal at the beginning of the cervical vertebrae. The spinal cord extends down to between the first and second lumbar vertebrae, where it tapers to become the cauda equina."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "nerve-tissue", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2577, "target_cluster_name": "nerve-tissue", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A major component of the central nervous system, composed of nervous tissue.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A major component of the central nervous system, composed of nervous tissue.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "nervous actions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2584, "target_cluster_name": "nervous actions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The spinal cord is a major component of the central nervous system, crucial for transmitting signals and coordinating nervous actions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The spinal cord is a major component of the central nervous system, crucial for transmitting signals and coordinating nervous actions.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "aromi", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "perfume", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "perfume", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["perfume"], "contexts": ["type of odor", "pleasant smell"]}, {"entity_id": "aromi", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "aromi", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 4, "variants": ["aromi", "aroma"], "contexts": ["aromatic substances used in medicines", "aromatic substances used in trochisci"]}, {"entity_id": "aromas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "aromas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["aromas"], "contexts": ["fedores pareção aromas", "aromas"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "perfume", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "aromi", "similarity": 0.893}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "perfume", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "aromas", "similarity": 0.924}, {"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "aromi", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "aromas", "similarity": 0.959}], "id": 1044, "stable_key": "clu_898326ea614f6f32", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "aromas", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Pleasant or sweet smells; fragrances used in medicine.", "wikipedia_extract": "A fragrance compound (or fragrance) is a chemical compound with a pleasant odor. Fragrances affect only the sense of smell, whereas flavors can affect both the sense of taste and smell. Fragrances are often mixtures of individual fragrance compounds. Although many fragrances are derived from natural sources, many are synthetic. Fragrances are widely used in cosmetics and are the basis for a large industry. Stench compounds have unpleasant odors."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Balsamis", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2936, "target_cluster_name": "Balsamis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Balsams are often used for their aromatic properties and are derived from plants known for their scents.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Balsams are often used for their aromatic properties and are derived from plants known for their scents.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Aromaticum Rosarum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2702, "target_cluster_name": "Aromaticum Rosarum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Aromaticum Rosarum is a specific preparation that would contain aromas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Aromaticum Rosarum is a specific preparation that would contain aromas."}, {"found_name": "alcanfor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1614, "target_cluster_name": "alcanfor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Camphor is known for its strong aroma, and 'aromas' is a general term for fragrant substances.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Camphor is known for its strong aroma, and 'aromas' is a general term for fragrant substances.", 