n is a crucial mechanism for the integration of immigrants into a society.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Pythagoreans", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2504, "target_cluster_name": "Pythagoreans", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pythagoras established communities that served as centers of learning and education.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Pythagoras established communities that served as centers of learning and education.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Simples", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "simples", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Simples", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Simples"], "contexts": ["basic medicinal ingredients"]}, {"entity_id": "simples", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Simples", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Simples"], "contexts": ["nature of single medicinal substances", "natural materials gathered for medicinal use"]}, {"entity_id": "semplici", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Semplici", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Semplici", "semplici"], "contexts": ["simple substances", "simple medicinal ingredients"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Simples", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Simples", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Simples", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Semplici", "similarity": 0.976}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Simples", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Semplici", "similarity": 0.976}], "id": 1065, "stable_key": "clu_9142e61da60c7466", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Simple Medicines", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "Single medicinal substances derived directly from nature, often plants.", "note": "Refers to the uncompounded ingredients used in traditional medicine.", "wikipedia_extract": "Ascorbic acid is an organic compound with formula C6H8O6, originally called hexuronic acid. It is a white solid, but impure samples can appear yellowish. It dissolves freely in water to give mildly acidic solutions. It is a mild reducing agent. Ascorbic acid exists as two enantiomers (mirror-image isomers), commonly denoted \"l\" (for \"levo\") and \"d\" (for \"dextro\"). The l isomer is the one most often encountered: it occurs naturally in many foods, and is one form (\"vitamer\") of vitamin C, an essential nutrient for humans and many animals."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "medicamente", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2482, "target_cluster_name": "medicamente", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The term 'Simple Medicines' (Simples) refers to basic, uncompounded medicinal substances, which are a type of medicament.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: The term 'Simple Medicines' (Simples) refers to basic, uncompounded medicinal substances, which are a type of medicament.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Aromaticum Rosarum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2702, "target_cluster_name": "Aromaticum Rosarum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Aromaticum Rosarum is a specific preparation that would have been composed of various 'simples', particularly aromatic ones.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Aromaticum Rosarum is a specific preparation that would have been composed of various 'simples', particularly aromatic ones."}, {"found_name": "Diarhodon Abhatis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2950, "target_cluster_name": "Diarhodon Abhatis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diarhodon Abhatis is a specific medicinal preparation that would have been composed of various 'simples'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Diarhodon Abhatis is a specific medicinal preparation that would have been composed of various 'simples'."}]}, {"canonical_name": "rhinoceros", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 11, "members": [{"entity_id": "rhinoceros", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Rhinoceros", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Rhinoceros"], "contexts": ["animal with a single sex"]}, {"entity_id": "rhinoceros", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "rhinoceros", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 4, "variants": ["rhinoceros"], "contexts": ["large herbivorous mammal", "large mammal, not destroyed by beasts of prey"]}, {"entity_id": "rhinoceros", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "rhinoceros", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["rhinoceros"], "contexts": ["extant animal found as fossil"]}, {"entity_id": "rhinoceroses", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "rhinoceroses", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "MAMMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["rhinoceroses"], "contexts": ["extant large mammal"]}, {"entity_id": "abada", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "abada", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Abada", "abada"], "contexts": ["animal sent as a gift", "name for rhinoceros"]}, {"entity_id": "abada", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Abada", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Abada"], "contexts": ["animal product, likely a type of animal"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Rhinoceros", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "rhinoceros", "similarity": 0.736}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Rhinoceros", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "rhinoceros", "similarity": 0.736}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "rhinoceros", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "rhinoceros", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "rhinoceros", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "rhinoceroses", "similarity": 0.921}], "id": 1066, "stable_key": "clu_4b328dc0efcdb235", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Rhinoceros", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "wikidata_id": "Q134657", "wikidata_description": "genus of mammals", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhinoceros%20%28genus%29", "wikipedia_extract": "A rhinoceros ( ry-NOSS-ə-rəss; from Ancient Greek  ῥινόκερως (rhinókerōs) 'nose-horned'; from  ῥίς (rhis) 'nose' and  κέρας (kéras) 'horn'; pl.: rhinoceros or rhinoceroses), commonly abbreviated to rhino, is a member of any of the five extant species (or numerous extinct species) of odd-toed ungulates (perissodactyls) in the family Rhinocerotidae. It is the only living family in the superfamily Rhinocerotoidea (whose members are also sometimes called rhinoceroses). Two of the extant species are native to Africa, and three to South and Southeast Asia. Rhinoceroses are some of the largest remaining megafauna: all weigh over half a tonne in adulthood. They have a herbivorous diet, small brains 400–600 g (14–21 oz) for mammals of their size, one or two horns, and a thick 1.5–5 cm (0.59–1.97 in), protective skin formed from layers of collagen positioned in a lattice structure. They generally eat leafy material, although their ability to ferment food in their hindgut allows them to subsist on more fibrous plant matter when necessary.", "note": "While 'abada' can refer to a rhinoceros in Portuguese, the context of being sent as a gift might also suggest other exotic animals. However, rhinoceros horn was a known medicinal substance."}, "member_count": 6, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "guerras", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 483, "target_cluster_name": "guerras", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "coiro. ORTA Eu não vi odres de camellos desta terra; posto que no Decam e em o Guzarate ha alguns camellos, que tem os reys e os capitães pêra levar o fato na guerra; mas nem sam tantos os que morrem ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: vernacular name for rhinoceros", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "pachyderms", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2724, "target_cluster_name": "pachyderms", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The historical classification 'pachyderm' was commonly used to describe rhinoceroses, among other thick-skinned mammals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The historical classification 'pachyderm' was commonly used to describe rhinoceroses, among other thick-skinned mammals.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Ibrahim", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "abraham", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Abraham", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Abraham"], "contexts": ["biblical figure"]}, {"entity_id": "ibrahim_ben_ahmed", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ibrahim ben Ahmed", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ibrahim ben Ahmed"], "c