to the establishment of Christianity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are foundational figures in Abrahamic religions. Abraham is the patriarch, and the Apostles are central to the establishment of Christianity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "S. Francisco", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2621, "target_cluster_name": "S. Francisco", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are significant religious figures, with Abraham being a patriarch in Abrahamic religions and Francis of Assisi a major figure in Christianity. Their roles as foundational or exemplary religious figures create a relationship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are significant religious figures, with Abraham being a patriarch in Abrahamic religions and Francis of Assisi a major figure in Christianity. Their roles as foundational or exemplary religious figures create a relationship.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Geography", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "geography", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Geography", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Geography"], "contexts": ["study of the Earth's features"]}, {"entity_id": "geography", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Geography", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Geography", "geography"], "contexts": ["study of landforms and regions", "study of Earth's surface"]}, {"entity_id": "geography", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Geography", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Geography", "geography"], "contexts": ["study of the Earth's surface", "study of Earth's surface"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Geography", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "Geography", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Geography", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Geography", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Geography", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Geography", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1068, "stable_key": "clu_6ca495a6e5c8b5c8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Geography", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q1071", "wikidata_description": "science that studies the terrestrial surface, the societies that inhabit it and the territories, landscapes, places or regions that form it when interacting with each other", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geography", "wikipedia_extract": "Geography (from Ancient Greek γεωγραφία geōgraphía; combining gê 'Earth' and gráphō 'write', literally 'Earth writing') is the study of the lands, features, inhabitants, and phenomena of Earth. Geography is an all-encompassing discipline that seeks an understanding of Earth and its human and natural complexities—not merely where objects are, but also how they have changed and come to be. While geography is specific to Earth, many concepts can be applied more broadly to other celestial bodies in the field of planetary science. Geography has been called \"a bridge between natural science and social science disciplines.\" The history of geography as a discipline spans cultures and millennia, being independently developed by multiple groups, and cross-pollinated by trade between these groups. Geography as a discipline dates back to the earliest attempts to understand the world spatially, with the earliest example of an attempted world map dating to the 9th century BC in ancient Babylon. Origins of many of the concepts in geography can be traced to Greek Eratosthenes of Cyrene, who may have coined the term \"geographia\" (c."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "latitude", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 551, "target_cluster_name": "latitude", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Latitude is a fundamental concept within the field of geography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Latitude is a fundamental concept within the field of geography.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "botany", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1098, "target_cluster_name": "botany", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Botany, particularly plant geography, is a subfield that intersects with geography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Botany, particularly plant geography, is a subfield that intersects with geography.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "sound", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 258, "target_cluster_name": "sound", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sounds are geographical features, and their study falls under the domain of geography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sounds are geographical features, and their study falls under the domain of geography.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Longitude", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 310, "target_cluster_name": "Longitude", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Longitude is a fundamental component of geographical coordinates.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Longitude is a fundamental component of geographical coordinates.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "agriculture", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "ta