ed with the geographical distribution of plants (and other organisms). There is a strong, direct relationship between the study of plant life and the study of where that life is found.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Botany is the study of plants, and biogeography is concerned with the geographical distribution of plants (and other organisms). There is a strong, direct relationship between the study of plant life and the study of where that life is found.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "organic life", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2127, "target_cluster_name": "organic life", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Botany is the study of plant life, a major component of organic life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Botany is the study of plant life, a major component of organic life.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Philosophy of nature", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2682, "target_cluster_name": "Philosophy of nature", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Botany, the scientific study of plants, was a significant area within natural philosophy, contributing to the understanding of the natural world.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Botany, the scientific study of plants, was a significant area within natural philosophy, contributing to the understanding of the natural world.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "akawerya", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "transcripto rametul na versão latina de Clusius, e depois todos citaram na ultima forma. Nem na primeira, nem na ultima forma se encontra; e já o antigo botânico Hermanno, nos rótulos do seu her- barí", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vulgar name for the plant in Ceylao"}]}, {"canonical_name": "understanding", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 5, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "understanding", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "understanding", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["understanding", "Understanding"], "contexts": ["ability to comprehend speech", "faculty of logical thought and judgment"]}, {"entity_id": "understanding", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "understanding", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["understanding"], "contexts": ["faculty for comprehension"]}, {"entity_id": "understanding", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "understanding", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["understanding"], "contexts": ["faculty for reasoning and comprehension"]}, {"entity_id": "entendimiento", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "entendimiento", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["entendimiento"], "contexts": ["faculty Ambar can improve"]}, {"entity_id": "entendimento", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Entendimento", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Entendimento", "conhecimento", "entendimento", "entendimiento"], "contexts": ["faculty of comprehension", "understanding"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "understanding", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "understanding", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "understanding", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "understanding", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "understanding", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "understanding", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1099, "stable_key": "clu_a9b2db5ff8393d2e", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Understanding", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q46744", "wikidata_description": "ability to think about and use concepts to deal adequately with an object", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Understanding", "wikipedia_extract": "Understanding is a cognitive process related to an abstract or physical object, such as a person, situation, or message whereby one is able to use concepts to model that object. Understanding is a relation between the knower and an object of understanding. Understanding implies abilities and dispositions with respect to an object of knowledge that are sufficient to support intelligent behavior. Understanding is often, though not always, related to learning concepts, and sometimes also the theory or theories associated with those concepts. However, a person may have a good ability to predict the behavior of an object, animal or system—and therefore may, in some sense, understand it—without necessarily being familiar with the concepts or theories associated with that object, animal, or system in their culture. They may have developed their own distinct concepts and theories, which may be equivalent, better or worse than the recognized standard concepts and theories of their culture."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Conceivability", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 4248, "target_cluster_name": "conceivability", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The ability to conceive of something is a prerequisite for understanding it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The ability to conceive of something is a prerequisite for understanding it."}, {"found_name": "Belief", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2125, "target_cluster_name": "belief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Understanding often underpins or is intertwined with belief.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Understanding often underpins or is intertwined with belief."}, {"found_name": "vertue", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2161, "target_cluster_name": "vertue", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Understanding, particularly moral understanding, is often considered a virtue or a prerequisite for virtuous action.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Understanding, particularly moral understanding, is often considered a virtue or a prerequisite for virtuous action.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "position", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "position", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "position", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["position"], "contexts": ["location of an entity", "location of the soul"]}, {"entity_id": "position", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "position", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["position"], "contexts": ["location in space"]}, {"entity_id": "position", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "position", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["position"], "contexts": ["changes effect of gravity"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "position", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "position", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psyc