e (e.g., the Vulgate Bible) studied in premodern times."}, {"found_name": "Law", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 377, "target_cluster_name": "law", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Latin was the language of Roman law, and legal terminology and concepts derived from Latin persisted in many European legal systems.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Latin was the language of Roman law, and legal terminology and concepts derived from Latin persisted in many European legal systems."}, {"found_name": "Logic", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 991, "target_cluster_name": "logic", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Latin was the dominant language for philosophical and logical discourse in medieval and early modern Europe, with many key logical terms originating or being transmitted through Latin.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Latin was the dominant language for philosophical and logical discourse in medieval and early modern Europe, with many key logical terms originating or being transmitted through Latin."}, {"found_name": "Fiber", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "hath been propagated by Emblems: and some have been so bad Grammarians as to be deceived by the Name, deriving _Castor à castrando_, whereas the proper Latine word is _Fiber_, and _Castor_ but borrowe", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "the correct Latin word for Castor"}, {"found_name": "Castor", "link_type": "derivation", "link_strength": 0.4, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "hath been propagated by Emblems: and some h