ontologically independent: they are able to exist all by themselves. Another defining feature often attributed to substances is their ability to undergo changes. Changes involve something existing before, during and after the change. They can be described in terms of a persisting substance gaining or losing properties.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Substance_theory"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Constitution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "constitution", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Constitution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Constitution"], "contexts": ["inherent nature or makeup"]}, {"entity_id": "constitution", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "constitution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["constitution"], "contexts": ["innate wide flexibility", "correlated with colour in animals"]}, {"entity_id": "constitution", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Constitution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["constitution", "Constitution"], "contexts": ["composition or structure", "composition or nature of the Moon"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Constitution", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "constitution", "similarity": 0.96}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Constitution", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Constitution", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "constitution", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Constitution", "similarity": 0.96}], "id": 1128, "stable_key": "clu_bd35