", "source_name": "Mayerus", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Mayer", "similarity": 0.87}], "id": 1156, "stable_key": "clu_ac4d4676ba85eab3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tobias Mayer", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1723, "death_year": 1762, "description": "German astronomer, geographer, and mathematician, known for lunar theory.", "wikidata_id": "Q60406", "wikidata_description": "German astronomer", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobias%20Mayer", "wikipedia_extract": "Tobias Mayer (17 February 1723 – 20 February 1762) was a German astronomer famous for his studies of the Moon. He was born at Marbach, in Württemberg, and brought up at Esslingen in poor circumstances. A self-taught mathematician, he earned a living by teaching mathematics while still a youth. He had already published two original geometrical works when, in 1746, he entered J. B. Homann's cartographic establishment at Nuremberg."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alexis Bouvard", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3594, "target_cluster_name": "M. Bouvard", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were astronomers who studied the Moon.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were astronomers who studied the Moon."}, {"found_name": "Friedrich Wilhelm Argelander", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1851, "target_cluster_name": "Argelander", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were astronomers who made significant contributions to lunar studies and star mapping.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were astronomers who made significant contributions to lunar studies and star mapping."}, {"found_name": "George Biddell Airy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2323, "target_cluster_name": "Airy", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent astronomers of their respective eras, with Airy being Astronomer Royal during a period of significant advancement in observational astronomy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent astronomers of their respective eras, with Airy being Astronomer Royal during a period of significant advancement in observational astronomy."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Mexicains", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "mexicains", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Mexicains", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 4, "variants": ["Mexicains"], "contexts": ["people of Mexico", "migrating people"]}, {"entity_id": "mexicans", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Mexicans", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mexicans"], "contexts": ["people known for wild and cruel incursions"]}, {"entity_id": "mexicans", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Mexicans", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mexicans"], "contexts": ["people who used picture-writing"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mexicains", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Mexicans", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mexicains", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Mexicans", "similarity": 0.965}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Mexicans", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Mexicans", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1157, "stable_key": "clu_685c9556e545c86c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Mexicans", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "des