 "dissections of bodies for study"]}, {"entity_id": "anatomy", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Anatomy", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Anatomy"], "contexts": ["study of bodily structure"]}, {"entity_id": "anatomy", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Anatomy", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Anatomy", "anatomy"], "contexts": ["study of the structure of living things", "Study of the body's structure"]}, {"entity_id": "anatomica", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Anatomica", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Anatomica"], "contexts": ["study of anatomy"]}, {"entity_id": "anatomy", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Anatomy", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Anatomy"], "contexts": ["science affecting medicine and hygiene"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "anatomie", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "anatomia", "similarity": 0.996}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "anatomie", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "anatomias", "similarity": 0.979}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "anatomia", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "anatomias", "similarity": 0.977}], "id": 1167, "stable_key": "clu_87b40e0510d7bd9c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Anatomy", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q514", "wikidata_description": "study of the internal structure of organisms and their parts", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anatomy", "wikipedia_extract": "Anatomy (from Ancient Greek  ἀνατομή (anatomḗ) 'dissection') is the branch of morphology concerned with the study of the internal and external structure of organisms and their parts. Anatomy is a branch of natural science that deals with the structural organization of living things. It is an old science, having its beginnings in prehistoric times. Anatomy is inherently tied to developmental biology, embryology, comparative anatomy, evolutionary biology, and phylogeny, as these are the processes by which anatomy is generated, both over immediate and long-term timescales. Anatomy and physiology, which study the structure and function of organisms and their parts respectively, make a natural pair of related disciplines, and are often studied together. Human anatomy is one of the essential basic sciences that are applied in medicine, and is often studied alongside physiology."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Philosophy of nature", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2682, "target_cluster_name": "Philosophy of nature", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anatomy, the study of the structure of living things, was a key discipline within natural philosophy, particularly in understanding the human body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Anatomy, the study of the structure of living things, was a key discipline within natural philosophy, particularly in understanding the human body.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "anatomy", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "evidence_snippet": "closely at the brain and at the ways in which its states may be supposed to condition those of the mind. THE FROG'S NERVE-CENTRES. Both the minute anatomy and the detailed physiology of the brain are ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Sangue di drago", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "sang_de_dragin", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "sang de Dragin", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "count": 1, "variants": ["sang de Dragin"], "contexts": ["red resin"]}, {"entity_id": "fangre_de_drago", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "fangre de Drago", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "count": 1, "variants": ["fangre de Drago"], "contexts": ["dragon's blood resin"]}, {"entity_id": "sangue_di_drago", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Sangue di drago", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "RESIN", "count": 4, "variants": ["Sangue di drago", "sangue di drago", "Sangue di Drago"], "contexts": ["resin from a tree, used in medicine", "dragon's blood resin"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "sang de Dragin", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Sangue di drago", "similarity": 0.882}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "fangre de Drago", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Sangue di drago", "similarity": 0.905}], "id": 1168, "stable_key": "clu_abea320248b4d1cc", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Dragon's blood", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "Resinous substance from certain plants, used in medicine and dyes.", "note": "Refers to the resin collected from various species of Daemonorops, Dracaena, and Croton trees.", "wikipedia_extract": "Dragon's blood is a bright red resin that is obtained from different species of a number of distinct plant genera: Calamus spp. (previously Daemonorops) also including Calamus rotang, Croton, Dracaena and Pterocarpus. The red resin has been in continuous use since ancient times as varnish, medicine, incense, pigment, and dye. A great  degree of confusion existed for the ancients in regard to the source and identity of dragon's blood. Some medieval encyclopedias claimed its source as the literal blood of elephants and dragons who had perished in mortal combat. The resin of Dracaena species, \"true\" dragon's blood, and the very poisonous mineral cinnabar (mercury sulfide) were often confused by the ancient Romans. In ancient China, little or no distinction was made among the types of dragon's blood from the different species."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Sweet Flag", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 620, "target_cluster_name": "calamo aromático", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The description of Dragon's Blood mentions 'Calamus spp.' and 'Calamus rotang' as sources. Sweet Flag is also known as 'calamo aromático' and 'Acoro', which are related to the genus Calamus. This suggests a potential connection or confusion in historical texts regarding these plants and their resins.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The description of Dragon's Blood mentions 'Calamus spp.' and 'Calamus rotang' as sources. Sweet Flag is also known as 'calamo aromático' and 'Acoro', which are related to the genus Calamus. This suggests a potential connection or confusion in historical texts regarding these plants and their resins."}, {"found_name": "Resin", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1481, "target_cluster_name": "resin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dragon's blood is explicitly described as a resin.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dragon's blood is explicitly described as a resin."}, {"found_name": "Plant gums", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2355, "target_cluster_name": "Gomma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dragon's blood is a resin, which is a type of plant exudate often grouped with gums in historical contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dragon's blood is a resin, which is a type of plant exudate often grouped with gums in historical contexts."}, {"found_name": "Tree", "link_type": "contested_identity", "link_strength": 0.7, "target_cluster_id": 24, "target_cluster_name": "Tree", "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "deluded, who conceive _sperma Coeti_ which is found about the head, to be the spawn of the Whale: Or take _sanguis draconis_ (which is the gumme of a tree,) to be the blood of a Dragon. By the same Lo", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "contested_identity", "found_relationship": "reverse: gum of a tree, mistaken for blood of Dragon", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Gomma", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2355, "target_cluster_name": "Gomma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dragon's blood is a red resin obtained from several different species of plants, notably Dracaena cinnabari, making it a specific type of plant gum/resin.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Dragon's blood is a red resin obtained from several different species of plants, notably Dracaena cinnabari, making it a specific type of plant gum/resin.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Chypre", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "chypre", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Chypre", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Chypre"], "contexts": ["island with serpentine and diorite"]}, {"entity_id": "chypre", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Chypre", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Chypre"], "contexts": ["island country", "island where plants were seen"]}, {"entity_id": "chypre", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Chypre", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "COUNTRY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Chypre", "Chipre"], "contexts": ["origin of acaparo", "source of Caparrofa"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Chypre", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Chypre", "similarity": 0.903}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Chypre", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Chypre", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Chypre", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Chypre", "similarity": 0.903}], "id": 1169, "stable_key": "clu_d867f8cabe5b6a7d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cyprus", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "Island country known for its plants and mineral resources.", "note": "Refers to the island of Cyprus.", "wikipedia_extract": "Cyprus, officially the Republic of Cyprus, is an island country in the eastern Mediterranean Sea, located off the coast of the Levant in West Asia. Cyprus’ capital is Nicosia, while its largest municipality is Limassol. The northeast portion of the island is occupied by Turkey, which is separated from the Republic of Cyprus by the United Nations Buffer Zone. In the south of the island of Cyprus are the British sovereign military bases of Akrotiri and Dhekelia. The island is the third largest and third most populous in the Mediterranean, after Sicily and Sardinia. Cyprus was first settled by hunter-gatherers around 13,000 years ago, with farming communities emerging by 8500 BC."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Méditerranée", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 256, "target_cluster_name": "Méditerranée", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cyprus is an island nation located in the Eastern Mediterranean Sea.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cyprus is an island nation located in the Eastern Mediterranean Sea.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Creta", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 510, "target_cluster_name": "Creta", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Crete (modern Greek: Kríti) is an island in the Mediterranean Sea, south of Cyprus. Both are significant islands in the Eastern Mediterranean with long histories.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Crete (modern Greek: Kríti) is an island in the Mediterranean Sea, south of Cyprus. Both are significant islands in the Eastern Mediterranean with long histories."}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cyprus is geographically located in West Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cyprus is geographically located in West Asia."}, {"found_name": "Europe", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 30, "target_cluster_name": "Europe", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cyprus is politically and culturally considered part of Europe, despite its geographical location in Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cyprus is politically and culturally considered part of Europe, despite its geographical location in Asia."}, {"found_name": "Ásia menor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2070, "target_cluster_name": "Ásia menor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cyprus is an island in the Eastern Mediterranean, historically and geographically linked to Anatolia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cyprus is an island in the Eastern Mediterranean, historically and geographically linked to Anat