es, 1984"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Isaac Newton", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 71, "target_cluster_name": "Newton", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Gauss is often referred to as the 'Prince of Mathematicians', a title that echoes the profound impact and foundational work of Isaac Newton in mathematics and physics. Gauss's work built upon and extended Newtonian principles in many areas, particularly in celestial mechanics and optics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Gauss is often referred to as the 'Prince of Mathematicians', a title that echoes the profound impact and foundational work of Isaac Newton in mathematics and physics. Gauss's work built upon and extended Newtonian principles in many areas, particularly in celestial mechanics and optics."}, {"found_name": "Archimedes", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 480, "target_cluster_name": "Archimedes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both Archimedes and Gauss are considered among the greatest mathematicians of all time. Gauss's rigorous approach and breadth of mathematical contributions are often compared to the foundational work of Archimedes in geometry and mechanics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both Archimedes and Gauss are considered among the greatest mathematicians of all time. Gauss's rigorous approach and breadth of mathematical contributions are often compared to the foundational work of Archimedes in geometry and mechanics."}, {"found_name": "Laplace", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 243, "target_cluster_name": "Laplace", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were leading mathematicians and scientists of the late 18th and early 19th centuries, known for their foundational work in their respective fields.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were leading mathematicians and scientists of the late 18th and early 19th centuries, known for their foundational work in their respective fields.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Bessel", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 269, "target_cluster_name": "Bessel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both Bessel and Gauss were highly influential mathematicians and scientists of the 19th century. Gauss made foundational contributions to many areas of mathematics and physics, while Bessel applied rigorous mathematical methods to astronomy and geodesy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both Bessel and Gauss were highly influential mathematicians and scientists of the 19th century. Gauss made foundational contributions to many areas of mathematics and physics, while Bessel applied rigorous mathematical methods to astronomy and geodesy.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Helmholtz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 624, "target_cluster_name": "Helmholtz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were leading mathematicians and physicists of the 19th century, and it is highly probable they were aware of each other's work and may have corresponded or met.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were leading mathematicians and physicists of the 19th century, and it is highly probable they were aware of each other's work and may have corresponded or met.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent figures in 19th-century science, with Humboldt being a renowned geographer and naturalist, and Gauss a leading mathematician and physicist. Their work, while in different primary fields, contributed to the broader scientific advancements of the era and they likely interacted or were aware of each other's contributions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent figures in 19th-century science, with Humboldt being a renowned geographer and naturalist, and Gauss a leading mathematician and physicist. Their work, while in different primary fields, contributed to the broader scientific advancements of the era and they likely interacted or were aware of each other's contributions."}, {"found_name": "Struve", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2068, "target_cluster_name": "Struve", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were highly influential mathematicians and scientists of the 19th century, with Gauss making significant contributions to astronomy and geodesy, fields in which Struve also excelled.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were highly influential mathematicians and scientists of the 19th century, with Gauss making significant contributions to astronomy and geodesy, fields in which Struve also excelled.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Chladni", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2131, "target_cluster_name": "Chladni", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were highly influential mathematicians and physicists of the 19th century, with Chladni's work on acoustics laying groundwork for later investigations in wave phenomena that Gauss also studied.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were highly influential mathematicians and physicists of the 19th century, with Chladni's work on acoustics laying groundwork for later investigations in wave phenomena that Gauss also studied.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "pulse", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "pulse", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "pulse", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["pulse"], "contexts": ["indicator of physiological change", "bodily rhythm quickened by alarm"]}, {"entity_id": "pulso", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "pulso", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 2, "variants": ["pulso"], "contexts": ["part of the body to be examined", "used to diagnose fever and humors"]}, {"entity_id": "pulses", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "pulses", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["pulses"], "contexts": ["body part for observation"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "pulse", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "pulso", "similarity": 0.978}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "pulse", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "pulses", "similarity": 0.943}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "pulso", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "pulses", "similarity": 0.911}], "id": 1177, "stable_key": "clu_50478d751e14abff", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "pulse", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "The rhythmic throbbing of arteries, used for diagnosis.", "wikipedia_extract": "In medicine, pulse is the rhythmic expansion and contraction of an artery in response to the cardiac cycle (heartbeat). The pulse may be felt (palpated) in any place that allows an artery to be compressed near the surface of the body, such as at the neck (carotid artery), wrist (radial artery or ulnar artery), at the groin (femoral artery), behind the knee (popliteal artery), near the ankle joint (posterior tibial artery), and on foot (dorsalis pedis artery). The pulse is most commonly measured at the wrist or neck for adults and at the brachial artery (inner upper arm between the shoulder and elbow) for infants and very young children. A sphygmograph is an instrument for measuring the pulse. Claudius Galen was perhaps the first physiologist to describe the pulse. The pulse is an expedient tactile method of determination of systolic blood pressure to a trained observer."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Blood vessels", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1267, "target_cluster_name": "blood-vessels", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The pulse is a phenomenon occurring in arteries, which are a type of blood vessel.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The pulse is a phenomenon occurring in arteries, which are a type of blood vessel."}]}, {"canonical_name": "insane", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "insane", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "insane", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 3, "variants": ["insane"], "contexts": ["state of mental illness", "patient's long-term mental condition"]}, {"entity_id": "insania", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Insania", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Insania"], "contexts": ["a synonym for madness"]}, {"entity_id": "insane", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "insane", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 2, "variants": ["insane"], "contexts": ["condition with peculiar odour", "state of mental illness"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "insane", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Insania", "simi