he Funky Homosapien, fellow rappers Casual, Pep Love, and all four members of the group Souls of Mischief—Phesto, A-Plus, Opio, and Tajai—as well as DJ Toure and producer/manager Domino. Since their inception, Hieroglyphics have found a following largely through their members, podcasts (\"Hierocasts\"), and promotion through their website. The collective uses a three-eyed, straight-lipped face logo that figures prominently on their albums, website, stickers, and clothing. As a collective, the Hieroglyphics have released three studio albums: 3rd Eye Vision in 1998, Full Circle in 2003, and The Kitchen in 2013. In 2005, the collective released a live DVD and accompanying CD of the Hiero's 2003 Full Circle Tour."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alphabet", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3074, "target_cluster_name": "alphabet", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hieroglyphics are a form of writing, and the alphabet is the fundamental system of written symbols in many languages. The development and nature of writing systems are closely linked.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hieroglyphics are a form of writing, and the alphabet is the fundamental system of written symbols in many languages. The development and nature of writing systems are closely linked."}]}, {"canonical_name": "anger", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "anger", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "anger", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["anger"], "contexts": ["strong feeling of displeasure"]}, {"entity_id": "angry", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "angry", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["angry"], "contexts": ["feeling of strong displeasure"]}, {"entity_id": "anger", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "anger", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["anger"], "contexts": ["strong feeling of displeasure", "feeling of displeasure and hostility"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "anger", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "angry", "similarity": 0.925}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "anger", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "anger", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "angry", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "anger", "similarity": 0.925}], "id": 1206, "stable_key": "clu_6dde21a2760f44cc", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Anger", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anger", "wikipedia_extract": "Anger is an intense emotional state involving a strong, uncomfortable and non-cooperative response to a perceived provocation, hurt, or threat. A person experiencing anger will often experience physical effects, such as increased heart rate, elevated blood pressure, and increased levels of the stress hormones adrenaline and noradrenaline. Some view anger as an emotion that triggers part of the fight or flight response. Anger becomes the predominant feeling behaviorally, cognitively, and physiologically when a person makes the conscious choice to take action to immediately stop the threatening behavior of another outside force. Anger can have many physical and mental consequences. The external expression of anger can be found in facial expressions, body language, physiological responses, and at times public acts of aggression."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Fear", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 147, "target_cluster_name": "Fear", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are strong emotions that can influence behavior and perception.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are strong emotions that can influence behavior and perception.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "feeling", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 245, "target_cluster_name": "feeling", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both 'feeling' and 'anger' refer to subjective states of mind, with anger being a specific type of negative feeling.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both 'feeling' and 'anger' refer to subjective states of mind, with anger being a specific type of negative feeling.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Human Nature", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 513, "target_cluster_name": "Human Nature", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anger is a core human emotion and disposition, frequently examined within discussions of human nature.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Anger is a core human emotion and disposition, frequently examined within discussions of human nature.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "feelings", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 618, "target_cluster_name": "feelings", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anger is a distinct and powerful emotion, frequently discussed in historical texts concerning human passions and behavior, making it a specific related concept to emotions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Anger is a distinct and powerful emotion, frequently discussed in historical texts concerning human passions and behavior, making it a specific related concept