 the tropics to the temperate zone. Pelicans are absent from interior Amazonian South America, from polar regions and the open ocean; at least one species is known to migrate to the inland desert of Australia's Red Centre, after heavy rains create temporary lakes.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pelican"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "discord", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "discord", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "discord", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["discord"], "contexts": ["negative quality, from evil principle"]}, {"entity_id": "discord", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "discord", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["discord"], "contexts": ["lack of harmony or agreement", "negative relation to topic"]}, {"entity_id": "discords", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "discords", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["discords"], "contexts": ["disagreeable sound from unrelated vibrations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "discord", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "discord", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "discord", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "discords", "similarity": 0.864}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "discord", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "discords", "similarity": 0.864}], "id": 1209, "stable_key": "clu_46581606f0e0902c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Discord", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q5281696", "wikidata_description":