"progenitor of offspring"]}, {"entity_id": "parente", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "parente", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["parente"], "contexts": ["relative of the narrator"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Parentis", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "parents", "similarity": 0.858}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Parentis", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "parent", "similarity": 0.902}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Parentis", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "parente", "similarity": 0.9}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "parents", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "parente", "similarity": 0.909}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "parent", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "parente", "similarity": 0.976}], "id": 1224, "stable_key": "clu_5f44fb4419aed9fa", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Parents", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Progenitors of offspring, biological or familial", "wikidata_id": "Q7566", "wikidata_description": "progenitor or caregiver of the offspring in their own species, inverse label for property P40", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parent", "wikipedia_extract": "A parent is either the progenitor of a child or, in humans, it can refer to a caregiver or legal guardian, generally called an adoptive parent or step-parent. Parents who are progenitors are first-degree relatives and have 50% genetic meet. A female can also become a parent through surrogacy. Some parents may be adoptive parents, who nurture and raise an offspring, but are not related to the child. Orphans without adoptive parents can be raised by their grandparents or other family members. A parent can also be elaborated as an ancestor removed one generation."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Swedish turnip", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "evidence_snippet": "roots as commonly called, of the Swedish turnip and Ruta baga, plants which several botanists rank as varieties produced by cultivation from a common parent: if this be not so, the case will then be o", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "variety of common parent"}, {"found_name": "Ruta baga", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "evidence_snippet": "roots as commonly called, of the Swedish turnip and Ruta baga, plants which several botanists rank as varieties produced by cultivation from a common parent: if this be not so, the case will then be o", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "variety of common parent"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Turner", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "turner", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Turner", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Turner"], "contexts": ["author"]}, {"entity_id": "turner", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Turner", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Turner"], "contexts": ["traveler in the Himalayas"]}, {"entity_id": "turner", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Turner", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Turner"], "contexts": ["author of Collections for the History of Grantham", "author of 'Collections for the History of Grantham'"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Turner", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Turner", "similarity": 0.797}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Turner", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Turner", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Turner", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Turner", "similarity": 0.797}], "id": 1225, "stable_key": "clu_84be5e5f1d94ed15", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "William Turner", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1508, "death_year": 1568, "description": "English physician, naturalist, and cleric", "note": "Multiple individuals named Turner existed. The context of early modern texts and natural history points to William Turner, a prominent physician and naturalist of the 16th century. While Humboldt's 'Kosmos' is later (19th C), it often referenced earlier naturalists."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Prayer", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "prayer", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Prayer", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Prayer"], "contexts": ["religious observance"]}, {"entity_id": "prayers", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "prayers", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["prayers"], "contexts": ["can be said with attention elsewhere"]}, {"entity_id": "prayer", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "prayer", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["prayer"], "contexts": ["communication with a deity"]}, {"entity_id": "oração", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Oração", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Oração"], "contexts": ["religious practice"]}, {"entity_id": "rezar", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "rezar", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["rezar"], "contexts": ["praying"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Prayer", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "prayers", "similarity": 0.919}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Prayer", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "prayer", "similarity": 0.97}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Prayer", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Oração", "similarity": 0.945}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Prayer", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "rezar", "similarity": 0.914}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "prayers", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "rezar", "similarity": 0.883}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "prayer", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Oração", "similarity": 0.939}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "prayer", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "rezar", "similarity": 0.919}], "id": 1226, "stable_key": "clu_42b95aa15b1bf557", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "prayer", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Communication with or worship of a deity; religious observance.", "wikipedia_extract": "Prayer is an invocation or act that seeks to activate a rapport with an object of worship through deliberate communication. In the narrow sense, the term refers to an act of supplication or intercession directed towards a deity or a deified ancestor. More generally, prayer can also have the purpose of giving thanks or praise, and in comparative religion is closely associated with more abstract forms of meditation and with charms or spells. Prayer can take a variety of forms: it can be part of a set liturgy or ritual, and it can be performed alone or in groups. Prayer may take the form of a hymn, incantation, formal creedal statement, or a spontaneous utterance in the praying person. The act of prayer is attested in written sources as early as five thousand years ago."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Faith", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 498, "target_cluster_name": "faith", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Faith is a core component and often a prerequisite for prayer.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Faith is a core component and often a prerequisite for prayer."}, {"found_name": "Belief", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2125, "target_cluster_name": "belief", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Belief in a deity or higher power is fundamental to the practice of prayer.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Belief in a deity or higher power is fundamental to the practice of prayer."}, {"found_name": "Divinity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2345, "target_cluster_name": "Divinity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Prayer is typically directed towards divinity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Prayer is typically directed towards divinity."}, {"found_name": "Hope", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3087, "target_cluster_name": "hope", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Prayer is often an expression of hope and a means to seek desired outcomes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Prayer is often an expression of hope and a means to seek desired outcomes."}, {"found_name": "Desire", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 925, "target_cluster_name": "desire", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Prayer frequently arises from or expresses desires.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Prayer frequently arises from or expresses desires."}, {"found_name": "Communication", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3561, "target_cluster_name": "communicação", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Prayer is a form of communication with a divine entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Prayer is a form of communication with a divine entity."}]}, {"canonical_name": "olives", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "olives", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Olives", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Olives"], "contexts": ["unripe fruit used for oil"]}, {"entity_id": "olives", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "olives", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["olives"], "contexts": ["dried fruit import"]}, {"entity_id": "olives", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "olives", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["olives"], "contexts": ["fruit-bearing trees", "cultivated plant"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Olives", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "olives", "similarity": 0.972}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Olives", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "olives", "similarity": 0.972}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "olives", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "olives", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1227, "stable_key": "clu_ba9a422b09fc36f4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "olive tree", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Olea europaea", "family": "Oleaceae", "description": "Tree producing olives and olive oil, valued for its fruit and oil.", "wikipedia_extract": "The olive (botanical name Olea europaea, \"European olive\") is a species of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Originating in Asia Minor, it is abundant throughout the Mediterranean Basin, with wild subspecies in Africa and western Asia; modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. The olive is the type species for its genus, Olea, and lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family, which includes lilac, jasmine, forsythia, and ash. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil—now used to describe any viscous water-insoluble liquid—was originally synonymous with olive oil, the liquid fat derived from olives. The olive has deep historical, economic, and cultural significance in the Mediterranean."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "oliveira", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1881, "target_cluster_name": "oliveira", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The fruit of the olive tree.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The fruit of the olive tree.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "azeitonas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2626, "target_cluster_name": "azeitonas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The entity 'olives' is the fruit of the 'olive tree'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The entity 'olives' is the fruit of the 'olive tree'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Sallet Oyl", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "which is commonly known by the name of Sallet Oyl, I suppose because it is usually eaten with Sallets by them that love it; If it be pressed out of ripe Olives, according to Galen is temperate, and ex", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for 'Olives' (pressed oil)"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Ceylon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "ceylon", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Ceylon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Ceylon"], "contexts": ["island nation in South Asia", "location of observation"]}, {"entity_id": "geylan", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Geylan", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Geylan"], "contexts": ["destination of voyage"]}, {"entity_id": "ceylon", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Ceylon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Ceylon"], "contexts": ["proposed location for magnetic stations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Ceylon", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Geylan", "similarity": 0.902}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Ceylon", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ceylon", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Geylan", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Ceylon", "similarity": 0.902}], "id": 1228, "stable_key": "clu_3ffbda68e4ed3174", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Sri Lanka", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Sri Lanka", "