evealing Indian literature to Europe", "cited for name of bamboo in Canará"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Wilson", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Wilson", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Wilson", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Wilson", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Wilson", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Wilson", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1248, "stable_key": "clu_11c374500922bc68", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Wilson", "confidence": "medium", "type": "person", "description": "Scholar observing heat radiation and revealing Indian literature.", "note": "Multiple individuals named Wilson existed during this period; context suggests scholars or naturalists."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Pisa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "pisa", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Pisa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["pisa", "Pisa"], "contexts": ["treading of clay", "city"]}, {"entity_id": "pisa", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Pisa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Pisa"], "contexts": ["city where scholar studied medicine"]}, {"entity_id": "pisa", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Pisa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Pisa"], "contexts": ["location of Professor Mossotti", "city where Professor Matteucci was from"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Pisa", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Pisa", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Pisa", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Pisa", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Pisa", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Pisa", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1249, "stable_key": "clu_eb85f40275159afd", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Pisa ( PEE-zə; Italian: [ˈpiːza]  or [ˈpiːsa]) is a city and comune (municipality) in Tuscany, Central Italy, straddling the Arno just before it empties into the Ligurian Sea. It is the capital city of the Province of Pisa. Although Pisa is known worldwide for the Leaning Tower of Pisa, the city contains more than twenty other historic churches, and several medieval and Renaissance palaces, mostly facing each other on the avenues along the Arno (\"Lungarno\"). Much of the city's architecture was financed from its history as one of the Italian maritime republics. The city is also home to the University of Pisa, which has a history going back to the 12th century, the Scuola Normale Superiore di Pisa, founded by Napoleon in 1810, and its offshoot, the Sant'Anna School of Advanced Studies. Most believe the hypothesis that the origin of the name Pisa comes from Etruscan and means 'mouth', as Pisa is at the mouth of the Arno river."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "villages", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "villages", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "villages", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["villages"], "contexts": ["settlements larger than hamlets", "settlement type"]}, {"entity_id": "hameaux", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "hameaux", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["hameaux"], "contexts": ["small rural settlements"]}, {"entity_id": "pueblos", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "pueblos", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["pueblos"], "contexts": ["locations with impure wells"]}, {"entity_id": "villages", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "villages", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["villages"], "contexts": ["small human settlements"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "villages", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "pueblos", "similarity": 0.953}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "villages", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "villages", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "hameaux", "target_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "target_name": "pueblos", "similarity": 0.884}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "hameaux", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "villages", "similarity": 0.898}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "pueblos", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "villages", "similarity": 0.953}], "id": 1250, "stable_key": "clu_ca70ad79751edff8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Settlement", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "note": "The term 'villages' encompasses various small human settlements, including hamlets and pueblos, and can also refer to specific locations with wells.", "wikidata_id": "Q486972", "wikidata_description": "place of any size, in which people permanently live", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human%20settlement", "wikipedia_extract": "In geography, statistics and archaeology, a settlement, locality or populated place is a community of people living in a particular place. The complexity of a settlement can range from a minuscule number of dwellings grouped together to the largest of cities with surrounding urbanized areas. Settlements include homesteads, hamlets, villages, towns and cities. A settlement may have known historical properties such as the date or era in which it was first settled or first settled by particular people. A number of factors like war, erosion, and the fall of great empires can result in the formation of abandoned settlements which provides relics for archaeological studies. The process of settlement involves human migration."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "City", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1222, "target_cluster_name": "City", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A city is a type of settlement, often a large and complex one.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "A city is a type of settlement, often a large and complex one."}, {"found_name": "casa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1272, "target_cluster_name": "casa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A settlement is a place where people establish a community, and houses are the primary structures within settlements.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A settlement is a place where people establish a community, and houses are the primary structures within settlements.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Archipelago", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 175, "target_cluster_name": "archipelago", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "An archipelago is a group of islands, which can contain multiple settlements.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "An archipelago is a group of islands, which can contain multiple settlements."}, {"found_name": "Continent", 