ations", "similarity": 0.956}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "condensation", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "condensation", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "condensation", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "condensations", "similarity": 0.956}, {"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "condensation", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "condensation", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1255, "stable_key": "clu_e949ac485a868f57", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Condensation", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q1780990", "wikidata_description": "psychological concept for when a single idea (an image, memory, or thought) or dream object stands for several associations and ideas", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Condensation%20%28psychology%29", "wikipedia_extract": "In Freudian psychoanalysis, a condensation (German: Verdichtung) is when a single idea (an image, memory, or thought) or dream object stands for several associations and ideas. This is an energetic reshuffling in which mental energy flows freely from one idea etc. to another. This free change of psychic energy is characteristic of so-called primary processes, which do not function with the aim of mental identity, but rather aim to fulfill pleasure, even self-deception to a certain extent, in order to make life easier, i.e. to avoid unpleasant and harmful things: a camouflage, reinterpretation, reconnection of disliked perceptions or memories. However, condensations can also be the determining factor for misperceptions, the psychoenergetic dynamics of which are not free-flowing, as certain external and internal motives are also involved."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "distillation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2, "target_cluster_name": "distillation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Condensation is the complementary process to boiling, which is the first step in distillation. Vapors are condensed to form the purified liquid.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Condensation is the complementary process to boiling, which is the first step in distillation. Vapors are condensed to form the purified liquid.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Humidity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 27, "target_cluster_name": "Humidity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Condensation is the process by which water vapor changes back into liquid water, often occurring when humidity is high.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Condensation is the process by which water vapor changes back into liquid water, often occurring when humidity is high.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "crystallization", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 986, "target_cluster_name": "crystallization", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Crystallization often follows or is a form of condensation, where a substance changes from a gaseous or liquid state to a solid crystalline state.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Crystallization often follows or is a form of condensation, where a substance changes from a gaseous or liquid state to a solid crystalline state.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Abstraction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 894, "target_cluster_name": "abstraction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Condensation in psychoanalysis involves the merging of multiple ideas into a single representation, which is a form of abstraction where specific details are generalized or combined.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Condensation in psychoanalysis involves the merging of multiple ideas into a single representation, which is a form of abstraction where specific details are generalized or combined."}, {"found_name": "decomposition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2085, "target_cluster_name": "decomposition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Condensation is the opposite process of decomposition of gas into liquid.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Condensation is the opposite process of decomposition of gas into liquid.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "evaporaçao", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3723, "target_cluster_name": "evaporaçao", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Evaporation and condensation are inverse processes in the water cycle and phase transitions of matter, often discussed together.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Evaporation and condensation are inverse processes in the water cycle and phase transitions of matter, often discussed together.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "mercadores", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "mercadorcs", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Mercadorcs", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Mercadorcs"], "contexts": ["merchants"]}, {"entity_id": "mercadores", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "mercadores", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 3, "variants": ["mercadores", "hum mercador"], "contexts": ["merchants consulted about camphor water", "friend who lost money on sândalo"]}, {"entity_id": "mercador", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "mercador", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["mercador"], "contexts": ["merchant who suffered from itching"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mercadorcs", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "mercadores", "similarity": 0.94}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Mercadorcs", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "mercador", "similarity": 0.899}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "mercadores", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "mercador", "similarity": 0.943}], "id": 1256, "stable_key": "clu_5d4b74f59e820d52", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Merchants", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Individuals involved in trade and commerce, often consulted on goods.", "wikipedia_extract": "A merchant is a person or company engaged in trade, conducting sales through stores or online platforms, particularly one that engages in international import and export activities. Merchants have been known for as long as humans have engaged in trade and commerce. Merchants and merchant networks operated in ancient Babylonia, Assyria, China, Egypt, Greece, India, Persia, Phoenicia and Rome. During the European medieval period, a rapid expansion in trade and commerce led to the rise of a wealthy and powerful merchant class. The European Age of Discovery opened up new trading routes and gave European consumers access to a much broader range of goods. By the 18th century, a new type of manufacturer-merchant had started to emerge and modernize for the purpose of generating profit, cash flow, sales, and revenue using a combination of human, financial, intellectual and physical capital with a view to fueling economic development and growth."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Judeus", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 356, "target_cluster_name": "Judeus", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "tocar com elles; o seu cuidado he limpar as çugidades das casas e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamado", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Portuguese comparison for esparcis"}, {"found_name": "arames", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "tocar com elles; o seu cuidado he limpar as çugidades das casas e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamado", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for deres"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Madras", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "madras", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Madras", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Madras"], "contexts": ["city with observed average temperature"]}, {"entity_id": "madras", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Madras", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Madras", "Madrasta"], "contexts": ["publication location of Indian Botany", "modern city mentioned"]}, {"entity_id": "madras", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Madras", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 2, "variants": ["Madras"], "contexts": ["location of astronomical observations", "Saturn’s ring discovered from"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Madras", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Madras", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Madras", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Madras", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Madras", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Madras", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1257, "stable_key": "clu_53eec313c48484c4", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Chennai, also known as Madras (its official name until 1996), is the capital and largest city of Tamil Nadu, the southernmost state of India. It is located on the Coromandel Coast of the Bay of Bengal. According to the 2011 Indian census, Chennai is the sixth-most-populous city in India and forms the fourth-most-populous urban agglomeration. Incorporated in 1688, the Greater Chennai Corporation is the oldest municipal corporation in India and the second oldest in the world after London. Historically, the region was part of the Chola, Pandya, Pallava and Vijayanagara kingdoms during various eras. The coastal land which then contained the fishing village Madrasapattinam, was purchased by the British East India Company from the Nayak ruler Chennapa Nayaka in the 17th century."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Scheele", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "schouw", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Schouw", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Schouw"], "contexts": ["observer of continental atmosphere temperatures"]}, {"entity_id": "schouw", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Schouw", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Schouw"], "contexts": ["rain distribution in Central Europe"]}, {"entity_id": "scheele", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Scheele", "category": "P