 "target_cluster_name": "Electrick attraction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Electrostatic attraction is a specific manifestation of attraction between charged particles.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Electrostatic attraction is a specific manifestation of attraction between charged particles."}, {"found_name": "Forces of attraction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4344, "target_cluster_name": "forces of attraction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This is a direct pluralization and specification of the concept of attraction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "This is a direct pluralization and specification of the concept of attraction."}, {"found_name": "Forces of attraction and repulsion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2658, "target_cluster_name": "attraction and repulsion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This phrase explicitly contrasts attraction with its opposite, repulsion, placing attraction within a broader framework of forces.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "This phrase explicitly contrasts attraction with its opposite, repulsion, placing attraction within a broader framework of forces."}, {"found_name": "Coition", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "haling of the weak unto the stronger. And this is also the doctrine of _Gilbertus_, by whom this motion is termed Coition, and that not made by any faculty attractive of one, but a Syndrome and concou", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name for motion"}]}, {"canonical_name": "inward Wounds", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "wounds", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "wounds", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["wounds"], "contexts": ["injuries healed by ointments and nature"]}, {"entity_id": "inward_wounds", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "inward Wounds", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 2, "variants": ["inward Wounds", "inward Ulcers"], "contexts": ["injuries to internal body parts", "sores within the body"]}, {"entity_id": "wounds", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "wounds", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 1, "variants": ["wounds"], "contexts": ["injury to the body"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "wounds", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "inward Wounds", "similarity": 0.968}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "wounds", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "wounds", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "inward Wounds", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "wounds", "similarity": 0.968}], "id": 1310, "stable_key": "clu_a99fd74f79882061", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Wounds", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "An injury to living tissue, typically involving a break in the skin.", "note": "Includes various types of wounds like 'green Wounds' and 'inward Wounds'. 'Contusões' (bruises) are also a form of wound.", "wikipedia_extract": "A wound is any disruption of or damage to living tissue, such as skin, mucous membranes, or organs. Wounds can either be the sudden result of direct trauma (mechanical, thermal, chemical), or can develop slowly over time due to underlying disease processes such as diabetes mellitus, venous/arterial insufficiency, or immunologic disease. Wounds can vary greatly in their appearance depending on wound location, injury mechanism, depth of injury, timing of onset (acute vs chronic), and wound sterility, among other factors. Treatment strategies for wounds will vary based on the classification of the wound, therefore it is essential that wounds be thoroughly evaluated by a healthcare professional for proper management. In normal physiology, all wounds will undergo a series of steps collectively known as the wound healing process, which include hemostasis, inflammation, proliferation, and tissue remodeling. Age, tissue oxygenation, stress, underlying medical conditions, and certain medications are just a few of the many factors known to affect the rate of wound healing."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "contusões", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 3320, "target_cluster_name": "contusões", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A specific type of wound mentioned in the list, directly related to the general term 'Wounds'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: A specific type of wound mentioned in the list, directly related to the general term 'Wounds'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "quebraduras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 800, "target_cluster_name": "quebraduras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fractures are a type of physical trauma, often occurring alongside or as a result of wounds.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Fractures are a type of physical trauma, often occurring alongside or as a result of wounds.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "DANDELYON", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "into the running Eyes of any doth much help them. The Herb is under the Sign Cancer, and un∣der the Dominion of Venus, and therfore ex∣cellent good for Wounds in the Breast, and ve∣ry fitting to be ke", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vulgar name for a plant"}, {"found_name": "Piss-a-beds", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "into the running Eyes of any doth much help them. The Herb is under the Sign Cancer, and un∣der the Dominion of Venus, and therfore ex∣cellent good for Wounds in the Breast, and ve∣ry fitting to be ke", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vulgar name for DANDELYON"}]}, {"canonical_name": "bórax", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "borax", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Borax", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Borax"], "contexts": ["mineral used in gunpowder formulations"]}, {"entity_id": "borax", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Borax", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Borax"], "contexts": ["powder mixed with juice for cleansing"]}, {"entity_id": "bórax", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "bórax", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["bórax"], "contexts": ["substance used for gold and metals", "substance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Borax", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Borax", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Borax", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "bórax", "similarity": 0.751}, {"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Borax", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "bórax", "similarity": 0.751}], "id": 1311, "stable_key": "clu_97d8ba8748867f9d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "borax", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "description": "Soft white crystalline mineral, a salt of boric acid.", "wikipedia_extract": "Borax (also referred to as sodium borate, tincal  and tincar ) is a salt (ionic compound) normally encountered as a hydrated borate of sodium, with the chemical formula Na2H20B4O17. Borax mineral is a crystalline borate mineral that occurs in only a few places worldwide in quantities that enable it to be mined economically. Borax can be dehydrated by heating into other forms with less water of hydration. The anhydrous form of borax can also be obtained from the decahydrate or other hydrates by heating and then grinding the resulting glasslike solid into a powder. It is a white crystalline solid that dissolves in water to make a basic solution due to the tetraborate anion. Borax is commonly available in powder or granular form and has many industrial and household uses, including as a pesticide, as a metal soldering flux, as a component of glass, enamel, and pottery glazes, for tanning of skins and hides, for artificial aging of wood, as a preservative against wood fungus, as a food additive, and as a pharmaceutic alkalizer."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 357, "target_cluster_name": "Alum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are mineral salts used in historical medicine and industry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are mineral salts used in historical medicine and industry."}, {"found_name": "Saltpeter", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 350, "target_cluster_name": "Nitro", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are mineral salts with historical uses in alchemy and industry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are mineral salts with historical uses in alchemy and industry."}, {"found_name": "Gypsum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 682, "target_cluster_name": "gypse", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are mineral substances with historical uses.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are mineral substances with historical uses."}, {"found_name": "Emery", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3247, "target_cluster_name": "Emery", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are mineral substances used historically.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are mineral substances used historically."}, {"found_name": "crísocola", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "qua. ORTA Si; mas he das drogas defesas, e por pouquo perdereis o muyto. RUANO Nâo o quero levar, senam quero saber onde o ha e o nome delle. ORTA Chamase bórax e crísocola, e fincar em arábio, e os G", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "fincar", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "qua. ORTA Si; mas he das drogas defesas, e por pouquo perdereis o muyto. RUANO Nâo o quero levar, senam quero saber onde o ha e o nome delle. ORTA Chamase bórax e crísocola, e fincar em arábio, e os G", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}]}, {"canonical_name": "rubino", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subc