ical state, in the context of these texts, it functions as a concept being discussed or contrasted.", "wikidata_id": "Q35831", "wikidata_description": "naturally recurring resting state of mind and body", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sleep", "wikipedia_extract": "Sleep is a state of reduced mental and physical activity in which consciousness is altered and certain sensory activity is inhibited. During sleep, there is a marked decrease in muscle activity and interactions with the surrounding environment. While sleep differs from wakefulness in terms of the ability to react to stimuli, it still involves active brain patterns, making it more reactive than a coma or disorders of consciousness. Sleep occurs in repeating periods, during which the body alternates between two distinct modes: rapid eye movement sleep (REM) and non-REM sleep. Although REM stands for \"rapid eye movement\", this mode of sleep has many other aspects, including virtual paralysis of the body. Dreams are a succession of images, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Coma", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2590, "target_cluster_name": "Coma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Coma is a state of prolonged unconsciousness that is a severe disruption of the normal state of sleep and wakefulness.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Coma is a state of prolonged unconsciousness that is a severe disruption of the normal state of sleep and wakefulness."}, {"found_name": "Stupor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2697, "target_cluster_name": "stupor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Stupor is a state of near-unconsciousness or insensibility, which is a significant deviation from normal sleep.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Stupor is a state of near-unconsciousness or insensibility, which is a significant deviation from normal sleep."}, {"found_name": "Unconsciousness", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1942, "target_cluster_name": "unconsciousness", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Unconsciousness is a state of being unaware of one's surroundings, which is the opposite of the conscious awareness typically present in wakefulness and a profound alteration of the sleep state.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Unconsciousness is a state of being unaware of one's surroundings, which is the opposite of the conscious awareness typically present in wakefulness and a profound alteration of the sleep state."}, {"found_name": "Lethargy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 651, "target_cluster_name": "lethargo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced activity, which can be an abnormal manifestation or disruption of normal sleep patterns.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Lethargy is a state of sluggishness and reduced activity, which can be an abnormal manifestation or disruption of normal sleep patterns."}, {"found_name": "Exhaustion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3509, "target_cluster_name": "exhaustion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Extreme exhaustion can lead to an inability to achieve normal, restorative sleep, or conversely, an overwhelming need for sleep that disrupts normal functioning.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Extreme exhaustion can lead to an inability to achieve normal, restorative sleep, or conversely, an overwhelming need for sleep that disrupts normal functioning."}, {"found_name": "modorras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1613, "target_cluster_name": "modorras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Lethargy is characterized by excessive sleepiness or a state of being drowsy, closely related to the natural state of sleep.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Lethargy is characterized by excessive sleepiness or a state of being drowsy, closely related to the natural state of sleep.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "fore-legs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "fore-legs", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "fore-legs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["fore-legs"], "contexts": ["front limbs of animals"]}, {"entity_id": "fore_leg", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "fore leg", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["fore leg"], "contexts": ["part of horse"]}, {"entity_id": "fore-limbs", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "fore-limbs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["fore-limbs"], "contexts": ["limbs used for locomotion and manipulation"]}, {"entity_id": "fore-limb", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "fore-limb", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["fore-limb"], "contexts": ["front limb of an animal"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "fore-legs", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "fore leg", "similarity": 0.943}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "fore-legs", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "fore-limbs", "similarity": 0.946}, {"source_book": "pseudodoxia