e": "Ethiopians", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Ethiopes", "similarity": 0.879}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Etiope", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Ethiopes", "similarity": 0.933}], "id": 1388, "stable_key": "clu_caedb77ad25cd2e8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ethiopian people", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Inhabitants of the historical region of Ethiopia and surrounding areas."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "relaxacion de miem", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "relaxacion_de_miem", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "relaxacion de miem", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 2, "variants": ["relaxacion de miem", "relaxaciones del eftomago"], "contexts": ["symptom caused by coldness", "loosening of the stomach"]}, {"entity_id": "relaxaçam", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "relaxaçam", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["relaxaçam"], "contexts": ["condition of the gums"]}, {"entity_id": "relaxados", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "relaxados", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["relaxados"], "contexts": ["limbs lacking tone"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "relaxacion de miem", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "relaxaçam", "similarity": 0.916}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "relaxacion de miem", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "relaxados", "similarity": 0.891}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "relaxaçam", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "relaxados", "similarity": 0.928}], "id": 1389, "stable_key": "clu_a1bf0384f07df285", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "flaccidity", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "flaccidity", "note": "'Relaxacion de miem' translates to 'relaxation of members' or flaccidity. 'Relaxaçam' and 'relaxados' also refer to a loss of tone or flaccidity.", "wikidata_id": "Q102186557", "wikidata_description": "symptom", "wikipedia_extract": "Flaccid paralysis is a neurological condition characterized by weakness or paralysis and reduced muscle tone without other obvious cause (e.g., trauma). This abnormal condition may be caused by disease or by trauma affecting the nerves associated with the involved muscles. For example, if the somatic nerves to a skeletal muscle are severed, then the muscle will exhibit flaccid paralysis. When muscles enter this state, they become limp and cannot contract. This condition can become fatal if it affects the respiratory muscles, posing the threat of suffocation. It also occurs in the spinal shock stage in complete transection of the spinal cord occurring in injuries such as gunshot wounds."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "dieta", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "dieta", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "dieta", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["dieta"], "contexts": ["necessary regimen for healing"]}, {"entity_id": "dieta", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "dieta", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 1, "variants": ["dieta"], "contexts": ["medical regimen"]}, {"entity_id": "dieta", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "dieta", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 2, "variants": ["dieta"], "contexts": ["diet", "medical practice for fevers"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "dieta", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "dieta", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "dieta", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "dieta", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "dieta", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "dieta", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1390, "stable_key": "clu_1bb8ce21c0248c7b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "dietary regimen", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "A prescribed course of eating for health or medical treatment.", "note": "Encompasses diet, medical regimen, and the practice of dieting.", "wikipedia_extract": "Dieting is the practice of eating food in a regulated way to decrease, maintain, or increase body weight, or to prevent and treat diseases such as diabetes and obesity. As weight loss depends on calorie intake, different kinds of calorie-reduced diets, such as those emphasising particular macronutrients (low-fat, low-carbohydrate, etc.), have been shown to be no more effective than one another. As weight regain is common, diet success is best predicted by long-term adherence. Regardless, the outcome of a diet can vary widely depending on the individual. The first popular diet was \"Banting\", named after English undertaker William Banting. In his 1863 pamphlet, Letter on Corpulence, Addressed to the Public, he outlined the details of a particular low-carbohydrate, low-calorie diet that led to his own dramatic weight loss."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Appetite", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2030, "target_cluster_name": "Appetite", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dietary regimen directly influences and is influenced by appetite.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dietary regimen directly influences and is influenced by appetite."}, {"found_name": "Digestion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 338, "target_cluster_name": "digestion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The process of digestion is a primary outcome and consideration of dietary regimen.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The process of digestion is a primary outcome and consideration of dietary regimen."}, {"found_name": "Exercise", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 691, "target_cluster_name": "exercicio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dietary regimen and exercise are often considered together as components of health and physical conditioning.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dietary regimen and exercise are often considered together as components of health and physical conditioning."}, {"found_name": "Fasting", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1752, "target_cluster_name": "comer", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fasting is a specific type of dietary regimen.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Fasting is a specific type of dietary regimen."}, {"found_name": "Health", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 152, "target_cluster_name": "salud", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dietary regimen is a key factor in maintaining or improving health.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Dietary regimen is a key factor in maintaining or improving health."}, {"found_name": "doces", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1722, "target_cluster_name": "doces", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sweets are a component of dietary regimens.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sweets are a component of dietary regimens.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name"