te": "The term 'conforta'/'confortativo' in early modern texts referred to a general property of providing comfort or strength, not a specific modern concept."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "David", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "david", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "David", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["David"], "contexts": ["praised fragrant things"]}, {"entity_id": "david", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "David", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["David"], "contexts": ["Biblical figure, psalmist"]}, {"entity_id": "rey_david", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Rey David", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Rey David"], "contexts": ["Biblical king cited for advice"]}, {"entity_id": "david", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "David", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["David"], "contexts": ["danced before the ark"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "David", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "David", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "David", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Rey David", "similarity": 0.856}, {"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "David", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "David", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "David", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "David", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Rey David", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "David", "similarity": 0.856}], "id": 1392, "stable_key": "clu_b1ded90e9665c7cf", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "David", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "description": "Biblical king and psalmist, cited as authority.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David", "wikipedia_extract": "David (; Biblical Hebrew: דָּוִד‎, romanized: Dāwīḏ, \"beloved one\") was a king of ancient Israel and Judah, according to the Hebrew Bible and Old Testament. David's reign may have occurred around the 9th century BC, although the timeframe of his reign and geographical boundaries of his kingdom are disputed. Most of what is known of David comes from biblical literature, the historicity of which has been extensively challenged, and there is little detail about David that is concrete and undisputed. Debates persist over several controversial issues: whether the story serves as a political defense of David's dynasty against accusations of tyranny, murder and regicide; the homoerotic relationship between David and Jonathan; whether the text is a Homer-like heroic tale adopting elements from its Ancient Near East parallels; and whether elements of the text date as late as the Hasmonean period. In the biblical narrative of the Books of Samuel, David is described as a young shepherd and harpist whose heart is devoted to Yahweh, the one true God. He gains fame and becomes a hero by killing Goliath."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Santos", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2401, "target_cluster_name": "Santos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "David is a biblical figure often venerated as a saint.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: David is a biblical figure often venerated as a saint.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Solomon", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 162, "target_cluster_name": "Solomon", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evid