.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Nails", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2711, "target_cluster_name": "Nails", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Nails are hard, protective coverings, similar to shells which are hard, protective coverings found on many animals and some plants.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Nails are hard, protective coverings, similar to shells which are hard, protective coverings found on many animals and some plants.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "teſta", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2739, "target_cluster_name": "teſta", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The 'testa' in botany refers to the protective outer layer of a seed, analogous to a shell.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The 'testa' in botany refers to the protective outer layer of a seed, analogous to a shell.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "ribs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 3, "members": [{"entity_id": "ribs", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "ribs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["ribs"], "contexts": ["bones protecting the chest cavity"]}, {"entity_id": "ribs", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "ribs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["ribs"], "contexts": ["bones protecting the chest"]}, {"entity_id": "ribs", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "ribs", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 1, "variants": ["ribs"], "contexts": ["bones forming the rib cage"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "ribs", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "ribs", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "ribs", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "ribs", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "ribs", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "ribs", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1426, "stable_key": "clu_361138602d74b5b0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ribs", "confidence": "high", "type": "object", "note": "Refers to the bony structures forming the rib cage, protecting internal organs.", "wikidata_id": "Q2576226", "wikidata_description": "arrangement of bones", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rib%20cage", "wikipedia_extract": "The rib cage or thoracic cage is an endoskeletal enclosure in the thorax of most vertebrates that comprises the ribs, vertebral column and sternum, which protect the vital organs of the thoracic cavity, such as the heart, lungs and great vessels and support the shoulder girdle to form the core part of the axial skeleton. A typical human thoracic cage consists of 12 pairs of ribs and the adjoining costal cartilages, the sternum (along with the manubrium and xiphoid process), and the 12 thoracic vertebrae articulating with the ribs. The thoracic cage also provides attachments for extrinsic skeletal muscles of the neck, upper limbs, upper abdomen and back, and together with the overlying skin and associated fascia and muscles, makes up the thoracic wall. In tetrapods, the rib cage intrinsically holds the muscles of respiration (diaphragm, intercostal muscles, etc.) that are crucial for active inhalation and forced exhalation, and therefore has a major ventilatory function in the respiratory system. There are thirty-three vertebrae in the human vertebral column. The rib cage is associated with TH1−TH12."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Bone", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4023, "target_cluster_name": "bone", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ribs are a type of bone and form part of the skeletal system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ribs are a type of bone and form part of the skeletal system."}, {"found_name": "Bones", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 347, "target_cluster_name": "Bones", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ribs are a type of bone and form part of the skeletal system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ribs are a type of bone and form part of the skeletal system."}, {"found_name": "Chest", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 311, "target_cluster_name": "Chest", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ribs form the primary structure of the chest.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ribs form the primary structure of the chest."}, {"found_name": "Body Part", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 467, "target_cluster_name": "parts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ribs are a specific anatomical body part.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ribs are a specific anatomical body part."}, {"found_name": "Body", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 220, "target_cluster_name": "Body", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ribs are a component of the overall body structure.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ribs are a component of the overall body structure."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Europeans", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 3, "members": [{"entity_id": "europeans", "book_id": "origin_o