depending on how one defines an organ. For example, this list contains more than 78 organs (about ~91). The list below is not comprehensive, as it is still not clear which definition of an organ is used for all the organs in the list."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "bodily parts", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 3109, "target_cluster_name": "bodily parts", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Internal organs are parts of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Internal organs are parts of the body.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "fegato", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3747, "target_cluster_name": "fegato", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The liver is a key internal organ.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The liver is a key internal organ.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Kidneys", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 74, "target_cluster_name": "Kidneys", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The kidneys are internal organs of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The kidneys are internal organs of the body.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "heart", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 85, "target_cluster_name": "heart", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The heart is a vital internal organ.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The heart is a vital internal organ.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "organs", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 141, "target_cluster_name": "organs", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Organs is a broader term 