"Wolf", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Wolff", "similarity": 0.957}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "wolf. Hoferus", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Wolff", "similarity": 0.877}], "id": 1463, "stable_key": "clu_afbc2e02db68b3ac", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Caspar Friedrich Wolff", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1734, "death_year": 1794, "description": "German physiologist who proposed evolutionary theory of epigenesis", "note": "While 'Wolf' and 'Wolff' are present, the context of organismal development points strongly to Caspar Friedrich Wolff. 'Hoferus' is likely a Latinized reference to a different individual, possibly associated with 'wolf. Hoferus' in a medical text."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Christian Wolff", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4207, "target_cluster_name": "C. Wolf", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Caspar Friedrich Wolff and Christian Wolff are often confused or conflated in historical texts due to the similarity in their names and the fact that Christian Wolff was a prominent philosopher and jurist of the same era. While Caspar Friedrich Wolff is known for his work in embryology and biology, Christian Wolff's philosophical contributions were also highly influential.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Caspar Friedrich Wolff and Christian Wolff are often confused or conflated in historical texts due to the similarity in their names and the fact that Christian Wolff was a prominent philosopher and jurist of the same era. While Caspar Friedrich Wolff is known for his work in embryology and biology, Christian Wolff's philosophical contributions were also highly influential."}]}, {"canonical_name": "moral", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "moral", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "moral", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["moral"], "contexts": ["relating to principles of right and wrong"]}, {"entity_id": "moral", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Moral", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Moral"], "contexts": ["ethics"]}, {"entity_id": "moral_ideal", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "moral ideal", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["moral ideal"], "contexts": ["goal of ethical progress"]}, {"entity_id": "morality", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Morality", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Morality"], "contexts": ["principles concerning the distinction between right and wrong"]}, {"entity_id": "principles_of_morality", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Principles of Morality", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Principles of Morality"], "contexts": ["book title"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "moral", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Moral", "similarity": 0.983}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "moral", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "moral ideal", "similarity": 0.891}, {"source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "source_name": "Moral", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "moral ideal", "similarity": 0.884}], "id": 1464, "stable_key": "clu_2c940b8da5a04201", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Morality", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q1132684", "wikidata_description": "ethical practice concerning scientific research", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Research%20ethics", "wikipedia_extract": "Research ethics is a discipline within the study of applied ethics. Its scope ranges from general scientific integrity and misconduct to the treatment of human and animal subjects. The social responsibilities of scientists and researchers are not traditionally included and are less well defined. The discipline is most developed in medical research. Beyond the issues of falsification, fabrication, and plagiarism that arise in every scientific field, research design in human subject research and animal testing are the areas that raise ethical questions most often. The list of historic cases includes many large-scale violations and crimes against humanity such as Nazi human experimentation and the Tuskegee syphilis experiment which led to international codes of research ethics."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "vertue", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2161, "target_cluster_name": "vertue", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Virtue is a core concept in morality, representing good character and ethical conduct.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Virtue is a core concept in morality, representing good character and ethical conduct.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Ethics", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3809, "target_cluster_name": "Ethicks", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Morality is a core component of ethical philosophy, dealing with principles of right and wrong conduct.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Morality is a core component of ethical philosophy, dealing with principles of right and wrong conduct."}]}, {"canonical_name": "vibrating string", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 3, "members": [{"entity_id": "vibrating_string", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "vibrating string", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["vibrating string"], "contexts": ["object producing sound through vibration"]}, {"entity_id": "vibrating_string", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "vibrating string", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["vibrating string"], "contexts": ["string that oscillates"]}, {"entity_id": "vibrating_strings", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "vibrating strings", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["vibrating strings"], "contexts": ["strings producing sound waves"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "vibrating string", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "vibrating string", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "vibrating string", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "vibrating strings", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "vibrating string", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "vibrating strings", "similarity": 0.961}], "id": 1465, "stable_key": "clu_4756209a1e3b9a2f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "vibrating string", "confidence": "high", "type": "object", "wikidata_id": "Q3252739", "wikidata_description": "A vibration in a string is a wave", "wikipedia_extract": "A sex toy is an object or device that is primarily used to facilitate sexual pleasure, such as a dildo, artificial vagina or vibrator. Many popular sex toys are designed to resemble human genitals, and may be vibrating or non-vibrating. The term sex toy can also include BDSM apparatus and sex furniture such as sex swings; however, it is not applied to items such as birth control, pornography, or condoms. Alternative terms for sex toy include adult toy and the dated euphemism marital aid. Marital aid also has a broader meaning and is applied to drugs and herbs marketed to enhance or prolong sex. Sex toys are most commonly sold at sex shops or online, but they may also be sold in a pharmacy, a pornography store, a head shop, or a department store.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sex_toy"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "tuning-fork", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1108, "target_cluster_name": "tuning-fork", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both tuning forks and vibrating strings produce sound through vibration, forming the basis of musical tones.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both tuning forks and vibrating strings produce sound through vibration, forming the basis of musical tones.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "thread", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1365, "target_cluster_name": "thread", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both 'thread' in the context of computer programming (thread-local storage) and 'vibrating string' can be conceptualized as entities that carry or transmit information or state, albeit in very different domains. A thread in computing is a sequence of execution that carries state, much like a vibrating string carries wave information. This is a conceptual analogy rather than a direct equivalence.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both 'thread' in the context of computer programming (thread-local storage) and 'vibrating string' can be conceptualized as entities that carry or transmit information or state, albeit in very different domains. A thread in computing is a sequence of execution that carries state, much like a vibrating string carries wave information. This is a 