ring Paracelsus's time. Paracelsus was a vocal critic of the Galenic-Avicennian medical tradition, positioning himself in opposition to Avicenna's authority.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Amat.", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 902, "target_cluster_name": "Amat.", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Avicenna, like Averroes, was a major Islamic philosopher whose work engaged deeply with Aristotelian philosophy, though sometimes diverging from it.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Avicenna, like Averroes, was a major Islamic philosopher whose work engaged deeply with Aristotelian philosophy, though sometimes diverging from it.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Hippocrates", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 31, "target_cluster_name": "Hippocrates", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Avicenna, like many physicians of his time, built upon the medical tradition established by Hippocrates.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Avicenna, like many physicians of his time, built upon the medical tradition established by Hippocrates."}, {"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Avicenna was a major philosopher who engaged deeply with and was influenced by Aristotelian thought, integrating it into his own philosophical and scientific works.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Avicenna was a major philosopher who engaged deeply with and was influenced by Aristotelian thought, integrating it into his own philosophical and scientific works."}, {"found_name": "Dioscorides", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 33, "target_cluster