 chamar regulus serpens; e pêra estas deu Deos nella este pao da cobra; e soubese aproveitar pêra a morde- dura de", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of 'bichos'"}]}, {"canonical_name": "lombrigas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 61, "members": [{"entity_id": "lombrigas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "lombrigas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 5, "variants": ["lombrigas"], "contexts": ["Worms, treated with medicine", "treated with anacardo"]}, {"entity_id": "lombrigas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "lombrigas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 56, "variants": ["lombrigas", "Lombrigas", "as lombricas", "lombri-", "lombrias", "lombricagas", "lombriga", "lombrigas Afcaridas", "lonmbrigas"], "contexts": ["condition treated by remedy", "worms"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "lombrigas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "lombrigas", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1536, "stable_key": "clu_20bf3ab40c523722", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "worms", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "Intestinal parasites causing ailments.", "note": "The terms 'lombrigas' and 'lumbrígas' are Portuguese for worms.", "wikipedia_extract": "Parasitic worms, also known as helminths, are a polyphyletic group of large macroparasites; adults can generally be seen with the naked eye. Many are intestinal worms that are soil-transmitted and infect the gastrointestinal tract. Other parasitic worms such as  schistosomes reside in blood vessels. Some parasitic worms, including leeches and monogeneans, are ectoparasites –  thus, they are not classified as helminths, which are endoparasites. Parasitic worms live in and feed in living hosts. They receive nourishment and protection while disrupting their hosts' ability to absorb nutrients."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "gora", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 234, "target_cluster_name": "Gout", "source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "evidence_snippet": "eſte en rez mojola hina; por.veyricery quarro:horas, antes +1: Curan ſecos edtaagua¡nruchao enfermedades: Las enfer todo genero de mal de Buuas, todas llagas viejas, medades uFccrds,desháterofódone an", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of gout"}, {"found_name": "landes", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "pareceme que dizem bem, porque sabem a bolotas de sovereiro, que em nossa terra chamam landes; e os caroços, scilicet, o miolo delles, dizem que mata as lombrigas, quando he verde, e tem rezão, porque", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for bolotas de sovereiro"}, {"found_name": "mal de Buuas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "evidence_snippet": "eſte en rez mojola hina; por.veyricery quarro:horas, antes +1: Curan ſecos edtaagua¡nruchao enfermedades: Las enfer todo genero de mal de Buuas, todas llagas viejas, medades uFccrds,desháterofódone an", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of disease"}, {"found_name": "llagas viejas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "evidence_snippet": "eſte en rez mojola hina; por.veyricery quarro:horas, antes +1: Curan ſecos edtaagua¡nruchao enfermedades: Las enfer todo genero de mal de Buuas, todas llagas viejas, medades uFccrds,desháterofódone an", "confidence": 0.65, "au