, "gemasde ovos cruas", "gemasdeovos freicos"], "contexts": ["food for the sick", "Egg yolks, used as a nutritive aid"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "gemas de ovos", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "gemas de ovos", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1537, "stable_key": "clu_575ab3aea731bbfa-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "egg", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "description": "Reproductive body laid by female birds, reptiles, amphibians, fish, and insects.", "note": "The context for 'ovelhas' (sheep) is anomalous; it appears to refer to animals that eat a plant, not the egg itself.", "wikipedia_extract": "An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has become an animal fetus that can survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\". Most arthropods, vertebrates (excluding live-bearing mammals), and mollusks lay eggs, although some, such as scorpions, do not. Reptile eggs, bird eggs, and monotreme eggs are laid out of water and are surrounded by a protective shell, either flexible or inflexible. Eggs laid on land or in nests are usually kept within a warm and favorable temperature range while the embryo grows."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "claradeovo", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 3198, "target_cluster_name": "claradeovo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The historical name 'gemas de ovos' is a direct Portuguese translation of 'egg yolks', referring to a component of the egg.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "reverse: The historical name 'gemas de ovos' is a direct Portuguese translation of 'egg yolks', referring to a component of the egg.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "ervas", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 60, "members": [{"entity_id": "erva", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "erva", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 6, "variants": ["erva", "erpa", "ervas"], "contexts": ["herb, used in medicine", "herb used in remedies"]}, {"entity_id": "ervas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "ervas", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 54, "variants": ["ervas", "erva", "erva crista", "ervadoce"], "contexts": ["herbs associated with coldness", "herbs used in remedies"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "erva", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "ervas", "similarity": 0.951}], "id": 1538, "stable_key": "clu_186ce6599f42c5e8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Herbs", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "description": "Plants or parts of plants used for medicinal or culinary purposes.", "wikipedia_extract": "Herbs are a widely distributed and widespread group of plants, excluding vegetables, with savory or aromatic properties that are used for flavoring and garnishing food, for medicinal purposes, or for fragrances. Culinary use typically distinguishes herbs from spices. Herbs generally refers to the leafy green or flowering parts of a plant (either fresh or dried), while spices are usually dried and produced from other parts of the plant, including seeds, bark, roots and fruits. Herbs have a variety of uses including culinary, medicinal, aromatic and in some cases, spiritual. General usage of the term \"herb\" differs between culinary herbs and medicinal herbs; in medicinal or spiritual use, any parts of the plant might be considered \"herbs\", including leaves, roots, flowers, seeds, root bark, inner bark (and cambium), resin and pericarp. The word \"herb\" is pronounced  in Commonwealth English, but  is standard among American English speakers as well as those from regions where h-dropping occurs."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "chá", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 855, "target_cluster_name": "chá", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tea is a type of herbal infusion, and the term 'herbs' encompasses a broad category to which tea belongs, often appearing in discussions of medicinal or culinary plants.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Tea is a type of herbal infusion, and the term 'herbs' encompasses a broad category to which tea belongs, often appearing in discussions of medicinal or culinary plants.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "fragrant herbs", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2868, "target_cluster_name": "odorata", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This is a specific type of herb, emphasizing its aromatic properties, which aligns with the general description of herbs.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "This is a specific type of herb, emphasizing its aromatic properties, which aligns with the general description of herbs."}, {"found_name": "Spices", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2144, "target_cluster_name": "especiarias", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Herbs and spices are often discussed together and distinguished by their culinary use (herbs typically from leaves, spices from other plant parts), indicating a close, albeit distinct, relationship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Herbs and spices are often discussed together and distinguished by their culinary use (herbs typically from leaves, spices from other plant parts), indicating a close, albeit distinct, relationship."}, {"found_name": "Simple remedies", "link_ty