. ORTA Nasce em Mascate e Calaiate (terras da Arábia) onde ha tanto, como a erva comum que pacem as bestas em Espanha; e ali ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for erva"}, {"found_name": "haxiscaçule", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "contraponto ao cabo. RUANO Isso não se escusa; por tanto começai em ora boa. ORTA Nasce em Mascate e Calaiate (terras da Arábia) onde ha tanto, como a erva comum que pacem as bestas em Espanha; e ali ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for erva"}, {"found_name": "alaf", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "da Arábia) onde ha tanto, como a erva comum que pacem as bestas em Espanha; e ali lhe chamam cachabar, e alguns lhe chamam haxiscaçule, que quer dizer erpa pêra lavar; e em Pérsia, que confina com as ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for erva"}, {"found_name": "atambor", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "de um pote de méo almude, e era de largura de dous parmos (palmos) na boca, a quail era muito grosa ao parecer, na qual talha lançava bagaço de humas ervas que os homens desta terra comem pella calma,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for erva"}]}, {"canonical_name": "ouro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 8, "total_mentions": 120, "members": [{"entity_id": "ouro", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "ouro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 14, "variants": ["ouro", "Ouro", "oro"], "contexts": ["precious metal used for payment", "merchandise from China"]}, {"entity_id": "ouro", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "ouro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 44, "variants": ["ouro", "Ouro", "auro", "ouro calcinado", "ouronão", "ouroſado"], "contexts": ["Precious metal from mines", "gold"]}, {"entity_id": "oro", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "oro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["oro"], "contexts": ["Spanish for gold", "gold, traded in the region"]}, {"entity_id": "oro", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Oro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 30, "variants": ["oro", "Oro"], "contexts": ["precious metal brought from the Indies", "gold"]}, {"entity_id": "oro", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "oro", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 9, "variants": ["oro"], "contexts": ["gold, a precious metal", "metal where borrace is found"]}, {"entity_id": "gold", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Gold", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 10, "variants": ["Gold"], "contexts": ["precious metal sought from Ophir", "metal"]}, {"entity_id": "gold", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Gold", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 9, "variants": ["gold", "Gold"], "contexts": ["malleable metal", "metal that can be beaten thin"]}, {"entity_id": "gold", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "gold", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["gold"], "contexts": ["metal used in remedies"]}, {"entity_id": "gold", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "gold", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["gold"], "contexts": ["precious yellow metal"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "ouro", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "ouro", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1539, "stable_key": "clu_64d81d6eb417e778", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Gold", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "The Spanish word 'oro' directly translates to 'gold'.", "wikidata_id": "Q897", "wikidata_description": "chemical element with symbol Au and atomic number 79", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold", "wikipedia_extract": "Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au (from Latin aurum) and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions. Gold often occurs as the free element (native state), as nuggets or grains, in rocks, veins, and alluvial deposits."}, "member_count": 9, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "metal", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 87, "target_cluster_name": "metal", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Gold is a fundamental metal.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Gold is a fundamental metal.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "copper", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 274, "target_cluster_name": "copper", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Gold and copper are both precious metals with distinct colors and properties, often discussed together in metallurgy and alchemy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Gold and copper are both precious metals with distinct colors and properties, often discussed together in metallurgy and alch