ous stone (ruby)", "precious stone, also called carbunculus"]}, {"entity_id": "rame", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "rame", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 36, "variants": ["rame", "Rame", "Rame .", "Rame abbruciato", "Rame arfo", "Rame arfo lauaco", "Rame àrfo", "rame roffo", "ramej"], "contexts": ["metal from under the earth", "metal where borrace is found"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "rubim", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "rame", "similarity": 0.888}], "id": 1552, "stable_key": "clu_ca01542294152be0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ruby", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "'Rubim' is the Portuguese for ruby, and 'rame' (in this context, likely a misspelling or variant of 'rubi') and 'precious stone' point to the gem.  The metal context is less likely given the gem identification.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "variety of corundum, mineral, gemstone", "wikipedia_url": "", "wikipedia_extract": ""}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Llanos", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 51, "members": [{"entity_id": "llanos", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Llanos", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 50, "variants": ["Llanos", "Los Llanos", "llanos"], "contexts": ["vast plains traversed by travelers", "region where insects are rare"]}, {"entity_id": "llanos", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "llanos", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["llanos"], "contexts": ["grassy plains in the New Continent"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Llanos", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "llanos", "similarity": 0.595}], "id": 1553, "stable_key": "clu_08ea6f182e554177", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Llanos", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Venezuela, Colombia", "note": "The original text has 'llermanos' which is likely a typo for 'Llanos' given the context of tropical grasslands in South America and the variant spelling 'llanoses'.", "wikidata_id": "", "wikidata_description": "family name"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Calabozo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1697, "target_cluster_name": "Calabozo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calabozo is a town located within the Llanos region of Venezuela.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Calabozo is a town located within the Llanos region of Venezuela."}, {"found_name": "Equatorial America", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1437, "target_cluster_name": "equatorial America", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Llanos are a vast tropical grassland plain in South America, often considered part of Equatorial America.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Llanos are a vast tropical grassland plain in South America, often considered part of Equatorial America."}]}, {"canonical_name": "vino", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 7, "total_mentions": 64, "members": [{"entity_id": "vino", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "vino", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 36, "variants": ["vino", "Vino", "vino aguado", "vino blanco", "vino tinto"], "contexts": ["wine", "vehicle and corroboration for the root's work"]}, {"entity_id": "vino", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Vino", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 15, "variants": ["Vino", "vino"], "contexts": ["substance drawn by art", "source of wine lees"]}, {"entity_id": "vins", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol