tion techniques. Wine has been produced for thousands of years, the earliest evidence dating from c. 6000 BCE in present-day Georgia. Its popularity spread around the Mediterranean during Classical antiquity, and was sustained in Western Europe by winemaking monks and a secular trade for general drinking. New World wine was established by settler colonies from the 16th century onwards, and the wine trade increased dramatically up to the latter half of the 19th century, when European vineyards were largely destroyed by the invasive pest phylloxera."}, "member_count": 7, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "vino", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 48, "target_cluster_name": "Wine", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Spanish for wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Spanish for wine."}, {"found_name": "Alcohol", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 131, "target_cluster_name": "alcohol", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alcohol is the primary intoxicating component of wine, produced through its fermentation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Alcohol is the primary intoxicating component of wine, produced through its fermentation."}, {"found_name": "Beer", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2169, "target_cluster_name": "Beer", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Beer is another fermented beverage, often compared to wine in historical texts discussing alcoholic drinks.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Beer is another fermented beverage, often compared to wine in historical texts discussing alcoholic drinks."}, {"found_name": "Beverage", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 321, "target_cluster_name": "licor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Wine is a type of beverage.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Wine is a type of beverage."}, {"found_name": "Grape must reduction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2362, "target_cluster_name": "Sapa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Grape must reduction (Sapa) is a concentrated form of grape juice, the primary ingredient in wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Grape must reduction (Sapa) is a concentrated form of grape juice, the primary ingredient in wine."}, {"found_name": "Hot wine", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3683, "target_cluster_name": "vino caliente", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Hot wine is a preparation of wine, often spiced, consumed as a beverage.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Hot wine is a preparation of wine, often spiced, consumed as a beverage."}]}, {"canonical_name": "chagas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 51, "members": [{"entity_id": "chagas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "chagas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 6, "variants": ["chagas", "chaga", "chagas muyto roins", "chaguas"], "contexts": ["Wounds or sores", "wounds treated with cataplasm"]}, {"entity_id": "chagas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "chagas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "OTHER_DISEASE", "count": 45, "variants": ["chagas", "Chagas"], "contexts": ["wounds or sores", "ulcers"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "chagas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "chagas", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1555, "stable_key": "clu_fdc2182b9bfa516b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Chagas disease", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "Chagas disease", "note": "The term 'chagas' in the 16th century likely referred to a more general concept of skin lesions or sores, as Chagas disease was not identified until much later. However, the modern association with the term is strong.", "wikidata_id": "Q649558", "wikidata_description": "human disease", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chagas%20disease", "wikipedia_extract": "Chagas disease, also known as American trypanosomiasis, is a tropical parasitic disease caused by Trypanosoma cruzi. It is spread mostly by insects in the subfamily Triatominae, known as \"kissing bugs\". The symptoms change throughout the infection. In the early stage, symptoms are typically either not present or mild and may include fever, swollen lymph nodes, headaches, or swelling at the site of the bite. After four to eight weeks, untreated individuals enter the chronic phase of disease, which in most cases does not result in further symptoms. Up to 45% of people with chronic infections develop heart disease 10–30 years after the initial illness, which can lead to heart failure."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Arte", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 51, "members": [{"entity_id": "arte", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Arte", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 10, "variants": ["Arte", "ARTE", "Arte dell'Arte"], "contexts": ["title of a book section", "guild or trade association"]}, {"entity_id": "arte", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Arte", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 41, "variants": ["Arte", "Art.", "Arte Medica", "Artes", "acredito da Arte", "arte"], "contexts": ["the art of medicine", "art that prepares substances"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Arte", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Arte", "si