modern) contexts, and in modern times in the context of Orientalism. Occasionally, the term may also include countries in Eastern Europe and the Balkans. The Eastern world is often seen as a counterpart to the Western world. The various regions included in the term are varied, hard to generalize, and do not have a single shared common heritage. Although the various parts of the Eastern world share many common threads, most notably being in the \"Global South\", they have never historically defined themselves collectively."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "asi", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "esta dirívaçam: e porque chamam oríen- taes a estas pérolas boas, por ventura porque eram de cor dourada? QRTA Nam, senão porque vinham da banda do Oriente, e porque este estreito de Ormuz era orienta", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for 'Oriente' in this context"}, {"found_name": "Arabia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 169, "target_cluster_name": "Arabia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arabia is considered part of the Eastern world in historical geographical contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arabia is considered part of the Eastern world in historical geographical contexts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Asia is a primary component of the 'Eastern world'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Asia is a primary component of the 'Eastern world'."}, {"found_name": "Levant", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_i