saber, e soubeo; e os figos na lingoa canarim e decanim e guzarate e b", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for figs"}, {"found_name": "figiio", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "alguns mais e outros menos; e k^ day avante naçe ao pé outra arvore dos mesmos nunos ou do tronco; porque o tronco he hum ajuntamento de coitezas% e os figuos nascem no dho da figueira ape- gados ao p", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Italian name for muse"}]}, {"canonical_name": "vinho tinto", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "vinho_branco", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "vinho branco", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["vinho branco"], "contexts": ["white wine, an ingredient"]}, {"entity_id": "vinho_tinto", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "vinho tinto", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 32, "variants": ["vinho tinto", "vinho alcanforado", "vinho muyto tinto", "vinho vermelho", "vinhobranco"], "contexts": ["liquid used for treatment", "used for trembling parts"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "vinho branco", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "vinho tinto", "similarity": 0.92}], "id": 1637, "stable_key": "clu_35ef18c1d7bbe7d4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Red Wine", "confidence": "high", "type": "chemical", "note": "The cluster includes both 'vinho tinto' (red wine) and 'vinho branco' (white wine). The broader context suggests it refers to wine as a substance or preparation, with red wine being the more frequently mentioned."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Alcohol", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 131, "target_cluster_name": "alcohol", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alcohol is a primary component of wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Alcohol is a primary component of wine."}, {"found_name": "Wine", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 48, "target_cluster_name": "Wine", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Red wine is a specific type of wine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Red wine is a specific type of wine."}]}, {"canonical_name": "diaprunis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "diaprunum", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Diaprunum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Diaprunum"], "contexts": ["medicinal preparation"]}, {"entity_id": "diaprunis", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "diaprunis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 32, "variants": ["diaprunis", "Diaphenica", "Diaphenicao", "Diaphenicaó", "Diaphenicone", "Diaphenicão", "diapheni", "diaphenica", "diaphenicam", "diaphenicao", "diaphenicaó", "diaphenicaõ", "diaphenicaō", "diaphenicão"], "contexts": ["a medicinal preparation", "prunes, a fruit"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "source_name": "Diaprunum", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "diaprunis", "similarity": 0.916}], "id": 1638, "stable_key": "clu_fe1a7cf0e0b8a583", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Diaprun", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A medicinal preparation, often containing prunes.", "note": "Historical term for a type of confection or electuary.", "wikipedia_extract": "A prune is a dried plum, most commonly from the European plum (Prunus domestica) tree. Not all plum species or varieties can be dried into prunes. Use of the term prune for fresh plums is obsolete except when applied to varieties of plum grown for drying. In this usage, a prune is the firm-fleshed plum fruit of P. domestica varieties that have a high soluble solids content and do not ferment during drying. Most prunes are freestone cultivars (i.e., the pit is easy to remove), whereas most plums grown for fresh consumption are clingstone (the pit is more difficult to remove). The sorbitol content of dietary fiber likely provides the laxative effect associated with consuming prunes."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "satellites", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 33, "members": [{"entity_id": "satellites", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "satellites", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 25, "variants": ["satellites", "Satellites"], "contexts": ["celestial bodies orbiting planets", "bodies orbiting planets"]}, {"entity_id": "satellite", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "satellite", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["satellite"], "contexts": ["celestial body orbiting a planet", "body orbiting a planet"]}, {"entity_id": "satellites", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "satellites", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["satellites"], "contexts": ["celestial bodies orbiting planets", "celestial bodies orbiting a planet"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "satellites", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "satellites", "similarity": 1.0}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "satellite", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "satellites", "similarity": 0.969}], "id": 1639, "stable_key": "clu_a18d38f2a9e7f8c4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Satellite", "confidence": "low", "type": "animal", "note": "The contexts 'celestial bodies orbiting planets' clearly indicate this is a celestial object, not an animal. The term 'satellite' in an animal context would be highly unusual and likely metaphorical, with no clear referent without more information.", "wikidata_id": "Q2537", "wikidata_description": "celestial body that orbits a planet or other smaller body in turn directly orbiting a star", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural%20satellite", "wikipedia_extract": "A natural satellite is, in the most common usage, an astronomical body that orbits a planet, dwarf planet, or small Solar System body (or sometimes another natural satellite). Natural satellites are colloquially referred to as moons, a derivation from the Moon of Earth. In the Solar System, there are six planetary satellite systems, altogether comprising 419 natural satellites with confirmed orbits. Seven objects commonly considered dwarf planets by astronomers are also known to have natural satellites: Orcus, Pluto, Haumea, Quaoar, Makemake, Gonggong, and Eris. As of January 2022, there are 447 other minor planets known to have natural satellites. The first known natural satellite was the Moon, but it was considered a \"planet\" until Copernicus' introduction of De revolutionibus orbium coelestium in 1543."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Glacial period", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "glacial_period", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Glacial period", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 24, "variants": ["glacial period", "Glacial period"], "contexts": ["period of extensive glaciation", "period of migration and climate change"]}, {"entity_id": "glacial_epoch", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Glacial epoch", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["glacial epoch", "Glacial epoch"], "contexts": ["period of extensive glaciation", "geological time period"]}, {"entity_id": "glacial_epoch", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "glacial epoch", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["glacial epoch"], "contexts": ["period of severe cold and ice", "geological epoch"]}, {"entity_id": "glacial_period", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "glacial period", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["glacial period"], "contexts": ["geological epoch"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Glacial period", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "glacial epoch", "similarity": 0.912}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Glacial period", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "glacial period", "similarity": 0.941}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Glacial epoch", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "glacial epoch", "similarity": 0.953}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Glacial epoch", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "glacial period", "similarity": 0.914}], "id": 1640, "stable_key": "clu_e434aed44f0237c2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Glacial Period", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q60689427", "wikidata_description": "scholarly article"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "geological period", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 846, "target_cluster_name": "geological period", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Glacial Period is a specific, significant epoch within geological time.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Glacial Period is a specific, significant epoch within geological time.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "geological changes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1387, "target_cluster_name": "geological changes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Glacial Period is a specific, major event within geological history characterized by extensive ice sheets, representing a significant instance of geological change.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Glacial Period is a specific, major event within geological history characterized by extensive ice sheets, representing a significant instance of geological change.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Glacial erosion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4010, "target_cluster_name": "glacial action", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Glacial Period is a geological epoch characterized by extensive glaciation, and glacial erosion is a direct consequence and defining feature of such periods.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Glacial Period is a geological epoch characterized by extensive glaciation, and glacial erosion is a direct consequence and defining feature of such periods."}, {"found_name": "palæozoic period", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2534, "target_cluster_name": "palæozoic period", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Paleozoic Era includes periods that experienced glaciation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Paleozoic Era includes periods that experienced glaciation.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Pliocene period", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2728, "target_cluster_name": "Pliocene period", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Pliocene period is a geological epoch that precedes the Quaternary Glacial Period, and understanding its context is important for studying subsequent glacial events.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Pliocene period is a geological epoch that precedes the Quaternary Glacial Period, and understanding its context is important for studying subsequent glacial events.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "cabo de Comorim", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "cape_comorin", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Cape Comorin", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cape Comorin"], "contexts": ["southern tip of India"]}, {"entity_id": "cabo_de_comorim", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "cabo de Comorim", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 31, "variants": ["cabo de Comorim", "Cabo de Comorim", "Comori", "Comorim", "cabo Comorim", "cabo Comorím", "cabo das Correntes", "cabo de Comorí", "cabo de Comorím", "cabo de G>morí", "cabo de Galimere", "cabo de Ganhameíra", "cabo do Comorim"], "contexts": ["geographical location", "promontory on the coast"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Cape Comorin", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "cabo de Comorim", "similarity": 0.916}], "id": 1641, "stable_key": "clu_2b90f67d52ce37a9", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Kanyakumari", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "India", "wikidata_id": "Q222267", "wikidata_description": "coastal city in the state of Tamil Nadu on main land India's southern tip", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kanyakumari", "wikipedia_extract": "Kanyakumari (lit. 'The virgin Girl', referring to Devi Kanya Kumari, officially known as Kanniyakumari, formerly known as Cape Comorin) is a town and municipality in Kanyakumari district in the state of Tamil Nadu, India. It is the southernmost tip of the contiguous Indian subcontinent and the southernmost city in mainland India, and thus it is informally referred to as \"The Land's End\". Kanyakumari town is about 90 kilometres (56 mi) from Thiruvananthapuram and  20 kilometres (12 mi) south of Nagercoil, the headquarters of Kanyakumari district. Kanyakumari is a popular tourist destination and pilgrimage centre in India. Notable tourist spots include its unique sunrise and sunset points, the 41-metre (133 ft) Thiruvalluvar Statue, and Vivekananda Rock Memorial off the coast."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 655, "target_cluster_name": "Cape of Good Hope", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are significant capes at the southern extremities of major landmasses, historically important for navigation and trade routes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are significant capes at the southern extremities of major landmasses, historically important for navigation and trade routes."}, {"found_name": "Malabar Coast", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 58, "target_cluster_name": "Malaca", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Kanyakumari is located at the southern tip of the Indian subcontinent, adjacent to the historical Malabar Coast, a region of significant trade and cultural exchange.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Kanyakumari is located at the southern tip of the Indian subcontinent, adjacent to the historical Malabar Coast, a region of significant trade and cultural exchange."}, {"found_name": "India", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 17, "target_cluster_name": "India", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Kanyakumari is a town within India, representing its southernmost point.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Kanyakumari is a town within India, representing its southernmost point."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Darien", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 32, "members": [{"entity_id": "darien", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Darien", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 31, "variants": ["Darien", "Daricn", "Darien del Norte", "Darinn"], "contexts": ["region in Panama", "gulf and region in Panama/Colombia"]}, {"entity_id": "daríen", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Daríen", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Daríen"], "contexts": ["region in the Americas"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Darien", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Daríen", "similarity": 0.701}], "id": 1642, "stable_key": "clu_dc3ed533efa7e4fb", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Darién", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Panama"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Choco", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1615, "target_cluster_name": "Choco", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Darién is a region in Panama and Colombia, historically and geographically connected to Chocó, often discussed in relation to exploration and indigenous populations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Darién is a region in Panama and Colombia, historically and geographically connected to Chocó, often discussed in relation to exploration and indigenous populations.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Caribbean Sea", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_clust