ociological, while Bain focused on empirical psychology and education."}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent figures in 19th-century science, though their fields differed significantly (Humboldt in geography and natural sciences, Bain in psychology and education). They represent prominent scientific figures of the era.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent figures in 19th-century science, though their fields differed significantly (Humboldt in geography and natural sciences, Bain in psychology and education). They represent prominent scientific figures of the era."}, {"found_name": "Charles Darwin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 118, "target_cluster_name": "Darwin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were significant figures in 19th-century intellectual life. Darwin's theory of evolution had a profound impact on many fields, including psychology, which Bain was developing.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were significant figures in 19th-century intellectual life. Darwin's theory of evolution had a profound impact on many fields, including psychology, which Bain was developing."}, {"found_name": "Francis Bacon", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 185, "target_cluster_name": "Bacon", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential figures in the development of empirical methods and scientific thought, though separated by centuries. Bain's work on associationism and scientific psychology can be seen as building on Baconian principles of observation and induction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "B