os. Porèm ſe eſta aguanão baſtar, podem recorrerparafomentações de agua cozida comhuma máo-chea de herva anagalis de flor vermelha , chamada vul", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vernacular name for 'anagalis de flor vermelha'"}, {"found_name": "cavallinha", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "feliciterdetinuo ufu xiga, &dos rins por virtude eſpecifica,hum delles he ouſo continuodebe- plovatum illudvefica ulcus , utfummè ber agua cozida com a herva equiceto, ou hipuris , a que vulgarmente c", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vernacular name for 'equiceto'"}, {"found_name": "rabodecavallo", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "evidence_snippet": "feliciterdetinuo ufu xiga, &dos rins por virtude eſpecifica,hum delles he ouſo continuodebe- plovatum illudvefica ulcus , utfummè ber agua cozida com a herva equiceto, ou hipuris , a que vulgarmente c", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "vernacular name for 'equiceto'"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Calabozo", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "calabozo", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Calabozo", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 24, "variants": ["Calabozo"], "contexts": ["location with astronomical determinations", "region with steppes"]}, {"entity_id": "calabozo", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Calabozo", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Calabozo"], "contexts": ["grassy plains where loud noise was heard"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Calabozo", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Calabozo", "similarity": 0.82}], "id": 1697, "stable_key": "clu_cbe382ce8a1d0206", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Calabozo", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Venezuela", "note": "Calabozo is a known location in Venezuela, particularly associated with Humboldt's travels and scientific observations.", "wikipedia_extract": "Calabozo, officially Villa de Todos los Santos de Calabozo, is a city in Venezuela located in Guárico state, capital of the Francisco de Miranda Municipality and former capital of the state. It has a population of 168,605, according to the National Institute of Statistics (INE) in 2020. It is located in the center-west of Guárico state, and is one of the main rice producers in the country. In addition, it has the largest irrigation system in Venezuela. Calabozo, is a mostly colonial city and is linked to its modern urban areas, being the largest colonial center in the country, and is located at 105 m a.s.l. n. m., at the margin of the Guárico River in the high central plain. Its location is on the banks of the Generoso Campilongo Dam, an important work both in its time and today, being the largest in Venezuela and one of the largest in Latin America."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Llanos", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1553, "target_cluster_name": "Llanos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Calabozo is a town located within the Llanos region of Venezuela.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Calabozo is a town located within the Llanos region of Venezuela.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Cayenne", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "cayenne", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Cayenne", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 22, "variants": ["Cayenne"], "contexts": ["capital of French Guiana", "region south of which plains extend"]}, {"entity_id": "cayenne", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Cayenne", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Cayenne"], "contexts": ["location of pendulum observation", "location for pendulum variation"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Cayenne", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Cayenne", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1698, "stable_key": "clu_9a799d4a551aa66c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cayenne", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "France", "note": "Cayenne is the capital of French Guiana, a territory often referenced in historical scientific and geographic accounts.", "wikidata_id": "Q44401", "wikidata_description": "commune and capital city of French Guiana"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Tourmaline", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "tourmaline_noire", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "tourmaline noire", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["tourmaline noire", "tourmaline"], "contexts": ["Black tourmaline mineral", "mineral in granite"]}, {"entity_id": "tourmaline", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Tourmaline", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 23, "variants": ["tourmaline", "Tourmaline"], "contexts": ["polarization by refraction properties", "mineral exhibiting double refraction"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "tourmaline noire", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Tourmaline", "similarity": 0.894}], "id": 1699, "stable_key": "clu_412ac61cbdbdede2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tourmaline", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "The references to 'tourmaline noire' and 'Tourmaline' in the given contexts strongly suggest the mineral tourmaline, particularly given its mention in relation to physical properties like polarization.", "wikidata_id": "Q179911", "wikidata_description": "cyclosilicate mineral supergroup", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tourmaline", "wikipedia_extract": "Tourmaline (  TOOR-mə-lin, -⁠leen) is a crystalline silicate mineral group in which boron is compounded with elements such as aluminium, iron, magnesium, sodium, lithium, or potassium. This gemstone comes in a wide variety of colors. The name is derived from the Sinhalese tōramalli (ටෝරමල්ලි), which refers to the carnelian gemstones. Brightly colored Ceylonese gem tourmalines were brought to Europe in great quantities by the Dutch East India Company, to satisfy a demand for curiosities and gems. Tourmaline was sometimes called the \"Ceylonese Magnet\" because it could attract and then repel hot ashes due to its pyroelectric properties. Tourmalines were used by chemists in the 19th century to polarize light by shining rays onto a cut and polished surface of the gem."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Amethyst", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2673, "target_cluster_name": "Amethyst", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are gemstones and are often discussed together in mineralogical texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are gemstones and are often discussed together in mineralogical texts."}, {"found_name": "Gems", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1119, "target_cluster_name": "gemms", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tourmaline is a type of gemstone.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tourmaline is a type of gemstone."}, {"found_name": "Minerals", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 138, "target_cluster_name": "minerals", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tourmaline is a mineral.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tourmaline is a mineral."}, {"found_name": "Crystal", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 696, "target_cluster_name": "Crystal", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tourmaline is a crystalline silicate mineral.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tourmaline is a crystalline silicate mineral."}, {"found_name": "Crystalline rocks", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3030, "target_cluster_name": "roches cristallines", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tourmaline is a crystalline silicate mineral, and crystalline rocks are composed of such minerals.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tourmaline is a crystalline silicate mineral, and crystalline rocks are composed of such minerals."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Sirius", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 25, "members": [{"entity_id": "sirius", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Sirius", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 4, "variants": ["Sirius"], "contexts": ["star used for distance measurement", "a bright star"]}, {"entity_id": "sirius", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Sirius", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 21, "variants": ["Sirius"], "contexts": ["star whose rising marked Egyptian year beginning", "star beyond which tail stretched"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Sirius", "target_book": "connexion_phys