tial geologists in the 19th century, contributing to the understanding of geological processes and history.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Charles Darwin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 118, "target_cluster_name": "Darwin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both Charles Lyell and Charles Darwin were prominent figures in 19th-century geology and natural history, with Darwin's theory of evolution being heavily influenced by Lyell's work on uniformitarianism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both Charles Lyell and Charles Darwin were prominent figures in 19th-century geology and natural history, with Darwin's theory of evolution being heavily influenced by Lyell's work on uniformitarianism."}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alexander von Humboldt was a highly influential geographer and naturalist whose extensive travels and scientific observations, particularly in the Americas, paralleled and influenced Lyell's own geological investigations and broader scientific interests.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Alexander von Humboldt was a highly influential geographer and naturalist whose extensive travels and scientific observations, particularly in the Americas, paralleled and influenced Lyell's own geological investigations and broader scientific interests."}, {"found_name": "Alfred Russel Wallace", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2104, "target_cluster_name": "Wallace", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alfred Russel Wallace, like Charles Darwin, was a key figure in the development of evolutionary theory, and his work, along with Darwin's, was part of the broader scientific discourse in which Lyell was a central figure in geology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Alfred Russel Wallace, like Charles Darwin, was a key figure in the development of evolutionary theory, and his work, along with Darwin's, was part of the broader scientific discourse in which Lyell was a central figure in geology."}, {"found_name": "Agassiz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1842, "target_cluster_name": "Agassiz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent geologists who significantly contributed to the understanding of Earth's history and geological processes. Lyell's work on uniformitarianism influenced Agassiz's theories on ice ages.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent geologists who significantly contributed to the understanding of Earth's history and geological processes. Lyell's work on uniformitarianism influenced Agassiz's theories on ice ages.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Murchison", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2183, "target_cluster_name": "Murchison", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent geologists in the 19th century, and Lyell's work on stratigraphy and uniformitarianism was foundational to the geological periodization Murchison contributed to.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent geologists in the 19th century, and Lyell's work on stratigraphy and uniformitarianism was foundational to the geological periodization Murchison contributed to.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Buckland", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2737, "target_cluster_name": "Buckland", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Charles Lyell was a leading geologist of the same era