lds, such as science, navigation and law."}, "member_count": 5, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "French", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 877, "target_cluster_name": "French", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The entity 'French' refers to a nation and culture. 'English people' refers to another distinct nation and culture, often in historical comparison or contrast with the French.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The entity 'French' refers to a nation and culture. 'English people' refers to another distinct nation and culture, often in historical comparison or contrast with the French.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Bartholomew Anglicus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3184, "target_cluster_name": "Bartholomeus Urbevetanus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Bartholomew Anglicus was an English Franciscan friar and encyclopedist, making him a direct historical and national antecedent to the concept of 'English people'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Bartholomew Anglicus was an English Franciscan friar and encyclopedist, making him a direct historical and national antecedent to the concept of 'English people'."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Baracoa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 22, "members": [{"entity_id": "baracoa", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Baracoa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 21, "variants": ["Baracoa", "Barracoa", "Barucoa"], "contexts": ["port and oldest European settlement", "port, oldest European settlement"]}, {"entity_id": "baracoa", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Baracoa", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Baracoa"], "contexts": ["location near fan palm"]}], "edge