": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "coentro seco", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1767, "stable_key": "clu_4da235b05a8199bf", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Coriander", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Coriandrum sativum", "family": "Apiaceae", "description": "Herb with aromatic seeds and leaves, used in medicine.", "wikipedia_extract": "Coriander (), or Coriandrum sativum, is an annual herb in the family Apiaceae. The leaves are known as cilantro () in the United States (but not in the United Kingdom). Most people perceive the leaves as having a fresh, slightly citrus taste. Due to variations in the gene OR6A2, some people perceive its flavor to be more soaplike or rotten. The species is native to the Mediterranean Basin. All parts of the plant are edible, with the fresh leaves and dried seeds most traditionally used in cooking."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Umbellifera", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 882, "target_cluster_name": "Umbellifera", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Coriander (Coriandrum sativum) is a species within the Apiaceae family.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Coriander (Coriandrum sativum) is a species within the Apiaceae family.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "ferula", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2476, "target_cluster_name": "ferula", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are aromatic herbs in the Apiaceae family, with seeds and leaves used in cooking and traditional medicine.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both are aromatic herbs in the Apiaceae family, with seeds and leaves used in cooking and traditional medicine.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Apiaceae", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 882, "target_cluster_name": "Umbelli