orities' (Antigos) referenced in premodern texts would have been Greek thinkers and writers, making 'Ancient Greeks' (Greci) a closely related entity."}, {"found_name": "Arab physicians", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 538, "target_cluster_name": "Arábios", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "While distinct, the medical traditions of Arab physicians were highly influential and often cited alongside or in succession to classical 'Ancient Authorities' (Antigos) in premodern scholarship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "While distinct, the medical traditions of Arab physicians were highly influential and often cited alongside or in succession to classical 'Ancient Authorities' (Antigos) in premodern scholarship."}, {"found_name": "Medicos Antigos", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1854, "target_cluster_name": "Medicos Antigos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ancient Physicians are a subset of the 'Ancient Authorities' referenced in texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ancient Physicians are a subset of the 'Ancient Authorities' referenced in texts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Philologos", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2867, "target_cluster_name": "Philologos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Philologists are scholars who study ancient texts and languages, making them a specific type of 'Ancient Authority'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Philologists are scholars who study ancient texts and languages, making them a specific type of 'Ancient Authority'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Elycrifon", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_