_ad2a90f941b69da9", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Dominique François Jean Arago", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1786, "death_year": 1853, "description": "French physicist, astronomer, and politician, known for magnetism and light.", "note": "The initials 'M.' are common for addressing gentlemen in this period. Arago was a prominent figure in science during the early 19th century."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Biot", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 723, "target_cluster_name": "Biot", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Dominique François Jean Arago was a contemporary French physicist and astronomer who collaborated with and was influenced by Biot.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Dominique François Jean Arago was a contemporary French physicist and astronomer who collaborated with and was influenced by Biot.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Fourier", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2132, "target_cluster_name": "Fourier", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent French scientists active in the same period. Arago was a physicist and astronomer, and he was involved in many of the same scientific societies and debates as Fourier, often engaging with Fourier's work on heat and mathematics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent French scientists active in the same period. Arago was a physicist and astronomer, and he was involved in many of the same scientific societies and debates as Fourier, often engaging with Fourier's work on heat and mathematics.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Melloni", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2444, "target_cluster_name": "Melloni", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Melloni was a physicist who worked on optics and heat, and Arago was a prominent physicist and astronomer who also worked on optics and magnetism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Melloni was a physicist who worked on optics and heat, and Arago was a prominent physicist and astronomer who also worked on optics and magnetism.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "salses", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 17, "members": [{"entity_id": "salses", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "salses", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Salses", "salses"], "contexts": ["phenomenon observed in the forest", "phenomenon observed by the author"]}, {"entity_id": "salses", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "salses", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 13, "variants": ["salses", "Salses"], "contexts": ["mud volcanoes or saline springs", "mud volcanoes"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "salses", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "salses", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1819, "stable_key": "clu_01e47070bcbbf972", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Salses", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Trinidad and Tobago, Venezuela, etc.", "note": "Refers to mud volcanoes or saline springs, often associated with geological activity.", "wikidata_id": "Q193457", "wikidata_description": "landform created by the eruption of mud or slurries, water and gases", "wikipedia_extract": "The Fronde (French pronunciation: [fʁɔ̃d] ) was a series of civil wars in the Kingdom of France between 1648 and 1653, occurring in the midst of the Franco-Spanish War, which had begun in 1635. The government of the young King Louis XIV confronted the combined opposition of the princes, the nobility, the noble regional court assemblies (parlements), as well as much of the French population, and managed to subdue them all. The dispute started when the government of France issued seven fiscal edicts, six of which were to increase taxation. The parlements resisted, questioned the constitutionality of the king's actions, and sought to check his powers. The Fronde was divided into two campaigns, the Parlementary Fronde and the Fronde of the Princes. The timing of the outbreak of the Parlementary Fronde, directly after the Peace of Westphalia (1648) that ended the Thirty Years' War, was significant.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fronde"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "volcanoes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 299, "target_cluster_name": "volcanoes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Salses are mud volcanoes, a type of volcanic feature.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Salses are mud volcanoes, a type of volcanic feature.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "mud volcanoes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "[See Daubeney 'On Volcanoes', 2d edit., 3848, p. 539, etc., on the so called 'mud volcanoes', and the reasons advanced in favor of adopting the term \"salses\" to designate these phenomena.] -- Tr. Larg", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of phenomenon"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Sulfur", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 17, "members": [{"entity_id": "sulfate", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "sulfate", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["sulfate"], "contexts": ["sulfate salt formed", "chemical compound"]}, {"entity_id": "sulfure_de_fer", "book_id": "relation_his