 work.", "wikidata_id": "Q15443", "wikidata_description": "Irish physician and botanist (1783-1856)"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Quartan Agues", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "quartane_ague", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Quartane Ague", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Quartane Ague"], "contexts": ["Type of fever"]}, {"entity_id": "quartan_agues", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Quartan Agues", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 13, "variants": ["Quartan Agues", "Quartan", "Quartan Ague", "Quartane Agues", "Quar∣tanes"], "contexts": ["fever cured by sympathy to Saturn", "ague removed by the herb"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Quartane Ague", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Quartan Agues", "similarity": 0.886}], "id": 1890, "stable_key": "clu_b3bafc6ad0a2cb5f-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Quartan fever", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A type of malaria characterized by fevers occurring every fourth day.", "wikipedia_extract": "Quartan fever is one of the four types of malaria which can be contracted by humans. It is specifically caused by the Plasmodium malariae species, one of the six species of the protozoan genus Plasmodium. Quartan fever is a form of malaria where an onset of fever occurs in an interval of three to four days, hence the name \"quartan\". It is transmitted by bites of infected female mosquitoes of the genus Anopheles. Symptoms include fevers which range from approximately 40–41 °C (104–106 °F) and occur periodically in 72 hour intervals. Although cases of malaria have occurred throughout the world, quartan fever typically occurs in the subtropics."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "lacca", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "lacca", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Lacca", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Lacca"], "contexts": ["juice concrete drawing not at all"]}, {"entity_id": "lacca", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "lacca", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 13, "variants": ["lacca", "laca"], "contexts": ["animal product from insect on tree branches", "animal product formed by insect on plant"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Lacca", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "lacca", "similarity": 0.814}], "id": 1891, "stable_key": "clu_7a80c0af1f61a6f8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Shellac", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Conserve", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 683, "target_cluster_name": "Conserve", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "This is the Italian word for shellac, often used in historical texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: This is the Italian word for shellac, often used in historical texts.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "resina", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2624, "target_cluster_name": "resina", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Shellac is a resin secreted by the lac insect.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Shellac is a resin secreted by the lac insect.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Countries", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "countries", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Countries", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 11, "variants": ["Countries"], "contexts": ["geographic locations where herbs grow", "divers countries of this Nation"]}, {"entity_id": "countries", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "countries", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["countries"], "contexts": ["geographic locations", "locations with domesticated animals"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Countries", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "countries", "similarity": 0.981}], "id": 1892, "stable_key": "clu_11ee66e3865f1caa", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Countries", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "wikidata_id": "Q6256", "wikidata_description": "distinct territorial body or political entity"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Continent", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 25, "target_cluster_name": "continent", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Continents are composed of multiple countries.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Continents are composed of multiple countries."}, {"found_name": "World", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 163, "target_cluster_name": "world", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The 'World' encompasses all countries.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The 'World' encompasses all countries."}, {"found_name": "Regions", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 517, "target_cluster_name": "Regions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Countries are a type of geographical region.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Countries are a type of geographical region."}]}, {"canonical_name": "transpiração", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "sweating", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "sweating", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 2, "variants": ["sweating"], "contexts": ["expulsion method for disease", "bodily process to expel venom"]}, {"entity_id": "transpiração", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "transpiração", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 12, "variants": ["transpiração", "tranfpiraçao", "transpiraçao", "tranſpiratio", "tranſpiração", "tranſpirem"], "contexts": ["bodily process", "bodily process, opening pores for"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "sweating", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "transpiração", "similarity": 0.929}], "id": 1893, "stable_key": "clu_958fc371295918b8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Perspiration", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q3503092", "wikidata_description": "substance secreted by sweat gland", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perspiration", "wikipedia_extract": "Perspiration, also known as sweat, is the fluid secreted by sweat glands in the skin of mammals. Two types of sweat glands can be found in humans: eccrine glands and apocrine glands. The eccrine sweat glands are distributed over much of the body and are responsible for secreting the watery, brackish sweat most often triggered by excessive body temperature. Apocrine sweat glands are restricted to the armpits and a few other areas of the body and produce an odorless, oily, opaque secretion which then gains its characteristic odor from bacterial decomposition. In humans, sweating is primarily a means of thermoregulation, which is achieved by the water-rich secretion of the eccrine glands. Maximum sweat rates of an adult can be up to 2–4 litres (0.5–1 US gal) per hour or 10–14 litres (2.5–3.5 US gal) per day, but is less in children prior to puberty."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "evacuação", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1559, "target_cluster_name": "evacuação", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Perspiration is a form of bodily evacuation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Perspiration is a form of bodily evacuation.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Human Body", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4153, "target_cluster_name": "Human Body", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Perspiration is a physiological process occurring in the human body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Perspiration is a physiological process occurring in the human body."}, {"found_name": "balneis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2167, "target_cluster_name": "balneis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Baths, particularly hot ones, often induced perspiration.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Baths, particularly hot ones, often induced perspiration.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Geographical distribution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "geographical_distribution", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Geographical distribution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 10, "variants": ["Geographical distribution", "geographical distribution", "GEOGRAPHICAL DISTRIBUTION"], "contexts": ["study of species locations", "spatial arrangement of organisms"]}, {"entity_id": "geographical_distribution", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "geographical distribution", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["geographical distribution"], "contexts