36", "wikidata_description": "Salt Lake City park with natural water source", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artesian_Well_Park", "wikipedia_extract": "Olympia is the capital city of the U.S. state of Washington. The population was 55,605 at the 2020 census, while the Olympia metropolitan statistical area has an estimated 300,000 people. Olympia is the county seat of Thurston County and anchors the South Puget Sound region of western Washington, 50 miles (80 km) southwest of Seattle. The Squaxin and other Coast Salish peoples inhabited the southern Puget Sound region prior to the arrival of European and American settlers in the 19th century. The Treaty of Medicine Creek was signed in 1854 and followed by the Treaty of Olympia in 1856; these two treaties forced the Squaxin to relocate to an Indian reservation."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "celestial bodies", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "celestial_regions", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "celestial regions", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["celestial regions"], "contexts": ["regions of the sky", "regions of the sky or outer space"]}, {"entity_id": "celestial_bodies", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "celestial bodies", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 11, "variants": ["celestial bodies", "Celestial Bodies", "Celestial bodies"], "contexts": ["astronomical objects", "astronomical objects like planets and stars"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "celestial regions", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "celestial bodies", "similarity": 0.947}], "id": 1910, "stable_key": "clu_8992759cb5dc084c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Celestial objects", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q6999", "wi