 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Photography is considered a fine art."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Grove", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 14, "members": [{"entity_id": "grove", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Grove", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 11, "variants": ["Grove"], "contexts": ["scientist who studied electricity and radiation", "gives paper, snow, and lime as instances"]}, {"entity_id": "grove", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Grove", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Grove"], "contexts": ["credited with enunciation of doctrine", "suggested connection between vital and physical forces"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Grove", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Grove", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1923, "stable_key": "clu_87ff717cb4df3cf4", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "William Grove", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1811, "death_year": 1896, "description": "Scientist who studied electricity and radiation", "wikidata_id": "Q75743296", "wikidata_description": "Peerage person ID=311924"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Michael Faraday", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 248, "target_cluster_name": "Faraday", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent scientists in the 19th century, known for their work in electricity and magnetism. Grove is credited with the concept of the 'correlation of forces', which Faraday explored experimentally.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent scientists in the 19th century, known for their work in electricity and magnetism. Grove is credited with the concept of the 'correlation of forces', which Faraday explored experimentally."}, {"found_name": "William Thomson", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2538, "target_cluster_name": "W. Thomson", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were leading physicists of the 19th century, contributing significantly to the understanding of thermodynamics and electricity. Grove's 'correlation of forces' laid groundwork for Thomson's later work.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were leading physicists of the 19th century, contributing significantly to the understanding of thermodynamics and electricity. Grove's 'correlation of forces' laid groundwork for Thomson's later work."}, {"found_name": "James Prescott Joule", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1276, "target_cluster_name": "Mr. Joule", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Grove's concept of the 'correlation of forces' was a precursor to Joule's experimental work on the mechanical equivalent of heat, a key aspect of the conservation of energy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Grove's concept of the 'correlation of forces' was a precursor to Joule's experimental work on the mechanical equivalent of heat, a key aspect of the conservation of energy."}, {"found_name": "John Frederic Daniell", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1165, "target_cluster_name": "Daniell", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Daniell's invention of the Daniell cell was a significant development in voltaic electricity, a field that Grove also contributed to with his work on electrochemistry and the 'correlation of forces'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Daniell's invention of the Daniell cell was a significant development in voltaic electricity, a field that Grove also contributed to with hi