dspars crystallize from magma as both intrusive and extrusive igneous rocks and are also present in many types of metamorphic rock. Rock formed almost entirely of calcic plagioclase feldspar is known as anorthosite. Feldspars are also found in many types of sedimentary rocks."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Kaolin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3422, "target_cluster_name": "kaolin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Kaolin is a type of clay mineral, and feldspar is a common component of many clays and argillaceous rocks.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Kaolin is a type of clay mineral, and feldspar is a common component of many clays and argillaceous rocks."}, {"found_name": "Granite", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1634, "target_cluster_name": "granite", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Granite is a common igneous rock that is largely composed of feldspar.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Granite is a common igneous rock that is largely composed of feldspar."}, {"found_name": "Basalt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1665, "target_cluster_name": "basalt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Basalt is an igneous rock that can contain feldspar minerals, particularly plagioclase feldspar.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Basalt is an igneous rock that can contain feldspar minerals, particularly plagioclase feldspar."}, {"found_name": "Diorite", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1717, "target_cluster_name": "diorite", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diorite is an intrusive igneous rock composed mainly of plagioclase feldspar, biotite, hornblende, and pyroxene.", "confidence": 0.85,