 "wikipedia_extract": "Paita is a city in northwestern Peru. It is the capital of the Paita Province which is in the Piura Region. It is a leading seaport in the region. Paita is located 1,089 km northwest of the country's capital Lima, and 57 km northwest of the regional capital of Piura. Starting in 2014, the city has considered ideas for separating from the Piura Region, proclaiming itself as the \"Miguel Grau Region\". Paita is located at 05°05′28″S 81°06′23″W on a small peninsula south of the mouth of the Río Chira on an area of 1,785 km2."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Andes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 207, "target_cluster_name": "Andes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paita is a city in northwestern Peru, located in the Andes mountain range region.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paita is a city in northwestern Peru, located in the Andes mountain range region."}, {"found_name": "Callao", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1845, "target_cluster_name": "Callao", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paita is a leading seaport in Peru, and Callao is another major port city in Peru.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paita is a leading seaport in Peru, and Callao is another major port city in Peru."}, {"found_name": "Equatorial America", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1437, "target_cluster_name": "equatorial America", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paita is located in northwestern Peru, which falls within the broader geographical region of Equatorial America.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paita is located in northwestern Peru, which falls within the broader geographical region of Equatorial America."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Mer Caspie