nterconnected body of seawaters referred to as 'the sea'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Volga", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1383, "target_cluster_name": "Volga", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Volga River flows directly into the Caspian Sea, making it the primary riverine source of water for this large inland body of water. Their geographical relationship is fundamental.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Volga River flows directly into the Caspian Sea, making it the primary riverine source of water for this large inland body of water. Their geographical relationship is fundamental.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Cauca", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1817, "target_cluster_name": "Cauca", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Caucasus is situated between the Black Sea and the Caspian Sea.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Caucasus is situated between the Black Sea and the Caspian Sea.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Astrakhan", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2753, "target_cluster_name": "Astrakhan", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A major port city on the Caspian Sea.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A major port city on the Caspian Sea."}, {"found_name": "Europe", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 30, "target_cluster_name": "Europe", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Caspian Sea forms part of the traditional boundary between Europe and Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Caspian Sea forms part of the traditional boundary between Europe and Asia."}, {"found_name": "Asia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 231, "target_cluster_name": "Asie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Caspian Sea forms part of the traditional boundary between Europe and Asia.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Caspian Sea forms part of the traditional boundary between Europe and Asia."}, {"found_name": "seas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2596, "target_cluster_name": "seas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Caspian Sea is a specific sea, and 'seas' is a general term for large bodies of saltwater.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The Caspian Sea is a specific sea, and 'seas' is a general term for large bodies of saltwater.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Sahara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "sahara", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Sahara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 9, "variants": ["Sahara"], "contexts": ["Sahara desert", "large desert in North Africa"]}, {"entity_id": "sahara_desert", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Sahara desert", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 2, "variants": ["Sahara desert"], "contexts": ["large desert in North Africa", "large desert in Africa"]}, {"entity_id": "sahara", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Sahara", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Sahara"], "contexts": ["causing monsoons"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Sahara", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Sahara desert", "similarity": 0.957}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Sahara", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Sahara", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 1984, "stable_key": "clu_4e7d97462e650141", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Sahara Desert", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Algeria, Chad, Egypt, Libya, Mali, Mauritania, Morocco, Niger, Sudan, Tunisia, Western Sahara", "wikidata_id": "Q1717126", "wikidata_description": "species of insect", "wikipedia_extract": "The Sahara (, ) is a desert spanning across North Africa. With an area of 9,200,000 square kilometres (3,600,000 sq mi), it is the largest hot desert in the world and the third-largest desert overall, smaller only than the deserts of Antarctica and the northern Arctic. The name \"Sahara\" is derived from Arabic: صَحَارَى, romanized: ṣaḥārā /sˤaħaːraː/, a broken plural form of ṣaḥrā' (صَحْرَاء /sˤaħraːʔ/), meaning \"desert\". The desert covers much of North Africa, excluding the fertile region on the Mediterranean Sea coast, the Atlas Mountains of the Maghreb, and the Nile Valley in Egypt and the Sudan. It stretches from the Red Sea in the east and the Mediterranean in the north to the Atlantic Ocean in the west, where the landscape gradually changes from desert to coastal plains. To the south it is bounded by the Sahel, a belt of semi-arid tropical savanna around the Niger River valley and the Sudan region of sub-Saharan Africa.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahara_Desert_ant"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Sahara Desert is a major geographical feature located within the continent of Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Sahara Desert is a major geographical feature located within the continent of Africa."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Santa Ro