 midst of a dense wood. The general movement of the sea from east to west between p 3", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Infinite", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "infinite", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "infinite", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["infinite"], "contexts": ["boundless and endless concept"]}, {"entity_id": "infinite", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Infinite", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 11, "variants": ["infinite", "Infinite"], "contexts": ["First Cause as infinite", "philosophical concept of boundless existence"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "infinite", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Infinite", "similarity": 0.968}], "id": 2005, "stable_key": "clu_a411e8a20d0f54ed", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "infinity", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q205", "wikidata_description": "mathematical concept of something without any limit"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Continuity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2059, "target_cluster_name": "continuity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The concept of infinity is intrinsically linked to the idea of continuity, as it represents a boundless or endless progression, which is a fundamental aspect of continuity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The concept of infinity is intrinsically linked to the idea of continuity, as it represents a boundless or endless progression, which is a fundamental aspect of continuity."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Hydropicos", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "hydropicos", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Hydropicos", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 11, "variants": ["Hydropicos", "Hidropefía", "Hydropefia", "Hydropeñia", "Hydropeſia", "hidropetia", "hidropicos", "hydropico"], "contexts": ["related to dropsy", "dropsy patients"]}, {"entity_id": "hidropici", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "hidropici", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["hidropici"], "contexts": ["patients with dropsy"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Hydropicos", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "hidropici", "similarity": 0.903}], "id": 2006, "stable_key": "clu_7c166543e5a30565-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Dropsy", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A condition characterized by abnormal accumulation of fluid in body tissues.", "note": "Includes variations like Hydropeſia, Hydropick diseases, Hydropicos, hydropí, hydroforbia, and hidropici.", "wikipedia_extract": "Edema (American English), also spelled oedema (Commonwealth English), and also known as fluid retention, swelling, dropsy and hydropsy, is the build-up of fluid in the body's tissue. Most commonly, the legs or arms are affected. Symptoms may include skin that feels tight, the area feeling heavy, and joint stiffness. Other symptoms depend on the underlying cause. Causes may include venous insufficiency, heart failure, kidney problems, low protein levels, liver problems, deep vein thrombosis, infections, kwashiorkor, angioedema, certain medications, and lymphedema. It may also occur in immobile patients (stroke, spinal cord injury, aging), or with temporary immobility such as prolonged sitting or standing, and during menstruation or pregnancy."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "ciudad", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "ciudad", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "ciudad", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 10, "variants": ["ciudad", "Ciudad", "Ciudades"], "contexts": ["geographic location, city", "city"]}, {"entity_id": "città", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Città", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Città"], "contexts": ["city", "cities"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "ciudad", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Città", "similarity": 0.906}], "id": 2007, "stable_key": "clu_bb91b9b91e864125", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "city", "confidence": "high", "type": "place"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "ciudad", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1222, "target_cluster_name": "City", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Spanish for 'city'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Spanish for 'city'."}, {"found_name": "Rome", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 281, "target_cluster_name": "Rome", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A historically significant city that served as a model for many other cities.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A historically significant city that served as a model for many other cities."}, {"found_name": "Alexandria", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 92, "target_cluster_name": "Alexandria", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A historically significant city.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A historically significant city."}, {"found_name": "Venice", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cl