n or idea, making 'Ideas' a closely related concept.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The term 'image' in historical texts often refers to a mental representation or idea, making 'Ideas' a closely related concept."}, {"found_name": "Mental", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2124, "target_cluster_name": "mental", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "'Image' is fundamentally a mental construct, and thus strongly related to the broader category of 'Mental' phenomena.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "'Image' is fundamentally a mental construct, and thus strongly related to the broader category of 'Mental' phenomena."}, {"found_name": "Metaphor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1400, "target_cluster_name": "Metaphors", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Images are often used metaphorically to convey meaning, creating a strong conceptual link between the two.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Images are often used metaphorically to convey meaning, creating a strong conceptual link between the two."}, {"found_name": "visual perception", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2419, "target_cluster_name": "visual perception", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Visual perception is directly concerned with the formation and interpretation of images.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Visual perception is directly concerned with the formation and interpretation of images.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "appearance", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2433, "target_cluster_name": "appearance", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "An image is a representation of appearance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: An image is a representation of appearance.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Idolatry", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2662, "target_cluster_name": "Idolatry", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Idolatry involves the worship of an image, making the concept of 'image' directly relevant.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Idolatry involves the worship of an image, making the concept of 'image' directly relevant.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "sense-impressions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2810, "target_cluster_name": "sense-impressions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sense-impressions are the basis for forming mental images, which are internal representations of external stimuli.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Sense-impressions are the basis for forming mental images, which are internal representations of external stimuli.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "primary-memory-image", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "evidence_snippet": "decide nothing at all about our attention, properly so called. They rather measure in part the distinctness of our vision--especially of the primary-memory-image[327]--in part the amount of associatio", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "a type of vision related to attention"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Crocus Martis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 11, "members": [{"entity_id": "crocus_martis", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Crocus Martis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Crocus Martis"], "contexts": ["steel corroded and reverberated"]}, {"entity_id": "crocus_martis", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Crocus Martis", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 10, "variants": ["Crocus Martis", "croco martis", "crocus martis"], "contexts": ["Crocus Martis, iron preparation", "aperitive substance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Crocus Martis", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Crocus Martis", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2027, "stable_key": "clu_1a67cdca5c8931fe", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Iron preparations", "confidence": "high", "type": "chemical", "note": "Refers to preparations of iron or steel, often corroded or reverberated, used medicinally."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Iron", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 251, "target_cluster_name": "Iron", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Iron preparations are derived from iron.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Iron preparations are derived from iron.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Banda", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 11, "members": [{"entity_id": "banda", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Banda", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Banda"], "contexts": ["isle where nutmeg tree fructifies"]}, {"entity_id": "banda", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Banda", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 10, "variants": ["Banda"], "contexts": ["region where clove is merchandise", "island group to be discovered"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Banda", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Banda", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2028, "stable_key": "clu_7e1c88b386c2c72f", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Banda Islands", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Indonesia", "note": "Historically a major source of nutmeg and mace.", "wikidata_id": "Q739411", "wikidata_description": "island group in Indonesia", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banda%20Islands", "wikipedia_extract": "The Banda Islands (Indonesian: Kepulauan Banda) are a volcanic group of ten small islands in the Banda Sea, about 140 km (87 mi) south of Seram Island and about 2,000 km (1,243 mi) east of Java, and constitute an administrative district (kecamatan) within the Central Maluku Regency in the Indonesian province of Maluku. The islands rise out of 4-to-6-kilometre (2.5 to 3.7 mi) deep ocean and have a total land area of approximately 172 square kilometres (66 sq mi); with associated maritime area this reaches 736.3 square kilometres (284.3 sq mi). They had a population of 18,544 at the 2010 Census and 20,924 at the 2020 Census; the official estimate as of mid-2023 was 21,902. Until the mid-19th century the Banda Islands were the world's only source of the spices nutmeg and mace, produced from the nutmeg tree. The islands are also popular destinations for scuba diving and snorkeling. The main town and administrative centre is Banda Neira, located on the island of the same name."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "East Indies", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 497, "target_cluster_name": "East Indies", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Banda Islands are a significant part of the historical East Indies, known for their spice trade.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Banda Islands are a significant part of the historical East Indies, known for their spice trade."}, {"found_name": "Malay Archipelago", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2275, "target_cluster_name": "Malay Archipelago", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Banda Islands are geographically located within the Malay Archipelago.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Banda Islands are geographically located within the Malay Archipelago."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Amomum", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 11, "members": [{"entity_id": "amomum", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Amomum", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Amomum"], "contexts": ["plant mistaken for Rose"]}, {"entity_id": "amomum", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Amomum", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 10, "variants": ["Amomum", "Amomum Koraríma", "Amomum korarima", "amamum", "amomum"], "contexts": ["ingredient for theriac", "ingredient for compositions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Amomum", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Amomum", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2029, "stable_key": "clu_49fb8a02aa3e81be", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Amomum", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "description": "Aromatic plant genus, often used in traditional medicine and perfumery.", "wikipedia_extract": "Amomum is a genus of plants containing about 111 species native to China, the Indian subcontinent, Southeast Asia, New Guinea, and Queensland. It includes several species of cardamom. Plants of this genus are remarkable for their pungency and aromatic properties. Among ancient writers, the name amomum was ascribed to various odoriferous plants that cannot be positively identified today. The word derives from Latin amomum, which is the latinisation of the Greek ἄμωμον (amomon), a kind of an Indian spice plant. Edmund Roberts noted on his 1834 trip to China that amomum was used as a spice to \"season sweet dishes\" in culinary practice."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "tamalapatra", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2233, "target_cluster_name": "tamalapatra", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amomum is a genus of plants in the ginger family (Zingiberaceae), which also includes cardamom. While not directly related botanically to Cinnamomum, both genera are important sources of aromatic spices used in historical pharmacopoeias and cuisines.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Amomum is a genus of plants in the ginger family (Zingiberaceae), which also includes cardamom. While not directly related botanically to Cinnamomum, both genera are important sources of aromatic spices used in historical pharmacopoeias and cuisines.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Scitaminea", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2852, "target_cluster_name": "Scitaminea", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amomum is a genus within the Zingiberaceae family, which is part of the Zingiberales order. Historical texts often refer to specific genera within a larger order.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: Amomum is a genus within the Zingiberaceae family, which is part of the Zingiberales order. Historical texts often refer to specific genera within a larger order.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Canela", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 44, "target_cluster_name": "Canela", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amomum is a genus closely related to Cinnamomum, and some species within Amomum have been historically used for similar aromatic purposes or confused with cinnamon.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Amomum i