red to as a \"thunderclap\" or \"peal of thunder\". The scientific study of thunder is known as brontology and the irrational fear (phobia) of thunder is called brontophobia. The d in Modern English thunder (from earlier Old English þunor) is epenthetic, and is now found as well in Modern Dutch donder (cf."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Atmospheric electricity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3166, "target_cluster_name": "atmospheric electricity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Thunder is a direct consequence of electrical discharge in the atmosphere.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Thunder is a direct consequence of electrical discharge in the atmosphere."}, {"found_name": "Electrical discharge", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1093, "target_cluster_name": "electric explosions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Thunder is the sound produced by the rapid expansion of air heated by an electrical discharge (lightning).", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Thunder is the sound produced by the rapid expansion of air heated by an electrical discharge (lightning)."}, {"found_name": "Explosion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3650, "target_cluster_name": "explosion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The rapid expansion of air that causes thunder is akin to an explosion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The rapid expansion of air that causes thunder is akin to an explosion."}, {"found_name": "Sound", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 258, "target_cluster_name": "sound", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Thunder is a type of sound.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found