front of the vertebrae. It contains the pharynx and larynx. An important section of it is the epiglottis, separating the esophagus from the trachea (windpipe), preventing food and drinks being inhaled into the lungs. The throat contains various blood vessels, pharyngeal muscles, the nasopharyngeal tonsil, the tonsils, the palatine uvula, the trachea, the esophagus, and the vocal cords. Mammal throats consist of two bones, the hyoid bone and the clavicle. The \"throat\" is sometimes thought to be synonymous for the fauces."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Plague", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 588, "target_cluster_name": "peste", "source_book": "english_physician_1652", "evidence_snippet": "not long since there was a raging Diseas called the Bloody Flux, the Colledg of Physitians not knowing what to make of it, called it the Plague in the Guts, for their wits were at ne plus ultra about ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "also called the Plague in the Guts"}, {"found_name": "Neck", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2031, "target_cluster_name": "Neck", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The throat is described as the front part of the neck.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The throat is described as the front part of the neck."}, {"found_name": "Mouth", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 237, "target_cluster_name": "Mouth", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The throat contains the pharynx, which is part of the passage from the mouth.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The throat contains the pharynx, which is part of the passage from the mouth."}, {"found_name": "Olofago", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": nul