lexipharmaca", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Alexipharmaca"], "contexts": ["work by Nicander on venemous beasts and antidotes"]}, {"entity_id": "alexipharmacum", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Alexipharmacum", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 9, "variants": ["Alexipharmacum", "adalexipharmaca", "alexipharmac", "alexipharmaca", "alexipharmacos", "alexipharmacum"], "contexts": ["remedy against poison", "remedy for plague"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Alexipharmaca", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Alexipharmacum", "similarity": 0.955}], "id": 2089, "stable_key": "clu_0ee7584da72d2d83", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Alexipharmic", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "Alexipharmacum/Alexipharmaca/Alexiphar refers to a substance or remedy that protects against poison or venom. It is a concept rather than a specific chemical or preparation.", "wikidata_id": "Q194168", "wikidata_description": "substance that can counteract a form of poisoning", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antidote", "wikipedia_extract": "Justus de Harduwijn, also written Hardwijn, Herdewijn, Harduyn or Harduijn (11 April 1582 – 21 June 1636 in Oudegem), was a 17th-century Roman Catholic priest and poet from the Southern Netherlands. He was the poetic link between the Renaissance and the Counter-Reformation in the Netherlands. De Harduwijn was born in a humanist, intellectual family in Ghent. His grandfather Thomas was a steward to Louis of Praet. His father Franciscus owned a bookbinding shop in Ghent and was a member of the Council of Flanders, the highest judicial college in the County of Flanders. His father was a friend of writer Jan van der Noot who had introduced him to the French poets of La Pléiade, and is said to have been the first translator of Anacreon into Dutch."}, "cross_references": [{"