rse: Both were prominent naturalists who made significant contributions to biogeography and evolutionary theory. Forbes's work on glacial refugia and island biogeography predated and influenced Wallace's later work.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Mr. Blyth", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 958, "target_cluster_name": "Mr. Blyth", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent zoologists who worked in India and made significant contributions to the understanding of its fauna, particularly birds. They were contemporaries and likely aware of each other's work.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent zoologists who worked in India and made significant contributions to the understanding of its fauna, particularly birds. They were contemporaries and likely aware of each other's work.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Lyell", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1710, "target_cluster_name": "Lyell", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alfred Russel Wallace, like Charles Darwin, was a key figure in the development of evolutionary theory, and his work, along with Darwin's, was part of the broader scientific discourse in which Lyell was a central figure in geology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Alfred Russel Wallace, like Charles Darwin, was a key figure in the development of evolutionary theory, and his work, along with Darwin's, was part of the broader scientific discourse in which Lyell was a central figure in geology.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Dr. Hooker", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1716, "target_cluster_name": "Dr. Hooker", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Alfred Russel Wallace was a contemporary naturalist and explorer, often associated with Darwin and Hooker in the context of 19th-century biological discovery.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Alfred Russel Wallace was a contemporary naturalist and explorer, often associated with Darwin and Hooker in the context of 19th-century biological discovery.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Owen", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1754, "target_cluster_name": "Owen", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were key figures in the development of evolutionary biology in the 19th century. While Darwin is more famous, Wallace independently conceived of natural selection and was a significant naturalist and collector.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were key figures in the development of evolutionary biology in the 19th century. While Darwin is more famous, Wallace independently conceived of natural selection and was a significant naturalist and collector.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "H. C. Watson", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2037, "target_cluster_name": "H. C. Watson", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent naturalists and proponents of evolutionary theory, with Wallace independently conceiving of natural selection.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent naturalists and proponents of evolutionary theory, with Wallace independently conceiving of natural selection.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Charles Darwin", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 118, "target_cluster_name": "Darwin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Wallace and Darwin independently conceived of the theory of evolution by natural selection.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found