r confirmed theoretical predictions made by Fourier."}, {"found_name": "Dominique François Jean Arago", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1818, "target_cluster_name": "M. Arago", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent French scientists active in the same period. Arago was a physicist and astronomer, and he was involved in many of the same scientific societies and debates as Fourier, often engaging with Fourier's work on heat and mathematics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were prominent French scientists active in the same period. Arago was a physicist and astronomer, and he was involved in many of the same scientific societies and debates as Fourier, often engaging with Fourier's work on heat and mathematics."}]}, {"canonical_name": "meteors", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 10, "members": [{"entity_id": "meteors", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "meteors", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Meteors", "meteors"], "contexts": ["celestial objects observed", "another name for aerolites"]}, {"entity_id": "meteor", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "meteor", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["meteor"], "contexts": ["celestial phenomenon"]}, {"entity_id": "meteors", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "meteors", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 3, "variants": ["meteors", "Meteors"], "contexts": ["celestial objects igniting in atmosphere", "celestial phenomena"]}, {"entity_id": "meteor", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Meteor", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Meteor"], "contexts": ["celestial phenomenon"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humbold