 "Vegetables", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 3853, "target_cluster_name": "Vegetables", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "While 'Vegetables' can refer to specific edible parts, historically it was often used more broadly to encompass plant matter, making it a near-synonym in some contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "While 'Vegetables' can refer to specific edible parts, historically it was often used more broadly to encompass plant matter, making it a near-synonym in some contexts."}, {"found_name": "Flora", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2595, "target_cluster_name": "Floras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A direct synonym for plant life, especially when referring to the collective plant life of a region or period.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "A direct synonym for plant life, especially when referring to the collective plant life of a region or period."}, {"found_name": "Floras", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2595, "target_cluster_name": "Floras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Flora refers to the plant life of a particular region or time, thus being a synonym for 'Plant life'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: Flora refers to the plant life of a particular region or time, thus being a synonym for 'Plant life'.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "chá", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 855, "target_cluster_name": "chá", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for 'Tea', a specific type of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Portuguese for 'Tea', a specific type of plant life."}, {"found_name": "café", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 642, "target_cluster_name": "café", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for 'Coffee', a specific type of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Portuguese for 'Coffee', a specific type of plant life."}, {"found_name": "riz", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2191, "target_cluster_name": "riz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "French for 'Rice', a specific type of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "French for 'Rice', a specific type of plant life."}, {"found_name": "coton", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 705, "target_cluster_name": "coton", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "French for 'Cotton', a specific type of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "French for 'Cotton', a specific type of plant life."}, {"found_name": "opio", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 665, "target_cluster_name": "opio", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Spanish for 'Opium', derived from a specific plant.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Spanish for 'Opium', derived from a specific plant."}, {"found_name": "páo", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1749, "target_cluster_name": "páo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Portuguese for 'Wood', a material derived from trees, a form of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Portuguese for 'Wood', a material derived from trees, a form of plant life."}, {"found_name": "frutas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 72, "target_cluster_name": "frutas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Fruits are a component of plant life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Fruits are a component of plant life.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "oxidation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 12, "members": [{"entity_id": "oxidation", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Oxidation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["oxidation", "Oxidation"], "contexts": ["chemical process of reacting with oxygen", "chemical reaction with oxygen"]}, {"entity_id": "oxidation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "oxidation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["oxidation"], "contexts": ["process of animal life", "process where absorbed nutriment gives out force"]}, {"entity_id": "deoxidation", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "deoxidation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["deoxidation"], "contexts": ["removal of oxygen"]}, {"entity_id": "de-oxidation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "de-oxidation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["de-oxidation"], "contexts": ["process of vegetal life"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Oxidation", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "oxidation", "similarity": 0.911}], "id": 2158, "stable_key": "clu_464e33f91df58487", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Oxidation", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q484152", "wikidata_description": "number that describes degree of oxidation of an atom in a chemical compound; the hypothetical charge that an atom would have if all bonds to atoms of different elements were fully ionic", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxidation_state", "wikipedia_extract": "In chemistry, the oxidation state, or oxidation number, is the hypothetical charge of an atom if all of its bonds to other atoms are fully ionic. It describes the degree of oxidation (loss of electrons) of an atom in a chemical compound. Conceptually, the oxidation state may be positive, negative or zero. Beside nearly-pure ionic bonding, many covalent bonds exhibit a strong ionicity, making oxidation state a useful predictor of charge. The oxidation state of an atom does not represent the \"real\" charge on that atom, or any other actual atomic property. This is particularly true of high oxidation states, where the ionization energy required to produce a multiply positive ion is far greater than the energies available in chemical reactions."}, "member_count": 4, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Combustion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 866, "target_cluster_name": "combustion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Historically, oxidation was often understood and studied in the context of combustion, as the process of burning involves rapid oxidation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Historically, oxidation was often understood and studied in the context of combustion, as the process of burning involves rapid oxidation."}, {"found_name": "Chemical reactions", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1769, "target_cluster_name": "chemical action", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Oxidation is a fundamental type of chemical reaction involving the loss of electrons.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Oxidation is a fundamental type of chemical reaction involving the loss of electrons."}, {"found_name": "Decomposition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2085, "target_cluster_name": "decomposition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Some forms of decomposition in chemistry involve oxidation processes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Some forms of decomposition in chemistry involve oxidation processes."}]}, {"canonical_name": "variable star", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 10, "members": [{"entity_id": "variable_star", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "variable star", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 4, "variants": ["variable star"], "contexts": ["star whose brightness changes", "Eta Aquilæ"]}, {"entity_id": "variable_stars", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Variable stars", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Variable stars", "variable stars"], "contexts": ["stars with changing brightness", "position in Milky Way"]}, {"entity_id": "variable_stars", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "variable stars", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 2, "variants": ["variable stars"], "contexts": ["stars with changing brightness", "celestial bodies that brighten and fade"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "variable star", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "variable stars", "similarity": 0.939}, {"source_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "source_name": "Variable stars", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "variable stars", "similarity": 0.976}], "id": 2159, "stable_key": "clu_8eff494e3048efda", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Variable star", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q6243", "wikidata_description"