and chronicler of Columbus's voyages, and his writings provide significant historical accounts of Columbus's expeditions and discoveries."}, {"found_name": "Alexander von Humboldt", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 42, "target_cluster_name": "Humboldt", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential figures in the exploration and scientific understanding of the Americas. Humboldt's extensive scientific expeditions and writings built upon the earlier explorations documented by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were influential figures in the exploration and scientific understanding of the Americas. Humboldt's extensive scientific expeditions and writings built upon the earlier explorations documented by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera."}, {"found_name": "Laet", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2748, "target_cluster_name": "Laet", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Johannes de Laet wrote a history of the New World, a subject also extensively covered by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera in his 'De Orbe Novo'. Both were early chroniclers of European exploration and encounters in the Americas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Johannes de Laet wrote a history of the New World, a subject also extensively covered by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera in his 'De Orbe Novo'. Both were early chroniclers of European exploration and encounters in the Americas.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "rain", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 9, "members": [{"entity_id": "rain", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "rain", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["rain"], "contexts": ["environmental factor"]}, {"entity_id": "rain", "book_id": "first_princ