ps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rheumatism", "wikipedia_extract": "Rheumatism  (from the Ancient Greek ῥεῦμα, rheûma) or rheumatic disorders are conditions causing chronic, often intermittent pain affecting the joints or connective tissue. Rheumatism does not designate any specific disorder, but covers at least 200 different conditions, including arthritis and  \"non-articular rheumatism\", also known as \"regional pain syndrome\" or \"soft tissue rheumatism\". There is a close overlap between the term soft tissue disorder and rheumatism. Sometimes the term \"soft tissue rheumatic disorders\" is used to describe these conditions. The term \"Rheumatic Diseases\" is used in MeSH to refer to connective tissue disorders. The branch of medicine devoted to the diagnosis and therapy of rheumatism is called rheumatology."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Gout", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 234, "target_cluster_name": "Gout", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Gout is a specific type of inflammatory arthritis that was historically often conflated with or considered a form of rheumatism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Gout is a specific type of inflammatory arthritis that was historically often conflated with or considered a form of rheumatism."}, {"found_name": "Chronic pain", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3319, "target_cluster_name": "dolores viejos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Rheumatism is characterized by chronic pain affecting joints or connective tissue.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Rheumatism is characterized by chronic pain affecting joints or connective tissue."}, {"found_name": "Sciatica", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1501, "target_cluster_name": "Ciatica", "source_book": "llm_generated", "e