-county (all of Clarke County except Winterville and a portion of Bogart) was 128,711."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "grego", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 773, "target_cluster_name": "grego", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Athens is the capital and largest city of Greece, a major historical and cultural center.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Athens is the capital and largest city of Greece, a major historical and cultural center.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "horns", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "horns", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "horns", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Horns", "horns"], "contexts": ["animal keratinous growths", "bony protrusions on animal heads"]}, {"entity_id": "horns", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "horns", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "count": 5, "variants": ["horns"], "contexts": ["bony outgrowths on heads of ungulates", "correlated with hair growth"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "horns", "target_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "target_name": "horns", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2258, "stable_key": "clu_aa155b8502e2eefe", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Horns", "confidence": "high", "type": "object"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "teeth of Elephants", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "might admit of discourse; and if we should question the teeth of Elephants, that is, whether they be properly so termed, or might not rather be called horns: it were no new enquiry of mine, but a Para", "conf