 mathematician and astronomer (1805-1865)"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Mathematicians", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1337, "target_cluster_name": "mathematicians", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton was a prominent mathematician.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton was a prominent mathematician."}, {"found_name": "Physicists", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 692, "target_cluster_name": "physiciens", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton made significant contributions to physics.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton made significant contributions to physics."}, {"found_name": "astronomers", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 901, "target_cluster_name": "Astronomers", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton was also an accomplished astronomer.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Sir William Rowan Hamilton was also an accomplished astronomer."}, {"found_name": "Archimedes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 480, "target_cluster_name": "Archimedes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Archimedes was a foundational figure in mathematics and physics, whose work Hamilton would have been aware of and built upon.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Archimedes was a foundational figure in mathematics and physics, whose work Hamilton would have been aware of and built upon."}]}, {"canonical_name": "hypnotism", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "hypnotism", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "hypnotism", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "PRACTICE", "count": 4, "variants": ["hypnotism"], "contexts": ["induced state of altered consciousness", "induced state of trance"]}, {"entity_id": "hypnotic", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "hypnotic", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["hypnotic"], "contexts": ["related to hypnosis"]}, {"entity_id": "hypnotically", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "hypnotically", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["hypnotically"], "contexts": ["in a state of hypnosis"]}, {"entity_id": "hypnotica", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "hypnotica", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["hypnotica"], "contexts": ["hypnotic quality"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "hypnotism", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "hypnotica", "similarity": 0.958}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "hypnotic", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "hypnotica", "similarity": 0.967}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "hypnotically", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "hypnotica", "similarity": 0.933}], "id": 2300, "stable_key": "clu_ff546d690f2ece9b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "hypnotic", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "Related to or inducing a state of hypnosis.", "wikipedia_extract": "A hypnotic (from Greek Hypnos, sleep), also known as a somnifacient or soporific, and commonly known as sleeping pills, are a class of psychoactive drugs whose primary function is to induce sleep and to treat insomnia (sleeplessness). Some hypnotics are also used to treat narcolepsy and hypersomnia by improving sleep at night and thereby reducing daytime sleepiness. Certain hypnotics can be used to treat non-restorative sleep and associated symptoms in conditions like fibromyalgia as well. This group of drugs is related to sedatives. Whereas the term sedative describes drugs that serve to calm or relieve anxiety, the term hypnotic generally describes drugs whose main purpose is to initiate, sustain, or lengthen sleep. Because these two functions frequently overlap, and because drugs in this class generally produce dose-dependent effects (ranging from anxiolysis to loss of consciousness), they are often referred to collectively as sedative–hypnotic drugs."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "post-hypnotic suggestion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "evidence_snippet": "bearing a number. He then told her that on waking she should _not see_ any card whose number was a multiple of three. This is the ordinary so-called 'post-hypnotic suggestion,' now well known, and for", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of suggestion being discussed"}]}, {"canonical_name": "representations", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "representations", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "representations", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["representations"], "contexts": ["mental images or ideas"]}, {"entity_id": "representation", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "representation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["representation"], "contexts": ["mental image or idea"]}, {"entity_id": "representation", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "representation", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCE