and the effects of cold.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Climatologie", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2199, "target_cluster_name": "Climatologie", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Isotherms (lines of equal temperature) are fundamental graphical representations used in climatology to depict temperature distributions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Isotherms (lines of equal temperature) are fundamental graphical representations used in climatology to depict temperature distributions.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "enfermo", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "enfermo", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "enfermo", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 7, "variants": ["enfermo", "enfermos"], "contexts": ["sick person", "patient undergoing treatment"]}, {"entity_id": "enfermo", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "ENFERMO", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["ENFERMO"], "contexts": ["patient in dialogue"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "enfermo", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "ENFERMO", "similarity": 0.941}], "id": 2325, "stable_key": "clu_99dec294877a0b63", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Patient", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "The Spanish/Portuguese term 'enfermo' translates directly to 'sick person' or 'patient'.", "wikidata_id": "Q181600", "wikidata_description": "person who takes a medical treatment or is subject of a case study"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "doente", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1753, "target_cluster_name": "doente", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Spanish for 'patient'", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Spanish for 'patient'"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Tercianas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 8, "members": [{"entity_id": "tercianas", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Tercianas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 6, "variants": ["Tercianas", "Teracianas", "Tercianas nothas", "terciana"], "contexts": ["tertian fevers", "fevers that were importunate"]}, {"entity_id": "tertiana", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Tertiana", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Tertiana"], "contexts": ["type of fever", "third-day fever"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Tercianas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Tertiana", "similarity": 0.898}], "id": 2326, "stable_key": "clu_44ae045b76c9e581", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tertian Fever", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "description": "A fever characterized by recurring chills and heats every third day.", "note": "Specifically refers to fevers with a 48-hour cycle, often malaria.", "wikipedia_extract": "The history of malaria extends from its prehistoric origin as a zoonotic disease in the primates of Africa through to the 21st century. A widespread and potentially lethal human infectious disease, at its peak malaria infested every continent except Antarctica. Its prevention and treatment have been targeted in science and medicine for hundreds of years. Since the discovery of the Plasmodium parasites which cause it, research attention has focused on their biology as well as that of the mosquitoes which transmit the parasites. References to its unique, periodic fevers are found throughout recorded history, beginning in the first millennium BC in Greece and China. For thousands of years, traditional herbal remedies have been used to treat malaria."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "febre latica", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4497, "target_cluster_name": "febre latica", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A type of fever characterized by occurring every third day.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: A type of fever characterized by occurring every third day.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "enfermedades largas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "book_count": 3, "total_mentions": 13, "members": [{"entity_id": "enfermedades_largas", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "enfermedades largas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 4, "variants": ["enfermedades largas", "enfermedades largas y importunas"], "contexts": ["long illnesses treated with the root", "long diseases"]}, {"entity_id": "doenças_prolongadas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "doenças prolongadas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 2, "variants": ["doenças prolongadas"], "contexts": ["long-lasting illnesses", "Long-lasting illnesses"]}, {"entity_id": "doenças_cronicas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "doenças cronicas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["doenças cronicas"], "contexts": ["chronic illnesses"]}, {"entity_id": "enfermidades_antigas", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "enfermidades antigas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 1, "variants": ["enfermidades antigas"], "contexts": ["long-standing illnesses"]}, {"entity_id": "enfermidades_velhas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "enfermidades velhas", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "CHRONIC", "count": 2, "variants": ["enfermidades velhas", "doenças velhas"], "contexts": ["old illnesses treated with the stone", "old diseases, chronic conditions"]}, {"enti