rk, clearly refers to the biological sex.", "wikidata_id": "Q2192288", "wikidata_description": "external genital organs of the female mammal"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "British plants", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "british_plants", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "British plants", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["British plants"], "contexts": ["examples of plant varieties", "Mr. Babington on"]}, {"entity_id": "british_flora", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "British flora", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 3, "variants": ["British flora"], "contexts": ["plants of the British Isles", "plant life of Britain"]}, {"entity_id": "british_plants", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "British Plants", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["British Plants"], "contexts": ["subject of Watson's remarks"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "British plants", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "British flora", "similarity": 0.926}, {"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "British plants", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "British Plants", "similarity": 0.99}], "id": 2375, "stable_key": "clu_1b6e33fd00f9e5a2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "British flora", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "This refers to the collective plant life of the British Isles, often studied in the context of natural history and evolution.", "wikidata_id": "Q56651604", "wikidata_description": "plants endemic to Great Britain", "wikipedia_extract": "The flora of India is one of the richest in the world due to the wide range of climate, topology and habitat in the country. Floral Diversity and Medicinal Plant Wealth There are estimated to be over 18,000 species of flowering plants in India, which constitute some 6-7 percent of the total plant species in the world. India is home to more than 50,000  species of plants, including a variety of endemics. The use of plants as a source of medicines has been an integral part of life in India from the earliest times. There are more than 3000 Indian plant species officially documented as possessing  into eight main floristic regions : Western Himalayas, Eastern Himalayas, Assam,  Indus plain, Ganges plain, the Deccan, Malabar and the Andaman Islands. Forest Cover and Vegetation Diversity In 1992, 743,534 km2 of land in the country was forested of which 92 percent was government land.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flora_of_India"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Flowering plants", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2985, "target_cluster_name": "flowering plants", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Flowering plants are a major component of any general flora, including British flora.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Flowering plants are a major component of any general flora, including British flora."}, {"found_name": "Plants", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 16, "target_cluster_name": "Plants", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "British flora is a specific instance of the general category of 'Plants'.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "British flora is a specific instance of the general category of 'Plants'."}, {"found_name": "Floras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2595, "target_cluster_name": "Floras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "British flora is a specific type of flora, defined by its geographical location (Britain).", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_rel