d": "Q42168", "wikidata_description": "commune in Puy-de-Dôme, France", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clermont-Ferrand", "wikipedia_extract": "Clermont-Ferrand Cathedral, or the Cathedral of Our Lady of the Assumption of Clermont-Ferrand (French: Cathédrale Notre-Dame-de-l'Assomption de Clermont-Ferrand), is a Gothic cathedral and French national monument located in the city of Clermont-Ferrand in the Auvergne. It is the seat of the Archbishops of Clermont (bishops until 2002). It is built entirely in black lava stone, which makes it highly distinctive, and visible from a great distance. Its twin spires are 96.1 metres tall, and tower above the city's rooftops. It has been listed since 1862 as a monument historique by the French Ministry of Culture. In the 5th century, bishop Namatius laid the foundations of the city's first cathedral, allowing the Christian community to leave its ghetto, the \"vicus christianorum\"."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Auvergne", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 890, "target_cluster_name": "Auvergne", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Clermont-Ferrand is located in the Auvergne region of France.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Clermont-Ferrand is located in the Auvergne region of France."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Arica", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "arica", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Arica", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 6, "variants": ["Arica"], "contexts": ["city in Chile", "port city"]}, {"entity_id": "arica", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Arica", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Arica"], "contexts": ["Peruvian coast location"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Arica", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Arica", "similarity": 0.787}], "id": 2384, "stable_key": "clu_454effa4174eda08", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Arica", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A port city in northern Chile.", "note": "Acra is likely referring to Acre, a port city.", "wikipedia_extract": "Arica ( ə-REE-kə; Spanish: [aˈɾika]) is a commune and a port city with a population of 241,653 in the Arica Province of northern Chile's Arica y Parinacota Region. It is Chile's northernmost city, being located only 18 km (11 mi) south of the border with Peru. The city is the capital of both the Arica Province and the Arica and Parinacota Region. Arica is located at the bend of South America's western coast known as the Arica Bend or Arica Elbow. At the location of the city are two valleys that dissect the Atacama Desert converge: Azapa and Lluta. These valleys provide citrus and olives for export."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Chili", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 603, "target_cluster_name": "Chili", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arica is a major port city in northern Chile.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arica is a major port city in northern Chile.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Callao", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1845, "target_cluster_name": "Callao", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arica is a port city in Chile, historically significant in the region and often discussed in relation to other South American ports like Callao.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Arica is a port city in Chile, historically significant in the region and often discussed in relation to other South American ports like Callao.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Andes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 207, "target_cluster_name": "Andes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arica is located in the Andes mountain range.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arica is located in the Andes mountain range."}, {"found_name": "Chile", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 603, "target_cluster_name": "Chili", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Arica is a city in Chile.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Arica is a city in Chile."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Strasbourg", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "strasbourg", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Strasbourg", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 6, "variants": ["STRASBOURG", "Strasbourg"], "contexts": ["location with barometer data", "location with latitude 48° 34' 56\""]}, {"entity_id": "strasbourg", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Strasbourg", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Strasbourg"], "contexts": ["city in France"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Strasbourg", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Strasbourg", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2385, "stable_key": "clu_bea8bd2758db347d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Strasbourg", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "France", "wikidata_id": "Q6602", "wikidata_description": "capital and largest city of Grand Est, located in the historical region of Alsace", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strasbourg", "wikipedia_extract": "Strasbourg (UK:  STRAZ-burg, US:  STRAHSS-boorg, STRAHZ-, -⁠burg; French: [stʁasbuʁ] ; German: Straßburg [ˈʃtʁaːsbʊʁk] ) is the prefecture and largest city of the Grand Est region of eastern France, in the historic region of Alsace. It is the prefecture of the Bas-Rhin department and the official seat of the European Parliament. The city has about three hundred thousand inhabitants, and together Greater Strasbourg and the arrondissement of Strasbourg have over five hundred thousand. Strasbourg's metropolitan area had a population of 860,744 in 2020, making it the eighth-largest metro area in France and home to 14% of the Grand Est region's inhabitants. The transnational Eurodistrict Strasbourg-Ortenau had a population of roughly 1,000,000 in 2022. Strasbourg is one of the de facto four main capitals of the European Union (alongside Brussels, Luxembourg and Frankfurt), as it is the seat of several European institutions, such as the European Parliament, the Eurocorps and the European Ombudsman of the European Union."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "France", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 46, "target_cluster_name": "France", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Strasbourg is a prefecture and largest city of the Grand Est region of eastern France.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Strasbourg is a prefecture and largest city of the Grand Est region of eastern France."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Lindenau", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "lindenau", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Lindenau", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 5, "variants": ["Lindenau", "M. de Lindcnau", "M. de Lindenau", "M. de Lindeneau", "MM. de Lindenau et Bauza"], "contexts": ["person who made calculations", "calculated the surface area of Cuba"]}, {"entity_id": "lindenau", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Lindenau", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Linde