he Himalayan and Karakoram mountain ranges. This is a list of mountaineers who have died on these mountains. Mount Everest, Earth's highest mountain at 8,848.86 metres (29,031.7 ft) above sea level, has been host to numerous tragedies. Deaths have occurred on the mountain every year since 1978, excluding 2020, when permits were not issued due to the COVID-19 pandemic. The most notable deadly events on Everest were the 1922 British Mount Everest expedition, 1970 Mount Everest disaster, 1974 French Mount Everest expedition, 1996 Mount Everest disaster, 2014 Mount Everest ice avalanche, 2015 Mount Everest avalanches and 2023 Mount Everest season.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_deaths_on_eight-thousanders"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Voyages", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "voyages_and_descr_", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Voyages and Descr.", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Voyages and Descr.", "Voyages and Descriptions"], "contexts": ["title of Dampier's work", "publication title"]}, {"entity_id": "travels", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Travels", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Travels"], "contexts": ["book by M. Melish"]}, {"entity_id": "voyages", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Voyages", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Voyages"], "contexts": ["work cited", "Tavernier, Voyages"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Voyages and Descr.", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Voyages", "similarity": 0.914}, {"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Travels", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Voyages",