ed", "found_relationship": "Both electric and magnetic field lines are used to visualize and describe forces in electromagnetism."}, {"found_name": "Induction", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 280, "target_cluster_name": "Induction", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Changes in magnetic field lines are directly related to electromagnetic induction.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Changes in magnetic field lines are directly related to electromagnetic induction."}, {"found_name": "magnetic lines of declination", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "evidence_snippet": "stars, 152; hypothesis of the earth being a hollow sphere, 171; his bold conjecture that the Aurora Borealis was a magnetic phenomenon, 193. Hansteen on magnetic lines of declination in Northern Asia,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of"}]}, {"canonical_name": "diameter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "diameter", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "diameter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["diameter"], "contexts": ["measurement of celestial body size"]}, {"entity_id": "diameter", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "diameter", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 6, "variants": ["diameter"], "contexts": ["measurement of spheres", "straight line passing through the center"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "diameter", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "diameter", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2457, "stable_key": "clu_da1d21618a67f630", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Diameter", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Jupiter", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 553, "target_cluster_name": "Jupiter", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The diameter is a key physical characteristic of Jupiter.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The diameter is a key physical characteristic of Jupiter.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "distances", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1373, "target_cluster_name": "distances", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diameter is a measure of size, and when combined with apparent diameter, allows for the calculation of distance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Diameter is a measure of size, and when combined with apparent diameter, allows for the calculation of distance.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "measurement", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1274, "target_cluster_name": "measurement", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diameter is a specific length that is measured, a direct application of the concept of measurement.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Diameter is a specific length that is measured, a direct application of the concept of measurement.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "size", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1342, "target_cluster_name": "size", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diameter is a fundamental measure of size for circular or spherical objects.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Diameter is a fundamental measure of size for circular or spherical objects.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "volume", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2219, "target_cluster_name": "volume", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Diameter is a linear measure that is a fundamental component in calculating the volume of many geometric shapes.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Diameter is a linear measure that is a fundamental component in calculating the volume of many geometric shapes.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Apparent diameter", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3634, "target_cluster_name": "Apparent diameter", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Apparent diameter is a specific type of diameter, referring to the angular size of an object as seen from a distance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Apparent diameter is a specific type of diameter, referring to the angular size of an object as seen from a distance."}]}, {"canonical_name": "agua de lengua de buey", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "agua_de_lengua_de_buey", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "agua de lengua de buey", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 6, "variants": ["agua de lengua de buey", "agua de legua de buey", "agua de lengua de Buey"], "contexts": ["water of ox tongue", "water with ox tongue"]}, {"entity_id": "agua_de_linguade_vacca", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "agua de linguade vacca", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["agua de linguade vacca"], "contexts": ["cow's tongue water for ointment"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "agua de lengua de buey", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "agua de linguade vacca", "similarity": 0.891}], "id": 2458, "stable_key": "clu_53a86599d55f2fb0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Water of Ox Tongue", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A medicinal preparation made with ox tongue.", "wikipedia_extract": "Redox potential (also known as oxidation / reduction potential, ORP, pe, ) is a measure of the tendency of a chemical species to acquire electrons from or lose electrons to an electrode and thereby be reduced or oxidised respectively. Redox potential is expressed in volts (V). Each species has its own intrinsic redox potential; for example, the more positive the reduction potential (reduction potential is more often used due to general formalism in electrochemistry), the greater the species' affinity for electrons and tendency to be reduced. In aqueous solutions, redox potential is a measure of the tendency of the solution to either gain or lose electrons in a reaction. A solution with a higher (more positive) reduction potential than some other molecule will have a tendency to gain electrons from this molecule (i.e. to be reduced by oxidizing this other molecule) and a solution with a lower (more negative) reduction potential will have a tendency to lose electrons to other substances (i.e. to be oxidized by reducing the other substance). Because the absolute potentials are next to impossible to accurately measure, reduction potentials are defined relative to a reference electrode."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Rosewater", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 292, "target_cluster_name": "Rosewater", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are specific types of 'waters' used medicinally, often prepared by infusion or distillation.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are specific types of 'waters' used medicinally, often prepared by infusion or distillation."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Xaraue", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "xaraue", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Xaraue", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 5, "variants": ["Xaraue", "xaraue", "xaraues"], "contexts": ["sweet liquid preparation", "syrup for medicinal preparations"]}, {"entity_id": "xaráo", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "xaráo", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "PREPARATION", "count": 2, "variants": ["xaráo", "xardo"], "contexts": ["stronger distilled spirit", "word for drink, derived from Arabic"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Xaraue", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "xaráo", "similarity": 0.891}], "id": 2459, "stable_key": "clu_175fecfaa2fa97b2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Xaraue", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A sweet, distilled liquid preparation, likely a spirit or syrup.", "note": "Derived from Arabic 'xaráo' meaning drink."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Pino", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "pino", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Pino", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 4, "variants": ["Pino", "Pinos"], "contexts": ["tree from which some thought it came", "tree used for size comparison"]}, {"entity_id": "pino", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "pino", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Pino", "pino"], "contexts": ["mixed with mastice", "tree from which resin is distilled"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Pino", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "pino", "similarity": 0.901}], "id": 2460, "stable_key": "clu_08c7710012f8fe23", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Pine", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "cedro", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2508, "target_cluster_name": "cedro", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are coniferous trees often used for timber.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are coniferous trees often used for timber."}, {"found_name": "abeto", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3182, "target_cluster_name": "abeto", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are coniferous trees, often grouped together in botanical and economic contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are coniferous trees, often grouped together in botanical and economic contexts."}, {"found_name": "Tree", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 24, "target_cluster_name": "Tree", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pine is a type of tree.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Pine is a type of tree."}, {"found_name": "Timber trees", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3930, "target_cluster_name": "Timber Trees", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pine is a significant timber tree.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Pine is a significant timber tree."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Alberto Magno", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 4, "total_mentions": 11, "members": [{"entity_id": "alberto_magno", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "Alberto magno", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Alberto magno", "Albertó magno"], "contexts": ["medieval scholar on treasures", "authority on metals"]}, {"entity_id": "alberto_magno", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Alberto Magno", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Alberto Magno"], "contexts": ["medieval philosopher and theologian, Albertus Magnus", "medieval scholar"]}, {"entity_id": "albertus_magnus", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Albertus Magnus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 3, "variants": ["Albertus Magnus"], "contexts": ["made mention of the magnet", "medieval scholar on badger leg inequality"]}, {"entity_id": "albertus_magnus", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Albertus Magnus", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Albertus Magnus"], "contexts": ["medieval philosopher and theologian"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "Alberto magno", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Alberto Magno", "similarity": 0.967}], "id": 2461, "stable_key": "clu_f3b1e59a59595ecb", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Albertus Magnus", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1200, "death_year": 1280, "description": "Medieval philosopher, theologian, and prolific writer on natural philosophy.", "wikidata_id": "Q60059", "wikidata_description": "German-Dominican friar and saint (c. 1200–1280)"}, "member_count": 4, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Aristotle", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 62, "target_cluster_name": "Aristotle", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who synthesized Aristotelian philosophy with Christian theology. He is often referred to as 'the Great Albert' and 'the Doctor Universalis' for his comprehensive knowledge, heavily influenced by Aristotle.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who synthesized Aristotelian philosophy with Christian theology. He is often referred to as 'the Great Albert' and 'the Doctor Universalis' for his comprehensive knowledge, heavily influenced by Aristotle."}, {"found_name": "Thomas Aquinas", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 2931, "target_cluster_name": "Thomas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was the teacher of Thomas Aquinas, another highly influential philosopher and theologian. Their intellectual relationship is central to the history of Scholasticism.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Albertus Magnus was the teacher of Thomas Aquinas, another highly influential philosopher and theologian. Their intellectual relationship is central to the history of Scholasticism."}, {"found_name": "Averroes", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 952, "target_cluster_name": "Averroes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus engaged with and commented on the works of Averroes, the Islamic philosopher whose commentaries on Aristotle were highly influential in medieval Europe. Albertus Magnus sought to reconcile Aristotelian thought with Christian doctrine, often in dialogue with Averroes' interpretations.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Albertus Magnus engaged with and commented on the works of Averroes, the Islamic philosopher whose commentaries on Aristotle were highly influential in medieval Europe. Albertus Magnus sought to reconcile Aristotelian thought with Christian doctrine, often in dialogue with Averroes' interpretations."}, {"found_name": "Avicenna", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1492, "target_cluster_name": "Avicena", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was familiar with and commented on the works of Avicenna, another key figure in Islamic philosophy whose medical and philosophical writings were important in the medieval period. Albertus Magnus's encyclopedic works often drew upon both Avicenna and Aristotle.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Albertus Magnus was familiar with and commented on the works of Avicenna, another key figure in Islamic philosophy whose medical and philosophical writings were important in the medieval period. Albertus Magnus's encyclopedic works often drew upon both Avicenna and Aristotle."}, {"found_name": "Theophrasto", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 98, "target_cluster_name": "Theophrasto", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential figures in natural philosophy and science, with Albertus Magnus being a significant medieval scholar whose work influenced later thinkers like Paracelsus.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were influential figures in natural philosophy and science, with Albertus Magnus being a significant medieval scholar whose work influenced later thinkers like Paracelsus.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "philosopher", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 431, "target_cluster_name": "philosopher", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent philosopher and theologian in the medieval period, known for his extensive commentaries on Aristotle and his contributions to natural philosophy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Albertus Magnus was a prominent philosopher and theologian in the medieval period, known for his extensive commentaries on Aristotle and his contributions to natural philosophy.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Italians", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 462, "target_cluster_name": "Italians", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a German Dominican friar, philosopher, and bishop who spent much of his career in Italy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Albertus Magnus was a German Dominican friar, philosopher, and bishop who spent much of his career in Italy.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Paracelsus", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 703, "target_cluster_name": "Paracelsus", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were influential figures in natural philosophy and alchemy, with Albertus Magnus being a significant predecessor whose work Paracelsus would have been aware of and potentially engaged with.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were influential figures in natural philosophy and alchemy, with Albertus Magnus being a significant predecessor whose work Paracelsus would have been aware of and potentially engaged with.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Amat.", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 902, "target_cluster_name": "Amat.", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who was heavily influenced by Aristotle's works and was known as 'the Great' for his comprehensive knowledge, much like Aristotle was revered in antiquity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who was heavily influenced by Aristotle's works and was known as 'the Great' for his comprehensive knowledge, much like Aristotle was revered in antiquity.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Agricola", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 907, "target_cluster_name": "Agricola", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval scholar whose work on natural philosophy and science influenced later thinkers like Agricola.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval scholar whose work on natural philosophy and science influenced later thinkers like Agricola.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Carlos Magno", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2881, "target_cluster_name": "Carlos Magno", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both were prominent figures in European history and intellectual life, Albertus Magnus as a philosopher and theologian, and Charlemagne as an emperor and patron of learning.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both were prominent figures in European history and intellectual life, Albertus Magnus as a philosopher and theologian, and Charlemagne as an emperor and patron of learning.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Thomas", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2931, "target_cluster_name": "Thomas", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who was a major influence on Thomas Aquinas's thought. Aquinas was a student of Albertus Magnus.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Albertus Magnus was a prominent medieval philosopher and theologian who was a major influence on Thomas Aquinas's thought. Aquinas was a student of Albertus Magnus.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "malicia", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "malicia", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "malicia", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["malicia"], "contexts": ["quality of being harmful or evil", "malice of poison"]}, {"entity_id": "malicia", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "malicia", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["malicia"], "contexts": ["negative judgment of actions", "malice, referring to disease"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "malicia", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "malicia", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2462, "stable_key": "clu_03d47c7ffbfe2c35", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Malice", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "The quality of being harmful, evil, or malevolent.", "note": "Can refer to intent, poison, or disease.", "wikipedia_extract": "Capoeira (Portuguese pronunciation: [kapuˈe(j)ɾɐ]) is an Afro-Brazilian martial art and game that includes elements of dance, acrobatics, music, and spirituality. It includes acrobatic and complex manoeuvres, often involving hands on the ground and inverted kicks. It emphasizes flowing movements rather than fixed stances; the ginga, a rocking step, is usually the focal point of the technique. Though often said to be a martial art disguised as a dance, capoeira also serves as a way to maintain spirituality and culture. Capoeira has been practiced among Black Brazilians for centuries. The date of its creation is unknown, but it was first mentioned in a judicial document under the name Capoeiragem in 1789, as \"the gravest of crimes\"."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "guerras", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 483, "target_cluster_name": "guerras", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Malice, or ill will, can be a driving motivation behind the initiation and conduct of war.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Malice, or ill will, can be a driving motivation behind the initiation and conduct of war.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "antipathia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 681, "target_cluster_name": "antipathia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Antipathy implies a negative disposition towards something or someone, which can be a component of malice.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Antipathy implies a negative disposition towards something or someone, which can be a component of malice.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Music", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1052, "target_cluster_name": "music", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Music is an integral component of Capoeira, accompanying its practice and performance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Music is an integral component of Capoeira, accompanying its practice and performance."}, {"found_name": "Spirit", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 476, "target_cluster_name": "spirit", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Capoeira incorporates spiritual elements and is often described as having a spiritual dimension.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Capoeira incorporates spiritual elements and is often described as having a spiritual dimension."}]}, {"canonical_name": "falitre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "falitre", "book_id": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "name": "falitre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["falitre"], "contexts": ["substance with cold virtue"]}, {"entity_id": "falitre", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "falitre", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 6, "variants": ["falitre"], "contexts": ["saltpeter, dissolved in water with oil", "saltpeter, a medicinal ingredient"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "historia_medicinal_monardes_1574", "source_name": "falitre", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "falitre", "similarity": 0.757}], "id": 2463, "stable_key": "clu_257403c609a0cca6", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Saltpeter", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "note": "The spelling 'falitre' is an archaic Portuguese form of saltpeter."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "croco indiaco", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "croco_indiaco", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "croco indiaco", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 6, "variants": ["croco indiaco", "CROCO INDIACO", "Croco Indiaco", "croco indiano"], "contexts": ["substance discussed", "Orta's name for Curcuma longa rhizome"]}, {"entity_id": "croco", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "croco", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["croco"], "contexts": ["ingredient in preparation"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "croco indiaco", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "croco", "similarity": 0.891}], "id": 2464, "stable_key": "clu_602934df4832c9b1", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Turmeric", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Curcuma longa", "family": "Zingiberaceae", "description": "A spice derived from a rhizome, used in medicine and as a dye.", "note": "Also known as 'croco indiaco' in the text.", "wikipedia_extract": "Turmeric (), or Curcuma longa (), is a flowering plant in the ginger family Zingiberaceae. It is a perennial, rhizomatous, herbaceous plant native to the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia that requires temperatures between 20 and 30 °C (68 and 86 °F) and high annual rainfall to thrive. Plants are gathered each year for their rhizomes, some for propagation in the following season and some for consumption or dyeing. The rhizomes can be used fresh, but they are often boiled in water and dried, after which they are ground into a deep orange-yellow shelf-stable spice powder commonly used as a coloring and flavoring agent in many Asian cuisines, especially for curries (curry powder). Turmeric powder has a warm, bitter, black pepper-like flavor and earthy, mustard-like aroma. Although long used in Ayurvedic medicine, there is no high-quality clinical evidence that consuming turmeric or the principal turmeric constituent, curcumin, is effective for treating any disease."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "zedoaria", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 767, "target_cluster_name": "zedoaria", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both 'zedoary' and 'croco indiaco' (Indian crocus) are historical names for Curcuma zedoaria, indicating they refer to the same plant.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both 'zedoary' and 'croco indiaco' (Indian crocus) are historical names for Curcuma zedoaria, indicating they refer to the same plant.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Curcuma", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 1807, "target_cluster_name": "Curcuma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The historical name 'croco indiaco' is a direct synonym for Turmeric, and 'Curcuma' is the genus name for Turmeric.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_synonyms", "found_relationship": "The historical name 'croco indiaco' is a direct synonym for Turmeric, and 'Curcuma' is the genus name for Turmeric."}, {"found_name": "ginger", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1688, "target_cluster_name": "gengibre", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Turmeric belongs to the same family (Zingiberaceae) as ginger and shares a similar rhizomatous growth habit and culinary/medicinal uses.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Turmeric belongs to the same family (Zingiberaceae) as ginger and shares a similar rhizomatous growth habit and culinary/medicinal uses."}, {"found_name": "Galangal", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 270, "target_cluster_name": "Galbano", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Galangal is also a rhizomatous plant in the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to turmeric and ginger, and often used in similar culinary and medicinal contexts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Galangal is also a rhizomatous plant in the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to turmeric and ginger, and often used in similar culinary and medicinal contexts."}, {"found_name": "Zedoary", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 767, "target_cluster_name": "zedoaria", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Zedoary is another rhizomatous plant in the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to turmeric, and shares some traditional medicinal applications.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Zedoary is another rhizomatous plant in the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to turmeric, and shares some traditional medicinal applications."}, {"found_name": "Amomum", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2029, "target_cluster_name": "Amomum", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Amomum is a genus within the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to Curcuma (turmeric), and often grouped with other spices from this family.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Amomum is a genus within the Zingiberaceae family, closely related to Curcuma (turmeric), and 