The date range 1220-1240 clearly indicates Frederick II. The 'Duke of Bavaria' mention is likely a confusion with other Fredericks."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Emperadores", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2523, "target_cluster_name": "Emperadores", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Frederick II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Frederick II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "moço", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "moço", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "moço", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 4, "variants": ["moço", "MOÇO", "Moça"], "contexts": ["interlocutor in dialogue", "boy who brought a branch"]}, {"entity_id": "moça", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "moça", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 3, "variants": ["moça", "moça nobre"], "contexts": ["young woman, patient description", "young woman, treated for baldness"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "moço", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "moça", "similarity": 0.918}], "id": 2469, "stable_key": "clu_759b8d22bdbc94b6", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "youth", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "note": "The terms 'moço' and 'moça' in Portuguese refer to a young male or female, often used in a general sense of youth or as an interlocutor in a dialogue."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "S. Francisco Xavier", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 7, "members": [{"entity_id": "s__francisco_xavier", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "S. Francisc