ividuals in the Roman Republic and later, the Emperor himself or his designated heir. Therefore, 'Emperor' is a closely related concept, representing the ultimate authority that 'Princes' might serve or aspire to.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The term 'Princes' (Principes) in Roman history often referred to the highest-ranking individuals in the Roman Republic and later, the Emperor himself or his designated heir. Therefore, 'Emperor' is a closely related concept, representing the ultimate authority that 'Princes' might serve or aspire to.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "King", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1604, "target_cluster_name": "elrey", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The King is a sovereign ruler, often subordinate to an Emperor in historical hierarchies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The King is a sovereign ruler, often subordinate to an Emperor in historical hierarchies."}, {"found_name": "Queen", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3203, "target_cluster_name": "Rainha", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Queen is a sovereign ruler, often subordinate to an Emperor in historical hierarchies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Queen is a sovereign ruler, often subordinate to an Emperor in historical hierarchies."}, {"found_name": "Princes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2143, "target_cluster_name": "Principes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Princes are typically rulers of principalities, often vassals or heirs to an Emperor.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Princes are typically rulers of principalities, often vassals or heirs to an Emperor."}, {"found_name": "Charles V, Holy Roman Emperor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 771, "target_cluster_name": "Carlos V.", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Charles V was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Charles V was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity."}, {"found_name": "Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3197, "target_cluster_name": "Dom Fernando", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ferdinand I was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ferdinand I was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity."}, {"found_name": "Ferdinand II, Holy Roman Emperor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 445, "target_cluster_name": "Ferdinand", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ferdinand II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Ferdinand II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity."}, {"found_name": "Frederick II, Holy Roman Emperor", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2468, "target_cluster_name": "Frederico II", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Frederick II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Frederick II was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity."}, {"found_name": "Charlemagne", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2881, "target_cluster_name": "Carlos Magno", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Charlemagne was crowned Emperor of the Romans, a foundational figure in the concept of Emperor in Western Europe.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Charlemagne was crowned Emperor of the Romans, a foundational figure in the concept of Emperor in Western Europe."}, {"found_name": "Carlos Magno", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2881, "target_cluster_name": "Carlos Magno", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Charlemagne was an Emperor, and this term refers to the role he held.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Charlemagne was an Emperor, and this term refers to the role he held.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Herb. Amb.", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "herbal", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Herbal", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Herbal"], "contexts": ["book on plants and their uses"]}, {"entity_id": "herb__amb_", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Herb. Amb.", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Herb. Amb.", "Herb. amb.", "Herh. amB."], "contexts": ["title of a botanical work", "book title"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "english_physician_1652", "source_name": "Herbal", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Herb. Amb.", "similarity": 0.895}], "id": 2524, "stable_key": "clu_32b88c98168fd1d6", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Herbal", "confidence": "high", "type": "object", "description": "A book containing descriptions and illustrations of plants and their uses.", "note": "Refers to specific botanical works and the general category of herbals.", "wikipedia_extract": "A herbal is a book containing the names and descriptions of plants, usually with information on their medicinal, tonic, culinary, toxic, hallucinatory, aromatic, or magical powers, and the legends associated with them. A herbal may also classify the plants it describes, may give recipes for herbal extracts, tinctures, or potions, and sometimes include mineral and animal medicaments in addition to those obtained from plants. Herbals were often illustrated to assist plant identification. Herbals were among the first literature produced in Ancient Egypt, China, India, and Europe as the medical wisdom of the day accumulated by herbalists, apothecaries and physicians. Herbals were also among the first books to be printed in both China and Europe. In Western Europe herbals flourished for two centuries following the introduction of moveable type (c. 1470–1670)."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Coliget", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4443, "target_cluster_name": "Coliget", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A 'colliget' or 'collyrium' is a medicinal preparation, often derived from herbs, and thus related to the contents of a herbal.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A 'colliget' or 'collyrium' is a medicinal preparation, often derived from herbs, and thus related to the contents of a herbal."}]}, {"canonical_name": "seedlings", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "seedlings", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "seedlings", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 5, "variants": ["Seedlings", "seedlings"], "contexts": ["young plants from the same fruit", "young plants grown from seeds"]}, {"entity_id": "seed-lobes", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Seed-lobes", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Seed-lobes"], "contexts": ["proportion in distribution of plants"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "seedlings", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Seed-lobes", "similarity": 0.923}], "id": 2525, "stable_key": "clu_efd8e778fddb9a95", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "seedling", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "note": "The term 'Seed-lobes' seems to be a misreading or less common variant for 'seedlings' in the given context.", "wikidata_id": "Q1385709", "wikidata_description": "a young seed plant just after germination"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "seed", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 211, "target_cluster_name": "Seed", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A seedling is a young plant grown from a seed.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A seedling is a young plant grown from a seed."}]}, {"canonical_name": "offspring", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "offspring", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "offspring", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 5, "variants": ["offspring"], "contexts": ["progeny of organisms", "progeny of an organism"]}, {"entity_id": "offspring", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "offspring", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["offspring"], "contexts": ["progeny of parents"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "offspring", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "offspring", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2526, "stable_key": "clu_c37369838e49d989", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "offspring", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "wikidata_id": "Q239526", "wikidata_description": "in biology, the product of reproduction of an organism"}, "cross_