ties, could find very few and, as it seems to me, quite unimportant differences between the so-called hybrid offspring of species, and the so-called mongre", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of offspring"}, {"found_name": "mongrel offspring", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "evidence_snippet": "line of distinction between species and varieties, could find very few and, as it seems to me, quite unimportant differences between the so-called hybrid offspring of species, and the so-called mongre", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of offspring"}]}, {"canonical_name": "destruction", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "destruction", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "destruction", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 5, "variants": ["destruction"], "contexts": ["process of elimination", "process of being eliminated"]}, {"entity_id": "destruction", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "destruction", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["destruction"], "contexts": ["the act of destroying"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "destruction", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "destruction", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2527, "stable_key": "clu_68785cabc9e65d5c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "destruction", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q552431", "wikidata_description": "state when natural environment becomes unable to support its native species due to human activity"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Decay", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4296, "target_cluster_name": "decay", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Decay is a process of destruction or decomposition.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Decay is a process of destruction or decomposition."}, {"found_name": "Flood", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3783, "target_cluster_name": "Flood", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "A flood is a natural disaster involving widespread destruction of property and life.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "A flood is a natural disaster involving widespread destruction of property and life."}, {"found_name": "Explosion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3650, "target_cluster_name": "explosion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "An explosion is a rapid and violent destruction of something.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "An explosion is a rapid and violent destruction of something."}, {"found_name": "Combustion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 866, "target_cluster_name": "combustion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Combustion is a process that often results in destruction by fire.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Combustion is a process that often results in destruction by fire."}, {"found_name": "Evolution", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 540, "target_cluster_name": "Evolution", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "While evolution is a process of change, it can involve the destruction of less adapted forms.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "While evolution is a process of change, it can involve the destruction of less adapted forms."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Milne Edwards", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "milne_edwards", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Milne Edwards", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 5, "variants": ["Milne Edwards"], "contexts": ["elucidated physiological division of labour", "naturalist quoted on nature's variety"]}, {"entity_id": "milne-edwards", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Milne-Edwards", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Milne-Edwards"], "contexts": ["described union of homogeneous parts in invertebrata"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Milne Edwards", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Milne-Edwards", "similarity": 0.887}], "id": 2528, "stable_key": "clu_3d66298a6da26a39", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Henri Milne Edwards", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1800, "death_year": 1885, "description": "Zoologist who studied physiological division of labor.", "wikidata_id": "Q505173", "wikidata_description": "French zoologist (1800-1885)", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Milne-Edwards", "wikipedia_extract": "Milne-Edwards's sifaka (Propithecus edwardsi), or Milne-Edwards's simpona, is a large arboreal, diurnal lemur endemic to the eastern coastal rainforest of Madagascar. Milne-Edwards's sifaka is characterized by a black body with a light-colored \"saddle\" on the lower part of its back. It is closely related to the diademed sifaka, and was until recently considered a subspecies of it. Like all sifakas, it is a primate in the family Indriidae. The species' name honors French zoologist Henri Milne-Edwards (1800–1885). Milne-Edwards's sifaka is categorized as endangered by the IUCN, and is listed in CITES Appendix I."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Isidore Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3984, "target_cluster_name": "M. Is. Geoffroy St. Hilaire", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Isidore Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire was a contemporary zoologist and a significant figure in the development of evolutionary thought, known for his work on teratology and classification. He was a colleague and sometimes collaborator with Milne Edwards, and they shared a similar scientific milieu and interests in comparative anatomy and zoology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Isidore Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire was a contemporary zoologist and a significant figure in the development of evolutionary thought, known for his work on teratology and classification. He was a colleague and sometimes collaborator with Milne Edwards, and they shared a similar scientific milieu and interests in comparative anatomy and zoology."}, {"found_name": "Georges Cuvier", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 119, "target_cluster_name": "Cuvier", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Georges Cuvier was a highly influential naturalist and zoologist, considered the father of paleontology and comparative anatomy. Milne Edwards was a student and successor to Cuvier's legacy, working within the framework of Cuvierian classification and research methods.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Georges Cuvier was a highly influential naturalist and zoologist, considered the father of paleontology and comparative anatomy. Milne Edwards was a student and successor to Cuvier's legacy, working within the framework of Cuvierian classification and research methods."}, {"found_name": "Frederick Cuvier", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3990, "target_cluster_name": "Frederick Cuvier", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Frederick Cuvier was the brother of Georges Cuvier and also a zoologist. He worked on mammals and comparative anatomy, areas that would have been of direct interest and relevance to Milne Edwards's own research.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Frederick Cuvier was the brother of Georges Cuvier and also a zoologist. He worked on mammals and comparative anatomy, areas that would have been of direct interest and relevance to Milne Edwards's own research."}, {"found_name": "Achille Valenciennes", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3364, "target_cluster_name": "Valenciennes", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Achille Valenciennes was a zoologist who collaborated with Henri Milne Edwards on several important works, particularly on ichthyology (the study of fish). Their joint publications indicate a close working relationship and shared scientific focus.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Achille Valenciennes was a zoologist who collaborated with Henri Milne Edwards on several important works, particularly on ichthyology (the study of fish). Their joint publications indicate a close working relationship and shared scientific focus."}, {"found_name": "Zoologist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3376, "target_cluster_name": "zoologist", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Henri Milne Edwards was a prominent zoologist, and this term represents his primary professional identity and field of study.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Henri Milne Edwards was a prominent zoologist, and this term represents his primary professional identity and field of study."}, {"found_name": "Naturalist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1650, "target_cluster_name": "naturalists", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Henri Milne Edwards was a naturalist, a broader term encompassing his study of the natural world, including zoology and comparative anatomy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Henri Milne Edwards was a naturalist, a broader term encompassing his study of the natural world, including zoology and comparative anatomy."}]}, {"canonical_name": "palæontologists", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "palæontologists", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "palæontologists", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 5, "variants": ["palæontologists"], "contexts": ["experts in fossils", "scientists studying fossils"]}, {"entity_id": "palæontologists", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "palæontologists", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["palæontologists"], "contexts": ["scientists studying fossils"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "palæontologists", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "palæontologists", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2529, "stable_key": "clu_b9f52d228a920156", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Paleontologists", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q7205", "wikidata_description": "scientific study of the past of life on Earth through fossils", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paleontology", "wikipedia_extract": "Persons of National Historic Significance (National Historic People) (French: Personnes d'importance historique nationale (personnages historiques nationaux)) are people designated by the Canadian government as being nationally significant in the history of the country. Designations are made by the Minister of the Environment on the recommendation of the Historic Sites and Monuments Board of Canada. Approximately 70 nominations are submitted to the board each year. A person is eligible to be listed 25 years after death, but Prime Ministers may be designated any time after death. Parks Canada administers the program, and installs and maintains the federal plaques commonly erected to commemorate each person, usually placed at a site closely associated with them. The intent is generally to honour the person's contribution to the country but is always to educate the public about that person."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Geologists", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 956, "target_cluster_name": "geologists", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paleontology is a sub-discipline of geology, focusing on the study of ancient life through fossils.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paleontology is a sub-discipline of geology, focusing on the study of ancient life through fossils."}, {"found_name": "Naturalist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1650, "target_cluster_name": "naturalists", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paleontologists are a type of naturalist, as they study the natural world, specifically ancient organisms.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paleontologists are a type of naturalist, as they study the natural world, specifically ancient organisms."}, {"found_name": "Zoologist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3376, "target_cluster_name": "zoologist", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paleontology often involves the study of fossil animals, making it closely related to zoology.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paleontology often involves the study of fossil animals, making it closely related to zoology."}, {"found_name": "Botanist", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2986, "target_cluster_name": "botanists", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Paleontology also includes the study of fossil plants, making it related to botany.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Paleontology also includes the study of fossil plants, making it related to botany."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Melipona", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "INSECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "melipona", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Melipona", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "INSECT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Melipona"], "contexts": ["intermediate bee structure", "bee species that saves wax"]}, {"entity_id": "melipones", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Melipones", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "INSECT", "count": 2, "variants": ["Melipones"], "contexts": ["genus of bees", "bees producing wax in Mexico"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "source_name": "Melipona", "target_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "target_name": "Melipones", "similarity": 0.894}], "id": 2530, "stable_key": "clu_67706966420e6e7e", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Melipona bees", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "family": "Apidae", "description": "Stingless bees known for producing wax and honey in various regions.", "note": "'Melipona' is a genus of stingless bees. 'Melipona domestica' is a species within this genus.", "wikipedia_extract": "Melipona is a genus of stingless bees, widespread in warm areas of the Neotropics, from Sinaloa and Tamaulipas (México) to Tucumán and Misiones (Argentina). About 70 species are known. The largest producer of honey from Melipona bees in Mexico is in the state of Yucatán where bees are studied at an interactive park called \"Bee Planet\" which is within the Cuxtal Ecological Reserve. Several species are kept for honey production, such as in Brazil, where some are well-known enough to have common names, including uruçu, mandaçaia, jandaíra, and manduri. Melipona honey has long been used by humans and now is of minor commercial importance. Research is going on in improved beekeeping techniques."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Bees", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2025, "target_cluster_name": "Bees", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Melipona bees are a genus of bees.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Melipona bees are a genus of bees."}, {"found_name": "Queen bee", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3391, "target_cluster_name": "queen-bee", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Queen bees are a specific type of bee within a colony, and Melipona bees form colonies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Queen bees are a specific type of bee within a colony, and Melipona bees form colonies."}, {"found_name": "Drone bee", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3325, "target_cluster_name": "drones", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Drone bees are a specific type of bee within a colony, and Melipona bees form colonies.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Drone bees are a specific type of bee within a colony, and Melipona bees form colonies."}, {"found_name": "Honey", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1544, "target_cluster_name": "mel", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Melipona bees are known for producing honey.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Melipona bees are known for producing honey."}]}, {"canonical_name": "eyelids", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "ANATOMY", "book_count": 2, "total_menti