lism, a movement to which Schelling belonged. Schelling's work can be seen as a development and extension of Kantian concepts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Kant's philosophy laid the groundwork for German idealism, a movement to which Schelling belonged. Schelling's work can be seen as a development and extension of Kantian concepts."}, {"found_name": "Baruch Spinoza", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4511, "target_cluster_name": "Spinola", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Schelling's philosophy, particularly his later work, engaged with and was influenced by Spinoza's pantheistic system and concept of substance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Schelling's philosophy, particularly his later work, engaged with and was influenced by Spinoza's pantheistic system and concept of substance."}]}, {"canonical_name": "carbureted hydrogen gas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 6, "members": [{"entity_id": "carbureted_hydrogen_gas", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "carbureted hydrogen gas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 4, "variants": ["carbureted hydrogen gas"], "contexts": ["gas extracted from fire-springs", "gas used for cooking and illumination"]}, {"entity_id": "hydrogen_gas", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "hydrogen gas", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 2, "variants": ["hydrogen gas"], "contexts": ["element that combines with oxygen", "gas mixed with air"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "carbureted hydrogen gas", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "hydrogen gas", "similarity": 0.916}], "id": 2601, "stable_key": "clu_43323e943beca0f0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": 