 "count": 2, "variants": ["tangential force"], "contexts": ["force acting perpendicular to radius"]}, {"entity_id": "tangential_force", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Tangential force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Tangential force", "tangential force", "Tangential Force"], "contexts": ["force acting along the orbit", "force acting along the tangent of an orbit"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "tangential force", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Tangential force", "similarity": 0.982}], "id": 2608, "stable_key": "clu_b04aa433f0940855", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Tangential force", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikidata_id": "Q91740473", "wikidata_description": "force component tangential to a curve or parallel to a (imaginary) surface"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Centrifugal force", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 315, "target_cluster_name": "Centrifugal force", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Tangential force is a component of the net force acting on an object moving in a circular path, perpendicular to the radius and in the direction of motion. Centrifugal force is often discussed in relation to circular motion, though it is a fictitious force experienced in a rotating frame of reference. Both concepts are deeply intertwined with the physics of circular motion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Tangential force is a component of the net force acting on an object moving in a circular path, perpendicular to the radius and in the direction of motion. Centrifugal force is often discussed in relation to circular motion, though it is a fictitious force experienced in a rotating frame of reference. Both concepts are deeply intertwined with the physics of circular motion.