heistic religions may apply similar rules. For instance, the phrase false god is a derogatory term used in Abrahamic religions to indicate cult images or deities of non-Abrahamic Pagan religions, as well as other competing entities or objects to which particular importance is attributed. Conversely, followers of animistic and polytheistic religions may regard the gods of various monotheistic religions as \"false gods\" because they do not believe that any real deity possesses the properties ascribed by monotheists to their sole deity."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Atheism", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 993, "target_cluster_name": "Atheism", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Atheism is the rejection of the worship of deities, which is central to idolatry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Atheism is the rejection of the worship of deities, which is central to idolatry.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Superstition", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1141, "target_cluster_name": "Superstition", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Idolatry, the worship of idols, can be considered a form of superstition, involving beliefs and practices deemed irrational by non-adherents.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Idolatry, the worship of idols, can be considered a form of superstition, involving beliefs and practices deemed irrational by non-adherents.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Divinity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2345, "target_cluster_name": "Divinity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Divinity refers to the state of being divine or a divine being, which is the object of worship, and thus related to the concept of idolatry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_labe