: 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Augustine of Hippo was a prominent figure in the early Christian church, and Augustus was the first Roman Emperor. Both are foundational figures in Western history and religion, with Augustine's theological work often engaging with the legacy of the Roman Empire established by Augustus.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Ovid", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2495, "target_cluster_name": "Ovid", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ovid lived during the reign of Augustus.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ovid lived during the reign of Augustus.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Julian", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2663, "target_cluster_name": "Julian", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Augustus was the first Roman Emperor and established the Principate, a system of governance that profoundly shaped the Roman Empire. Julian, as a later Roman Emperor, operated within and reacted to the legacy of the Augustan system.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Augustus was the first Roman Emperor and established the Principate, a system of governance that profoundly shaped the Roman Empire. Julian, as a later Roman Emperor, operated within and reacted to the legacy of the Augustan system.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Augustine of Hippo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1967, "target_cluster_name": "Austin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are prominent figures from late antiquity and early Christianity, often discussed in relation to the intellectual and religious history of the period.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are prominent figures from late antiquity and early Christianity, often discussed in relation to the intellectual and religious history of the period."}, {"found_name": "Herod", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2926, "target_cluster_name": "Herod", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Herod the Great was a client king of Rome, appointed by Julius Caesar and later confirmed by Augustus. His reign and interactions with Rome were heavily influenced by the political landscape under Augustus.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Herod the Great was a client king of Rome, appointed by Julius Caesar and later confirmed by Augustus. His reign and interactions with Rome were heavily influenced by the political landscape under Augustus.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Justinian", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2927, "target_cluster_name": "Justinian", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Augustus was the first Roman Emperor, establishing the Principate. Justinian I, ruling centuries later, sought to restore the Roman Empire to its former glory, echoing Augustus's foundational role.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Augustus was the first Roman Emperor, establishing the Principate. Justinian I, ruling centuries later, sought to restore the Roman Empire to its former glory, echoing Augustus's foundational role.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Lewis", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2944, "target_cluster_name": "Lewis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Louis IX was sometimes seen as a figure comparable to Augustus in terms of establishing a stable and prosperous reign, particularly in French historiography.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Louis IX was sometimes seen 