nsciousness with confusion and altered perception, which can sometimes overlap with or be associated with stupor.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Delirium is a state of disturbed consciousness with confusion and altered perception, which can sometimes overlap with or be associated with stupor."}, {"found_name": "Mania", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1323, "target_cluster_name": "Madness", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "While mania is characterized by excessive excitement, severe forms can lead to altered states of consciousness that might include stupor-like features or be associated with conditions that also cause stupor.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "While mania is characterized by excessive excitement, severe forms can lead to altered states of consciousness that might include stupor-like features or be associated with conditions that also cause stupor."}, {"found_name": "confusion", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2814, "target_cluster_name": "confusion", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Stupor is a state of near-unconsciousness or insensibility, which can involve profound confusion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Stupor is a state of near-unconsciousness or insensibility, which can involve profound confusion.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Meal", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "meal", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Meal", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 4, "variants": ["Meal", "Meals"], "contexts": ["ground grain, likely flour", "used with parsley leaves for eyes"]}, {"entity_id": "food", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "food", 