"clu_0acb16b74075b3b8", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cabo Verde", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Cape Verde", "wikidata_id": "Q3023340", "wikidata_description": "former colony of the Portuguese Empire in the Cape Verde Islands"}, "member_count": 4, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Africa", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3, "target_cluster_name": "Africa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cabo Verde is an island nation off the coast of West Africa.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cabo Verde is an island nation off the coast of West Africa."}, {"found_name": "Azores", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 874, "target_cluster_name": "Azores", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cabo Verde and the Azores are both Atlantic archipelagos with historical connections to Portuguese exploration and settlement.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Cabo Verde and the Azores are both Atlantic archipelagos with historical connections to Portuguese exploration and settlement."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Pondichéry", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "pondichéry", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Pondichéry", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Pondichéry", "Pondiciiéry"], "contexts": ["independent settlement", "Pondicherry"]}, {"entity_id": "pondichéry", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Pondichéry", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Pondichéry"], "contexts": ["location of cholera epidemics"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Pondichéry", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Pondichéry", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2742, "stable_key": "clu_a78d89c8f8f81b7d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Pondicherry", "confidence": "high", "type": "PLACE", "description": "A city and union territory in India, formerly a French colonial settlement.", "wikipedia_extract": "Pondicherry, officially known as Puducherry, is the capital and most populous city of the Union Territory of Puducherry in India. The city is in the Puducherry district on the southeast coast of India and is surrounded by the Bay of Bengal to the east and the state of Tamil Nadu, with which it shares most of its culture, heritage, and language. Puducherry, formerly known as Pondicherry, gained its significance as \"the French Riviera of the East\" after the advent of French colonialisation in India. Puducherry is the Tamil interpretation of \"new town\" and mainly derives from \"Poduke\", the name of the marketplace or \"port town\" for Roman trade in the 1st century, as mentioned in the Periplus of the Erythraean Sea. The settlement was once an abode of learned scholars versed in the Vedas, hence it was also known as Vedapuri. The history of Puducherry can broadly be classified into two periods: pre-colonial and colonial."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "India", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 17, "target_cluster_name": "India", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Pondicherry is a city and Union Territory within India.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Pondicherry is a city and Union Territory within India."}]}, {"canonical_name": "région équinoxiale", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "région_équinoxiale", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "région équinoxiale", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 4, "variants": ["région équinoxiale", "Régions équinoxiales"], "contexts": ["geographic zone of Chandernagor", "equatorial climate zone"]}, {"entity_id": "regions_equinoxiales", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Regions Equinoxiales", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 1, "variants": ["Regions Equinoxiales"], "contexts": ["equatorial regions"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "région équinoxiale", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Regions Equinoxiales", "similarity": 0.898}], "id": 2743, "stable_key": "clu_83d0d9cdff3e83cc", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Equatorial regions", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Global"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Equator", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 61, "target_cluster_name": "equator", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The Equator is the line of 0 degrees latitude, which defines the Equatorial regions.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The Equator is the line of 0 degrees latitude, which defines the Equatorial regions."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Moreau de Jonnès", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "moreau_de_jonnès", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Moreau de Jonnès", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Moreau de Jonnès", "Moreau de Jonnes", "Moreau de Jonnés"], "contexts": ["mentioned in passage", "author of 'Hist. phys. dct Ant.'"]}, {"entity_id": "moreau_de_jonnes", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Moreau de Jonnes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Moreau de Jonnes"], "contexts": ["author of 'Hist. Phys. des Antilles'"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Moreau de Jonnès", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Moreau de Jonnes", "similarity": 0.931}], "id": 2744, "stable_key": "clu_27a48860a32d7fa3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Alexandre Moreau de Jonnès", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1778, "death_year": 1870, "description": "French naturalist, physician, and politician; author of works on natural history.", "wikidata_id": "Q2833893", "wikidata_description": "French geologist, officer, physician and politician", "wikipedia_extract": "San Diego de los Baños is a consejo popular (\"popular council\") and urban settlement in Los Palacios, Pinar del Río Province, Cuba. The consejo popular is in the east of the Pinar del Río Province. It is located 22 km north-east of Los Palacios, in the Vuelta Abajo area. It borders the consejos populares Entronque de Palacios to the east and Paso Quemado to the south-east. Pinar del Río is 56 km (by road) to the south-west. It stands near the western end and at the foot of sierra de Rosarios, on the south side of that mountain range.", "wikipedia_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandre_Moreau_de_Jonn%C3%A8s"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "hypersthénite", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "hypersthénite", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "hypersthénite", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 4, "variants": ["hypersthénite", "hypersthène", "hypersthéne"], "contexts": ["rock type", "hypersthene mineral"]}, {"entity_id": "hypersthene", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "hypersthene", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["hypersthene"], "contexts": ["mineral component"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "hypersthénite", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "hypersthene", "similarity": 0.932}], "id": 2745, "stable_key": "clu_c89c3ab144face1b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Hypersthene", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral", "wikidata_id": "Q60706831", "wikidata_description": "scholarly article", "wikipedia_extract": "Hypersthene is a common rock-forming inosilicate mineral belonging to the group of orthorhombic pyroxenes. Its chemical formula is (Mg,Fe)SiO3. It is found in igneous and some metamorphic rocks as well as in stony and iron meteorites. Many references have formally abandoned this term, preferring to categorise this mineral as enstatite or ferrosilite. It forms a solid solution series with the minerals enstatite and ferrosilite, being a mid-way member between the two. Pure enstatite contains no iron, while pure ferrosilite contains no magnesium; hypersthene is the name given to the mineral when a significant amount of both elements are present."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "livres sterling", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "livres_sterling", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "livres sterling", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 4, "variants": ["livres sterling", "livres sterl."], "contexts": ["currency unit in English colonies", "currency unit for value"]}, {"entity_id": "pounds_sterling", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "pounds sterling", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["pounds sterling"], "contexts": ["more than one hundred pounds sterling"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "livres sterling", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "pounds sterling", "similarity": 0.932}], "id": 2746, "stable_key": "clu_eb3154519a251a74", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "pound sterling", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Drachma", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3488, "target_cluster_name": "drachma", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are historical units of currency.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are historical units of currency."}, {"found_name": "Treasury", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3408, "target_cluster_name": "trésor", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are related to the concept of wealth and finance.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are related to the concept of wealth and finance."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Gambey", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "gambey", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Gambey", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Gambey", "Gambon", "M. Gambey"], "contexts": ["instrument maker", "talented instrument maker"]}, {"entity_id": "gambey", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Gambey", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Gambey"], "contexts": ["maker of a declination instrument"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Gambey", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Gambey", "similarity": 0.715}], "id": 2747, "stable_key": "clu_0bd765455c36bf7c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Jean-Louis Gambey", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1768, "death_year": 1837, "description": "French instrument maker, known for astronomical instruments"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Laet", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 1, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "laet", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Laet", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Laet"], "contexts": ["author cited", "author cited in notes"]}], "edges": [], "id": 2748, "stable_key": "clu_8009cd14511344aa", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Johannes de Laet", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1593, "death_year": 1649, "description": "Flemish humanist, geographer, and naturalist", "note": "The citation context regarding emerald mines aligns with his geographical and natural history interests."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Amerigo Vespucci", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3017, "target_cluster_name": "Amerigo Vespucci", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Johannes de Laet was a Dutch geographer and historian who wrote extensively on the Americas, including a history of the New World. Amerigo Vespucci was an Italian explorer and cartographer whose name was given to the Americas. Laet's work would have engaged with Vespucci's explorations and legacy.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Johannes de Laet was a Dutch geographer and historian who wrote extensively on the Americas, including a history of the New World. Amerigo Vespucci was an Italian explorer and cartographer whose name was given to the Americas. Laet's work would have engaged with Vespucci's explorations and legacy."}, {"found_name": "Conrad Malte-Brun", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3010, "target_cluster_name": "Malte-Brun", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both Johannes de Laet and Conrad Malte-Brun were prominent geographers and writers on exploration and geography. Laet's work on the New World predates Malte-Brun's, but they belong to the same intellectual tradition of geographical scholarship.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both Johannes de Laet and Conrad Malte-Brun were prominent geographers and writers on exploration and geography. Laet's work on the New World predates Malte-Brun's, but they belong to the same intellectual tradition of geographical scholarship."}, {"found_name": "James Rennell", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2392, "target_cluster_name": "Rennell", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Johannes de Laet was a significant figure in early modern geography and exploration, particularly concerning the Americas. James Rennell was a highly influential geographer of the 18th and 19th centuries, known for his maps and geographical treatises. Both were key figures in the development of geographical knowledge.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Johannes de Laet was a significant figure in early modern geography and exploration, particularly concerning the Americas. James Rennell was a highly influential geographer of the 18th and 19th centuries, known for his maps and geographical treatises. Both were key figures in the development of geographical knowledge."}, {"found_name": "Peter Martyr d'Anghiera", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2195, "target_cluster_name": "Anghiera", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Johannes de Laet wrote a history of the New World, a subject also extensively covered by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera in his 'De Orbe Novo'. Both were early chroniclers of European exploration and encounters in the Americas.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Johannes de Laet wrote a history of the New World, a subject also extensively covered by Peter Martyr d'Anghiera in his 'De Orbe Novo'. Both were early chroniclers of European exploration and encounters in the Americas."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Quixos", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "quixos", "book_id": "relation_historique_hum