, is a peninsula and geographic region in Southern Greece, and the southernmost region of the Balkans. It is connected to the central part of the country by the Isthmus of Corinth land bridge, which separates the Gulf of Corinth from the Saronic Gulf. From the late Middle Ages until the 19th century, the peninsula was known as the Morea, a name still in colloquial use in its demotic form. The peninsula is divided among three administrative regions: most belong to the Peloponnese region, with smaller parts belonging to the West Greece and Attica regions. The Peloponnese is a peninsula located at the southern tip of the mainland, 21,549.6 square kilometres (8,320.3 mi2) in area, and constitutes the southernmost part of mainland Greece. It is connected to the mainland by the Isthmus of Corinth, where the Corinth Canal was constructed in 1893.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peloponnese_wall_lizard"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Greece", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 773, "target_cluster_name": "grego", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Peloponnese is a region within Greece.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Peloponnese is a region within Greece."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "webb", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 2, "variants": ["Webb"], "contexts": ["measurer of mountain heights", "measured Himalayan peaks"]}, {"entity_id": "webb", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Webb", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 3, "variants": ["Webb"], "contexts": ["made determination of Dhawalagiri elevation", "provided data on mountain elevations"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "