"subcategory": "CITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Santarem"], "contexts": ["town where case occurred", "city where a patient previously resided"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Santarem", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Santarem", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2790, "stable_key": "clu_dc350236252422eb", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Santarém", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "City in Portugal on the Amazon River.", "wikipedia_extract": "Santarém (European Portuguese pronunciation: [sɐ̃tɐˈɾɐ̃j] ) is a Portuguese city and municipality located in the district of Santarém. The population of the historic Ribatejo capital  in 2021 was 58,671, in an area of 552.54 km2. The population of the city proper was 29,929 in 2012. The mayor is Ricardo Gonçalves (PSD). The municipal holiday is March 19, the day of Saint Joseph (São José). The city is on the Portuguese Way variant of the Way of Saint James."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Fichtelgebirge", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "fichtelgebirge", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Fichtelgebirge", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Fichtelgebirge"], "contexts": ["mountain range in Franconia"]}, {"entity_id": "fichtelgebirge", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Fichtelgebirge", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "REGION", "count": 4, "variants": ["Fichtelgebirge"], "contexts": ["mountain range location", "mountain range"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Fichtelgebirge", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "Fichtelgebirge", "similarity": 0.756}], "id": 2791, "stable_key": "clu_3991d31dacba541b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Fichtel Mountains", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Germany", "wikidata_id": "Q572747", "wikidata_description": "hiking and voluntary association in Germany", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fichtelgebirge%20Club", "wikipedia_extract": "The Fichtelgebirge Club (German: Fichtelgebirgsverein or FGV) is a large walking club and local heritage society in Bavaria and recognised conservation group with 20,000 members in 55 local groups. As the name says, its main sphere of activity is in the Fichtel Mountains in north Bavaria. Its emblem is the Arctic starflower (the Siebenstern). The aims of the club are the fostering of hiking, training of hiking guides, marking of footpaths, construction and maintenance of rock climbing facilities, observation towers and accommodation facilities, conservation work and support, landscape conservation, support of local culture, monument protection, running the Fichtelgebirge Museum and other local history and natural history collections, publication of the club magazine Der Siebenstern and other heritage publications, youth work and youth support. In 1878 the Fichtel Mountains Section (Sektion Fichtelgebirg) of the German and Austrian Alpine Club was founded in Wunsiedel. From the outset it focussed only on the development of the Fichtel Mountains."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Laugier", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "laugier", "book_id": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "name": "Laugier", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Laugier"], "contexts": ["author in Annales de Chimie"]}, {"entity_id": "laugier", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Laugier", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 4, "variants": ["Laugier"], "contexts": ["made calculations on comet returns", "calculated comet returns"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "relation_historique_humboldt_vol3_1825", "source_name": "Laugier", "tar