 "evidence_snippet": "Both were central figures in German Idealism and intellectual discourse. Hegel's philosophy engaged with and built upon the ideas of earlier thinkers, and his work is often discussed in relation to the broader intellectual climate shaped by figures like Schiller.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both were central figures in German Idealism and intellectual discourse. Hegel's philosophy engaged with and built upon the ideas of earlier thinkers, and his work is often discussed in relation to the broader intellectual climate shaped by figures like Schiller."}, {"found_name": "Immanuel Kant", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 643, "target_cluster_name": "Kant", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Kant's philosophy was foundational to German Idealism, a movement with which Schiller was deeply engaged. Schiller's aesthetic and ethical theories often responded to or developed Kantian concepts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Kant's philosophy was foundational to German Idealism, a movement with which Schiller was deeply engaged. Schiller's aesthetic and ethical theories often responded to or developed Kantian concepts."}]}, {"canonical_name": "experiences", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "experiences", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "experiences", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["experiences"], "contexts": ["events or sensations undergone", "events and sensations that fill time"]}, {"entity_id": "experiences", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "experiences", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["experiences"], "contexts": ["events that shape understanding", "events or observations that info