shape deviates from being a perfect circle or sphere, and an ellipsoid of revolution is a specific geometric form that exhibits ellipticity."}, {"found_name": "Elliptical orbit", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2341, "target_cluster_name": "elliptical orbit", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "An elliptical orbit is a specific type of orbit that follows an elliptical path. Ellipticity is a parameter used to describe the shape of an ellipse, and thus is directly related to the description of an elliptical orbit.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "An elliptical orbit is a specific type of orbit that follows an elliptical path. Ellipticity is a parameter used to describe the shape of an ellipse, and thus is directly related to the description of an elliptical orbit."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Amboyna", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "amboyna", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Amboyna", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Amboyna"], "contexts": ["location of experiments"]}, {"entity_id": "amboyna", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Amboyna", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "CITY", "count": 4, "variants": ["Amboyna"], "contexts": ["place where Rumphius wrote", "island in Indonesia"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Amboyna", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Amboyna", "similarity": 0.849}], "id": 2848, "stable_key": "clu_86d2fc3b08f1d680", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ambon", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Indonesia", "note": "Amboyna is the historical name for the island and city of Ambon.", "wikidata_id": "Q18970", "wikidata_description": "city in Maluku Province, Indonesia", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ambon%2C_Maluku", "wikipedia_extract": "Ambon (Indonesian pronunciation: [ˈambɔn]; formerly Dutch: Amboina) is the capital and largest city of the Indonesian province of Maluku. This city is also known as Ambon Manise, which means \"beautiful\" or \"pretty\" Ambon in the Ambonese language. It covers a land area of 359.45 square kilometres (138.78 sq mi), and had a population of 331,254 at the 2010 Census and 347,288 at the 2020 Census; the official estimate as of mid 2024 was 357,289. The city is divided into five administrative districts (kecamatan) – namely Nusaniwe, Sirimau, Teluk Ambon (Ambon Bay), Baguala (officially Teluk Ambon Baguala) and Leitimur Selatan (South Leitimur). Known as Indonesia's music city, Ambon became the first city in Southeast Asia to be recognised as the UNESCO City of Music in 2019. The city is populated by a mix of ethnic Alifuru (original Moluccans), Javanese, Balinese, Butonese, Bugis, Makassar, Papuan, Minahasa, Minang, Flobamora (Flores, Sumba, Alor and Timor ethnics) and those of foreign descent (Chinese, Arabian-Ambonese, Spanish-Ambonese, German-Ambonese, Portuguese-Ambonese and Dutch-Ambonese)."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "electric force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 5, "members": [{"entity_id": "electric_force", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "electric force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["electric force"], "contexts": ["force exerted by electric charge"]}, {"entity_id": "electric_force", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "electric force", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["electric force", "Electric Force"], "contexts": ["force exerted by electric charges", "force associated with electric charge"]}, {"entity_id": "electric_forces", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "electric forces", "category": "CON