es. In historical contexts, the understanding of chemical forces was often intertwined with or seen as a manifestation of electrical interactions between particles.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Both 'Chemical force' and 'Electric force' are fundamental forces. In historical contexts, the understanding of chemical forces was often intertwined with or seen as a manifestation of electrical interactions between particles.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Attraction (physics)", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4186, "target_cluster_name": "attractions", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Electric force is a fundamental type of attraction (and repulsion), and historical discussions of attraction in physics would frequently encompass electrical phenomena.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Electric force is a fundamental type of attraction (and repulsion), and historical discussions of attraction in physics would frequently encompass electrical phenomena."}, {"found_name": "Electrical phenomena", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3624, "target_cluster_name": "electrical phenomena", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Electric force is the underlying cause of many electrical phenomena, and texts discussing the latter would inherently be related to the former.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Electric force is the underlying cause of many electrical phenomena, and texts discussing the latter would inherently be related to the former."}, {"found_name": "Atmospheric electricity", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3166, "target_cluster_name": "atmospheric electricity", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Atmospheric electricity is a specific domain where elec