tch, or Brimstone, to purifie the air from his ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "St. Johns Wort", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "evidence_snippet": "which set together do signifie nothing, not only in the dictionary of man, but the subtiler vocabulary of Satan. That there is any power in _Bitumen_, Pitch, or Brimstone, to purifie the air from his ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym of Hipericon"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Manes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "manes", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Manes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 3, "variants": ["Manes"], "contexts": ["founder of Manichaeism", "body was phantastical"]}, {"entity_id": "menezes", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Menezes", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["Menezes"], "contexts": ["uncle of Senhor de Aguas Bellas"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Manes", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Menezes", "similarity": 0.851}], "id": 2905, "stable_key": "clu_01623d3f02e34694", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Manes", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 216, "death_year": 274, "description": "Founder of Manichaeism, ancient religious figure", "note": "The mention of 'Menezes' in 'polyanthea_medicinal' is likely a distinct individual, but 'Manes' as the founder of Manichaeism is the primary referent given the context of pseudodoxia epidemica."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Moses", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 673, "target_cluster_name": "Musa", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Both are significant figures in Abrahamic religions, often depicted as lawgivers and prophets.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Both are significant figures in Abrahamic religions, often depicted as lawgivers and prophets."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Charms", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "charms", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Charms", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 3, "variants": ["Charms"], "contexts": ["danger and delusion in cures", "superstitious cures"]}, {"entity_id": "charms", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "charms", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["charms"], "contexts": ["objects believed to have magical power"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Charms", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "charms", "similarity": 0.903}], "id": 2906, "stable_key": "clu_ea577a02f42abbd2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Charm", "confidence": "high", "type": "object", "note": "Refers to amulets or objects believed to possess magical properties, often used for protection or healing.", "wikipedia_extract": "Charm++ is a parallel object-oriented programming paradigm based on C++ and developed in the Parallel Programming Laboratory at the University of Illinois at Urbana–Champaign. Charm++ is designed with the goal of enhancing programmer productivity by providing a high-level abstraction of a parallel program while at the same time delivering good performance on a wide variety of underlying hardware platforms. Programs written in Charm++ are decomposed into a number of cooperating message-driven objects called chares. When a programmer invokes a method on an object, the Charm++ runtime system sends a message to the invoked object, which may reside on the local processor or on a remote processor in a parallel computation. This message triggers the execution of code within the chare to handle the message asynchronously. Chares may be organized into indexed collections called chare arrays and messages may be sent to individual chares within a chare array or to the entire chare array simultaneously.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charm++"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Flint", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "flint", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Flint", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Flint"], "contexts": ["stone that strikes fire with steel", "vulgar stone with no attractive power"]}, {"entity_id": "flint", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Flint", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["Flint"], "contexts": ["implement material found in geologic deposits"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Flint", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "Flint", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 2907, "stable_key": "clu_53689a65883a1a5d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Flint", "confidence": "high", "type": "mineral"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "stone", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 132, "target_cluster_name": "stone", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Flint is a hard, sedimentary cryptocrystalline form of the mineral quartz, a type of stone known for its use in tools.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Flint is a hard, sedimentary cryptocrystalline form of the mineral quartz, a type of stone known for its use in tools.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "quartz", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 323, "target_cluster_name": "quartz", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Flint is a microcrystalline or cryptocrystalline sedimentary rock form of quartz, often found in nodules within chalk or limestone.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Flint is a microcrystalline or cryptocrystalline sedimentary rock form of quartz, often found in nodules within chalk or limestone.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Urine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "urine", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Urine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Urine"], "contexts": ["bodily fluid", "source of volatile salt and Aqua vitæ"]}, {"entity_id": "urine", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "urine", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_SUBSTANCE", "count": 1, "variants": ["urine"], "contexts": ["fluid secreted by kidneys"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Urine", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "urine", "similarity": 0.974}], "id": 2908, "stable_key": "clu_625b9c30c980a1a0-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Urine", "confidence": "high", "type": "substance", "description": "A bodily fluid produced by the kidneys and excreted from the body.", "note": "Refers to the bodily fluid itself and the passages through which it travels.", "wikipedia_extract": "Urine, excreted by the kidneys, is a liquid containing excess water and water-soluble nitrogen-rich by-products of metabolism including urea, uric acid, and creatinine, which must be cleared from the bloodstream. Urinalysis detects these nitrogenous wastes in mammals. In placental mammals, urine travels from the kidneys via the ureters to the bladder and exits the urethra through the penis or vulva during urination. Other vertebrates excrete urine through the cloaca. Urine plays an important role in the earth's nitrogen cycle. In balanced ecosystems, urine fertilizes the soil and thus helps plants to grow."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Kidney", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3844, "target_cluster_name": "Kidney", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Urine is produced by the kidneys.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Urine is produced by the kidneys."}, {"found_name": "Bladder", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 543, "target_cluster_name": "bexiga", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Urine is stored in the bladder before excretion.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Urine is stored in the bladder before excretion."}, {"found_name": "Fluids", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 393, "target_cluster_name": "fluids", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Urine is a type of fluid.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Urine is a type of fluid."}, {"found_name": "Liquid", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 946, "target_cluster_name": "liquori", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Urine is a liquid.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Urine is a liquid."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Iris", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "iris", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Iris", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["Iris"], "context