 (politics/monarchy for Louis IX, philosophy/science for Bacon) and their works or legacies were discussed in relation to broader historical and intellectual trends.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "While from different eras, both were influential figures in their respective fields (politics/monarchy for Louis IX, philosophy/science for Bacon) and their works or legacies were discussed in relation to broader historical and intellectual trends."}, {"found_name": "Jesus Christ", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 13, "target_cluster_name": "Christ", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Louis IX was canonized as a saint, and his life and reign were often interpreted through a lens of Christian piety and divine favor, drawing parallels to Christ's teachings and example.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Louis IX was canonized as a saint, and his life and reign were often interpreted through a lens of Christian piety and divine favor, drawing parallels to Christ's teachings and example."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Turkey", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "BIRD", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "turkeys", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Turkeys", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "BIRD", "count": 1, "variants": ["Turkeys"], "contexts": ["large domesticated fowl"]}, {"entity_id": "turkey", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "Turkey", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "BIRD", "count": 2, "variants": ["Turkey", "turkey"], "contexts": ["bird whose digestive organs pass fruit seeds", "naked skin on head"]}, {"entity_id": "turkeys", "book_id": "origin_of_species_darwin_1859", "name": "turkeys", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "BIRD", "count": 1, "variants": ["turkeys"], "contexts": ["large domesticated fowl"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epid