the body"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "bodily parts", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "body parts", "similarity": 0.982}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "bodily parts", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "partesdocorpo", "similarity": 0.961}, {"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "bodily parts", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "partes do corpo", "similarity": 0.971}], "id": 3109, "stable_key": "clu_d6fc48c8f15b7709-3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Body", "confidence": "high", "type": "anatomy", "description": "The physical structure of a person or animal.", "wikipedia_extract": "The human body is the entire structure of a human being. It is composed of many different types of cells that together create tissues and subsequently organs and then organ systems. The external human body consists of a head, hair, neck, torso (which includes the thorax and abdomen), genitals, arms, hands, legs, and feet. The internal human body includes organs, teeth, bones, muscle, tendons, ligaments, blood vessels and blood, lymphatic vessels and lymph. The study of the human body includes anatomy, physiology, histology and embryology. The body varies anatomically in known ways."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "corpo humano", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 2645, "target_cluster_name": "corpo humano", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Direct translation of 'Human Body' to Portuguese, which is a synonym for 'Body' in this context.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "Direct translation of 'Human Body' to Portuguese, which is a synonym for 'Body' in this context."}, {"found_name": "Internal organs", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1428, "target_cluster_name": "internal organ", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Internal organs are parts of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Internal organs are parts of the body."}, {"found_name": "Organs", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 141, "target_cluster_name": "organs", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Organs are components of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Organs are components of the body."}, {"found_name": "Skin", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 600, "target_cluster_name": "skin", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Skin is the outer covering of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Skin is the outer covering of the body."}, {"found_name": "Anatomy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2892, "target_cluster_name": "Anatomia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anatomy is the study of the structure of the body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Anatomy is the study of the structure of the body."}, {"found_name": "Human Anatomy", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 3628, "target_cluster_name": "humani corporis", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Human Anatomy is the study of the structure of the human body.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Human Anatomy is the study of the structure of the human body."}]}, {"canonical_name": "Babel", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "babylon", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "Babylon", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Babylon"], "contexts": ["biblical city, symbol of power"]}, {"entity_id": "babel", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Babel", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["Babel"], "contexts": ["original name for Babylon", "biblical city"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "Babylon", "target_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "target_name": "Babel", "similarity": 0.881}], "id": 3110, "stable_key": "clu_5f7750a5886103b9-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Babylon", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "An ancient Mesopotamian city, historically significant.", "note": "'Babilónia' is the Portuguese spelling for Babylon.", "wikipedia_extract": "Babylon ( BAB-il-on) was an ancient city located on the lower Euphrates river in southern Mesopotamia, within modern-day Hillah, Iraq, about 85 kilometres (53 miles) south of modern-day Baghdad. Babylon functioned as the main cultural and political centre of the Akkadian-speaking region of Babylonia. Its rulers established two important empires in antiquity, the 19th–16th century BC Old Babylonian Empire, and the 7th–6th century BC Neo-Babylonian Empire. Babylon was also used as a regional capital of other empires, such as the Achaemenid Empire. Babylon was one of the most important urban centres of the ancient Near East, until its decline during the Hellenistic period. Nearby ancient sites are Kish, Borsippa, Dilbat, and Kutha."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Babylonia", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2628, "target_cluster_name": "Babylonia", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Babylonia was the Akkadian-speaking region of which Babylon was the main political and cultural center.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "Babylonia was the Akkadian-speaking region of which Babylon was the main political and cultural center."}]}, {"canonical_name": "heaven", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "heaven", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "heaven", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["heaven"], "contexts": ["alleged temporary dwelling of Lurancy's spirit"]}, {"entity_id": "heaven", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "heaven", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 3, "variants": ["heaven"], "contexts": ["starry vault of heaven", "celestial sphere"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "source_name": "heaven", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "heaven", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3111, "stable_key": "clu_ecad5e945f7e70e3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "sky", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "note": "In this context, 'heaven' refers to the celestial sphere or the sky, not the religious afterlife."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "attributes", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "attributes", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "attributes", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["attributes"], "contexts": ["qualities composing a concept"]}, {"entity_id": "attribute", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "attribute", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["attribute"], "contexts": ["characteristic of a thing"]}, {"entity_id": "attributes", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "attributes", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["attributes"], "contexts": ["qualities or characteristics"]}, {"entity_id": "attribute", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "a