 up of 4 historic subdivisions; Virginia Place, East Kensington, Park Place, and East Old Dominion Place. The Park Place Historic District is a national historic district listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 2005 and enlarged in 2017. It encompasses 1,525 contributing buildings, 2 contributing sites, and 5 contributing structures in the Park Place neighborhood of Norfolk. It is an example of streetcar suburban development in Norfolk during the late 19th and early 20th centuries.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Park_Place_Historic_District_(Norfolk,_Virginia)"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Cygnus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "cygnus", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "Cygnus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Cygnus"], "contexts": ["constellation with a star", "constellation where new star appeared"]}, {"entity_id": "cygnus", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Cygnus", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Cygnus"], "contexts": ["constellation in northern sky", "constellation containing part of Milky Way"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "source_name": "Cygnus", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Cygnus", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3133, "stable_key": "clu_929be6abe876674b", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Cygnus", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "wikipedia_extract": "Swans are birds of the genus Cygnus within the family Anatidae. The swans' closest relatives include geese and ducks. Swans are grouped with the closely related geese in the subfamily Anserinae, forming the tribe Cygnini. Sometimes, they are considered a distinct subfamily, Cygninae. They are the largest waterfowl and are often among the largest flighted birds in their range. There are six living and many extinct species of swan; in addition, there is a species known as the coscoroba swan, which is no longer considered one of the true swans.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swan"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "celestial", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 4317, "target_cluster_name": "celestial", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cygnus is a constellation, a grouping of celestial objects.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cygnus is a constellation, a grouping of celestial objects.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Coma Berenices", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2454, "target_cluster_name": "Coma Berenices", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Coma Berenices is a constellation, and Cygnus is another constellation, both part of the celestial sphere discussed in astronomical texts.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Coma Berenices is a constellation, and Cygnus is another constellation, both part of the celestial sphere discussed in astronomical texts.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "intellectual progress", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "intellectual_progress", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "intellectual progress", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 2, "variants": ["intellectual progress"], "contexts": ["advancement in knowledge and understanding", "advancement of human intellect"]}, {"entity_id": "intellectual_progress", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "Intellectual Progress", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Intellectual Progress"], "contexts": ["growth of classifications and