is a mineral form of mercuric sulfide (HgS), and mercury (quicksilver) was historically often associated with copper in alchemical and metallurgical discussions.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "chumbo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1692, "target_cluster_name": "chumbo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Cinnabar is a mineral form of mercury sulfide, and both mercury and lead were key substances in alchemy and early chemistry.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Cinnabar is a mineral form of mercury sulfide, and both mercury and lead were key substances in alchemy and early chemistry.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "pólvora", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "pólvora", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "pólvora", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["pólvora"], "contexts": ["gunpowder", "explosive substance used in warfare"]}, {"entity_id": "polvora", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "polvora", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "MINERAL", "count": 2, "variants": ["polvora"], "contexts": ["powdered substance", "explosive substance"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "pólvora", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "polvora", "similarity": 0.777}], "id": 3195, "stable_key": "clu_b3cc1648577c715f", "ground_truth": {"wikipedia_extract": "Pólvora (born July 19, 1979) is the ring name of a Mexican Luchador Enmascarado, or masked professional wrestler best known for his work in the Mexican professional wrestling promotion Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL). Pólvora's real name is not a matter of public record, as is often the case with masked wrestlers in Mexico where their private lives are kept a secret from the wrestling fans. His name is the Spanish term for Gunpowder. Pólvora's brother is also a professional wrestler, under the ring name Inquisidor. Pólvora made his professional wrestling debut in 2000, mainly teaming with his brother Vaquero on the Mexican independent circuit By 2005 both Pólvora and Vaquero began working for Consejo Mundial de Lucha Libre (CMLL), mainly on the promotions minor shows or in the opening match of their big shows from Arena México. On June 22, 2008 Pólvora and Vaquero participated in a tournament for the vacant CMLL Arena Coliseo Tag Team Championship, but lost in the opening round to Mictlán and Fabian el Gitano."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "reino", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "reino", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "reino", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["reino", "Reino"], "contexts": ["kingdom whose ships were loaded", "destination for drugs"]}, {"entity_id": "regno", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Regno", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 2, "variants": ["Regno"], "contexts": ["the Kingdom", "origin of yellow earth"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "reino", "target_book": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "target_name": "Regno", "similarity": 0.939}], "id": 3196, "stable_key": "clu_b60ed571f57d7094", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "kingdom", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "description": "A territory ruled by a king or queen.", "note": "Includes references to specific kingdoms and generic 'kingdom' as a political entity.", "wikipedia_extract": "The United Kingdom is a country located off the north-western coast of continental Europe. It comprises England, Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland. With a total area of approximately 244,376 square kilometres (94,354 sq mi), the UK occupies the major part of the British Isles archipelago and includes the island of Great Britain, the north-eastern one-sixth of the island of Ireland and many smaller surrounding islands. It is the world's 7th largest island country. The mainland areas lie between latitudes 49°N and 59°N (the Shetland Islands reach to nearly 61°N), and longitudes 8°W to 2°E. The Royal Observatory, Greenwich, in south-east London, is the defining point of the Prime Meridian."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "paese", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 10, "target_cluster_name": "country", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "completamente ignoradas de Car- da da Orta e de Tavernier. Duarte Barbosa tem, porém, a este respeito uma indicaçio muito notável: «as esmeraldas nascem no Reino (paese) de Babilónia, aonde os indios ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for Reino"}, {"found_name": "Judeus", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 356, "target_cluster_name": "Judeus", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamados coaris, e no reino de Cambaiete lhe chamam esparcis, e nós os ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym used by Portuguese for a group of people"}, {"found_name": "Zhnmey", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e Jangamá de Barros — era uma província ou estado da terra ou reino dos Laos, chamada pelos burmeses Zhnméy e pelos siameses Kiang-mai ou Xiang-mai. O reino dos Laos dos nossos escriptores qui- nhenti", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name"}, {"found_name": "Kiang-mai", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e Jangamá de Barros — era uma província ou estado da terra ou reino dos Laos, chamada pelos burmeses Zhnméy e pelos siameses Kiang-mai ou Xiang-mai. O reino dos Laos dos nossos escriptores qui- nhenti", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name"}, {"found_name": "Xiang-mai", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e Jangamá de Barros — era uma província ou estado da terra ou reino dos Laos, chamada pelos burmeses Zhnméy e pelos siameses Kiang-mai ou Xiang-mai. O reino dos Laos dos nossos escriptores qui- nhenti", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name"}, {"found_name": "Chiamay", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "de Yun-nan, e o norte de Sião, desde Kiang-mai na bacia do Me-nam até Luang-prabang na do Me-kong. Barros define correctamente o que chama Chiamay no reino dos Laos, quando diz : o primeiro estado dos", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "alternative name"}, {"found_name": "guzaratas", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "varanda, e parecem cousa pequena. SERVO Loguo virei com recado. ORTA Nascem as mangas no tempo que eu dixe, e as de Ormuz sam as mais gabadas; e as do reino do Guzarate também sam muyto boas, em espec", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym"}, {"found_name": "esparcis", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamados coaris, e no reino de Cambaiete lhe chamam esparcis, e nós os ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "synonym for coaris in Cambaiete"}, {"found_name": "coaris", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "e ruas; estes sam chamados deres ou /arames, e servem também estes de algozes. Ha outros mercadores de buticas, que por nome sam chamados coaris, e no reino de Cambaiete lhe chamam esparcis, e nós os ", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "subtype_relation", "found_relationship": "type of merchant"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Dom Fernando", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PATRON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "dom_fernando", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "Dom Fernando", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PATRON", "count": 2, "variants": ["Dom Fernando"], "contexts": ["king of Naples", "nickname for King Ferdinand II"]}, {"entity_id": "dom_fernando", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Dom Fernando", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "PATRON", "count": 2, "variants": ["Dom Fernando", "Fernando"], "contexts": ["Regedor mentioned in an anecdote", "Cardinal, brother of Cosme de Medicis"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "Dom Fernando", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Dom Fernando", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3197, "stable_key": "clu_fd041cd2b8b04193", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ferdinand I, Holy Roman Emperor", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1503, "death_year": 1564, "description": "King of Bohemia and Hungary, later Holy Roman Emperor.", "note": "The text refers to 'Dom Fernando' as King of Naples, which historically could refer to several rulers. Given the 16th-century context (coloquios_da_orta_1563), Ferdinand I of Habsburg (who was King of Hungary) is the most likely figure, especially as the anecdote involves a 'Regedor'.", "wikidata_id": "Q150611", "wikidata_description": "Holy Roman Emperor of the Habsburg dynasty and king of Bohemia, Croatia and Hungary (1503–1564)"}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Ferdinand", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 445, "target_cluster_name": "Ferdinand", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ferdinand I was the paternal uncle of Ferdinand II and was Holy Roman Emperor before him. They are related through dynastic succession and family ties within the Habsburg dynasty.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ferdinand I was the paternal uncle of Ferdinand II and was Holy Roman Emperor before him. They are related through dynastic succession and family ties within the Habsburg dynasty.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "Emperadores", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2523, "target_cluster_name": "Emperadores", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Ferdinand I was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Ferdinand I was a Holy Roman Emperor, a specific historical instance of the entity.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "claradeovo", "category": "SUBSTANCE", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "clara_de_ovo", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "clara de ovo", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["clara de ovo"], "contexts": ["mixed with falcon plaster ingredients"]}, {"entity_id": "claradeovo", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "claradeovo", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["claradeovo", "clara deovo freſca"], "contexts": ["egg white", "fresh egg white, animal product"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "clara de ovo", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "claradeovo", "similarity": 0.81}], "id": 3198, "stable_key": "clu_575ab3aea731bbfa-3", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "egg", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "description": "Reproductive body laid by female birds, reptiles, amphibians, fish, and insects.", "note": "The context for 'ovelhas' (sheep) is anomalous; it appears to refer to animals that eat a plant, not the egg itself.", "wikipedia_extract": "An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has become an animal fetus that can survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\". Most arthropods, vertebrates (excluding live-bearing mammals), and mollusks lay eggs, although some, such as scorpions, do not. Reptile eggs, bird eggs, and monotreme eggs are laid out of water and are surrounded by a protective shell, either flexible or inflexible. Eggs laid on land or in nests are usually kept within a warm and favorable temperature range while the embryo grows."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "gemas de ovos", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1537, "target_cluster_name": "gemas de ovos", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The historical name 'gemas de ovos' is a direct Portuguese translation of 'egg yolks', referring to a component of the egg.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "The historical name 'gemas de ovos' is a direct Portuguese translation of 'egg yolks', referring to a component of the egg."}, {"found_name": "ovo", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 558, "target_cluster_name": "ovo", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The entity 'egg' is directly related to 'ovo', which is the Portuguese word for egg, indicating a linguistic variation within the same concept.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "The entity 'egg' is directly related to 'ovo', which is the Portuguese word for egg, indicating a linguistic variation within the same concept."}]}, {"canonical_name": "boy", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "boy", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "boy", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 1, "variants": ["boy"], "contexts": ["blood of a boy mixed in medicine"]}, {"entity_id": "boy", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "boy", "category": "ANIMAL", "subcategory": "OTHER_ANIMAL", "count": 3, "variants": ["boy"], "contexts": ["source of gall bladder stone", "animal product used for water"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "boy", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "boy", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3199, "stable_key": "clu_06a28e4f85333d77", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Ox", "confidence": "high", "type": "animal", "linnaean": "Bos taurus", "family": "Bovidae", "description": "Animal whose gall bladder stone and blood were used in medicine.", "note": "'Boy' in this context refers to an ox or bull, not a human child, especially when referring to 'fel de boy' (ox gall) or animal products.", "wikipedia_extract": "Cattle (Bos taurus) are large, domesticated, bovid ungulates widely kept as livestock. They are prominent modern members of the subfamily Bovinae and the most widespread species of the genus Bos. Mature female cattle are called cows and mature males are called bulls. Taurine cattle are widely distributed across Europe and temperate areas of Asia, the Americas, and Australia. Zebus are found mainly in India and tropical areas of Asia, America, and Australia. Sanga cattle are found primarily in sub-Saharan Africa."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "cheyroſo", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "cheirosa", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "cheirosa", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "QUALITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["cheirosa"], "contexts": ["quality of a substance"]}, {"entity_id": "cheyroſo", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "cheyroſo", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 3, "variants": ["cheyroſo", "cheyros"], "contexts": ["fragrant", "smell of roses"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "cheirosa", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "cheyroſo", "similarity": 0.959}], "id": 3200, "stable_key": "clu_234cfcb0b720d86f-2", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Scent", "confidence": "high", "type": "concept", "description": "A distinctive smell, especially a pleasant one.", "note": "Refers to smell or odor, and adjectives describing it, used to assess quality or describe something.", "wikipedia_extract": "An odor (American English) or odour (Commonwealth English; see spelling differences) is a smell or a scent caused by one or more volatilized chemical compounds generally found in low concentrations that humans and many animals can perceive via their olfactory system. While smell can refer to pleasant and unpleasant odors, the terms scent, aroma, and fragrance are usually reserved for pleasant-smelling odors and are frequently used in the food and cosmetic industry to describe floral scents or to refer to perfumes. The perception of odors, or sense of smell, is mediated by the olfactory nerve. The olfactory receptor (OR) cells are neurons present in the olfactory epithelium, which is a small patch of tissue at the back of the nasal cavity. There are millions of olfactory receptor neurons that act as sensory signaling cells. Each neuron has cilia in direct contact with the air."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "galanga", "link_type": "same_referent", "link_strength": 1.0, "target_cluster_id": 270, "target_cluster_name": "Galbano", "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "corrutamente escreve, nam lhe deis fé; porque todos os Arábios lhe chamão asi. E esta que chamamos galanga he de duas maneiras, scilicet, huma pequena, muyto cheirosa, trazida da China a estas terras,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "true_synonym", "found_relationship": "known as"}, {"found_name": "lavandou", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": null, "target_cluster_name": null, "source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "evidence_snippet": "corrutamente escreve, nam lhe deis fé; porque todos os Arábios lhe chamão asi. E esta que chamamos galanga he de duas maneiras, scilicet, huma pequena, muyto cheirosa, trazida da China a estas terras,", "confidence": 0.65, "auto_label": "cross_linguistic", "found_relationship": "called in China"}]}, {"canonical_name": "Rocha", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 4, "members": [{"entity_id": "roch_há", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "roch há", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 1, "variants": ["roch há"], "contexts": ["chess piece, tiger"]}, {"entity_id": "rocha", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Rocha", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "OTHER_PERSON", "count": 3, "variants": ["Rocha"], "contexts": ["approver", "signer of official documents"]}], "e