xts, often discussed in relation to its magnetic properties, which are particularly pronounced in soft iron.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Cæsar", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "cæsar", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Cæsar", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cæsar"], "contexts": ["described Britain"]}, {"entity_id": "cæsar", "book_id": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "name": "Cæsar", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "AUTHORITY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Cæsar"], "contexts": ["Julius, era computed from his reign"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Cæsar", "target_book": "connexion_physical_sciences_somerville_1858", "target_name": "Cæsar", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3835, "stable_key": "clu_9bfb8151aa8cc858", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Julius Caesar", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": -100, "death_year": -44, "description": "Roman general and statesman, first emperor of Rome."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Julian", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2663, "target_cluster_name": "Julian", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Julius Caesar was a pivotal figure in the transition from the Roman Republic to the Roman Empire. Julian, as a later Roman Emperor, would have been aware of and potentially influenced by Caesar's actions and the historical narrative surrounding him.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Julius Caesar was a pivotal figure in the transition from the Roman Republic to the Roman Empire. Julian, as a later Roman Emperor, would have been aware of and potentially influenced by Caesar's actions and the historical narrative surrounding him.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Saxo