"subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Petrus Joannes Faber"], "contexts": ["author of 'Univerſalis Sapientia'"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Johannes Faber", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Petrus Joannes Faber", "similarity": 0.85}], "id": 3863, "stable_key": "clu_ab0f2fbb0022b1b0", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Joannes Faber", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1574, "death_year": 1629, "description": "Physician and botanist, known for botanical illustrations.", "wikidata_id": "Q41569344", "wikidata_description": "French jurist-consult (m. 1340?)"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Liverwort", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "HERB", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "liverwort", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Liverwort", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "HERB", "count": 1, "variants": ["Liverwort"], "contexts": ["plant with trifoliate leaves"]}, {"entity_id": "liverwort", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Liverwort", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLANT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Liverwort"], "contexts": ["plant growing in moist places"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Liverwort", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Liverwort", "similarity": 0.795}], "id": 3864, "stable_key": "clu_5a53fa928f7160bd", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "liverwort", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Marchantiopsida", "family": "Marchantiaceae", "note": "The early modern term 'liverwort' encompasses various plants now classified under different orders and families within the division Bryophyta. Marchantiopsida is a broad class that includes the most common forms referred to by this name historically. The specific family is harder to pinpoint without more context, but Marchantiaceae is a representative example.", "wikidata_id": "Q161050", "wikidata_description": "species of plant", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anemone%20hepatica", "wikipedia_extract": "Marchantiopsida is a class of liverworts within the phylum Marchantiophyta. The species in this class are known as complex thalloid liverworts. The species in this class are widely distributed and can be found worldwide. Complex oil bodies are only found in the gametophyte. Marchantiidae Engl. 1893 sensu He-Nygrén et al. 2006 Marchantiales Limpr. 1877 (complex thalloids) Aytoniaceae Cavers 1911  [Rebouliaceae; Grimaldiaceae] Conocephalaceae Müll.Frib. ex Grolle 1972 Cyathodiaceae Stotler & Crand.-Stotl. 2000 Exormothecaceae Müll.Frib."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "sore Throats", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "sore_throats", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "sore Throats", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "ACUTE", "count": 1, "variants": ["sore Throats"], "contexts": ["condition treated by Jews ear"]}, {"entity_id": "sore_throat", "book_id": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "name": "sore throat", "category": "DISEASE", "subcategory": "SYMPTOM", "count": 1, "variants": ["sore throat"], "contexts": ["pain or irritation in the throat"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "sore Throats", "target_book": "first_principles_spencer_1862", "target_name": "sore throat", "similarity": 0.886}], "id": 3865, "stable_key": "clu_f5a536ade3bcda9d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "sore throat", "confidence": "high", "type": "disease", "modern_term": "pharyngitis", "wikidata_id": "Q1292082", "wikidata_description": "Pain of the throat", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sore_throat", "wikipedia_extract": "Tonsillectomy is a surgical procedure in which both palatine tonsils are fully removed from the back of the throat. The procedure is mainly performed for recurrent tonsillitis, throat infections and obstructive sleep apnea (OSA). For those with frequent throat infections, surgery results in 0.6 (95% confidence interval: 1.0 to 0.1) fewer sore throats in the following year, but there is no evidence of long term benefits. In children with OSA, it results in improved quality of life. While generally safe, complications may include bleeding, vomiting, dehydration, trouble eating, and trouble talking. Throat pain typically lasts about one to two weeks after surgery."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Hollerius", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "hollerius", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Hollerius", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Hollerius"], "contexts": ["scholar who advanced a theory"]}, {"entity_id": "hollerius", "book_id": "english_physician_1652", "name": "Hollerius", "category": "PERSON", "subcategory": "SCHOLAR", "count": 1, "variants": ["Hollerius"], "contexts": ["French physician on scorpion in brain"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Hollerius", "target_book": "english_physician_1652", "target_name": "Hollerius", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3866, "stable_key": "clu_da9da0c17c54d56c", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Guillaume de Hollerius", "confidence": "high", "type": "person", "birth_year": 1500, "death_year": 1577, "description": "French physician and anatomist, known for his anatomical works."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "Anatomia Sambuci", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "anatomia_sambuci", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Anatomia Sambuci", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["Anatomia Sambuci"], "contexts": ["work by Galen"]}, {"entity_id": "anatomiasambuci", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "Anatomiasambuci", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "THEORY", "count": 1, "variants": ["Anatomiasambuci"], "contexts": ["anatomy of elder tree"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Anatomia Sambuci", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "Anatomiasambuci", "similarity": 0.844}], "id": 3867, "stable_key": "clu_8d77965027c5f41d", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Anatomia Sambuci", "confidence": "high", "type": "text", "note": "This refers to an anatomical work, likely on plants, not Galen's anatomy."}, "cross_references": [{"found_name": "Chymica", "link_type": "cross_linguistic", "link_strength": 0.9, "target_cluster_id": 1531, "target_cluster_name": "Chymica", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Anatomia Sambuci is a specific alchemical text.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Anatomia Sambuci is a specific alchemical text.", "is_reverse": true}]}, {"canonical_name": "Yew", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "yew", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "Yew", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["Yew"], "contexts": ["plant and its berries are known to be harmless"]}, {"entity_id": "yews", "book_id": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "name": "yews", "category": "PLANT", "subcategory": "TREE", "count": 1, "variants": ["yews"], "contexts": ["tree species in ancient forests"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "Yew", "target_book": "kosmos_humboldt_1845", "target_name": "yews", "similarity": 0.905}], "id": 3868, "stable_key": "clu_6d1cfc92ee7f7982", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "Yew", "confidence": "high", "type": "plant", "linnaean": "Taxus baccata Linnaeus", "family": "Taxaceae", "note": "The note about berries being 'harmless' is historically inaccurate for *Taxus baccata*, as the seeds within the arils are toxic. This reflects early modern knowledge, not the modern understanding of toxicity.", "wikidata_id": "Q8053327", "wikidata_description": "electoral ward of Liverpool City Council", "wikipedia_extract": "Taxus is a genus of coniferous trees or shrubs known as yews in the family Taxaceae. Yews occur around the globe in temperate zones of the northern hemisphere, northernmost in Norway and southernmost in the South Celebes. Some populations exist in tropical highlands. The oldest known fossil species are from the Early Cretaceous. They are relatively slow-growing and can be very long-lived, and reach heights of 2.5–20 m (8.2–65.6 ft), with trunk girth averaging 5 m (16 ft). They have reddish bark, lanceolate, flat, dark-green leaves 10–40 mm (1⁄2–1+1⁄2 in) long and 2–3 mm (3⁄32–1⁄8 in) broad, arranged spirally on the stem, but with the leaf bases twisted to align the leaves in two flat rows either side of the stem.", "wikipedia_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxus"}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "progression", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "progression", "book_id": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "name": "progression", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["progression"], "contexts": ["movement or advancement"]}, {"entity_id": "progression", "book_id": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "name": "progression", "category": "CONCEPT", "subcategory": "OTHER_CONCEPT", "count": 1, "variants": ["progression"], "contexts": ["abstract concept in spiritualist philosophy"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "pseudodoxia_epidemica_browne_1646", "source_name": "progression", "target_book": "principles_of_psychology_james_1890", "target_name": "progression", "similarity": 1.0}], "id": 3869, "