ods and services.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Industry is a fundamental component of a nation's economy, encompassing the production of goods and services.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "civilisation", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 756, "target_cluster_name": "civilisation", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Civilizations, with their complex social structures and urbanization, develop sophisticated economic systems.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Civilizations, with their complex social structures and urbanization, develop sophisticated economic systems.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "production", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1320, "target_cluster_name": "production", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "Economy is the system of production, distribution, and consumption.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: Economy is the system of production, distribution, and consumption.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "transport", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 1438, "target_cluster_name": "transport", "source_book": "llm_generated", "evidence_snippet": "The concept of 'transport' is often discussed within economic contexts, referring to the movement of goods and people as a factor of production and trade.", "confidence": 0.85, "auto_label": "llm_related", "found_relationship": "reverse: The concept of 'transport' is often discussed within economic contexts, referring to the movement of goods and people as a factor of production and trade.", "is_reverse": true}, {"found_name": "économie politique", "link_type": "conceptual_overlap", "link_strength": 0.5, "target_cluster_id": 2387, "target_cluster_name": "économie politique", "sourc