in the municipality of Esposende, Portugal. In 2013, the parish merged into the new parish Apúlia e Fão. It has a population of 4,323 inhabitants and a total area of 10.51 km2, population density 411.3. It was a town and a municipality until 1834, when it was incorporated into Esposende. Apúlia is known for its dune beaches and Roman-style folk costumes. It may be related to the region of Apulia in Italy, and a possible migration from there during the Roman Empire."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "apothecas", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "apothecas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "apothecas", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["apothecas"], "contexts": ["apothecaries' shops"]}, {"entity_id": "apoſento", "book_id": "polyanthea_medicinal", "name": "apoſento", "category": "PLACE", "subcategory": "OTHER_PLACE", "count": 1, "variants": ["apoſento"], "contexts": ["room"]}], "edges": [{"source_book": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "source_name": "apothecas", "target_book": "polyanthea_medicinal", "target_name": "apoſento", "similarity": 0.885}], "id": 4467, "stable_key": "clu_c20727213f2b07fa", "ground_truth": {"modern_name": "apothecary's shop", "confidence": "high", "type": "place", "country": "Global", "note": "While 'apoſento' can mean room, in the context of apothecaries' shops, it refers to the space where medicines are prepared and sold."}, "cross_references": []}, {"canonical_name": "tavolas", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "book_count": 2, "total_mentions": 2, "members": [{"entity_id": "tavolas", "book_id": "coloquios_da_orta_1563", "name": "tavolas", "category": "OBJECT", "subcategory": "OTHER_OBJECT", "count": 1, "variants": ["tavolas"], "contexts": ["ivory backgammon boards"]}, {"entity_id": "tavola", "book_id": "ricettario_fiorentino_1597", "name": "Tavola", "category": "OBJECT", "subcateg